export const sectionals = [{"id":"sectional-maths","title":"Mathematics sectional","kind":"sectional","minutes":40,"strict":true,"concept":"50 unseen mathematics questions. 40 minutes. The paper submits when time ends.","questions":[{"id":"m-rational-16","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"A rational number lying exactly halfway between 1/5 and 2/7 is","options":["1/4","17/35","1/5","17/70"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The halfway value is the average. (1/5 + 2/7) / 2 = 17/70. 1/4 adds the tops and the bottoms, which is a different number. 17/35 is the sum of the two fractions, not half of that sum. 1/5 is one end of the interval, not the middle."},{"id":"m-rational-17","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"The additive inverse of −6/10 is","options":["3/5","-3/5","5/3","-5/3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The additive inverse of a number is what you add to it to get 0. −6/10 + 3/5 = 0, so the inverse is 3/5. −6/10 is the number itself, not its inverse. 5/3 and -5/3 are reciprocals, which multiply to 1 or −1. They do not add to 0."},{"id":"m-rational-18","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"The multiplicative inverse of 4/9 is","options":["-9/4","9/4","4/9","-4/9"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The multiplicative inverse (reciprocal) of 4/9 is 9/4, because 4/9 × 9/4 = 1. 4/9 is the same number. -9/4 and -4/9 introduce a minus sign, so the product would be −1 or not 1."},{"id":"m-rational-19","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 3/5 + 2/7.","options":["5/12","11/35","31/35","6/35"],"answer":2,"explanation":"To add fractions, use a common denominator. 3/5 + 2/7 = (3×7 + 2×5) / (5×7) = 31/35 = 31/35. Adding tops and bottoms to get 5/12 is not addition. 11/35 is the subtraction. 6/35 is the product of the numerators over the product of the denominators, which is not this sum."},{"id":"m-rational-20","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 6/6 − 2/3.","options":["5/3","4/3","2/3","1/3"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Subtract with a common denominator: 6/6 − 2/3 = (6×3 − 2×6) / (6×3) = 1/3. 5/3 adds instead of subtracting. 4/3 subtracts tops and bottoms separately, which is not the rule. 2/3 is a product, not a difference."},{"id":"m-rational-21","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 2/5 × 3/7.","options":["6/35","14/15","5/12","29/35"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply numerators and denominators: 2/5 × 3/7 = 6/35 = 6/35. 14/15 swaps the second fraction as if this were division. 5/12 adds. 29/35 is the addition formula."},{"id":"m-rational-22","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 3/5 ÷ 4/3.","options":["4/5","9/20","20/9","-11/15"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal. 3/5 ÷ 4/3 = 3/5 × 3/4 = 9/20. 4/5 multiplies the fractions instead of dividing. 20/9 is the reciprocal of the correct value. -11/15 uses a subtraction pattern that does not belong here."},{"id":"m-rational-23","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Which is larger: 3/7 or 5/10?","options":["3/7","They are equal","1/2","8/17"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Cross-multiply. 3×10 = 30 and 5×7 = 35. The larger product belongs to the larger fraction, so 1/2 is larger. 3/7 is the smaller one. They are not equal. 8/17 adds the tops and the bottoms, which is not a comparison."},{"id":"m-rational-24","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"A rational number lying exactly halfway between 4/6 and 5/8 is","options":["9/14","31/24","2/3","31/48"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The halfway value is the average. (4/6 + 5/8) / 2 = 31/48. 9/14 adds the tops and the bottoms, which is a different number. 31/24 is the sum of the two fractions, not half of that sum. 2/3 is one end of the interval, not the middle."},{"id":"m-rational-25","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"The additive inverse of −2/7 is","options":["2/7","-2/7","7/2","-7/2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The additive inverse of a number is what you add to it to get 0. −2/7 + 2/7 = 0, so the inverse is 2/7. −2/7 is the number itself, not its inverse. 7/2 and -7/2 are reciprocals, which multiply to 1 or −1. They do not add to 0."},{"id":"m-rational-26","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"The multiplicative inverse of 2/8 is","options":["-4","4","1/4","-1/4"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The multiplicative inverse (reciprocal) of 2/8 is 4, because 2/8 × 4 = 1. 1/4 is the same number. -4 and -1/4 introduce a minus sign, so the product would be −1 or not 1."},{"id":"m-rational-27","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 3/6 + 1/7.","options":["4/13","5/14","9/14","1/14"],"answer":2,"explanation":"To add fractions, use a common denominator. 3/6 + 1/7 = (3×7 + 1×6) / (6×7) = 27/42 = 9/14. Adding tops and bottoms to get 4/13 is not addition. 5/14 is the subtraction. 1/14 is the product of the numerators over the product of the denominators, which is not this sum."},{"id":"m-rational-28","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 6/7 − 1/3.","options":["25/21","5/4","2/7","11/21"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Subtract with a common denominator: 6/7 − 1/3 = (6×3 − 1×7) / (7×3) = 11/21. 25/21 adds instead of subtracting. 5/4 subtracts tops and bottoms separately, which is not the rule. 2/7 is a product, not a difference."},{"id":"m-rational-29","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 2/6 × 3/6.","options":["1/6","2/3","5/12","5/6"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Multiply numerators and denominators: 2/6 × 3/6 = 6/36 = 1/6. 2/3 swaps the second fraction as if this were division. 5/12 adds. 5/6 is the addition formula."},{"id":"m-rational-30","topicId":"m-rational","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 6/6 ÷ 4/3.","options":["4/3","3/4","-1/3","0"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal. 6/6 ÷ 4/3 = 6/6 × 3/4 = 3/4. 4/3 multiplies the fractions instead of dividing. 4/3 is the reciprocal of the correct value. -1/3 uses a subtraction pattern that does not belong here."},{"id":"m-integers-16","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Add 2.1 + 2.6.","options":["5.7","4.70","-0.5","4.7"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Line up the decimal points. 2.1 + 2.6 = 4.7. The other options come from a shifted decimal, from subtracting, or from adding an extra tenth."},{"id":"m-integers-17","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Convert 25°C to Fahrenheit. Use F = (9/5)C + 32.","options":["77","57","45.9","45"],"answer":0,"explanation":"F = (9/5)×25 + 32 = 77. 57 only adds 32. 45.888888888888886 uses the reverse formula. 45 forgets to add 32."},{"id":"m-integers-18","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 7 × 5 − (7 + 5).","options":["47","23","35","24"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Do the multiplication before the subtraction. 7 × 5 = 35, then 35 − 12 = 23. 47 adds the bracket instead of subtracting it. 35 stops before the subtraction. The last option multiplies a difference and a sum, which is a different expression."},{"id":"m-integers-19","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (−11) + 7.","options":["18","4","-4","-18"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Adding a positive number moves right on the number line. −11 + 7 = -4. 18 adds the absolute values and drops the sign. 4 subtracts the wrong way. -18 subtracts 7 instead of adding it."},{"id":"m-integers-20","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (−22) × (−7).","options":["-154","29","-29","154"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The product of two negative integers is positive. (−22) × (−7) = 154. -154 keeps a minus sign, which would be right only if one factor were negative. 29 and -29 are sums, not products."},{"id":"m-integers-21","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"3/4 of 88 is","options":["66","88","264","22"],"answer":0,"explanation":"3/4 of 88 means 88 × 3/4 = 66. 88 forgets to take the fraction. 264 multiplies by 3 and never divides by 4. 22 is only the multiplier used to build 88, not the result."},{"id":"m-integers-22","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Add 1.8 + 2.5.","options":["5.3","4.3","4.30","-0.7"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Line up the decimal points. 1.8 + 2.5 = 4.3. The other options come from a shifted decimal, from subtracting, or from adding an extra tenth."},{"id":"m-integers-23","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Convert 30°C to Fahrenheit. Use F = (9/5)C + 32.","options":["62","48.7","86","54"],"answer":2,"explanation":"F = (9/5)×30 + 32 = 86. 62 only adds 32. 48.66666666666667 uses the reverse formula. 54 forgets to add 32."},{"id":"m-integers-24","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 7 × 6 − (7 + 6).","options":["55","42","13","29"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Do the multiplication before the subtraction. 7 × 6 = 42, then 42 − 13 = 29. 55 adds the bracket instead of subtracting it. 42 stops before the subtraction. The last option multiplies a difference and a sum, which is a different expression."},{"id":"m-integers-25","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (−17) + 6.","options":["-11","23","11","-23"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Adding a positive number moves right on the number line. −17 + 6 = -11. 23 adds the absolute values and drops the sign. 11 subtracts the wrong way. -23 subtracts 6 instead of adding it."},{"id":"m-integers-26","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (−28) × (−5).","options":["-140","140","33","-33"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The product of two negative integers is positive. (−28) × (−5) = 140. -140 keeps a minus sign, which would be right only if one factor were negative. 33 and -33 are sums, not products."},{"id":"m-integers-27","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"3/4 of 112 is","options":["112","336","84","28"],"answer":2,"explanation":"3/4 of 112 means 112 × 3/4 = 84. 112 forgets to take the fraction. 336 multiplies by 3 and never divides by 4. 28 is only the multiplier used to build 112, not the result."},{"id":"m-integers-28","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Add 1.5 + 3.1.","options":["5.6","4.60","-1.6","4.6"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Line up the decimal points. 1.5 + 3.1 = 4.6. The other options come from a shifted decimal, from subtracting, or from adding an extra tenth."},{"id":"m-integers-29","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Convert 35°C to Fahrenheit. Use F = (9/5)C + 32.","options":["95","67","51.4","63"],"answer":0,"explanation":"F = (9/5)×35 + 32 = 95. 67 only adds 32. 51.44444444444444 uses the reverse formula. 63 forgets to add 32."},{"id":"m-integers-30","topicId":"m-integers","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 7 × 7 − (7 + 7).","options":["63","35","49","0"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Do the multiplication before the subtraction. 7 × 7 = 49, then 49 − 14 = 35. 63 adds the bracket instead of subtracting it. 49 stops before the subtraction. The last option multiplies a difference and a sum, which is a different expression."},{"id":"m-playing-16","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"What digit should replace * so that 163* is divisible by 3?","options":["0","1","3","2"],"answer":3,"explanation":"A number is divisible by 3 when the sum of its digits is divisible by 3. The digits of 163 add up to 10. With * = 2, the total is divisible by 3, so 1632 works. The other digits leave a remainder when the digit sum is divided by 3."},{"id":"m-playing-17","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"Which of these is true about 31?","options":["31 is not divisible by 2","31 is divisible by 2","31 is divisible by 9","31 is divisible by 5"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A number is divisible by 2 when its last digit is even. The last digit of 31 is 1, so the true statement is the one about 2. Divisibility by 5 needs the last digit 0 or 5. Divisibility by 9 needs the digit sum to be a multiple of 9. 31 is odd."},{"id":"m-playing-18","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"The HCF of 22 and 24 is 2. Their LCM is","options":["528","264","2","46"],"answer":1,"explanation":"For two whole numbers, HCF × LCM = product of the numbers. So LCM = 22 × 24 / 2 = 264. 528 is the product, which still contains the common factor. 2 is the HCF, not the LCM. 46 is the sum and is not used in this rule."},{"id":"m-playing-19","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"The prime factorisation of 96 is","options":["96 × 1","2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2","2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 3","2 × 49"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Keep dividing by the smallest prime until you reach 1. 96 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 3. 96 × 1 is not a prime factorisation because 96 is not prime. Stopping early leaves a composite factor. The last option changes a factor, so the product is no longer 96."},{"id":"m-playing-20","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"Is 113 divisible by 5?","options":["Yes, because the last digit is 0 or 5","Yes, because it is greater than 50","No, because it is even","No, because the last digit is not 0 or 5"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Divisibility by 5 depends only on the last digit. The last digit of 113 is 3. That is not 0 or 5, so it is not divisible by 5. Being large, or being even, does not decide divisibility by 5."},{"id":"m-playing-21","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"What digit should replace * so that 136* is divisible by 3?","options":["2","0","1","3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A number is divisible by 3 when the sum of its digits is divisible by 3. The digits of 136 add up to 10. With * = 2, the total is divisible by 3, so 1362 works. The other digits leave a remainder when the digit sum is divided by 3."},{"id":"m-playing-22","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"Which of these is true about 36?","options":["36 is not divisible by 2","36 is divisible by 2","36 is divisible by 9","36 is divisible by 5"],"answer":1,"explanation":"A number is divisible by 2 when its last digit is even. The last digit of 36 is 6, so the true statement is the one about 2. Divisibility by 5 needs the last digit 0 or 5. Divisibility by 9 needs the digit sum to be a multiple of 9. 36 is even."},{"id":"m-playing-23","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"The HCF of 20 and 24 is 4. Their LCM is","options":["480","4","120","44"],"answer":2,"explanation":"For two whole numbers, HCF × LCM = product of the numbers. So LCM = 20 × 24 / 4 = 120. 480 is the product, which still contains the common factor. 4 is the HCF, not the LCM. 44 is the sum and is not used in this rule."},{"id":"m-playing-24","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"The prime factorisation of 126 is","options":["126 × 1","2 × 3 × 3","2 × 64","2 × 3 × 3 × 7"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Keep dividing by the smallest prime until you reach 1. 126 = 2 × 3 × 3 × 7. 126 × 1 is not a prime factorisation because 126 is not prime. Stopping early leaves a composite factor. The last option changes a factor, so the product is no longer 126."},{"id":"m-playing-25","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"Is 160 divisible by 5?","options":["Yes, because the last digit is 0 or 5","No, because the last digit is not 0 or 5","Yes, because it is greater than 50","No, because it is even"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Divisibility by 5 depends only on the last digit. The last digit of 160 is 0. That is 0 or 5, so it is divisible by 5. Being large, or being even, does not decide divisibility by 5."},{"id":"m-playing-26","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"What digit should replace * so that 109* is divisible by 3?","options":["0","2","1","3"],"answer":1,"explanation":"A number is divisible by 3 when the sum of its digits is divisible by 3. The digits of 109 add up to 10. With * = 2, the total is divisible by 3, so 1092 works. The other digits leave a remainder when the digit sum is divided by 3."},{"id":"m-playing-27","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"Which of these is true about 41?","options":["41 is divisible by 2","41 is divisible by 9","41 is not divisible by 2","41 is divisible by 5"],"answer":2,"explanation":"A number is divisible by 2 when its last digit is even. The last digit of 41 is 1, so the true statement is the one about 2. Divisibility by 5 needs the last digit 0 or 5. Divisibility by 9 needs the digit sum to be a multiple of 9. 41 is odd."},{"id":"m-playing-28","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"The HCF of 18 and 24 is 6. Their LCM is","options":["432","6","42","72"],"answer":3,"explanation":"For two whole numbers, HCF × LCM = product of the numbers. So LCM = 18 × 24 / 6 = 72. 432 is the product, which still contains the common factor. 6 is the HCF, not the LCM. 42 is the sum and is not used in this rule."},{"id":"m-playing-29","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"The prime factorisation of 108 is","options":["2 × 2 × 3 × 3 × 3","108 × 1","2 × 2 × 3 × 3","2 × 55"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Keep dividing by the smallest prime until you reach 1. 108 = 2 × 2 × 3 × 3 × 3. 108 × 1 is not a prime factorisation because 108 is not prime. Stopping early leaves a composite factor. The last option changes a factor, so the product is no longer 108."},{"id":"m-playing-30","topicId":"m-playing","subject":"maths","stem":"Is 121 divisible by 5?","options":["Yes, because the last digit is 0 or 5","No, because the last digit is not 0 or 5","Yes, because it is greater than 50","No, because it is even"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Divisibility by 5 depends only on the last digit. The last digit of 121 is 1. That is not 0 or 5, so it is not divisible by 5. Being large, or being even, does not decide divisibility by 5."},{"id":"m-exponents-16","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Write 3^−2 with a positive power.","options":["1/3^2","3^2","−3^2","−1/3^2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A negative power means the reciprocal: 3^−2 = 1/3^2. 3^2 drops the minus in the power. −3^2 and −1/3^2 put a minus sign in front. A negative index does not make the value negative when the base is positive."},{"id":"m-exponents-17","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 5^4 × 5^1.","options":["5^4","25^5","5^5","5^4 + 5^1"],"answer":2,"explanation":"When the bases are the same, add the powers: 5^4 × 5^1 = 5^5. 5^4 multiplies the powers, which is the rule for a power of a power. 25^5 changes the base. Adding the two powers as terms is not multiplication."},{"id":"m-exponents-18","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (8^4)^2.","options":["8^8","8^6","16^4","8^4"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A power of a power multiplies the indices: (8^4)^2 = 8^8. Adding the indices is for multiplying the same base. 16^4 changes the base. 8^4 drops the outside power."},{"id":"m-exponents-19","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"The value of 8^0 is","options":["0","1","8","-1"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Any non-zero number to the power 0 is 1, so 8^0 = 1. It is not 0, and it is not the base itself. −1 would be a negative power or a sign error, not the zero-power rule."},{"id":"m-exponents-20","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Write 4^−2 with a positive power.","options":["4^2","−4^2","1/4^2","−1/4^2"],"answer":2,"explanation":"A negative power means the reciprocal: 4^−2 = 1/4^2. 4^2 drops the minus in the power. −4^2 and −1/4^2 put a minus sign in front. A negative index does not make the value negative when the base is positive."}]},{"id":"sectional-science","title":"Science sectional","kind":"sectional","minutes":40,"strict":true,"concept":"50 unseen science questions. 40 minutes. The paper submits when time ends.","questions":[{"id":"s-cell-16","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Why does a plant cell keep a firm shape?","options":["Its cell membrane is a hard shell like bone","The nucleus forms a thick coat around the whole cell","Its cell wall is a firm extra covering made of cellulose","Mitochondria join up to make a cage around the cell"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Its cell wall is a firm extra covering made of cellulose. Outside the cell membrane, a plant cell has a cell wall. The wall is mostly cellulose, and it makes the cell rigid and protective. Its cell membrane is a hard shell like bone is wrong because the cell membrane is thin and flexible, not a bony shell. The nucleus forms a thick coat around the whole cell is wrong because the nucleus is inside the cell and is not an outer coat. Mitochondria join up to make a cage around the cell is wrong because mitochondria are small organelles in the cytoplasm and do not form an outer cage.\nयाद रखो: पौधे की शक्ल सेल्यूलोज़ की दीवार से कड़ी रहती है, हड्डी जैसी झिल्ली से नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Its cell membrane is a hard shell like bone गलत है: झिल्ली मुलायम दरवाज़ा है।"},{"id":"s-cell-17","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Which cell usually contains one large central vacuole?","options":["A plant cell","A bacterial cell","A typical animal cell","A virus"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is A plant cell. A vacuole is a sac filled with cell sap. In many plant cells it is large and central and helps the cell stay firm. Vacuoles in animal cells are small. A bacterial cell is wrong because bacteria are prokaryotes and are not described as having one large central vacuole like a plant cell. A typical animal cell is wrong because animal cells have small vacuoles, or sometimes none, rather than one huge central vacuole. A virus is wrong because a virus is not a true cell and has no vacuole.\nयाद रखो: पौधे के बीच बड़ा पानी का टैंक (vacuole) होता है। जानवर के टैंक छोटे होते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: A typical animal cell में बड़ा केंद्रीय टैंक नहीं होता।"},{"id":"s-cell-18","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"What do chromosomes carry?","options":["Chlorophyll","Cellulose","Only stored starch and nothing inherited","Genes"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Genes. Chromosomes lie in the nucleus of a eukaryotic cell. Each one carries many genes, which are the units of inheritance. Chlorophyll is wrong because chlorophyll is the green pigment stored in chloroplasts. Cellulose is wrong because cellulose is the building material of the plant cell wall. Only stored starch and nothing inherited is wrong because chromosomes are inheritance structures, and starch is a stored food.\nयाद रखो: क्रोमोसोम जीन की माला उठाए घूमते हैं। क्लोरोफिल हरे रसोईघर में रहता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Chlorophyll क्रोमोसोम का सामान नहीं, क्लोरोप्लास्ट का हरा रंग है।"},{"id":"s-cell-19","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Green plants prepare their own food. What are organisms that do this called?","options":["Parasites","Autotrophs","Saprotrophs","Insectivores"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Autotrophs. Auto means self and troph refers to nutrition. Green plants are autotrophs because photosynthesis lets them make food. Animals that depend on other organisms are heterotrophs. Parasites is wrong because a parasite such as Cuscuta takes ready-made food from another living plant. Saprotrophs is wrong because saprotrophs such as fungi feed on dead and decaying matter. Insectivores is wrong because an insectivore such as the pitcher plant traps insects, but ordinary green plants are not classed that way.\nयाद रखो: ऑटो मतलब खुद। हरा पौधा अपना खाना खुद पकाता है, इसलिए ऑटोट्रॉफ।\nगलत मत याद करना: Parasites जैसे अमरबेल तैयार खाना चुराते हैं, खुद नहीं पकाते।"},{"id":"s-cell-20","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Which job belongs to the nucleus?","options":["It traps sunlight for photosynthesis","It is the rigid outer covering of a plant cell","It controls the activities of the cell","It pumps blood around an animal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is It controls the activities of the cell. The nucleus is covered by a nuclear membrane in eukaryotic cells. It contains the chromosomes and directs how the cell grows, works, and divides. It traps sunlight for photosynthesis is wrong because chloroplasts trap sunlight. It is the rigid outer covering of a plant cell is wrong because that covering is the cell wall. It pumps blood around an animal is wrong because the heart pumps blood, and the nucleus is not a pump.\nयाद रखो: न्यूक्लियस कोशिका का मालिक है। बढ़ना, काम और बँटवारा वही चलाता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: It traps sunlight for photosynthesis क्लोरोप्लास्ट का काम है, मालिक का नहीं।"},{"id":"s-cell-21","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Blue-green algae are grouped with bacteria as prokaryotes because their nuclear material is...","options":["Packed inside a large nucleus with a nuclear membrane","Stored in a cellulose wall like the wall of a rose cell","Absent, so these organisms have no hereditary material at all","Not enclosed by a nuclear membrane"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Not enclosed by a nuclear membrane. Prokaryotic cells lack a well organised nucleus. Both bacteria and blue-green algae belong to this group, unlike plant and animal cells. Packed inside a large nucleus with a nuclear membrane is wrong because a membrane-bound nucleus would make the cell eukaryotic. Stored in a cellulose wall like the wall of a rose cell is wrong because the wall is not the nuclear material, and a wall does not decide the prokaryote group. Absent, so these organisms have no hereditary material at all is wrong because they do have hereditary material, but it is not in an organised nucleus.\nयाद रखो: नील-हरित शैवाल और बैक्टीरिया दोनों का न्यूक्लियस बिना झिल्ली के खुला पड़ा है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Packed inside a large nucleus with a nuclear membrane तो यूकैरियोट का कमरा है।"},{"id":"s-cell-22","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement about plastids is correct?","options":["Chloroplasts are plastids that help a green plant make food","Plastids are found in every animal cell","Plastids release energy and are called the powerhouses","Plastids are the empty cork rooms that Hooke named"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Chloroplasts are plastids that help a green plant make food. Plastids are present only in plant cells. The green ones contain chlorophyll and are called chloroplasts. They are the sites of photosynthesis. Plastids are found in every animal cell is wrong because plastids occur in plant cells, not in animal cells. Plastids release energy and are called the powerhouses is wrong because mitochondria are the powerhouses. Plastids are the empty cork rooms that Hooke named is wrong because Hooke named those rooms cells, and plastids are organelles inside plant cells.\nयाद रखो: प्लास्टिड सिर्फ पौधे की थैली है। हरी वाली क्लोरोप्लास्ट खाना बनाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Plastids release energy and are called the powerhouses गलत है: बिजली घर माइटोकॉन्ड्रिया है।"},{"id":"s-cell-23","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"A nerve cell is long and branched, while a red blood cell is rounded. What does this show?","options":["Every cell in the human body has the same shape","The shape of a cell is related to the work it does","Only plant cells are allowed to have different shapes","A nerve cell has no nucleus because it is long"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is The shape of a cell is related to the work it does. Cells are not all boxes of one shape. A long nerve cell can carry messages over a distance, and a rounded red blood cell can move through narrow vessels. Every cell in the human body has the same shape is wrong because nerve cells, muscle cells, and red blood cells do not look alike. Only plant cells are allowed to have different shapes is wrong because animal cells also vary in shape. A nerve cell has no nucleus because it is long is wrong because a nerve cell does have a nucleus, and its long shape helps it carry messages.\nयाद रखो: नस की कोशिका लंबी तार है, लाल रक्त गोली है। शक्ल काम के हिसाब से बनती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Every cell in the human body has the same shape गलत है: सब एक जैसी डिब्बी नहीं।"},{"id":"s-cell-24","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"The human heart pumps blood around the body. How many chambers does that heart have?","options":["Two","One","Four","Sixteen"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Four. The human heart has four chambers: two upper atria and two lower ventricles. It pumps blood, and haemoglobin in the red blood cells carries oxygen in that blood. Two is wrong because the human heart is not a two-chamber pump. One is wrong because a single chamber could not separate the blood the way the human heart does. Sixteen is wrong because sixteen is far more than the four chambers of the human heart.\nयाद रखो: इंसान के दिल के चार कमरे: ऊपर दो आलिंद, नीचे दो निलय।\nगलत मत याद करना: Two कमरे वाला पंप इंसान का दिल नहीं होता।"},{"id":"s-cell-25","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Which of these cells has a cell wall?","options":["An onion peel cell","A human cheek cell","A muscle cell from the arm","A nerve cell"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is An onion peel cell. Onion peel cells are plant cells, so each one has a cellulose cell wall. Cheek cells, muscle cells, and nerve cells are animal cells and lack that wall. A human cheek cell is wrong because a cheek cell is an animal cell and has no cell wall. A muscle cell from the arm is wrong because muscle cells are animal cells and have no cellulose wall. A nerve cell is wrong because a nerve cell is an animal cell bounded by a cell membrane only.\nयाद रखो: प्याज़ की कोशिका पौधे की है, दीवार सहित। गाल, मांस और नस जानवर हैं, दीवार नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: A human cheek cell जानवर की है, उसके पास दीवार नहीं।"},{"id":"s-cell-26","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"What happens inside the chloroplasts of a leaf cell in sunlight?","options":["Oxygen is used up to manufacture carbon dioxide","Light energy is used to help the cell make food","Chromosomes are stored there for inheritance","The vacuole pumps blood through the leaf"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Light energy is used to help the cell make food. Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll. In sunlight they help the cell turn carbon dioxide and water into food. That is why green leaves are the main food-making parts of a plant. Oxygen is used up to manufacture carbon dioxide is wrong because in photosynthesis carbon dioxide is used and oxygen is released, so this gas story is reversed. Chromosomes are stored there for inheritance is wrong because chromosomes are in the nucleus, not in the chloroplast. The vacuole pumps blood through the leaf is wrong because a leaf cell has no blood, and the vacuole does not act as a heart.\nयाद रखो: धूप में क्लोरोप्लास्ट रसोई खोलता है और कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड व पानी से खाना बनाता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Oxygen is used up to manufacture carbon dioxide उलटी रेसिपी है।"},{"id":"s-cell-27","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement about the size of cells is correct?","options":["Every cell is large enough to see with the naked eye","The nucleus is always bigger than the whole cell","Most cells are too small to see without a microscope","Bacteria are the largest cells known"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Most cells are too small to see without a microscope. Cell size is usually measured in micrometres, and a microscope is needed. An ostrich egg is an unusually large single cell, and a nerve cell can be long, but those are special cases. Every cell is large enough to see with the naked eye is wrong because a few cells, such as a bird egg, are large, but most cells are microscopic. The nucleus is always bigger than the whole cell is wrong because the nucleus is a part inside the cell, so it cannot be larger than the whole cell. Bacteria are the largest cells known is wrong because bacteria are among the smallest cells.\nयाद रखो: ज़्यादातर कोशिकाएँ इतनी छोटी हैं कि बिना माइक्रोस्कोप नहीं दिखतीं। शुतुरमुर्ग का अंडा अपवाद है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Every cell is large enough to see with the naked eye गलत है।"},{"id":"s-cell-28","topicId":"s-cell","subject":"science","stem":"A leaf cell and a root cell of the same plant both have a nucleus and a cell wall. Which extra feature is expected in the green leaf cell?","options":["A cell membrane that root cells completely lack","A total absence of cytoplasm","An organised nucleus found only in the leaf","Chloroplasts"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Chloroplasts. Cells in a green leaf that receive light contain chloroplasts so they can make food. Underground root cells usually lack chloroplasts, but they still have a wall, a membrane, cytoplasm, and a nucleus. A cell membrane that root cells completely lack is wrong because root cells also have a cell membrane. A total absence of cytoplasm is wrong because both leaf cells and root cells contain cytoplasm. An organised nucleus found only in the leaf is wrong because both cells are eukaryotic plant cells with a nucleus.\nयाद रखो: हरी पत्ती के पास अतिरिक्त हरा रसोईघर (chloroplast) है। अँधेरी जड़ के पास नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: A cell membrane that root cells completely lack गलत है: जड़ के पास भी झिल्ली होती है।"},{"id":"s-micro-16","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Sodium benzoate and sodium metabisulphite are examples of...","options":["Machines that separate grain from chaff","The heating and chilling steps of pasteurisation","Chemical preservatives used in jams and squashes","Bacteria that fix nitrogen in pea roots"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Chemical preservatives used in jams and squashes. These salts are common chemical preservatives. They are added to jams, squashes, and similar foods to check microbes. Salt, sugar, oil, and vinegar are the everyday preservatives used at home. Machines that separate grain from chaff is wrong because separating grain from chaff is winnowing, not a chemical preservative. The heating and chilling steps of pasteurisation is wrong because pasteurisation uses heat and cold, not these named salts. Bacteria that fix nitrogen in pea roots is wrong because that bacterium is Rhizobium.\nयाद रखो: सोडियम बेंजोएट और सोडियम मेटाबाइसल्फाइट जैम-स्क्वैश के रासायनिक पहरेदार हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Bacteria that fix nitrogen in pea roots राइजोबियम है, ये नमक नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-17","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Dengue is spread from person to person by the","options":["female Aedes mosquito","female Anopheles mosquito","housefly","earthworm"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is female Aedes mosquito. The female Aedes mosquito is the carrier of the dengue virus. Female Anopheles mosquito is wrong because the female Anopheles mosquito carries the protozoan that causes malaria, not dengue. Housefly is wrong because a housefly can carry germs such as those of cholera onto uncovered food, but it does not spread dengue. Earthworm is wrong because an earthworm helps to loosen soil and does not carry the dengue virus.\nयाद रखो: Aedes डेंगू लाता है। मैडम अनोफ़ीलिज मलेरिया लाती है। दोनों को एक मच्छर मत बना देना।\nगलत मत याद करना: female Anopheles mosquito मलेरिया की टैक्सी है, डेंगू की नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-18","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"How does a vaccine protect the body?","options":["Oil preserves the body in the same way that it preserves a pickle","The vaccine kills every virus living in the soil","It is a fertiliser that raises nitrogen in the blood","Dead or weakened microbes teach the body to make antibodies"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Dead or weakened microbes teach the body to make antibodies. If a disease microbe enters, the body produces antibodies. A vaccine introduces dead or weakened microbes so those antibodies form without a full attack of the disease. Cholera, tuberculosis, smallpox, and hepatitis can be prevented by vaccination. Oil preserves the body in the same way that it preserves a pickle is wrong because oil is a food preservative, and a vaccine works through the body's defences. The vaccine kills every virus living in the soil is wrong because a vaccine is given to a person or animal, and it is not a soil treatment. It is a fertiliser that raises nitrogen in the blood is wrong because fertilisers feed crops, and vaccines do not work that way.\nयाद रखो: वैक्सीन मरा या कमज़ोर कीटाणु है, जो शरीर को एंटीबॉडी सिखाता है। बीमारी के बाद की दवा नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: It is a fertiliser that raises nitrogen in the blood खाद है, टीका नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-19","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Cholera is caused by bacteria. How does it mainly spread?","options":["Through the bite of a female Anopheles mosquito","Through contaminated water or food","Through air in the same way as measles","By contact with rust on a wheat leaf"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Through contaminated water or food. The disease table lists cholera as a bacterial disease spread by water or food. Typhoid bacteria spread through water. Clean water, cooked food, and covering food from houseflies help prevent such illnesses. Through the bite of a female Anopheles mosquito is wrong because that bite spreads malaria, not cholera. Through air in the same way as measles is wrong because measles is a viral disease that spreads through air. By contact with rust on a wheat leaf is wrong because rust of wheat is a fungal disease of a plant.\nयाद रखो: हैजा बैक्टीरिया गंदा पानी या खाने से आता है, मच्छर के काटने से नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Through the bite of a female Anopheles mosquito मलेरिया का रास्ता है, हैजा का नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-20","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Which disease is caused by a bacterium and spreads through air?","options":["Measles","Malaria","Tuberculosis","Polio"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Tuberculosis. Tuberculosis is a bacterial disease. The microbes can pass through the air from an infected person. Patients are kept apart, and vaccination is given at a suitable age. Measles is wrong because measles spreads through air, but it is caused by a virus. Malaria is wrong because malaria is caused by a protozoan and is spread by a mosquito. Polio is wrong because polio is caused by a virus and spreads through air or water.\nयाद रखो: टीबी बैक्टीरिया है और हवा से फैलता है। खसरा भी हवा से आता है, पर वह वायरस है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Measles हवा से फैलता है, पर उसका कीटाणु वायरस है, बैक्टीरिया नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-21","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Rust of wheat is caused by which microorganism?","options":["A bacterium","A virus","A protozoan","A fungus"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is A fungus. The plant disease table lists rust of wheat under fungi. It spreads by air and seeds. Citrus canker is bacterial and spreads by air. A bacterium is wrong because citrus canker is a bacterial plant disease, while rust of wheat is fungal. A virus is wrong because yellow vein mosaic of bhindi is caused by a virus. A protozoan is wrong because malaria is the protozoan disease in the human table, and wheat rust is not malaria.\nयाद रखो: गेहूँ का रतुआ (rust) फफूँद का दाग है। सिट्रस कैंकर बैक्टीरिया का है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A bacterium सिट्रस कैंकर वाला है, गेहूँ के रतुए वाला नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-22","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"How is yellow vein mosaic of bhindi, or okra, transmitted?","options":["By an insect","By a frog sitting on the leaf","By winnowing grain in the wind","By pasteurising the leaves"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is By an insect. Yellow vein mosaic of bhindi is caused by a virus. The table gives its mode of transmission as an insect. Plant diseases like this reduce the crop yield. By a frog sitting on the leaf is wrong because frogs are not the carriers listed for this plant virus. By winnowing grain in the wind is wrong because winnowing separates chaff from grain and is not the mode in the disease table. By pasteurising the leaves is wrong because pasteurisation is a treatment for milk.\nयाद रखो: भिंडी की पीली नाड़ियों वाला मोजेक वायरस कीड़ा लेकर आता है। मेंढक डाकिया नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: By a frog sitting on the leaf मज़ेदार है, पर किताब का रास्ता कीट है।"},{"id":"s-micro-23","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Which human disease in the chapter table is caused by a protozoan?","options":["Typhoid","Malaria","Chickenpox","Hepatitis A"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Malaria. In the human disease table, malaria is the disease caused by protozoa and spread by a mosquito. Typhoid is bacterial. Chickenpox and hepatitis A are viral. Typhoid is wrong because typhoid is caused by bacteria. Chickenpox is wrong because chickenpox is caused by a virus. Hepatitis A is wrong because hepatitis A is caused by a virus and spreads through water.\nयाद रखो: सारणी में प्रोटोजोआ वाला इंसानी रोग मलेरिया है। टाइफाइड बैक्टीरिया, चेचक वायरस।\nगलत मत याद करना: Typhoid बैक्टीरिया का बुखार है, प्रोटोजोआ का नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-24","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Anthrax in cattle and humans is caused by...","options":["A virus","A shortage of fertiliser in the grass","A bacterium","The bite of a male Anopheles mosquito"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is A bacterium. Robert Koch, in 1876, discovered the bacterium Bacillus anthracis that causes anthrax. Anthrax is dangerous for both humans and cattle. Foot and mouth disease of cattle is caused by a virus. A virus is wrong because foot and mouth disease of cattle is viral, but anthrax is bacterial. A shortage of fertiliser in the grass is wrong because anthrax is an infection, not a lack of crop fertiliser. The bite of a male Anopheles mosquito is wrong because the female Anopheles spreads malaria, which is a different disease.\nयाद रखो: एंथ्रैक्स बैक्टीरिया बैसिलस एंथ्रासिस का काम है। कोच ने उसे 1876 में पकड़ा।\nगलत मत याद करना: A virus मवेशियों का खुरपका-मुँहपका है, एंथ्रैक्स नहीं।"},{"id":"s-micro-25","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Why must the full antibiotic course prescribed by a doctor be finished?","options":["A wrong dose or an unfinished course can make the drug less effective later","Antibiotics work only when mixed with yeast and sugar","A short course turns the antibiotic into a vaccine","Leftover tablets should be sprayed on kharif crops as urea"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is A wrong dose or an unfinished course can make the drug less effective later. Antibiotics should be taken only on the advice of a qualified doctor. If they are taken when not needed, or in the wrong dose, the drug may work less well later. An unnecessary dose can also kill helpful bacteria in the body. Antibiotics work only when mixed with yeast and sugar is wrong because yeast and sugar are used in fermentation, not as a way of taking antibiotics. A short course turns the antibiotic into a vaccine is wrong because an antibiotic does not become a vaccine if the course is cut short. Leftover tablets should be sprayed on kharif crops as urea is wrong because urea is a fertiliser, and antibiotic tablets are not a crop spray.\nयाद रखो: एंटीबायोटिक का कोर्स बीच में छोड़ोगे तो दवा बाद में सुस्त पड़ सकती है। डॉक्टर की बात पूरी करो।\nगलत मत याद करना: A short course turns the antibiotic into a vaccine कोर्स आधा छोड़ने से टीका नहीं बनता।"},{"id":"s-micro-26","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"How do some bacteria and fungi help clean the environment?","options":["They all cause measles","They break down dead plants and animals into usable substances","They build a cell wall around every animal","They turn every sugar straight into penicillin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is They break down dead plants and animals into usable substances. Organic waste such as vegetable peels and remains of plants and animals is broken down by bacteria and fungi. Harmful-looking waste becomes harmless substances that nature can use again. This is why decomposer microbes are friends of the environment. They all cause measles is wrong because measles is a particular viral disease, not the work of decomposers. They build a cell wall around every animal is wrong because animal cells do not have cell walls, and decomposers do not add them. They turn every sugar straight into penicillin is wrong because penicillin comes from a particular mould, not from every decomposer.\nयाद रखो: कुछ बैक्टीरिया और फफूँद मुर्दा पौधों-जानवरों को फिर से इस्तेमाल लायक मिट्टी बना देते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: They all cause measles गलत है: सफाई वाले सब खसरा नहीं फैलाते।"},{"id":"s-micro-27","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement about algae is correct?","options":["All algae are viruses","Algae are the eggs of Anopheles mosquitoes","Some algae, such as Chlamydomonas, are microorganisms","Algae never make their own food"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Some algae, such as Chlamydomonas, are microorganisms. Algae are one of the four major groups. Some, such as Chlamydomonas, are microscopic, while others, such as many seaweeds, are larger. Several algae make food with chlorophyll. All algae are viruses is wrong because algae are a separate group, and viruses are not algae. Algae are the eggs of Anopheles mosquitoes is wrong because mosquito eggs are not algae. Algae never make their own food is wrong because many algae contain chlorophyll and make food, as the chapter figures of Chlamydomonas and Spirogyra suggest.\nयाद रखो: क्लैमाइडोमोनास जैसी कुछ शैवाल सूक्ष्मजीव हैं। सब शैवाल वायरस नहीं होतीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: All algae are viruses शैवाल को वायरस की टोपी मत पहनाओ।"},{"id":"s-micro-28","topicId":"s-micro","subject":"science","stem":"A packet of milk was heated to about 70 degrees Celsius for 15 to 30 seconds and then chilled at once. Which method is this?","options":["Fermentation","Vaccination","Nitrogen fixation","Pasteurisation"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Pasteurisation. The short heat treatment followed by sudden cooling is pasteurisation. It prevents the growth of microbes in milk. It is different from setting curd with Lactobacillus and from boiling milk for a long time at home. Fermentation is wrong because fermentation is the change of sugar into alcohol by yeast. Vaccination is wrong because vaccination uses dead or weakened microbes to build protection. Nitrogen fixation is wrong because nitrogen fixation is the work of bacteria such as Rhizobium.\nयाद रखो: सत्तर डिग्री पर थोड़ी देर, फिर झटके से ठंडक: यही पाश्चरीकरण है। किण्वन नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Fermentation यीस्ट का शराब वाला काम है, दूध की यह गर्मी-ठंडक नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-16","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"When is a sprinkler system especially useful?","options":["When the farmer wants wind to separate chaff","When seeds are being tested in a beaker","When the land is uneven and water should be sprayed like rain","When dry grain is stored with neem leaves"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is When the land is uneven and water should be sprayed like rain. In a sprinkler system, water moves under pressure through pipes and sprays from rotating nozzles. It suits uneven land and sandy soil because the water is spread without flooding. When the farmer wants wind to separate chaff is wrong because that job is winnowing. When seeds are being tested in a beaker is wrong because the beaker test is for choosing healthy seeds. When dry grain is stored with neem leaves is wrong because neem leaves protect stored grain from pests.\nयाद रखो: ऊँचे-नीचे खेत पर स्प्रिंकलर पानी को बारिश की तरह छिड़कता है, बाढ़ नहीं लाता।\nगलत मत याद करना: When the farmer wants wind to separate chaff फटकने की ज़रूरत है, फव्वारे की नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-17","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Which leaf pores let gases in and out, and are opened and closed by guard cells?","options":["Stomata","Anthers","Platelets","Seed drills"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Stomata. Stomata are tiny pores on a leaf. A pair of guard cells opens or closes each stoma, so carbon dioxide can enter for photosynthesis and oxygen and water vapour can leave. Anthers is wrong because anthers are the parts of a stamen that produce pollen. Platelets is wrong because platelets help blood to clot in animals. Seed drills is wrong because a seed drill is a sowing tool, not a pore on a leaf.\nयाद रखो: स्टोमेटा पत्ती के छोटे दरवाज़े हैं। रक्षक कोशिकाएँ उन्हें खोलती-बंद करती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Anthers पराग बनाने वाले पुंकेसर के हिस्से हैं, पत्ती के छिद्र नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-18","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Why are weeds harmful?","options":["They produce penicillin for the next crop","They are the same thing as manure","They change a rabi crop into a kharif crop","They compete with the crop for water, nutrients, space, and light"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is They compete with the crop for water, nutrients, space, and light. Weeds are undesirable plants growing along with the crop. If they are left in the field, the crop gets a smaller share of water, minerals, space, and light, so the yield falls. They produce penicillin for the next crop is wrong because penicillin comes from the fungus Penicillium, not from weeds. They are the same thing as manure is wrong because manure is decomposed waste added on purpose, while weeds are unwanted plants. They change a rabi crop into a kharif crop is wrong because weeds do not change the season in which a crop was sown.\nयाद रखो: खरपतवार फसल से पानी, खाद, जगह और रोशनी छीनते हैं, इसलिए पैदावार गिरती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: They are the same thing as manure खरपतवार खाद नहीं, मुफ्त के प्रतिद्वंद्वी हैं।"},{"id":"s-crop-19","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"What is weeding?","options":["Heating milk and then cooling it","Removing unwanted plants from the crop field","Letting a bud detach from Hydra","Timing one swing of a pendulum"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Removing unwanted plants from the crop field. Weeding can be done by hand, with a khurpi, or by spraying weedicides. A weedicide such as 2,4-D must be used with care, and the person spraying should cover the nose and mouth. Heating milk and then cooling it is wrong because that treatment is pasteurisation. Letting a bud detach from Hydra is wrong because that is asexual reproduction in Hydra. Timing one swing of a pendulum is wrong because that measurement belongs to motion and time.\nयाद रखो: निराई मतलब खेत से अनचाही घास निकालना। दूध गर्म करना पाश्चरीकरण है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Heating milk and then cooling it दूध का काम है, खेत की निराई नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-20","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"What is harvesting?","options":["Sowing seeds with a seed drill","Adding vermicompost before sowing","Cutting and gathering the crop when it is mature","Levelling the soil"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Cutting and gathering the crop when it is mature. Harvesting is done when the crop is ripe. Farmers may cut it with a sickle or use a harvester machine. A combine both harvests and threshes. Sowing seeds with a seed drill is wrong because sowing is the start of the crop, not the harvest. Adding vermicompost before sowing is wrong because that step is manuring. Levelling the soil is wrong because levelling is part of preparing the field.\nयाद रखो: कटाई (harvesting) पकी फसल को काटकर इकट्ठा करना है। बुआई तो शुरुआत है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Sowing seeds with a seed drill फसल की शुरूआत है, कटाई नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-21","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Threshing is done in order to...","options":["Increase area so that pressure falls","Turn wheat into a kharif crop","Pollinate the flowers","Separate the grain from the stalks and chaff"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Separate the grain from the stalks and chaff. After the crop is cut, grain is still attached to stalks and covered by chaff. Threshing breaks the grain free. A thresher or a combine can do this work. Increase area so that pressure falls is wrong because pressure and area belong to the study of force, not to threshing. Turn wheat into a kharif crop is wrong because threshing does not change the season of a crop. Pollinate the flowers is wrong because pollination happens while the plants are flowering, before harvest.\nयाद रखो: थ्रेशिंग डंठल और भूसे से दाना अलग करती है। हवा से फटकना उसके बाद आता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Turn wheat into a kharif crop थ्रेशिंग मौसम नहीं बदलती।"},{"id":"s-crop-22","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"How does winnowing separate grain from chaff?","options":["Wind blows the lighter chaff aside while heavier grain falls down","A magnet pulls the grain out of the chaff","The mixture is heated like milk to about 70 degrees Celsius","Chaff always sinks and grain always floats in water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Wind blows the lighter chaff aside while heavier grain falls down. Farmers drop the mixture from a height in a breeze, and a winnowing machine uses the same idea. Chaff is light so the air carries it aside, while heavier grain falls in a heap. A magnet pulls the grain out of the chaff is wrong because grain and chaff are not separated with a magnet in this method. The mixture is heated like milk to about 70 degrees Celsius is wrong because that temperature treatment is pasteurisation. Chaff always sinks and grain always floats in water is wrong because the water test is used to select seeds, while winnowing uses moving air.\nयाद रखो: फटकने में हवा हल्का भूसा उड़ा ले जाती है, भारी दाना नीचे गिरता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A magnet pulls the grain out of the chaff चुंबक अनाज नहीं छाँटता।"},{"id":"s-crop-23","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Bread mould living on stale bread gets its food as a","options":["parasite on a living host","saprotroph","green autotroph","pitcher plant"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is saprotroph. Bread mould is a fungus. It releases digestive juices onto dead bread, then absorbs the broken-down food. That way of feeding on dead matter is saprotrophic nutrition. Parasite on a living host is wrong because the bread is not a living host; Cuscuta is a parasite. Green autotroph is wrong because mould has no chlorophyll and cannot make food by photosynthesis. Pitcher plant is wrong because a pitcher plant is a green insectivorous plant, not a mould on bread.\nयाद रखो: ब्रेड की फफूँद मरे हुए आटे पर रस छोड़कर खाती है, इसलिए सैप्रोट्रॉफ।\nगलत मत याद करना: parasite on a living host अमरबेल जैसा है। बासी ब्रेड जिंदा मेज़बान नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-24","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Why must harvested grain be dried before storage?","options":["Wet grain turns into the fertiliser urea","Drying changes rabi grain into kharif grain","Moisture lets fungi, bacteria, and insects spoil the grain","Moisture is needed so that weeds can grow inside the sack"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Moisture lets fungi, bacteria, and insects spoil the grain. Freshly harvested grain holds water, and microbes or pests attack it if it is stored wet. Drying in the sun, then using silos, granaries, or dried neem leaves, protects the store. Wet grain turns into the fertiliser urea is wrong because urea is made in a factory, and wet grain does not become urea. Drying changes rabi grain into kharif grain is wrong because drying does not change the season of the crop. Moisture is needed so that weeds can grow inside the sack is wrong because weeds grow in fields, and moisture in storage causes spoilage.\nयाद रखो: गीला अनाज फफूँद, बैक्टीरिया और कीड़ों को दावत देता है। धूप में सुखाकर रखो।\nगलत मत याद करना: Wet grain turns into the fertiliser urea नमी यूरिया नहीं बनती।"},{"id":"s-crop-25","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Why are legume crops useful in crop rotation?","options":["Rhizobium in their root nodules adds nitrogen compounds to the soil","Their roots manufacture penicillin for the next crop","They turn the rainy season into winter","They remove the need for any water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Rhizobium in their root nodules adds nitrogen compounds to the soil. Crop rotation means growing different crops one after another in the same field. A legume such as gram or pea hosts Rhizobium, which fixes nitrogen. The next crop then finds the soil richer. Their roots manufacture penicillin for the next crop is wrong because penicillin comes from the fungus Penicillium, not from pea roots. They turn the rainy season into winter is wrong because rotation does not change the climate. They remove the need for any water is wrong because legumes still need water at the right times.\nयाद रखो: फसल चक्र में फली की जड़ का राइजोबियम मिट्टी में नाइट्रोजन जमा देता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Their roots manufacture penicillin for the next crop जड़ें पेनिसिलिन की फैक्टरी नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-26","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Green crop plants make food in sunlight. Which statement matches that idea?","options":["They must eat insects in order to survive","They are autotrophs and prepare food by photosynthesis","They take all their food from a host, like Cuscuta","They feed only on dead wood, like bread mould"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is They are autotrophs and prepare food by photosynthesis. Green plants contain chlorophyll. They use carbon dioxide, water, and sunlight to make carbohydrates. This nutrition idea explains why a healthy green crop can feed animals and people. They must eat insects in order to survive is wrong because a pitcher plant traps insects, but cereal crops are green autotrophs. They take all their food from a host, like Cuscuta is wrong because Cuscuta is a parasite without chlorophyll, unlike a green crop. They feed only on dead wood, like bread mould is wrong because bread mould is a saprotroph, while green crops make food.\nयाद रखो: हरी फसल ऑटोट्रॉफ है: क्लोरोफिल, धूप, हवा और पानी से अपना खाना खुद बनाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: They take all their food from a host, like Cuscuta अमरबेल का चोर तरीका है।"},{"id":"s-crop-27","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"The pitcher of a pitcher plant is a","options":["root nodule full of Rhizobium","seed dispersed by the wind","modified leaf that traps insects","chemical fertiliser"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is modified leaf that traps insects. The pitcher is a modified leaf. Insects fall in and are digested. The plant can still photosynthesise, but the insects supply nitrogen where the soil is poor. Root nodule full of Rhizobium is wrong because root nodules of legumes house the bacterium Rhizobium, whereas the pitcher traps insects. Seed dispersed by the wind is wrong because a seed forms after fertilisation and is not the insect trap. Chemical fertiliser is wrong because a fertiliser is a manufactured nutrient, not a leaf.\nयाद रखो: घट पौधे की बदली हुई पत्ती है, जो कीड़े फँसाती है। जड़ की गाँठ नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: root nodule full of Rhizobium मटर की जड़ है, घट नहीं।"},{"id":"s-crop-28","topicId":"s-crop","subject":"science","stem":"Paddy, also called rice, stands in water for much of its growth. In which season is it normally sown?","options":["In winter, as a rabi crop","Only during threshing","Only inside a sealed silo","In the rainy season, as a kharif crop"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is In the rainy season, as a kharif crop. Rice is a kharif crop sown in the rainy season. It is often grown where water can stand in the field. Wheat, sown in winter, is a rabi crop. In winter, as a rabi crop is wrong because wheat is the familiar winter grain, while paddy is sown with the rains. Only during threshing is wrong because threshing is done after the plants are mature. Only inside a sealed silo is wrong because a silo stores dry grain and is not a field for growing paddy.\nयाद रखो: धान यानी चावल खरीफ है, बरसात में बोया जाता है और अक्सर पानी में खड़ा रहता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: In winter, as a rabi crop गेहूँ की पहचान है, धान की नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-16","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"Which parts of a flower take part directly in sexual reproduction?","options":["Root hair and xylem","Cell wall and chloroplast","Stamen and pistil","Sepals only"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Stamen and pistil. The stamen is the male part, and its anther makes pollen. The pistil is the female part, with stigma, style, and ovary. Ovules lie inside the ovary. Root hair and xylem is wrong because those parts transport water and are not the reproductive organs of the flower. Cell wall and chloroplast is wrong because those are structures inside a cell, not parts of a flower. Sepals only is wrong because sepals protect the bud, while stamens and the pistil produce the sex cells.\nयाद रखो: फूल में जनन के दो कलाकार: पुंकेसर (stamen) और स्त्रीकेसर (pistil)।\nगलत मत याद करना: Sepals only बाह्यदल पंखुड़ियों के पहरेदार हैं, जनन अंग नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-17","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"What is pollination?","options":["Transfer of pollen from an anther to a stigma","Fusion of a male gamete with an egg","Growth of a bud on Hydra","Falling of a ripe fruit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Transfer of pollen from an anther to a stigma. Pollen grains land on the stigma of the same flower or of another flower of the same kind. Insects, wind, or water may carry them. Fertilisation can then take place in the ovule. Fusion of a male gamete with an egg is wrong because that fusion is fertilisation, which comes after pollination. Growth of a bud on Hydra is wrong because budding is asexual reproduction in Hydra. Falling of a ripe fruit is wrong because a fruit develops after fertilisation, and its fall is not pollination.\nयाद रखो: परागण: परागकोश से पराग वर्तिकाग्र पर पहुँचना। मिलना तो बाद में निषेचन है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Fusion of a male gamete with an egg निषेचन है, पराग की यात्रा नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-18","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"After fertilisation in a flowering plant, which change is correct?","options":["The anther becomes a root nodule","The petal becomes the embryo","The stigma becomes a tadpole","The ovary becomes a fruit and the ovule becomes a seed"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is The ovary becomes a fruit and the ovule becomes a seed. The zygote grows into an embryo inside the ovule. The ovule then becomes the seed, and the ovary ripens into the fruit. Petals and stamens usually dry and fall. The anther becomes a root nodule is wrong because root nodules form on legume roots with Rhizobium, not from anthers. The petal becomes the embryo is wrong because the embryo develops from the zygote inside the ovule. The stigma becomes a tadpole is wrong because a tadpole is a young frog, not a flower part.\nयाद रखो: निषेचन के बाद अंडाशय फल बनता है और बीजांड बीज। पंखुड़ियाँ अक्सर झड़ जाती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: The stigma becomes a tadpole वर्तिकाग्र मेंढक का बच्चा नहीं बनता।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-19","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"Which flower is bisexual?","options":["A papaya flower, because it always has both parts","Hibiscus, because it has both stamens and a pistil","A fern leaf, because ferns bear flowers","A male frog, because it produces pollen"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Hibiscus, because it has both stamens and a pistil. A bisexual flower contains both stamens and a pistil. Hibiscus, mustard, and rose are examples. Papaya, watermelon, and cucumber have unisexual flowers. A papaya flower, because it always has both parts is wrong because papaya flowers are unisexual, with either stamens or a pistil. A fern leaf, because ferns bear flowers is wrong because ferns do not bear flowers and they reproduce by spores. A male frog, because it produces pollen is wrong because a male frog produces sperms, not pollen.\nयाद रखो: गुड़हल में पुंकेसर और स्त्रीकेसर दोनों हैं, इसलिए द्विलिंगी। पपीता अक्सर एकलिंगी है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A papaya flower, because it always has both parts पपीते पर दोनों अंग मान लेना गलती है।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-20","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"New potato plants can grow from the eyes on a potato. This is...","options":["External fertilisation","Metamorphosis","Vegetative propagation","Binary fission"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Vegetative propagation. The potato tuber is a stem, and each eye is a bud. A new plant grows from that bud without seeds. Reproduction from roots, stems, leaves, or buds is vegetative propagation. External fertilisation is wrong because eyes growing into plants do not involve sperms and eggs released in water. Metamorphosis is wrong because a potato eye does not pass through a larva and an adult animal. Binary fission is wrong because binary fission is the division of a one-celled animal such as Amoeba.\nयाद रखो: आलू की आँख एक कली है। बीज के बिना नया पौधा: यही कायिक प्रवर्धन है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Binary fission अमीबा का दो टुकड़ों वाला तरीका है, आलू की आँख नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-21","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"Bryophyllum grows new plants from...","options":["Pollen tubes only","The eardrum of a visiting insect","Root nodules of Rhizobium","Buds along the margins of its leaves"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Buds along the margins of its leaves. Tiny buds on the leaf edge of Bryophyllum can grow into new plants on moist soil, which is vegetative propagation by leaves. Rose and sugarcane, by contrast, are often grown from stem cuttings. Pollen tubes only is wrong because a pollen tube is part of sexual reproduction in a flower. The eardrum of a visiting insect is wrong because an eardrum is not a plant reproductive organ. Root nodules of Rhizobium is wrong because nodules fix nitrogen and are not the leaf buds of Bryophyllum.\nयाद रखो: ब्रायोफिलम की पत्ती के किनारे की कलियाँ गीली मिट्टी पर नया पौधा बनाती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Root nodules of Rhizobium नाइट्रोजन की गाँठ हैं, पत्ती की कली नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-22","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"Which tissue carries water and minerals from the roots to the leaves?","options":["Xylem","Phloem","Blood platelets","Stamen"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Xylem. Root hairs absorb water and dissolved minerals. Xylem forms continuous tubes and carries this sap upward. Food made by the leaves travels in a different tissue, the phloem. Phloem is wrong because phloem carries food made in the leaves, not the main stream of water from the soil. Blood platelets is wrong because platelets help blood to clot in animals and are not a plant tissue. Stamen is wrong because the stamen produces pollen.\nयाद रखो: जाइलम जड़ से पानी और खनिज ऊपर ले जाता है। फ्लोएम खाने की पाइप है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Phloem पत्ती का बना खाना ले जाता है, मिट्टी का पानी नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-23","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"In plants, translocation means the movement of...","options":["Pollen from an anther","Food through the phloem","Blood through arteries","Sound through a vacuum"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Food through the phloem. Leaves make food by photosynthesis. Phloem carries that food to stems, roots, fruits, and growing parts. This transport of food is called translocation, and it can move both upward and downward. Pollen from an anther is wrong because movement of pollen to a stigma is pollination, not translocation. Blood through arteries is wrong because arteries are blood vessels of animals. Sound through a vacuum is wrong because sound cannot travel through a vacuum, and this is not a plant process.\nयाद रखो: स्थानांतरण मतलब फ्लोएम में खाने का चलना, ऊपर या नीचे। पराग की उड़ान नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Pollen from an anther परागण है, भोजन की यात्रा नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-24","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"What is the job of haemoglobin in red blood cells?","options":["It clots blood at a cut","It carries water up a tree","It carries oxygen","It produces pollen"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is It carries oxygen. Haemoglobin is the red pigment inside red blood cells. It binds oxygen in the lungs and gives that oxygen up to body cells. The liquid part of blood, called plasma, carries many dissolved substances. It clots blood at a cut is wrong because clotting is helped by platelets. It carries water up a tree is wrong because water transport in a tree is the job of xylem. It produces pollen is wrong because pollen is produced in the anthers of flowers.\nयाद रखो: हीमोग्लोबिन लाल रक्त कोशिका का लाल रंग है और ऑक्सीजन ढोता है। थक्का प्लेटलेट्स का काम है।\nगलत मत याद करना: It clots blood at a cut थक्का प्लेटलेट्स जमाते हैं, हीमोग्लोबिन नहीं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-25","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement about blood vessels is correct?","options":["Arteries carry blood away from the heart, and veins bring blood back toward the heart","Veins carry blood away from the heart and have no valves","Arteries are the tubes that carry water in a stem","Capillaries are the male parts of a flower"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Arteries carry blood away from the heart, and veins bring blood back toward the heart. Arteries have thick elastic walls because blood leaves the heart under pressure. Veins have valves so that blood does not flow backward. Very thin capillaries connect arteries and veins and allow exchange with the cells. Veins carry blood away from the heart and have no valves is wrong because veins return blood to the heart, and they do have valves. Arteries are the tubes that carry water in a stem is wrong because the water tubes in a stem are xylem. Capillaries are the male parts of a flower is wrong because the male parts of a flower are the stamens.\nयाद रखो: धमनी दिल से खून ले जाती है। शिरा खून दिल की तरफ वापस लाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Veins carry blood away from the heart and have no valves दिशा और वाल्व दोनों उल्टे हैं।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-26","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"How many chambers does the human heart have?","options":["Two","Four","One","Sixteen"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Four. The two upper chambers are the atria and the two lower chambers are the ventricles. A partition keeps oxygen-rich blood from mixing with carbon dioxide-rich blood. Rhythmic contraction of the heart muscles is the heartbeat. Two is wrong because the human heart is not a two-chamber pump; it has two atria and two ventricles. One is wrong because one chamber could not keep the two blood streams apart in the way the human heart does. Sixteen is wrong because sixteen is far more than the four chambers of the human heart.\nयाद रखो: दिल के चार कमरे: ऊपर दो आलिंद, नीचे दो निलय। सोलह कमरों वाला महल नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Two कमरे इंसान के दिल में नहीं होते।"}]},{"id":"sectional-paper1","title":"Paper 1 sectional","kind":"sectional","minutes":75,"strict":true,"concept":"English 50, Hindi 20, Social Science 30. 75 minutes. You need 50% on this paper by itself.","questions":[{"id":"e-tenses-13","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The sentence gives one total for the whole class, not a loose group of several pupils. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The number of students in the class are small","The number of students in the class am small","The number of students in the class were small","The number of students in the class is small"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The number of students in the class is small\" because the number of takes a singular verb because it treats the count as one amount. \"The number of students in the class are small\" fails because the number of points to one total and takes the singular verb is. \"The number of students in the class am small\" fails because am agrees only with I, while this subject needs the singular is. \"The number of students in the class were small\" fails because the remark is about the present total, so the past plural were is the wrong tense and the wrong number."},{"id":"e-tenses-14","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"Someone is describing an ordinary breakfast dish eaten as one item. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Bread and butter is a common breakfast","Bread and butter are a common breakfast","Bread and butter were a common breakfast","Bread and butter be a common breakfast"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Bread and butter is a common breakfast\" because when two food words together name one dish, they take a singular verb. \"Bread and butter are a common breakfast\" fails because bread and butter names one dish, so the verb stays singular: is, not are. \"Bread and butter were a common breakfast\" fails because the sentence states a present fact, so the past verb were does not fit. \"Bread and butter be a common breakfast\" fails because be is not a complete present verb for this subject."},{"id":"e-tenses-15","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The whole class is prepared at this moment. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Everyone in the class are ready","Everyone in the class is ready","Everyone in the class were ready","Everyone in the class ready"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Everyone in the class is ready\" because pronouns such as everyone are singular and take a singular verb. \"Everyone in the class are ready\" fails because everyone is a singular pronoun and takes is, not are. \"Everyone in the class were ready\" fails because the readiness is present, and everyone would still need a singular verb. \"Everyone in the class ready\" fails because the adjective ready cannot stand without the verb is."},{"id":"e-tenses-16","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"Only one girl in the group sings well. Which sentence is correct?","options":["One of the girls sing well","One of the girl sings well","One of the girls sings well","One of the girls singing well"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"One of the girls sings well\" because one of plus a plural noun still takes a singular verb because the subject is one. \"One of the girls sing well\" fails because the true subject is one, which is singular, so the verb is sings, not sing. \"One of the girl sings well\" fails because the noun after one of must be plural: girls, not girl. \"One of the girls singing well\" fails because singing has no finite verb, so the sentence is incomplete."},{"id":"e-tenses-17","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The teacher is the grammatical subject, and the pupils are only joined on with along with. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The teacher, along with the pupils, is in the hall","The teacher, along with the pupils, are in the hall","The teacher, along with the pupils, were in the hall","The teacher, along with the pupils, be in the hall"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The teacher, along with the pupils, is in the hall\" because words such as along with do not change the number of the main subject. \"The teacher, along with the pupils, are in the hall\" fails because along with does not make the subject plural, so the verb agrees with the singular teacher. \"The teacher, along with the pupils, were in the hall\" fails because the meaning is present, and the verb must also stay singular to match teacher. \"The teacher, along with the pupils, be in the hall\" fails because be does not complete the present tense of this sentence."},{"id":"e-tenses-18","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"Ravi may come, or else his friends may come. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Either Ravi or his friends is coming","Either Ravi or his friends are coming","Either Ravi or his friends was coming","Either Ravi or his friends coming"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Either Ravi or his friends are coming\" because with either...or or neither...nor, the verb agrees with the subject closer to it. \"Either Ravi or his friends is coming\" fails because when subjects are joined by or, the verb agrees with the nearer subject, and friends is plural. \"Either Ravi or his friends was coming\" fails because the plan is a present arrangement, so the past verb was is the wrong tense. \"Either Ravi or his friends coming\" fails because coming needs the helper are; without it the sentence has no finite verb."},{"id":"e-tenses-19","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"Yesterday the girl was not late, and the boys were not late either. The girl is placed next to the verb. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Neither the boys nor the girl were late","Neither the boys nor the girl are late","Neither the boys nor the girl was late","Neither the boys or the girl was late"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Neither the boys nor the girl was late\" because after neither...nor, choose was or were according to the subject nearest the verb. \"Neither the boys nor the girl were late\" fails because the verb agrees with the nearer subject girl, which is singular, so it is was, not were. \"Neither the boys nor the girl are late\" fails because the lateness belongs to yesterday, and the nearer subject still needs a singular verb. \"Neither the boys or the girl was late\" fails because neither must be paired with nor; or belongs with either."},{"id":"e-tenses-20","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The chairs, tables, and beds are thought of as one uncountable collection. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The furniture in this room are new","The furnitures in this room are new","The furniture in this room were new","The furniture in this room is new"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The furniture in this room is new\" because uncountable nouns such as furniture take a singular verb and do not add -s. \"The furniture in this room are new\" fails because furniture is an uncountable noun and takes the singular verb is. \"The furnitures in this room are new\" fails because furniture has no plural furnitures in standard English. \"The furniture in this room were new\" fails because the newness is a present state, and furniture would still take a singular verb."},{"id":"e-tenses-21","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The test lasts a total of two hours, treated as one amount of time. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Two hours are enough for this test","Two hours is enough for this test","Two hours be enough for this test","Two hour is enough for this test"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Two hours is enough for this test\" because a measurement of time, distance, or money, taken as one unit, takes a singular verb. \"Two hours are enough for this test\" fails because a period of time taken as one whole amount uses a singular verb. \"Two hours be enough for this test\" fails because be is not a finished present verb for this subject. \"Two hour is enough for this test\" fails because the number two still needs the plural noun hours, even though the verb is singular."},{"id":"e-tenses-22","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The sentence praises soldiers one by one in a formal pattern. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Many a soldier have fought bravely","Many a soldiers has fought bravely","Many a soldier has fought bravely","Many a soldier have fight bravely"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Many a soldier has fought bravely\" because many a plus a singular noun takes a singular verb such as has. \"Many a soldier have fought bravely\" fails because many a is followed by a singular noun and a singular verb, so the helper is has. \"Many a soldiers has fought bravely\" fails because many a takes a singular noun, so the noun is soldier, not soldiers. \"Many a soldier have fight bravely\" fails because both the plural have and the base form fight break the many-a pattern."},{"id":"e-tenses-23","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"A Class 8 timetable includes this science subject now. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Physics are taught in Class 8","Physics were taught in Class 8","Physics teaching in Class 8","Physics is taught in Class 8"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Physics is taught in Class 8\" because subject names such as physics take a singular verb. \"Physics are taught in Class 8\" fails because physics, as the name of one subject, takes the singular verb is. \"Physics were taught in Class 8\" fails because the timetable fact is present, and physics does not take a plural verb. \"Physics teaching in Class 8\" fails because teaching cannot replace the finite verb is taught."},{"id":"e-tenses-24","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The sentence is about poor people as a group. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The poor are often generous","The poor is often generous","The poor was often generous","The poors are often generous"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The poor are often generous\" because the plus an adjective can mean a whole group of people and then takes a plural verb. \"The poor is often generous\" fails because the poor means poor people and therefore takes the plural verb are. \"The poor was often generous\" fails because the statement is a present general truth and needs a plural verb. \"The poors are often generous\" fails because English uses the poor for the group, not a plural poors."},{"id":"e-tenses-25","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"One cutting tool is lying on the desk right now. Which sentence is correct?","options":["A pair of scissors are on the desk","A pair of scissor is on the desk","A pair of scissors is on the desk","A pair of scissors were on the desk"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"A pair of scissors is on the desk\" because a pair of, even before a plural-only noun such as scissors, takes a singular verb. \"A pair of scissors are on the desk\" fails because the subject is a pair, which is singular, so the verb is is. \"A pair of scissor is on the desk\" fails because the noun scissors keeps its plural shape even after a pair of. \"A pair of scissors were on the desk\" fails because the sentence describes the present, so were is the wrong tense."},{"id":"e-tenses-26","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"Look up at a clear night sky full of points of light. Which sentence is correct?","options":["There is many stars in the sky","There are much stars in the sky","There be many stars in the sky","There are many stars in the sky"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"There are many stars in the sky\" because after there, the verb agrees with the real subject that follows it. \"There is many stars in the sky\" fails because stars is plural, so the there-construction uses are, not is. \"There are much stars in the sky\" fails because stars can be counted, so the determiner is many, not much. \"There be many stars in the sky\" fails because be is not a present finite verb in this sentence."},{"id":"e-tenses-27","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker is including himself together with his friends as the people who will run. Which sentence is correct?","options":["My friends and I are ready for the race","My friends and I is ready for the race","Me and my friends is ready for the race","My friends and myself is ready for the race"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"My friends and I are ready for the race\" because a compound subject joined by and takes a plural verb, and the subject pronoun is I. \"My friends and I is ready for the race\" fails because two subjects joined by and make a plural subject, so the verb is are. \"Me and my friends is ready for the race\" fails because the subject pronoun must be I, not me, and the verb must be plural. \"My friends and myself is ready for the race\" fails because myself is not the ordinary subject form, and the verb still has to be plural."},{"id":"e-tenses-28","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct form of the proverb about keeping a steady pace.","options":["Slow and steady win the race","Slow and steady wins the race","Slow and steady winning the race","Slow and steady won the race"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Slow and steady wins the race\" because two qualities joined as one proverbial idea can take a singular verb. \"Slow and steady win the race\" fails because the proverb treats slow and steady as one idea, so the verb is the singular wins. \"Slow and steady winning the race\" fails because winning has no finite verb, so it is not a complete proverb. \"Slow and steady won the race\" fails because the proverb states a general present truth, not a single past victory."},{"id":"e-tenses-29","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The captain is the subject, and the players are only added with as well as. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The captain, as well as the players, are ready","The captain, as well as the players, were ready","The captain, as well as the players, am ready","The captain, as well as the players, is ready"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The captain, as well as the players, is ready\" because as well as, like along with, leaves the verb agreeing with the main subject only. \"The captain, as well as the players, are ready\" fails because as well as does not add to the number of the subject, so the verb agrees with captain. \"The captain, as well as the players, were ready\" fails because readiness here is present, and the verb must stay singular. \"The captain, as well as the players, am ready\" fails because am agrees only with I and cannot follow the captain."},{"id":"e-tenses-30","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"She began waiting at four o'clock, and she is still waiting. Which sentence is correct?","options":["She has been waiting for an hour","She is waiting for an hour","She has been wait for an hour","She waited for an hour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She has been waiting for an hour\" because an action that started earlier and is still continuing uses has or have been plus the -ing form. \"She is waiting for an hour\" fails because a length of time continuing up to now needs the present perfect continuous, not the present continuous alone. \"She has been wait for an hour\" fails because after has been, the verb must be the -ing form waiting. \"She waited for an hour\" fails because the simple past would mean the waiting is finished, but she is still waiting."},{"id":"e-tenses-31","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"The family came to this town in 2019 and still lives here. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We lived here since 2019","We have lived here since 2019","We have lived here for 2019","We are living here since 2019"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We have lived here since 2019\" because since plus a point of time that still holds true takes the present perfect. \"We lived here since 2019\" fails because a starting point that continues to the present takes the present perfect, not the simple past. \"We have lived here for 2019\" fails because for must be followed by a length of time, while the year 2019 is a starting point and needs since. \"We are living here since 2019\" fails because since a past starting point needs a perfect tense, not the present continuous alone."},{"id":"e-tenses-32","topicId":"e-tenses","subject":"english","stem":"Both sisters are short, and the sentence uses neither. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Neither of the two sisters are tall","Neither of the two sister is tall","Neither of the two sisters is tall","Neither of the two sisters am tall"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Neither of the two sisters is tall\" because neither of plus a plural noun still takes a singular verb. \"Neither of the two sisters are tall\" fails because neither of is singular, so the verb is is, not are. \"Neither of the two sister is tall\" fails because after of the two, the noun must be the plural sisters. \"Neither of the two sisters am tall\" fails because am agrees only with I and cannot follow neither."},{"id":"e-voice-13","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: Ravi posted the letter.","options":["The letter is posted by Ravi","The letter was post by Ravi","Ravi was posted by the letter","The letter was posted by Ravi"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The letter was posted by Ravi\" because simple past passive uses was or were plus the past participle. \"The letter is posted by Ravi\" fails because is posted is present, but posted is simple past. \"The letter was post by Ravi\" fails because was needs the past participle posted, not the base form post. \"Ravi was posted by the letter\" fails because this reverses the doer and the receiver."},{"id":"e-voice-14","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct active form of this sentence: The letter was posted by Ravi.","options":["Ravi posted the letter","Ravi posts the letter","Ravi was posted the letter","Ravi had posted the letter"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Ravi posted the letter\" because to turn a simple past passive back into the active, use the simple past and make the by-agent the subject. \"Ravi posts the letter\" fails because posts is simple present, but was posted is simple past. \"Ravi was posted the letter\" fails because was posted cannot stay in the active sentence; the active verb is simply posted. \"Ravi had posted the letter\" fails because had posted is past perfect and changes the tense of the simple past passive."},{"id":"e-voice-15","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct active form of this sentence: The mice were chased by the cat.","options":["The cat chases the mice","The cat chased the mice","The mice chased the cat","The cat was chased the mice"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The cat chased the mice\" because the noun after by becomes the active subject, and the tense stays simple past. \"The cat chases the mice\" fails because chases is present, but were chased is simple past. \"The mice chased the cat\" fails because this reverses the action, so the mice become the chasers. \"The cat was chased the mice\" fails because was chased is still passive in shape and cannot take the mice as an object in this way."},{"id":"e-voice-16","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: We must follow the rules.","options":["The rules must followed by us","The rules must be follow by us","The rules must be followed by us","The rules are followed by us"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The rules must be followed by us\" because after a modal, the passive pattern is modal plus be plus the past participle. \"The rules must followed by us\" fails because a modal passive needs be between must and the past participle followed. \"The rules must be follow by us\" fails because follow must be the past participle followed. \"The rules are followed by us\" fails because are followed drops the modal must and changes a duty into a plain present fact."},{"id":"e-voice-17","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: She gave me a book.","options":["I was given a book by her","I was gave a book by her","A book is given to me by her","I am given a book by her"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I was given a book by her\" because when a verb has two objects, either object can become the passive subject, and the tense stays the same. \"I was gave a book by her\" fails because the passive needs the past participle given, not the past form gave. \"A book is given to me by her\" fails because is given is present, but gave is simple past. \"I am given a book by her\" fails because am given is present and does not keep the simple past tense."},{"id":"e-voice-18","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: The wind blew the roof off.","options":["The roof was blew off by the wind","The roof was blown off by the wind","The roof is blown off by the wind","The wind was blown off by the roof"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The roof was blown off by the wind\" because simple past passive uses was or were plus the past participle of the active verb. \"The roof was blew off by the wind\" fails because the past participle of blow is blown, not blew. \"The roof is blown off by the wind\" fails because is blown is present, but blew is simple past. \"The wind was blown off by the roof\" fails because this reverses the doer and the receiver."},{"id":"e-voice-19","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this question: Are they making a kite?","options":["Is a kite made by them?","Was a kite being made by them?","Is a kite being made by them?","Are a kite being made by them?"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Is a kite being made by them?\" because a present continuous question becomes is, am, or are plus being plus the past participle. \"Is a kite made by them?\" fails because is made drops being, so it loses the continuous tense of are making. \"Was a kite being made by them?\" fails because was being made is past, but are making is present. \"Are a kite being made by them?\" fails because the new subject a kite is singular, so the helper is is, not are."},{"id":"e-voice-20","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence can be changed into the passive voice?","options":["The baby sleeps at noon","The flowers look fresh","They arrived late","The chef cooked the rice"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The chef cooked the rice\" because only a verb that takes an object can be turned into the passive voice. \"The baby sleeps at noon\" fails because sleeps has no object, and a verb without an object cannot form a passive. \"The flowers look fresh\" fails because look is a linking verb here, not an action verb with an object. \"They arrived late\" fails because arrived has no object, so there is nothing to become the subject of a passive verb."},{"id":"e-voice-21","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: Let him finish the sum.","options":["Let the sum finished by him","Let the sum be finished by him","Let him be finished the sum","The sum is finished by him"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Let the sum be finished by him\" because a Let-order becomes Let plus the object plus be plus the past participle. \"Let the sum finished by him\" fails because be is required before the past participle finished. \"Let him be finished the sum\" fails because this keeps him as the subject of a passive verb and does not make the sum the receiver in a clear way. \"The sum is finished by him\" fails because is finished changes an order with Let into an ordinary present statement."},{"id":"e-voice-22","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: He can lift this box.","options":["This box can lifted by him","This box can be lift by him","This box can be lifted by him","This box is lifted by him"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"This box can be lifted by him\" because modal passive keeps the same modal and adds be plus the past participle. \"This box can lifted by him\" fails because can in the passive must be followed by be and then the past participle. \"This box can be lift by him\" fails because the past participle is lifted, not the base form lift. \"This box is lifted by him\" fails because is lifted removes the modal can and changes ability into a plain fact."},{"id":"e-voice-23","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: The police caught the thief.","options":["The thief is caught by the police","The thief was catch by the police","The police were caught by the thief","The thief was caught by the police"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The thief was caught by the police\" because the object of a simple past verb becomes the subject of was or were plus the past participle. \"The thief is caught by the police\" fails because is caught is present, but caught is simple past. \"The thief was catch by the police\" fails because the past participle is caught, not catch. \"The police were caught by the thief\" fails because this reverses who caught whom."},{"id":"e-voice-24","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct active form of this sentence: The song is being sung by the children.","options":["The children are singing the song","The children sang the song","The children are sung the song","The children sing the song"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The children are singing the song\" because is, am, or are being plus a past participle returns to the present continuous active. \"The children sang the song\" fails because sang is simple past, but is being sung is present continuous. \"The children are sung the song\" fails because are sung is passive and cannot be the active form. \"The children sing the song\" fails because sing is simple present and drops the continuous meaning."},{"id":"e-voice-25","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: They elected her captain.","options":["She is elected captain by them","She was elect captain by them","She was elected captain by them","They were elected captain by her"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She was elected captain by them\" because simple past passive uses was or were plus the past participle and can keep a complement such as captain. \"She is elected captain by them\" fails because is elected is present, but elected is simple past. \"She was elect captain by them\" fails because the past participle is elected, not elect. \"They were elected captain by her\" fails because this reverses the voters and the person who was chosen."},{"id":"e-voice-26","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this order: Close the gate.","options":["Let the gate closed","The gate is closed","Let the gate be close","Let the gate be closed"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Let the gate be closed\" because orders in the passive use Let plus the object plus be plus the past participle. \"Let the gate closed\" fails because be must come before the past participle closed. \"The gate is closed\" fails because is closed states a fact and is not the passive form of an order. \"Let the gate be close\" fails because close is not the past participle; the participle is closed."},{"id":"e-voice-27","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this question: Who teaches you English?","options":["By whom are you taught English?","By whom were you taught English?","Who are you taught English?","By whom do you taught English?"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"By whom are you taught English?\" because a simple present question in the passive uses by whom plus am, is, or are plus the past participle. \"By whom were you taught English?\" fails because were taught is past, but teaches is simple present. \"Who are you taught English?\" fails because the agent needs by whom; who are you taught leaves out by and uses the wrong pronoun form. \"By whom do you taught English?\" fails because do you taught is an active question pattern with a wrong verb, not a passive."},{"id":"e-voice-28","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: The mason is building a wall.","options":["A wall is built by the mason","A wall is being built by the mason","A wall was being built by the mason","A wall is being build by the mason"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"A wall is being built by the mason\" because present continuous passive uses is, am, or are being plus the past participle. \"A wall is built by the mason\" fails because is built drops the continuous being that matches is building. \"A wall was being built by the mason\" fails because was being built is past continuous, but is building is present continuous. \"A wall is being build by the mason\" fails because the past participle is built, not build."},{"id":"e-voice-29","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this question: Had she finished the essay?","options":["Has the essay been finished by her?","Had the essay finished by her?","Was the essay been finished by her?","Had the essay been finished by her?"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Had the essay been finished by her?\" because past perfect passive uses had been plus the past participle. \"Has the essay been finished by her?\" fails because has been finished is present perfect, but had finished is past perfect. \"Had the essay finished by her?\" fails because the passive perfect needs been before the past participle finished. \"Was the essay been finished by her?\" fails because was been is not a passive helper; past perfect passive uses had been."},{"id":"e-voice-30","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: I will write a letter.","options":["A letter will be written by me","A letter would be written by me","A letter is written by me","A letter will written by me"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"A letter will be written by me\" because future passive is will be plus the past participle. \"A letter would be written by me\" fails because would changes will into a different modal. \"A letter is written by me\" fails because is written is present and drops the future will. \"A letter will written by me\" fails because will must be followed by be in the passive."},{"id":"e-voice-31","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this sentence: The horse kicked the boy.","options":["The boy is kicked by the horse","The boy was kicked by the horse","The boy was kick by the horse","The horse was kicked by the boy"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The boy was kicked by the horse\" because the object of a simple past verb becomes the subject of was or were plus the past participle. \"The boy is kicked by the horse\" fails because is kicked is present, but kicked is simple past. \"The boy was kick by the horse\" fails because the past participle is kicked, not kick. \"The horse was kicked by the boy\" fails because this reverses the doer and the receiver."},{"id":"e-voice-32","topicId":"e-voice","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correct passive form of this order: Do not waste water.","options":["Let water not wasted","Water is not wasted","Let water not be wasted","Let water be not waste"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Let water not be wasted\" because a negative order becomes Let plus the object plus not be plus the past participle. \"Let water not wasted\" fails because be is missing before the past participle wasted. \"Water is not wasted\" fails because is not wasted is a present statement, not the passive of a negative order. \"Let water be not waste\" fails because waste is not the past participle wasted, and be not is not the order of this negative passive command."},{"id":"e-narration-13","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"She said to me, \"Please help me.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["She requested me to help me","She requested me that help her","She said me to please help me","She requested me to help her"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She requested me to help her\" because please makes the sentence a request, so requested plus to plus the verb is used, and pronouns change. \"She requested me to help me\" fails because her final me refers to herself and becomes her, not me. \"She requested me that help her\" fails because a request uses to plus the verb, not that help. \"She said me to please help me\" fails because said me is not a correct reporting pattern, and the pronouns are unchanged."},{"id":"e-narration-14","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"Father said to me, \"Do not shout.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["Father told me not to shout","Father told me to do not shout","Father told me that not shout","Father said me not to shout"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Father told me not to shout\" because a negative command becomes told someone not to plus the base verb. \"Father told me to do not shout\" fails because the negative command becomes not to plus the verb, not to do not shout. \"Father told me that not shout\" fails because that not shout is not the pattern for a negative order. \"Father said me not to shout\" fails because said me is incorrect; with a listener the verb is told me."},{"id":"e-narration-15","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said to me, \"Are you ready?\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He asked me if I am ready","He asked me if I was ready","He asked me if was I ready","He told me if I was ready"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He asked me if I was ready\" because a yes-no question becomes asked plus if or whether, with statement word order and a tense shift. \"He asked me if I am ready\" fails because are should become was after the past verb asked. \"He asked me if was I ready\" fails because the reported question uses statement order, I was, not the inverted was I. \"He told me if I was ready\" fails because a question is introduced by asked, not told."},{"id":"e-narration-16","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"She said to him, \"Where do you live?\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["She asked him where did he live","She asked him where he lives","She asked him where he lived","She asked him that where he lived"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She asked him where he lived\" because a wh-question keeps the wh-word, drops the question order, and shifts the tense. \"She asked him where did he live\" fails because the reported question does not keep the helping did or the question order. \"She asked him where he lives\" fails because do you live is present and should shift to lived. \"She asked him that where he lived\" fails because that should not be placed before the question word where."},{"id":"e-narration-17","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"The teacher said, \"The earth moves round the sun.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["The teacher said that the earth moves round the sun","The teacher said that the earth moved round the sun","The teacher said that the earth move round the sun","The teacher told that the earth moves round the sun"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The teacher said that the earth moves round the sun\" because universal truths usually stay in the simple present in indirect speech. \"The teacher said that the earth moved round the sun\" fails because a permanent scientific truth keeps the present tense even after said. \"The teacher said that the earth move round the sun\" fails because the earth needs the singular verb moves. \"The teacher told that the earth moves round the sun\" fails because told needs a listener; without one, the verb remains said."},{"id":"e-narration-18","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said, \"Let us play cricket.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He suggested that they shall play cricket","He suggested that they should play cricket","He said that let us play cricket","He ordered that we must play cricket"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He suggested that they should play cricket\" because let us in a proposal becomes suggested that plus should plus the verb. \"He suggested that they shall play cricket\" fails because shall does not replace the suggested should in this report. \"He said that let us play cricket\" fails because let us is changed into suggested that, not left as a raw let us clause. \"He ordered that we must play cricket\" fails because let us is a suggestion, not an order, and the modal pattern is should."},{"id":"e-narration-19","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"Ravi said, \"I have lost my pen.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["Ravi said that he had lost my pen","Ravi said that I have lost his pen","Ravi said that he had lost his pen","Ravi said that he has lost his pen"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Ravi said that he had lost his pen\" because I becomes he, my becomes his, and the present perfect becomes the past perfect. \"Ravi said that he had lost my pen\" fails because Ravi's my becomes his, because the pen belongs to him. \"Ravi said that I have lost his pen\" fails because the pronoun I should be he, and have lost should be had lost. \"Ravi said that he has lost his pen\" fails because has lost should shift back to had lost."},{"id":"e-narration-20","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"She said to me, \"You are late.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["She told me that you were late","She told me that I am late","She said me that I was late","She told me that I was late"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She told me that I was late\" because you becomes I when the words were spoken to the reporter, and the verb shifts back. \"She told me that you were late\" fails because you, spoken to me, becomes I, and are becomes was. \"She told me that I am late\" fails because are should change to was after told. \"She said me that I was late\" fails because said me is not correct; the reporting verb with a person is told me."},{"id":"e-narration-21","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said, \"I live here.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He said that he lived here","He said that he lived there","He said that he lives there","He said that I lived here"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He said that he lived there\" because here becomes there, and the simple present becomes the simple past. \"He said that he lived here\" fails because here usually changes to there in a later report. \"He said that he lives there\" fails because live should become lived after said. \"He said that I lived here\" fails because I should become he, and here should become there."},{"id":"e-narration-22","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"She said, \"I slept early last night.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["She said that she slept early last night","She said that she had slept early tonight","She said that she had slept early the previous night","She said that she has slept early the previous night"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She said that she had slept early the previous night\" because last night becomes the previous night, and the simple past usually becomes the past perfect. \"She said that she slept early last night\" fails because slept should become had slept, and last night should become the previous night. \"She said that she had slept early tonight\" fails because tonight is not the reported form of last night. \"She said that she has slept early the previous night\" fails because has slept is present perfect and is the wrong backshift."},{"id":"h-nouns-13","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«जो» किस प्रकार का सर्वनाम है?","options":["संबंधवाचक","प्रश्नवाचक","अनिश्चयवाचक","निश्चयवाचक"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is संबंधवाचक because जो relates one clause to a noun, as in जो लड़का आया था, so it is a relative pronoun. प्रश्नवाचक is wrong because a प्रश्नवाचक pronoun asks a direct question, and जो in this use connects clauses. अनिश्चयवाचक is wrong because an अनिश्चयवाचक pronoun such as कोई or कुछ leaves the person unknown, which is a different job. निश्चयवाचक is wrong because a निश्चयवाचक pronoun such as यह points to a definite nearby thing and does not relate two clauses."},{"id":"h-nouns-14","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«मैं अपना काम करता हूँ» में «अपना» किस प्रकार का सर्वनाम है?","options":["प्रश्नवाचक","निजवाचक","अनिश्चयवाचक","संबंधवाचक"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is निजवाचक because अपना points back to the subject's own work, so it is the reflexive pronoun. प्रश्नवाचक is wrong because a प्रश्नवाचक pronoun would ask कौन or क्या, and अपना does not ask a question. अनिश्चयवाचक is wrong because an अनिश्चयवाचक pronoun would mean an unknown person, such as कोई, and अपना is definite. संबंधवाचक is wrong because a संबंधवाचक pronoun such as जो links a relative clause, and अपना does not do that here."},{"id":"h-nouns-15","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«सुंदर फूल» में «सुंदर» किस प्रकार का विशेषण है?","options":["संख्यावाचक","परिमाणवाचक","गुणवाचक","सार्वनामिक"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is गुणवाचक because सुंदर tells the quality of the flower, so it is an adjective of quality. संख्यावाचक is wrong because a संख्यावाचक विशेषण tells how many, such as पाँच, and सुंदर is not a number. परिमाणवाचक is wrong because a परिमाणवाचक विशेषण tells how much of a mass, such as थोड़ा, and सुंदर is not a quantity. सार्वनामिक is wrong because a सार्वनामिक विशेषण points with a pronoun form, such as यह फूल, and सुंदर does not point."},{"id":"h-nouns-16","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«पाँच पुस्तकें» में «पाँच» किस प्रकार का विशेषण है?","options":["गुणवाचक","परिमाणवाचक","सार्वनामिक","संख्यावाचक"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is संख्यावाचक because पाँच tells the number of books, so it is an adjective of number. गुणवाचक is wrong because a गुणवाचक विशेषण would describe a quality, such as अच्छी पुस्तकें, and पाँच is not a quality. परिमाणवाचक is wrong because a परिमाणवाचक विशेषण is used for amount of an uncountable thing, such as थोड़ा दूध, not a count of books. सार्वनामिक is wrong because a सार्वनामिक विशेषण would be a pointing word such as ये पुस्तकें, and पाँच does not point."},{"id":"h-nouns-17","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«थोड़ा दूध» में «थोड़ा» किस प्रकार का विशेषण है?","options":["परिमाणवाचक","संख्यावाचक","गुणवाचक","सार्वनामिक"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is परिमाणवाचक because थोड़ा tells the amount of the mass noun दूध, so it is an adjective of quantity. संख्यावाचक is wrong because a संख्यावाचक विशेषण counts separate things, such as दो लड़के, and दूध here is not being counted as separate items. गुणवाचक is wrong because a गुणवाचक विशेषण would describe quality, such as गरम दूध, and थोड़ा is not a quality. सार्वनामिक is wrong because a सार्वनामिक विशेषण would point, such as यह दूध, and थोड़ा does not point to a particular noun by itself."},{"id":"h-nouns-18","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«यह पुस्तक नई है» में «यह» किस प्रकार का शब्द है?","options":["गुणवाचक विशेषण","सार्वनामिक विशेषण","संख्यावाचक विशेषण","परिमाणवाचक विशेषण"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is सार्वनामिक विशेषण because यह comes before पुस्तक and points to it, so the pronoun form is working as an adjective. गुणवाचक विशेषण is wrong because a गुणवाचक विशेषण would describe quality, and in this sentence the quality word is नई, not यह. संख्यावाचक विशेषण is wrong because a संख्यावाचक विशेषण would give a number, and यह does not say how many books. परिमाणवाचक विशेषण is wrong because a परिमाणवाचक विशेषण would give an amount such as थोड़ी, and यह does not measure the book."},{"id":"h-nouns-19","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"कर्ता कारक में «लड़का» का स्त्रीलिंग रूप कौन-सा है?","options":["लड़के","लड़कियाँ","लड़की","लड़कपन"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is लड़की because the feminine of लड़का is लड़की, a girl, in the singular subject form. लड़के is wrong because लड़के is the masculine plural subject form of लड़का, not the feminine. लड़कियाँ is wrong because लड़कियाँ is the feminine plural, while the question asks for the feminine singular form. लड़कपन is wrong because लड़कपन is not the standard noun form asked here; the matching feminine person-noun is लड़की."},{"id":"h-nouns-20","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"कर्ता कारक में «घोड़ा» का बहुवचन कौन-सा है?","options":["घोड़ों","घोड़ियाँ","घोड़ाएँ","घोड़े"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is घोड़े because in the subject position the plural of घोड़ा is घोड़े, as in घोड़े दौड़ते हैं. घोड़ों is wrong because घोड़ों is the oblique plural used before a postposition, such as घोड़ों ने, not the plain subject plural. घोड़ियाँ is wrong because घोड़ियाँ is not the plural of the masculine noun घोड़ा. घोड़ाएँ is wrong because घोड़ाएँ is not a Hindi plural form of घोड़ा."},{"id":"h-nouns-21","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"कर्ता कारक में «लड़की» का बहुवचन कौन-सा है?","options":["लड़कियाँ","लड़कियों","लड़के","लड़कीयाँ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is लड़कियाँ because the subject plural of लड़की is लड़कियाँ, as in लड़कियाँ पढ़ती हैं. लड़कियों is wrong because लड़कियों is the oblique plural used with a postposition, such as लड़कियों ने. लड़के is wrong because लड़के is the plural of लड़का, not of लड़की. लड़कीयाँ is wrong because लड़कीयाँ is a wrong formation; the accepted subject plural is लड़कियाँ."},{"id":"h-nouns-22","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«रात» किस लिंग का शब्द है?","options":["पुल्लिंग","स्त्रीलिंग","उभयलिंग","नपुंसकलिंग"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is स्त्रीलिंग because रात is feminine, which is why Hindi says अँधेरी रात बीत गई and uses a feminine verb. पुल्लिंग is wrong because पुल्लिंग would take a masculine verb such as बीता, and रात does not do that. उभयलिंग is wrong because उभयलिंग would mean the word is freely both genders, and रात is fixed as feminine. नपुंसकलिंग is wrong because नपुंसकलिंग is not the gender class used for रात in this Class 8 Hindi grammar."},{"id":"h-nouns-23","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"«पानी» किस लिंग का शब्द है?","options":["स्त्रीलिंग","उभयलिंग","पुल्लिंग","नपुंसकलिंग"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is पुल्लिंग because पानी is masculine, which is why Hindi says ठंडा पानी गिर रहा है. स्त्रीलिंग is wrong because स्त्रीलिंग would give ठंडी पानी गिर रही है, and that agreement is not used for पानी. उभयलिंग is wrong because उभयलिंग would allow either gender, and पानी is regularly masculine. नपुंसकलिंग is wrong because नपुंसकलिंग is not the school-grammar gender of पानी; the working gender is पुल्लिंग."},{"id":"h-nouns-24","topicId":"h-nouns","subject":"hindi","stem":"आदर देते समय «आप» के साथ क्रिया किस वचन में रहती है?","options":["एकवचन","केवल स्त्रीलिंग रूप","केवल भूतकाल रूप","बहुवचन"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is बहुवचन because a respectful आप takes a plural verb, as in आप जा रहे हैं, even when only one person is addressed. एकवचन is wrong because एकवचन would give a form such as है or रहा है, which does not match respectful आप. केवल स्त्रीलिंग रूप is wrong because केवल स्त्रीलिंग रूप is wrong because the honorific plural is used for a respected man or woman. केवल भूतकाल रूप is wrong because केवल भूतकाल रूप is wrong because the plural agreement is needed in the present and the future as well."},{"id":"h-verbs-13","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«शीला ने गीत गाया है» कौन-सा काल है?","options":["आसन्न भूत","सामान्य भूत","पूर्ण भूत","अपूर्ण वर्तमान"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is आसन्न भूत because गाया है is the recent or proximate past, called आसन्न भूत in school grammar. सामान्य भूत is wrong because सामान्य भूत would be गाया without है. पूर्ण भूत is wrong because पूर्ण भूत would be गा चुकी थी or गा चुका था, using था rather than है. अपूर्ण वर्तमान is wrong because अपूर्ण वर्तमान would be गा रही है, an action still continuing."},{"id":"h-verbs-14","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«बच्चे मैदान में खेल रहे थे» कौन-सा काल है?","options":["अपूर्ण वर्तमान","अपूर्ण भूत","पूर्ण भूत","सामान्य भविष्यत्"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is अपूर्ण भूत because खेल रहे थे means they were playing, an unfinished action in the past, so it is continuous past. अपूर्ण वर्तमान is wrong because अपूर्ण वर्तमान would be खेल रहे हैं, with हैं instead of थे. पूर्ण भूत is wrong because पूर्ण भूत would be खेल चुके थे, stressing that the playing was already complete. सामान्य भविष्यत् is wrong because सामान्य भविष्यत् would be खेलेंगे, and थे marks the past."},{"id":"h-verbs-15","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«वह पत्र लिख चुका था» कौन-सा काल है?","options":["आसन्न भूत","सामान्य भूत","पूर्ण भूत","पूर्ण वर्तमान"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is पूर्ण भूत because लिख चुका था means the writing had already been completed in the past, which is पूर्ण भूत. आसन्न भूत is wrong because आसन्न भूत would be लिखा है, without the चुका था pattern. सामान्य भूत is wrong because सामान्य भूत would be लिखा, a plain past form. पूर्ण वर्तमान is wrong because पूर्ण वर्तमान would be लिख चुका है, with है rather than था."},{"id":"h-verbs-16","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«हम कल फिल्म देखेंगे» कौन-सा काल है?","options":["संभाव्य भविष्यत्","सामान्य वर्तमान","संदिग्ध भूत","सामान्य भविष्यत्"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is सामान्य भविष्यत् because देखेंगे is the simple future ending, meaning we will watch. संभाव्य भविष्यत् is wrong because संभाव्य भविष्यत् would use a shorter form such as देखें, often with शायद, not देखेंगे. सामान्य वर्तमान is wrong because सामान्य वर्तमान would be देखते हैं. संदिग्ध भूत is wrong because संदिग्ध भूत would be देखा होगा, a guess about the past."},{"id":"h-verbs-17","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«शायद आज वर्षा हो» कौन-सा काल है?","options":["संभाव्य भविष्यत्","सामान्य भविष्यत्","सामान्य भूत","पूर्ण वर्तमान"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is संभाव्य भविष्यत् because हो with शायद expresses a possible future event, which is संभाव्य भविष्यत्. सामान्य भविष्यत् is wrong because सामान्य भविष्यत् would be होगी, the plain future, and this sentence uses the possible form हो. सामान्य भूत is wrong because सामान्य भूत would be हुई, and शायद आज points forward, not to a completed past event. पूर्ण वर्तमान is wrong because पूर्ण वर्तमान would be हो चुकी है, meaning the rain has already finished."},{"id":"h-verbs-18","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«यदि वह पढ़ता तो सफल होता» कौन-सा भूतकाल है?","options":["सामान्य भूत","हेतुहेतुमद् भूत","आसन्न भूत","अपूर्ण भूत"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is हेतुहेतुमद् भूत because the तो pattern states an unfulfilled past condition: if he had studied, he would have succeeded. सामान्य भूत is wrong because सामान्य भूत would simply say वह पढ़ा or वह सफल हुआ, without this if-then past condition. आसन्न भूत is wrong because आसन्न भूत would use a है form such as पढ़ा है. अपूर्ण भूत is wrong because अपूर्ण भूत would be पढ़ रहा था, an action that was going on, not a condition with तो."},{"id":"h-verbs-19","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«राम फल खाता है» कौन-सा वाच्य है?","options":["कर्मवाच्य","भाववाच्य","कर्तृवाच्य","प्रेरणार्थक रूप"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is कर्तृवाच्य because राम is the doer and the verb खाता है agrees with him, so the voice is active, कर्तृवाच्य. कर्मवाच्य is wrong because कर्मवाच्य would turn it into राम से फल खाया जाता है, which is not this sentence. भाववाच्य is wrong because भाववाच्य is used when there is no object and the verb stays impersonal, and फल is an object here. प्रेरणार्थक रूप is wrong because प्रेरणार्थक रूप would be a causative such as खिलाना, and खाता है is not causative."},{"id":"h-verbs-20","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«राम से फल खाया जाता है» कौन-सा वाच्य है?","options":["कर्तृवाच्य","भाववाच्य","प्रेरणार्थक रूप","कर्मवाच्य"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is कर्मवाच्य because the object फल is in front of the meaning, the doer is marked by से, and the verb is खाया जाता है. कर्तृवाच्य is wrong because कर्तृवाच्य would be राम फल खाता है, with the doer as the ordinary subject. भाववाच्य is wrong because भाववाच्य would drop the object, as in राम से सोया जाता है, and this sentence keeps फल. प्रेरणार्थक रूप is wrong because प्रेरणार्थक रूप would mean someone is made to eat, and जाता है here marks voice, not a causative stem."},{"id":"t-resources-13","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which action conserves a non-renewable metal?","options":["Recycling aluminium instead of throwing it away","Dumping metal scrap in a river","Mining ore and never reusing the metal","Burning aluminium cans as if they were firewood"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is Recycling aluminium instead of throwing it away because recycling lets the same metal be used again, which slows the drain on a limited stock. Dumping metal scrap in a river is wrong because dumping scrap pollutes water and loses the metal. Mining ore and never reusing the metal is wrong because never reusing the metal forces more mining of a limited resource. Burning aluminium cans as if they were firewood is wrong because aluminium is not a fuel, and burning cans wastes the metal.\nयाद रखो: एल्युमिनियम फिर इस्तेमाल करना अनवीकरणीय धातु बचाता है। नदी में फेंकना बर्बादी है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Dumping metal scrap in a river कबाड़ नदी में फेंकना संरक्षण नहीं।"},{"id":"t-resources-14","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"What improves the quality of a country's human resources?","options":["Closing schools","Education and health care","Ignoring illness and skill","Treating knowledge as useless"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is Education and health care because healthy, educated, and skilled people can do more, so education and health raise the quality of human resources. Closing schools is wrong because closing schools reduces learning and lowers that quality. Ignoring illness and skill is wrong because ignoring illness and skill leaves people's abilities undeveloped. Treating knowledge as useless is wrong because knowledge is exactly what makes human resources more valuable.\nयाद रखो: पढ़ाई और स्वास्थ्य सेवा मानव संसाधन को बेहतर बनाती हैं। स्कूल बंद करना उल्टा है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Closing schools स्कूल बंद करना हुनर बढ़ाता नहीं।"},{"id":"t-resources-15","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Petroleum is non-renewable because","options":["new petroleum is produced in every rainy season","petroleum is manufactured in kitchens","it forms over a vast span of time and the usable stock is limited","sunlight turns into fresh petroleum every afternoon"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is it forms over a vast span of time and the usable stock is limited because petroleum is a fossil fuel. Nature does not replace the amount people burn within a human lifetime. new petroleum is produced in every rainy season is wrong because the rainy season does not refill oil fields. petroleum is manufactured in kitchens is wrong because petroleum is extracted from the earth, not cooked in a kitchen. sunlight turns into fresh petroleum every afternoon is wrong because sunlight is renewable, but it does not create a new tank of petroleum each day.\nयाद रखो: पेट्रोलियम लाखों साल में बनता है और भंडार सीमित है, इसलिए अनवीकरणीय है।\nगलत मत याद करना: new petroleum is produced in every rainy season हर बरसात नई तेल की फसल नहीं होती।"},{"id":"t-resources-16","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which of these is renewable?","options":["Coal","Petroleum","Natural gas","Sunlight"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is Sunlight because sunlight arrives every day and is a renewable energy source. Coal is wrong because coal is a fossil fuel with a limited stock. Petroleum is wrong because petroleum is a limited fossil fuel. Natural gas is wrong because natural gas is also a fossil fuel and is non-renewable.\nयाद रखो: सूरज नवीकरणीय है। कोयला, पेट्रोलियम और प्राकृतिक गैस नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Coal कोयला सूरज की तरह रोज़ नया नहीं बनता।"},{"id":"t-resources-17","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which group contains only human-made resources?","options":["Bridges, machines, and roads","Air, coal, and soil","Sunlight, wind, and rain","Forests, wildlife, and fish"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is Bridges, machines, and roads because bridges, machines, and roads are all built by people. Air, coal, and soil is wrong because air, coal, and soil occur in nature. Sunlight, wind, and rain is wrong because sunlight, wind, and rain are natural. Forests, wildlife, and fish is wrong because forests, wildlife, and fish are natural, even though people may use them.\nयाद रखो: पुल, मशीन और सड़क सिर्फ मानव-निर्मित हैं। हवा, कोयला और मिट्टी कुदरती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Air, coal, and soil ये तीनों कुदरत के हैं, कारखाने के नहीं।"},{"id":"t-resources-18","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which practice matches sustainable development?","options":["Clearing a forest and never replanting it","Replanting trees after cutting and using groundwater carefully","Pumping a well dry with no recharge","Pouring untreated factory waste into a river"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is Replanting trees after cutting and using groundwater carefully because replanting and careful water use meet present needs while keeping resources for later. Clearing a forest and never replanting it is wrong because clearing a forest with no replanting destroys a resource for the future. Pumping a well dry with no recharge is wrong because emptying a well with no recharge creates scarcity. Pouring untreated factory waste into a river is wrong because untreated waste pollutes water and harms both present and future users.\nयाद रखो: काटने के बाद पेड़ लगाना और भूजल सँभालना सतत विकास है। कुआँ सुखा देना नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Clearing a forest and never replanting it जंगल काटकर भूल जाना सतत नहीं।"},{"id":"t-resources-19","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which statement about the spread of resources is correct?","options":["Every district has the same minerals","Every country has the same amount of petroleum","Resources are distributed unevenly over the earth","A large area always has every resource people need"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is Resources are distributed unevenly over the earth because minerals, water, and fertile soil are not shared out equally, which is why places differ. Every district has the same minerals is wrong because mineral deposits are localised, so districts do not all have the same ones. Every country has the same amount of petroleum is wrong because petroleum is concentrated in some regions and absent in many others. A large area always has every resource people need is wrong because size alone does not guarantee coal, oil, or fertile soil.\nयाद रखो: संसाधन धरती पर असमान बँटे हैं। हर ज़िले में एक जैसे खनिज नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Every district has the same minerals हर ज़िला एक जैसी खदान नहीं।"},{"id":"t-resources-20","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"A substance in nature becomes a resource when","options":["it is buried so deep that nobody can reach it","nobody knows that it exists","it has no utility","people find a use for it"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is people find a use for it because use, or utility, is the change that turns a natural substance into a resource. it is buried so deep that nobody can reach it is wrong because if nobody can reach it, it stays unused and is not yet an actual resource in practice. nobody knows that it exists is wrong because an unknown substance is not being used to meet a need. it has no utility is wrong because no utility means it does not satisfy a need.\nयाद रखो: कुदरत की चीज़ संसाधन तब बनती है जब लोग उसका उपयोग पा लें।\nगलत मत याद करना: it has no utility बिना उपयोग के वह संसाधन नहीं कहलाती।"},{"id":"t-resources-21","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which description of forests is accurate?","options":["They can regrow, but overcutting can still destroy them","They are impossible to harm","They form again overnight like a manufactured tool","They are human-made resources"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is They can regrow, but overcutting can still destroy them because forests are renewable only if growth is allowed to continue. Reckless cutting can wipe them out. They are impossible to harm is wrong because forests are damaged by clearing, fire, and overuse, so they are not impossible to harm. They form again overnight like a manufactured tool is wrong because a forest does not regrow overnight the way a factory might make a tool. They are human-made resources is wrong because forests grow in nature, so they are natural resources.\nयाद रखो: जंगल फिर उग सकते हैं, पर बहुत काटने से मिट भी सकते हैं। रात भर में औज़ार नहीं बनते।\nगलत मत याद करना: They are impossible to harm जंगल को नुकसान नहीं हो सकता, यह गलत है।"},{"id":"t-resources-22","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which is a human resource rather than a human-made object?","options":["The loom in the workshop","The skill of a weaver","The finished cloth","The workshop building"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is The skill of a weaver because the weaver's skill is a human ability, so it is a human resource. The loom in the workshop is wrong because the loom is a machine that people made. The finished cloth is wrong because the finished cloth is a product, not the person. The workshop building is wrong because the workshop building is human-made.\nयाद रखो: जुलाहे का हुनर मानव संसाधन है। करघा, कपड़ा और इमारत मानव-निर्मित चीज़ें हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: The loom in the workshop करघा वस्तु है, आदमी का हुनर नहीं।"},{"id":"t-resources-23","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which pair helps to explain how resources become available?","options":["Colour and luck alone","Noise and darkness","Time and technology","A patent on rainfall"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is Time and technology because over time, and with technology, people learn to use things that earlier generations could not use. Colour and luck alone is wrong because colour and luck are not the textbook explanation of how substances become resources. Noise and darkness is wrong because noise and darkness do not create utility. A patent on rainfall is wrong because rainfall is not something a patent assigns to one inventor.\nयाद रखो: समय और तकनीक बताते हैं कि संसाधन कैसे उपलब्ध होता है। किस्मत अकेले काफी नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Colour and luck alone रंग और किस्मत संसाधन का नियम नहीं।"},{"id":"t-resources-24","topicId":"t-resources","subject":"sst","stem":"Which person is using a resource sustainably?","options":["A miner who extracts ore with no plan to reuse or restore anything","A household that burns plastic in the open every evening","A factory that dumps dye into the only village stream","A farmer who saves seed, guards the soil, and limits waste of water"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is A farmer who saves seed, guards the soil, and limits waste of water because saving seed, protecting soil, and limiting water waste keeps the farm productive for later years. A miner who extracts ore with no plan to reuse or restore anything is wrong because extraction with no reuse or restoration drains a limited stock and damages the site. A household that burns plastic in the open every evening is wrong because burning plastic pollutes the air and wastes material that might have been reused. A factory that dumps dye into the only village stream is wrong because dumping dye destroys a shared water resource.\nयाद रखो: जो किसान बीज बचाए, मिट्टी रखे और पानी कम बहाए, वह संसाधन सतत इस्तेमाल कर रहा है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A miner who extracts ore with no plan to reuse or restore anything बिना योजना खुदाई सतत नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-13","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Most of the water on earth is","options":["salty ocean water that people cannot drink as it is","fresh water stored in village wells","water kept in kitchen pots","rain falling on one city in one hour"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is salty ocean water that people cannot drink as it is because oceans hold most of the water, and that water is saline. fresh water stored in village wells is wrong because wells hold only a tiny local share of fresh water. water kept in kitchen pots is wrong because kitchen pots are not the earth's water store. rain falling on one city in one hour is wrong because one hour of rain over one city is a minute fraction of the earth's water.\nयाद रखो: धरती का ज़्यादातर पानी नमकीन समुद्री है, जैसे का तैसा पी नहीं सकते।\nगलत मत याद करना: fresh water stored in village wells गाँव के कुएँ पृथ्वी का ज़्यादातर पानी नहीं हैं।"},{"id":"t-land-14","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Which combination can cause water scarcity?","options":["Careful drip irrigation by itself","Rising demand, wastage, and pollution","Harvesting roof rain and using it wisely","A single unused well in a very rainy forest"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is Rising demand, wastage, and pollution because more users, wasted water, and dirty sources together leave less usable water. Careful drip irrigation by itself is wrong because drip irrigation is a way to save water, not a cause of scarcity. Harvesting roof rain and using it wisely is wrong because wise harvesting increases the supply people can use. A single unused well in a very rainy forest is wrong because one unused well in a rainy forest does not describe scarcity.\nयाद रखो: बढ़ती माँग, बर्बादी और प्रदूषण मिलकर पानी की कमी ला सकते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Harvesting roof rain and using it wisely छत का पानी सँभालना कमी बढ़ाता नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-15","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Rainwater harvesting means","options":["sending every drop straight to the sea","covering fields so that no rain can touch the soil","collecting and storing rain so it can be used later","replacing rain with seawater"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is collecting and storing rain so it can be used later because harvesting rain means catching and keeping it for drinking or farming. sending every drop straight to the sea is wrong because sending all rain to the sea wastes the fresh water. covering fields so that no rain can touch the soil is wrong because blocking rain from the soil is not harvesting. replacing rain with seawater is wrong because seawater is salty and is not harvested rain.\nयाद रखो: वर्षाजल संग्रहण बारिश को इकट्ठा करके बाद के लिए रखना है। समुद्र में बहाना नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: sending every drop straight to the sea हर बूँद समुद्र में उड़ेलना संग्रहण नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-16","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Natural vegetation in a place depends mainly on","options":["the official language","the date of a festival","the number of television channels","temperature and rainfall"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is temperature and rainfall because plants grow according to heat and moisture, so climate decides the vegetation. the official language is wrong because language does not decide which plants can grow. the date of a festival is wrong because a festival date does not set the climate. the number of television channels is wrong because television channels do not determine natural vegetation.\nयाद रखो: प्राकृतिक वनस्पति मुख्यतः ताप और वर्षा पर टिकी है। भाषा या त्योहार पर नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the official language राजभाषा जंगल का मौसम नहीं बदलती।"},{"id":"t-land-17","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"A wildlife sanctuary is meant to","options":["protect wild animals and the habitat they need","replace every forest with a city","allow free trade in rare animals","open the whole area to mining first"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is protect wild animals and the habitat they need because a sanctuary is a protected area where wildlife and its home are conserved. replace every forest with a city is wrong because replacing the forest removes the habitat. allow free trade in rare animals is wrong because free trade in rare animals is what protection tries to stop. open the whole area to mining first is wrong because mining first would destroy the habitat the sanctuary is meant to guard.\nयाद रखो: वन्यजीव अभयारण्य जंगली जानवरों और उनके घर को बचाता है। शहर या खदान के लिए नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: allow free trade in rare animals दुर्लभ जानवरों का खुला व्यापार अभयारण्य नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-18","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"CITES is important because it","options":["is a method of contour ploughing","restricts international trade in endangered wild plants and animals","is a type of desert soil","is a beverage crop grown on hills"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is restricts international trade in endangered wild plants and animals because CITES is the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species, and it limits trade that threatens rare wildlife. is a method of contour ploughing is wrong because contour ploughing is a farming method, not a wildlife treaty. is a type of desert soil is wrong because CITES is not a soil type. is a beverage crop grown on hills is wrong because a beverage crop such as tea is not a conservation treaty.\nयाद रखो: CITES संकटग्रस्त जंगली पौधों और जानवरों के अंतर्राष्ट्रीय व्यापार को रोकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: is a method of contour ploughing यह संधि जुताई का तरीका नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-19","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Careless use of chemical fertilisers can","options":["remove the need for parent rock in soil formation","turn a desert into a glacier in one night","harm the soil over time","plant a shelter belt without trees"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is harm the soil over time because too many chemicals can damage soil life and structure, which is a form of degradation. remove the need for parent rock in soil formation is wrong because parent rock remains a natural factor, and fertiliser does not replace it. turn a desert into a glacier in one night is wrong because fertiliser cannot turn a desert into a glacier overnight. plant a shelter belt without trees is wrong because a shelter belt needs trees, not a bag of fertiliser.\nयाद रखो: रासायनिक उर्वरक लापरवाही से डालो तो समय के साथ मिट्टी को नुकसान हो सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: turn a desert into a glacier in one night एक रात में रेगिस्तान ग्लेशियर नहीं बनता।"},{"id":"t-land-20","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Which list is made up of land uses?","options":["Patents, poems, and prices","Only lines of latitude","Only ocean currents","Farms, forests, pastures, and settlements"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is Farms, forests, pastures, and settlements because people use land to grow crops, keep forests and pastures, and build places to live. Patents, poems, and prices is wrong because patents, poems, and prices are not ways of using the land surface. Only lines of latitude is wrong because latitude is a map line, not a use of land. Only ocean currents is wrong because ocean currents are movements of water, not land uses.\nयाद रखो: भूमि उपयोग: खेत, जंगल, चरागाह और बस्तियाँ। पेटेंट और अक्षांश नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Patents, poems, and prices कीमत और कविता ज़मीन के उपयोग नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-21","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Soil erosion means","options":["the removal of topsoil by wind or running water","the adding of humus to a field","the building of terraces","the planting of a shelter belt"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is the removal of topsoil by wind or running water because erosion carries away the fertile top layer. the adding of humus to a field is wrong because adding humus improves soil; it is not erosion. the building of terraces is wrong because terraces are built to reduce erosion. the planting of a shelter belt is wrong because a shelter belt is planted to protect soil from wind.\nयाद रखो: मृदा अपरदन: हवा या बहता पानी ऊपरी मिट्टी उठा ले जाए। ह्यूमस जोड़ना अपरदन नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the adding of humus to a field खाद मिलाना मिट्टी का बहना नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-22","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Community land is best described as","options":["land with no rules of any kind","land kept for common village use rather than seized by one person","the private courtyard of one factory owner only","the floor of the deep ocean"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is land kept for common village use rather than seized by one person because community or common land serves the village, and encroachment takes that shared resource away. land with no rules of any kind is wrong because common land still needs care and rules so that everyone can use it fairly. the private courtyard of one factory owner only is wrong because one factory courtyard is private, not community land. the floor of the deep ocean is wrong because the ocean floor is not the village common.\nयाद रखो: सामुदायिक भूमि गाँव के साझे काम की ज़मीन है, एक आदमी की हथियाई हुई नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the private courtyard of one factory owner only एक मालिक का आँगन सामुदायिक भूमि नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-23","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Drip irrigation saves water because","options":["it floods the field every hour","it uses only seawater","it releases water slowly near the roots instead of flooding the field","it stops clouds from forming"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is it releases water slowly near the roots instead of flooding the field because slow delivery at the roots cuts waste from runoff and evaporation. it floods the field every hour is wrong because hourly flooding wastes water. it uses only seawater is wrong because seawater is salty and is not the idea of drip irrigation. it stops clouds from forming is wrong because irrigation does not control cloud formation.\nयाद रखो: ड्रिप सिंचाई जड़ों के पास धीरे पानी छोड़ती है, पूरा खेत नहीं डुबोती।\nगलत मत याद करना: it floods the field every hour हर घंटे बाढ़ लाना बचत नहीं।"},{"id":"t-land-24","topicId":"t-land","subject":"sst","stem":"Intercropping helps the soil because","options":["the land is left completely bare between the rows","only one mining trench is dug between the crops","all plants are removed before every rain","different crops grown in alternate rows give the soil better cover"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is different crops grown in alternate rows give the soil better cover because alternate rows of different crops protect the soil from rain wash better than a bare surface. the land is left completely bare between the rows is wrong because bare soil between rows would increase erosion, which intercropping tries to avoid. only one mining trench is dug between the crops is wrong because a mining trench is not intercropping. all plants are removed before every rain is wrong because removing all plants before rain would expose the soil.\nयाद रखो: अंतःफसल में अलग-अलग फसलें कतारों में मिट्टी को बेहतर ढकती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the land is left completely bare between the rows बीच की नंगी ज़मीन इस मदद का उल्टा है।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-13","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Tea is grown successfully where there are","options":["well-drained soils and frequent showers, often on hills in India and in Kenya","frozen polar plains","only deep desert sand and no rain","flooded mangrove swamps as the ideal site"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is well-drained soils and frequent showers, often on hills in India and in Kenya because frequent rain keeps tender tea leaves growing, and the water must drain. Hill regions of India and Kenya are important producers. frozen polar plains is wrong because polar cold does not suit tea. only deep desert sand and no rain is wrong because tea cannot thrive with no rain on deep desert sand. flooded mangrove swamps as the ideal site is wrong because tea is not a swamp crop; it needs drainage.\nयाद रखो: चाय अच्छे निकास वाली मिट्टी और बार-बार बौछार चाहती है, भारत और केन्या की पहाड़ियों पर।\nगलत मत याद करना: flooded mangrove swamps as the ideal site डूबा मैंग्रोव चाय का आदर्श खेत नहीं।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-14","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Maize grows well with","options":["continuous frost","moderate temperature, moderate rainfall, and plenty of sunshine","no soil","total darkness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is moderate temperature, moderate rainfall, and plenty of sunshine because maize likes a moderate climate, rainfall that is not extreme, sunshine, and well-drained fertile soil. continuous frost is wrong because frost is not the climate maize needs. no soil is wrong because a crop cannot grow with no soil. total darkness is wrong because maize needs lots of sunshine, not darkness.\nयाद रखो: मक्का मध्यम ताप, मध्यम वर्षा और खूब धूप में अच्छी उगती है। अँधेरा और पाला नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: continuous frost लगातार पाला मक्का का मौसम नहीं।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-15","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Nomadic herding means that people","options":["stay on one plantation of tea for generations without animals","grow rice in standing water and never keep herds","move with their animals in search of fodder and water","run a factory that makes steel"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is move with their animals in search of fodder and water because herders shift from place to place so the animals can find grass and water. stay on one plantation of tea for generations without animals is wrong because a tea plantation is settled cultivation, not nomadic herding. grow rice in standing water and never keep herds is wrong because rice farming is cultivation, not herding. run a factory that makes steel is wrong because a steel factory is an industry, not herding.\nयाद रखो: चलवासी पशुचारण: लोग जानवरों के साथ चारा और पानी ढूँढते फिरते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: stay on one plantation of tea for generations without animals बिना जानवर एक चाय बागान यह नहीं।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-16","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Rice is a staple food especially in","options":["the frozen interior of Greenland","the driest cores of the Sahara only","Antarctica","the hot, wet monsoon regions of Asia"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is the hot, wet monsoon regions of Asia because rice feeds large populations in the tropical and subtropical monsoon lands. the frozen interior of Greenland is wrong because Greenland is too cold for rice. the driest cores of the Sahara only is wrong because the driest Sahara cannot supply the water rice needs. Antarctica is wrong because Antarctica has no rice farming.\nयाद रखो: चावल खासकर एशिया के गर्म, नम मानसूनी इलाकों का मुख्य भोजन है।\nगलत मत याद करना: the frozen interior of Greenland ग्रीनलैंड की बर्फ चावल का कटोरा नहीं।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-17","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"In India, wheat is mainly a","options":["rabi, or winter, crop","crop that must stand in deep water through the hottest monsoon","shifting crop of the tundra","kind of jute"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is rabi, or winter, crop because Indian wheat is sown in winter and harvested as a rabi crop. crop that must stand in deep water through the hottest monsoon is wrong because deep water in the hot monsoon describes rice, which is mainly kharif. shifting crop of the tundra is wrong because the tundra is not an Indian wheat region, and wheat is not grown by shifting cultivation there. kind of jute is wrong because jute is a fibre, not wheat.\nयाद रखो: भारत में गेहूँ मुख्यतः रबी, यानी सर्दी की फसल है। खड़े मानसून पानी वाली नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: crop that must stand in deep water through the hottest monsoon गहरा पानी चावल माँगता है।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-18","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Which crop is typically grown as a plantation crop?","options":["Bajra","Tea","Jowar","Ragi"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is Tea because tea is grown on plantations with large labour and capital inputs. Bajra is wrong because bajra is a millet, usually a hardy food crop, not a plantation beverage. Jowar is wrong because jowar is also a millet. Ragi is wrong because ragi is a millet grown on less fertile and drier land.\nयाद रखो: चाय आम बागान फसल है। बाजरा, ज्वार और रागी मोटे अनाज हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Bajra बाजरा बागान की चाय नहीं, मोटा अनाज है।"}]}] as TestView[];
export const mocks = [{"id":"mock-1","title":"Full mock 1","kind":"mock","minutes":150,"strict":true,"concept":"Full RMS CET Class 9 paper. 200 questions, 2 hours 30 minutes, no negative marking. English 50, Hindi 20, Social Science 30, Mathematics 50, Science 50. Paper 1 and Paper 2 are marked separately. Each needs 50%.","questions":[{"id":"e-narration-23","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said, \"I will start next week.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He said that he will start next week","He said that he would start the previous week","He said that I would start next week","He said that he would start the following week"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He said that he would start the following week\" because next week becomes the following week, and will becomes would. \"He said that he will start next week\" fails because will becomes would, and next week becomes the following week. \"He said that he would start the previous week\" fails because the previous week would report a past week, not next week. \"He said that I would start next week\" fails because I becomes he, and next week still needs to change."},{"id":"e-narration-24","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said, \"I must finish the work.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He said that he had to finish the work","He said that he must finished the work","He said that I had to finish the work","He says that he had to finish the work"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He said that he had to finish the work\" because must showing obligation often becomes had to when the reporting verb is past. \"He said that he must finished the work\" fails because must finished is not a verb pattern; the obligation becomes had to finish. \"He said that I had to finish the work\" fails because the speaker's I becomes he. \"He says that he had to finish the work\" fails because the reporting verb in the direct sentence is said, so it should not be changed to says."},{"id":"e-narration-25","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said, \"What a fine day it is!\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He exclaimed that it is a fine day","He asked what a fine day it was","He exclaimed that it was a fine day","He exclaimed that what a fine day it was"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He exclaimed that it was a fine day\" because an exclamation of delight is reported with exclaimed that, and the tense shifts back. \"He exclaimed that it is a fine day\" fails because is in the exclamation becomes was after a past reporting verb. \"He asked what a fine day it was\" fails because this is an exclamation of pleasure, not a question, so exclaimed is the reporting verb. \"He exclaimed that what a fine day it was\" fails because the what a pattern is dropped, and the report becomes a plain that-clause."},{"id":"e-narration-26","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said to me, \"Good morning.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He wished me that good morning","He asked me good morning","He said that he was a good morning","He wished me good morning"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He wished me good morning\" because greetings such as good morning are reported with wished. \"He wished me that good morning\" fails because a greeting does not take that before the words good morning. \"He asked me good morning\" fails because good morning is a wish or greeting, not a question. \"He said that he was a good morning\" fails because this changes the greeting into a false statement about himself."},{"id":"e-narration-27","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"The indirect sentence is: He said that he was tired. Choose the matching direct speech.","options":["He said, \"I am tired.\"","He said, \"He was tired.\"","He said, \"I was tired.\"","He said, \"I will be tired.\""],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He said, \"I am tired.\"\" because he was in indirect speech often comes from I am in the speaker's exact words. \"He said, \"He was tired.\"\" fails because inside the quotation the speaker calls himself I, and the present am matches was in the report. \"He said, \"I was tired.\"\" fails because was in the quotation would normally be reported as had been, not as was. \"He said, \"I will be tired.\"\" fails because will be would be reported as would be, not as was."},{"id":"e-narration-28","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"She said, \"I like these flowers.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["She said that she liked these flowers","She said that she liked those flowers","She said that she likes those flowers","She said that I liked those flowers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She said that she liked those flowers\" because these becomes those, and the simple present becomes the simple past. \"She said that she liked these flowers\" fails because these changes to those when the words are reported elsewhere. \"She said that she likes those flowers\" fails because like should become liked after said. \"She said that I liked those flowers\" fails because her I becomes she."},{"id":"e-narration-29","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said to me, \"I shall help you.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He told me that he shall help me","He told me that I would help you","He told me that he will help you","He told me that he would help me"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He told me that he would help me\" because shall for a future action becomes would, and you becomes the right pronoun for the listener. \"He told me that he shall help me\" fails because shall becomes would, and you becomes me. \"He told me that I would help you\" fails because this swaps the helper and the person helped. \"He told me that he will help you\" fails because will is the wrong backshift of shall here, and you should become me."},{"id":"e-narration-30","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"He said, \"I may come.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["He said that he might come","He said that he may come","He said that he might came","He said that I may come"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He said that he might come\" because may in direct speech normally becomes might in indirect speech. \"He said that he may come\" fails because may usually becomes might after said. \"He said that he might came\" fails because might is followed by the base form come, not came. \"He said that I may come\" fails because I should be he, and may should be might."},{"id":"e-narration-31","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"The indirect sentence is: She asked me where I lived. Choose the matching direct speech.","options":["She said to me, \"Where did I live?\"","She said to me, \"Where do you live?\"","She said to me, \"Where do I live?\"","She said to me, \"Where you live?\""],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She said to me, \"Where do you live?\"\" because where I lived in indirect speech comes from Where do you live in the exact question. \"She said to me, \"Where did I live?\"\" fails because the original question uses you for the listener and the present do you live. \"She said to me, \"Where do I live?\"\" fails because I would be her own home, but she was asking the listener, so the pronoun is you. \"She said to me, \"Where you live?\"\" fails because a direct question needs the helping verb do: Where do you live."},{"id":"e-narration-32","topicId":"e-narration","subject":"english","stem":"Mother said to me, \"I am cooking now.\" Choose the correct indirect speech.","options":["Mother told me that she is cooking now","Mother told me that I was cooking then","Mother told me that she was cooking then","Mother said me that she was cooking then"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Mother told me that she was cooking then\" because now becomes then, the speaker's I becomes she, and the present continuous becomes the past continuous. \"Mother told me that she is cooking now\" fails because am cooking becomes was cooking, and now becomes then. \"Mother told me that I was cooking then\" fails because Mother's I becomes she, not I. \"Mother said me that she was cooking then\" fails because said me is incorrect; with a listener the verb is told me."},{"id":"e-articles-13","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The sentence names one famous peak with the word Mount. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world","A Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world","An Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world","Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world\" because do not put the before Mount plus the name of one peak, though the superlative highest still needs the. \"The Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world\" fails because a single peak named with Mount does not take the before Mount. \"A Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world\" fails because a is not used before this proper name. \"An Mount Everest is the highest peak in the world\" fails because an is the wrong article, and Mount Everest takes no article before Mount."},{"id":"e-articles-14","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"Neha sings better than every other person in the choir. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Neha is the best singer in the choir","Neha is a best singer in the choir","Neha is an best singer in the choir","Neha is best singer in the choir"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Neha is the best singer in the choir\" because superlative adjectives are normally used with the. \"Neha is a best singer in the choir\" fails because a superlative such as best takes the, not a. \"Neha is an best singer in the choir\" fails because an is the wrong article before best, which needs the. \"Neha is best singer in the choir\" fails because the superlative best needs the article the."},{"id":"e-articles-15","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The boys are playing a game, not a particular named match. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The boys play the cricket after school","The boys play cricket after school","The boys play a cricket after school","The boys play an cricket after school"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The boys play cricket after school\" because names of games usually take no article when we mean playing the game. \"The boys play the cricket after school\" fails because games played in general do not take the. \"The boys play a cricket after school\" fails because cricket as a game is not used with a. \"The boys play an cricket after school\" fails because cricket does not begin with a vowel sound, and the game needs no article."},{"id":"e-articles-16","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"This is the family's ordinary morning meal, not a special banquet. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We have the breakfast at seven","We have an breakfast at seven","We have breakfast at seven","We have breakfasts at seven"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We have breakfast at seven\" because meals such as breakfast, lunch, and dinner usually take no article. \"We have the breakfast at seven\" fails because an ordinary meal name such as breakfast takes no article. \"We have an breakfast at seven\" fails because breakfast begins with a consonant sound, and the meal needs no article here. \"We have breakfasts at seven\" fails because the plural breakfasts changes the ordinary meal into an odd plural."},{"id":"e-articles-17","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"These children are going there as pupils for their classes. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The pupils go to school by bus","The pupils go to the school by bus","The pupils go to an school by bus","The pupils goes to school by bus"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The pupils go to school by bus\" because go to school, without the, is the pattern for pupils going to study. \"The pupils go to the school by bus\" fails because when school means attending class, no article is used. \"The pupils go to an school by bus\" fails because school begins with a consonant sound, and pupils attending class use no article. \"The pupils goes to school by bus\" fails because pupils is plural, so the verb is go, not goes."},{"id":"e-articles-18","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"Father is not a pupil. He is visiting the building to meet the principal. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Father went to school to meet the principal","Father went to the school to meet the principal","Father went to an school to meet the principal","Father going to the school to meet the principal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Father went to the school to meet the principal\" because use the school when the building is visited for a purpose other than attending class. \"Father went to school to meet the principal\" fails because without the, go to school sounds like attending class, but Father is only visiting the building. \"Father went to an school to meet the principal\" fails because an is the wrong article before school, which starts with a consonant sound. \"Father going to the school to meet the principal\" fails because going has no finite verb, so the sentence is incomplete."},{"id":"e-articles-19","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The jug does contain milk. The sentence is affirmative. Which sentence is correct?","options":["There is any milk in the jug","There is many milk in the jug","There is some milk in the jug","There is much milks in the jug"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"There is some milk in the jug\" because some is commonly used with uncountable nouns in affirmative sentences. \"There is any milk in the jug\" fails because any is the usual choice in negatives and questions, not in this affirmative sentence. \"There is many milk in the jug\" fails because milk is uncountable, so many is the wrong determiner. \"There is much milks in the jug\" fails because milk has no plural milks, and the affirmative sentence is better with some."},{"id":"e-articles-20","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The tea has no sugar left in it. Which sentence is correct?","options":["There is not some sugar in the tea","There is not many sugar in the tea","There is not a sugars in the tea","There is not any sugar in the tea"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"There is not any sugar in the tea\" because any is the usual determiner in negative statements with uncountable nouns. \"There is not some sugar in the tea\" fails because in a negative sentence the usual determiner is any, not some. \"There is not many sugar in the tea\" fails because sugar is uncountable, so many does not fit. \"There is not a sugars in the tea\" fails because sugar is not counted with a or with the plural sugars in this sentence."},{"id":"e-articles-21","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The host is warmly offering tea and expects that the guest may want it. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Would you like many tea?","Would you like some tea?","Would you like a teas?","Would you like much tea?"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Would you like some tea?\" because some is used in polite offers even though the sentence is a question. \"Would you like many tea?\" fails because tea is uncountable, so many cannot describe it. \"Would you like a teas?\" fails because a teas mixes a singular article with a wrong plural. \"Would you like much tea?\" fails because much tea sounds like a question about quantity, not a warm offer."},{"id":"e-articles-22","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"Books can be counted one by one on the shelf. Which sentence is correct?","options":["There are much books on the shelf","There is many books on the shelf","There are many books on the shelf","There are many book on the shelf"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"There are many books on the shelf\" because many is used with plural countable nouns, and the verb agrees with that plural. \"There are much books on the shelf\" fails because books are countable, so the word is many, not much. \"There is many books on the shelf\" fails because books is plural, so the verb is are, not is. \"There are many book on the shelf\" fails because many is followed by a plural noun: books, not book."},{"id":"e-articles-23","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"Rice cannot be counted one grain at a time in this sack. Which sentence is correct?","options":["There is not many rice in the sack","There are not much rice in the sack","There is not much rices in the sack","There is not much rice in the sack"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"There is not much rice in the sack\" because much is used with uncountable nouns, which take a singular verb. \"There is not many rice in the sack\" fails because rice is uncountable, so the word is much, not many. \"There are not much rice in the sack\" fails because rice takes a singular verb, so the verb is is, not are. \"There is not much rices in the sack\" fails because rice does not take a plural rices."},{"id":"e-articles-24","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"Reema has some friends in this town, though not a large number. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Reema has a few friends in this town","Reema has few friends in this town","Reema has a little friends in this town","Reema has the few friends in this town"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Reema has a few friends in this town\" because a few means a small number, some, and is used with countable nouns. \"Reema has few friends in this town\" fails because few without a means almost none, but the stem says she does have some friends. \"Reema has a little friends in this town\" fails because a little is for an uncountable noun, while friends are countable. \"Reema has the few friends in this town\" fails because the few needs a defining phrase such as the few friends she has, which is not the meaning here."},{"id":"e-articles-25","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"Almost nobody came, and the hall looked empty. Which sentence is correct?","options":["A few people came to the show","A little people came to the show","Few people came to the show","The little people came to the show"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Few people came to the show\" because few without a means almost none and is used with countable nouns. \"A few people came to the show\" fails because a few would mean some people came, but the hall was nearly empty. \"A little people came to the show\" fails because little is for uncountable nouns, not for people. \"The little people came to the show\" fails because the little does not mean almost nobody, and little does not fit the countable noun people."},{"id":"e-articles-26","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"There is a small but usable amount of water, enough for a drink. Which sentence is correct?","options":["There is little water in the bottle, so you may drink","There is a few water in the bottle, so you may drink","There are a little water in the bottle, so you may drink","There is a little water in the bottle, so you may drink"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"There is a little water in the bottle, so you may drink\" because a little means a small amount of an uncountable noun, enough to be useful. \"There is little water in the bottle, so you may drink\" fails because little without a means almost none, which clashes with enough water for a drink. \"There is a few water in the bottle, so you may drink\" fails because a few is for countable nouns, but water is uncountable. \"There are a little water in the bottle, so you may drink\" fails because water is uncountable and takes is, not are."},{"id":"e-articles-27","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"Almost no water remains. It is not a small usable amount. Which sentence is correct?","options":["There is little water left","There is a little water left","There is a few water left","There are little water left"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"There is little water left\" because little without a means almost none of an uncountable noun. \"There is a little water left\" fails because a little means some water is available, but the speaker means almost none. \"There is a few water left\" fails because a few cannot describe the uncountable noun water. \"There are little water left\" fails because water takes the singular verb is, not are."},{"id":"e-articles-28","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"He did not have many friends, but every one of that small group stood by him. Which sentence is correct?","options":["A few friends he had were loyal","The few friends he had were loyal","Few friends he had were loyal","The little friends he had were loyal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The few friends he had were loyal\" because the few means all of a small known number and is often followed by a clause that defines them. \"A few friends he had were loyal\" fails because a few does not mean the whole of a known small group, and the clause he had needs the. \"Few friends he had were loyal\" fails because few alone does not complete the pattern the few plus a defining clause. \"The little friends he had were loyal\" fails because little is for an amount, not for friends, who are counted."},{"id":"e-articles-29","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"She had only a small sum, and all of it was spent on books. Which sentence is correct?","options":["A little money she had was spent on books","Little money she had was spent on books","The few money she had was spent on books","The little money she had was spent on books"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The little money she had was spent on books\" because the little means the whole of a small amount and is used with an uncountable noun. \"A little money she had was spent on books\" fails because a little does not mean the whole of that small known sum. \"Little money she had was spent on books\" fails because little alone misses the, which marks the whole small amount she had. \"The few money she had was spent on books\" fails because few is for countable nouns, while money is uncountable."},{"id":"e-articles-30","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The pupils in the room can be counted. Which sentence is correct?","options":["How many pupils are present today?","How much pupils are present today?","How many pupils is present today?","How much pupil are present today?"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"How many pupils are present today?\" because how many is used for countable nouns, and the verb agrees with the plural noun. \"How much pupils are present today?\" fails because pupils are countable, so the question word is many, not much. \"How many pupils is present today?\" fails because pupils is plural, so the verb is are, not is. \"How much pupil are present today?\" fails because much does not fit a countable noun, and pupil should be plural after many."},{"id":"e-articles-31","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The letters MLA are spoken with a vowel sound at the start. Which sentence is correct?","options":["He is a MLA from this district","He is an MLA from this district","He is an MLAs from this district","He is a MLAs from this district"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He is an MLA from this district\" because use an before an abbreviation whose spoken form begins with a vowel sound. \"He is a MLA from this district\" fails because MLA begins with the sound em, a vowel sound, so the article is an. \"He is an MLAs from this district\" fails because he is one person, so the noun stays MLA, not MLAs. \"He is a MLAs from this district\" fails because both the article and the plural MLAs are wrong."},{"id":"e-articles-32","topicId":"e-articles","subject":"english","stem":"The same dog is mentioned for the first time and then again. Which sentence is correct?","options":["I saw a dog, and a dog was limping","I saw dog, and the dog was limping","I saw a dog, and the dog was limping","I saw the dog, and a dog was limping"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I saw a dog, and the dog was limping\" because use a for a first mention and the when the same noun is mentioned again. \"I saw a dog, and a dog was limping\" fails because the second mention of that same dog uses the, not another a. \"I saw dog, and the dog was limping\" fails because the first mention of a singular countable noun needs a. \"I saw the dog, and a dog was limping\" fails because an unknown dog is introduced with a, and the later mention of the same dog uses the."},{"id":"e-prepositions-13","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Four cousins received shares of the sweets. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The sweets were shared between the four cousins","The sweets were shared among of the four cousins","The sweets were shared between of the four cousins","The sweets were shared among the four cousins"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The sweets were shared among the four cousins\" because among is used for a group of more than two. \"The sweets were shared between the four cousins\" fails because between is for two, while four people take among. \"The sweets were shared among of the four cousins\" fails because among is not followed by of in this pattern. \"The sweets were shared between of the four cousins\" fails because between of is not a pattern, and four people are not a pair."},{"id":"e-prepositions-14","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"The sentence praises Reema's skill in the subject. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Reema is good at mathematics","Reema is good on mathematics","Reema is good for mathematics","Reema is good into mathematics"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Reema is good at mathematics\" because good at is the fixed preposition pattern for a skill. \"Reema is good on mathematics\" fails because the adjective good in this meaning takes at, not on. \"Reema is good for mathematics\" fails because good for would mean beneficial to the subject, not skilled at it. \"Reema is good into mathematics\" fails because into is not the preposition after good."},{"id":"e-prepositions-15","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Music is the subject that attracts him. Which sentence is correct?","options":["He is interested on music","He is interested in music","He is interested at music","He is interested for music"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He is interested in music\" because interested is followed by the preposition in. \"He is interested on music\" fails because interested takes in, not on. \"He is interested at music\" fails because at is not the preposition after interested. \"He is interested for music\" fails because for does not complete the adjective interested."},{"id":"e-prepositions-16","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Darkness frightens many children. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Many children are afraid from the dark","Many children are afraid by the dark","Many children are afraid of the dark","Many children are afraid off the dark"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Many children are afraid of the dark\" because afraid of is the fixed pattern. \"Many children are afraid from the dark\" fails because afraid takes of, not from. \"Many children are afraid by the dark\" fails because by would suit a passive agent, not the adjective afraid. \"Many children are afraid off the dark\" fails because off is a different word and is not the preposition after afraid."},{"id":"e-prepositions-17","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Mumbai is a large city, and the travellers reached it at dawn. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We arrived in Mumbai at dawn","We arrived at Mumbai at dawn","We arrived to Mumbai at dawn","We arrived on Mumbai at dawn"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We arrived in Mumbai at dawn\" because arrive in is used for countries and large cities. \"We arrived at Mumbai at dawn\" fails because a large city takes arrive in, while arrive at is kept for smaller points such as stations. \"We arrived to Mumbai at dawn\" fails because arrive is not followed by to. \"We arrived on Mumbai at dawn\" fails because on is not the preposition after arrive for a city."},{"id":"e-prepositions-18","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"The station is a point on the journey, not a large city. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We arrived in the station before noon","We arrived at the station before noon","We arrived to the station before noon","We arrived on the station before noon"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We arrived at the station before noon\" because arrive at is used for buildings, stations, and other particular points. \"We arrived in the station before noon\" fails because a station or other small point takes arrive at, not arrive in. \"We arrived to the station before noon\" fails because arrive does not take to. \"We arrived on the station before noon\" fails because on is not the preposition used after arrive for a station."},{"id":"e-prepositions-19","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"The bus is their kind of transport, not one particular vehicle they are sitting on. Which sentence is correct?","options":["They travelled on bus","They travelled by the bus","They travelled by bus","They travelled with bus"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"They travelled by bus\" because by is used with a means of transport such as bus, train, or car when no article is used. \"They travelled on bus\" fails because the means of travel is by bus; on bus leaves out the and means something else. \"They travelled by the bus\" fails because by the bus would point to one particular bus, not the type of transport. \"They travelled with bus\" fails because with is not the preposition for a means of transport."},{"id":"e-prepositions-20","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"They walked, using their feet and no vehicle. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We came to school by foot","We came to school on feet","We came to school by walk","We came to school on foot"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We came to school on foot\" because walking as a means of travel is expressed by the fixed phrase on foot. \"We came to school by foot\" fails because the fixed phrase is on foot, not by foot. \"We came to school on feet\" fails because the idiom uses the singular foot, not feet. \"We came to school by walk\" fails because by walk is not the English phrase for walking."},{"id":"e-prepositions-21","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Rain did not stop the match. The rain is a noun, not a clause. Which sentence is correct?","options":["In spite of it rained, the match continued","In spite of the rain, the match continued","In spite the rain, the match continued","Although of the rain, the match continued"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"In spite of the rain, the match continued\" because in spite of is a preposition and is followed by a noun phrase. \"In spite of it rained, the match continued\" fails because in spite of must be followed by a noun or pronoun, not by a clause such as it rained. \"In spite the rain, the match continued\" fails because of is required: in spite of, not in spite alone. \"Although of the rain, the match continued\" fails because although introduces a clause and is not followed by of the rain."},{"id":"e-prepositions-22","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Both Ravi and Nita attended. Join the two names with the negative pair. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Neither Ravi or Nita was absent","Neither Ravi but Nita was absent","Neither Ravi nor Nita was absent","Either Ravi nor Nita was absent"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Neither Ravi nor Nita was absent\" because neither and nor form a pair, just as either and or form a pair. \"Neither Ravi or Nita was absent\" fails because neither pairs with nor, not with or. \"Neither Ravi but Nita was absent\" fails because but is not the partner of neither. \"Either Ravi nor Nita was absent\" fails because either pairs with or, while nor belongs with neither."},{"id":"e-prepositions-23","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"The listener must choose one of the two actions. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Either take the bus nor walk home","Either take the bus but walk home","Neither take the bus or walk home","Either take the bus or walk home"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Either take the bus or walk home\" because either is always paired with or when it offers a choice. \"Either take the bus nor walk home\" fails because either is completed by or, not by nor. \"Either take the bus but walk home\" fails because but does not complete either. \"Neither take the bus or walk home\" fails because neither would need nor, and this sentence is offering a choice with either."},{"id":"e-prepositions-24","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"The teacher and the pupils are both included. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Both the teacher and the pupils were ready","Both the teacher and the pupils was ready","Both the teacher or the pupils were ready","Both the teacher nor the pupils were ready"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Both the teacher and the pupils were ready\" because both...and links two subjects, and the verb that follows is plural. \"Both the teacher and the pupils was ready\" fails because both...and joins two subjects and takes a plural verb, so were is required. \"Both the teacher or the pupils were ready\" fails because both is paired with and, not with or. \"Both the teacher nor the pupils were ready\" fails because nor belongs with neither, not with both."},{"id":"e-prepositions-25","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"She has two good qualities, and both are being stressed. Which sentence is correct?","options":["She is not only kind and also brave","She is not only kind or also brave","She is not only kind but also brave","She is both only kind but also brave"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She is not only kind but also brave\" because not only and but also form a correlative pair. \"She is not only kind and also brave\" fails because not only is completed by but also, not by and also. \"She is not only kind or also brave\" fails because or does not complete the pair not only. \"She is both only kind but also brave\" fails because both only is not the partner of but also; the pair is not only...but also."},{"id":"e-prepositions-26","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"The temple is next to the lake, not merely an extra item. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The temple stands besides the lake","The temple stands beside of the lake","The temple stands besides of the lake","The temple stands beside the lake"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The temple stands beside the lake\" because beside means next to, without of after it. \"The temple stands besides the lake\" fails because besides means in addition to, while next to is beside. \"The temple stands beside of the lake\" fails because beside is not followed by of. \"The temple stands besides of the lake\" fails because besides of is not a pattern, and the meaning needed is next to."},{"id":"e-prepositions-27","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Milk is not the only thing the shop sells. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Besides milk, the shop sells bread","Beside milk, the shop sells bread","Besides of milk, the shop sells bread","Beside of milk, the shop sells bread"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Besides milk, the shop sells bread\" because besides means in addition to and is not followed by of. \"Beside milk, the shop sells bread\" fails because beside means next to, while in addition to is besides. \"Besides of milk, the shop sells bread\" fails because besides is not followed by of. \"Beside of milk, the shop sells bread\" fails because beside of is not English, and the sense here is in addition."},{"id":"e-prepositions-28","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Grandmother takes care of the baby. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Grandmother looks for the baby","Grandmother looks after the baby","Grandmother looks after to the baby","Grandmother looks on the baby"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Grandmother looks after the baby\" because look after means to take care of someone. \"Grandmother looks for the baby\" fails because looks for means she is searching, not that she is taking care. \"Grandmother looks after to the baby\" fails because after is not followed by to in the phrase look after. \"Grandmother looks on the baby\" fails because looks on does not mean takes care of."},{"id":"e-prepositions-29","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"They stood until the bus arrived. They were not already riding in it. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We waited on the bus","We waited to the bus","We waited from the bus","We waited for the bus"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We waited for the bus\" because wait for is the pattern when someone expects a person or a vehicle. \"We waited on the bus\" fails because on the bus would mean the waiting happened inside the bus, but they were waiting for it to arrive. \"We waited to the bus\" fails because wait is not followed by to for the thing expected. \"We waited from the bus\" fails because from does not complete the verb wait in this meaning."},{"id":"e-prepositions-30","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker shares a person's opinion. Which sentence is correct?","options":["I agree with my partner","I agree to my partner","I agree on my partner","I agree into my partner"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I agree with my partner\" because agree with is used before a person. \"I agree to my partner\" fails because agree to is used for a plan or proposal, while a person takes agree with. \"I agree on my partner\" fails because agree on is for a shared topic, not for the person in this sentence. \"I agree into my partner\" fails because into is not a preposition after agree."},{"id":"e-prepositions-31","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"A fever was the illness that caused the calf's death. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The calf died by a fever","The calf died of a fever","The calf died for a fever","The calf died with a fever"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The calf died of a fever\" because die of is used before the name of a disease. \"The calf died by a fever\" fails because by is not the preposition for dying from a disease. \"The calf died for a fever\" fails because for would suggest a purpose or exchange, not the illness. \"The calf died with a fever\" fails because with would mean accompanied by a fever, not that the fever was the cause in this pattern."},{"id":"e-prepositions-32","topicId":"e-prepositions","subject":"english","stem":"Saving the money had a purpose: buying a book. Which sentence is correct?","options":["She saved her pocket money so as she could buy a book","She saved her pocket money because she could buy a book","She saved her pocket money so that she could buy a book","She saved her pocket money although she could buy a book"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She saved her pocket money so that she could buy a book\" because so that plus a clause with can, could, or would expresses purpose. \"She saved her pocket money so as she could buy a book\" fails because so as must be followed by to plus a verb, not by a clause with could. \"She saved her pocket money because she could buy a book\" fails because because gives a reason looking backward, but the stem asks for a purpose. \"She saved her pocket money although she could buy a book\" fails because although shows contrast, not the purpose of the saving."},{"id":"h-verbs-21","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«मुझसे चला नहीं जाता» कौन-सा वाच्य है?","options":["भाववाच्य","कर्तृवाच्य","कर्मवाच्य","पूर्वकालिक रूप"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is भाववाच्य because चलना has no object, the doer is marked by से, and the verb stays impersonal. That is भाववाच्य. कर्तृवाच्य is wrong because कर्तृवाच्य would be मैं नहीं चल पाता or मैं चलता हूँ, with the doer as a normal subject. कर्मवाच्य is wrong because कर्मवाच्य needs an object to become the focus, and चला has no object. पूर्वकालिक रूप is wrong because पूर्वकालिक रूप would be चलकर before another verb, and चला नहीं जाता is the whole impersonal verb."},{"id":"h-verbs-22","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«लड़की गीत गाती है» का सही कर्मवाच्य कौन-सा है?","options":["लड़की गीत गाती है","लड़की से गीत गाया जाता है","लड़की से हँसा जाता है","गीत लड़की को गाती है"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is लड़की से गीत गाया जाता है because in कर्मवाच्य the doer takes से, the object गीत stays, and the masculine गीत takes गाया जाता है. लड़की गीत गाती है is wrong because लड़की गीत गाती है is still कर्तृवाच्य, the original active sentence. लड़की से हँसा जाता है is wrong because लड़की से हँसा जाता है changes the verb to हँसना and drops गीत, so it is not the passive of this sentence. गीत लड़की को गाती है is wrong because गीत लड़की को गाती है is not a grammatical voice change; the verb agreement and the को are both wrong."},{"id":"h-verbs-23","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"«बच्चे हँसते हैं» का सही भाववाच्य कौन-सा है?","options":["बच्चे से हँसते हैं","बच्चों को हँसाया जाता है","बच्चों से हँसा जाता है","बच्चों ने हँस किया"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is बच्चों से हँसा जाता है because the intransitive verb becomes impersonal: the doers take से and the verb is masculine singular हँसा जाता है. बच्चे से हँसते हैं is wrong because बच्चे से हँसते हैं keeps the plural verb and uses the wrong subject form, so it is not भाववाच्य. बच्चों को हँसाया जाता है is wrong because बच्चों को हँसाया जाता है is causative: it means they are made to laugh, not the भाववाच्य of हँसना. बच्चों ने हँस किया is wrong because बच्चों ने हँस किया is not a real Hindi verb phrase."},{"id":"h-verbs-24","topicId":"h-verbs","subject":"hindi","stem":"भाववाच्य में क्रिया सामान्यतः किस रूप में रहती है?","options":["स्त्रीलिंग बहुवचन में","सदा कर्ता के लिंग में","सदा भविष्यत् काल में","पुल्लिंग एकवचन में"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is पुल्लिंग एकवचन में because in भाववाच्य the verb does not follow a subject or an object, so it stays masculine singular, as in हँसा जाता है. स्त्रीलिंग बहुवचन में is wrong because स्त्रीलिंग बहुवचन में would follow a feminine plural noun, and भाववाच्य does not do that. सदा कर्ता के लिंग में is wrong because सदा कर्ता के लिंग में describes कर्तृवाच्य, where the verb agrees with the doer. सदा भविष्यत् काल में is wrong because सदा भविष्यत् काल में is wrong because भाववाच्य can be past or present; the fixed point is gender and number, not tense."},{"id":"h-case-13","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"«धीरे चलो» में «धीरे» क्या है?","options":["क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय","संबंधबोधक अव्यय","समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय","भाववाचक संज्ञा"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय because धीरे tells how the action of walking is done, and it does not change its form, so it is an adverb. संबंधबोधक अव्यय is wrong because a संबंधबोधक अव्यय would link a noun, such as के साथ, and धीरे does not follow a noun. समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय is wrong because a समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय would join words or clauses, such as और, and धीरे does not join anything. भाववाचक संज्ञा is wrong because a भाववाचक संज्ञा would name a quality as a noun, such as धीरज, and धीरे modifies the verb."},{"id":"h-case-14","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"«राम और श्याम खेलते हैं» में «और» क्या है?","options":["क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय","समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय","विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय","गुणवाचक विशेषण"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय because और joins the two names राम and श्याम, so it is a conjunction. क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय is wrong because a क्रियाविशेषण would describe the manner of खेलते हैं, and और does not tell how they play. विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय is wrong because a विस्मयादिबोधक would show a sudden feeling, such as वाह, and और is not an exclamation. गुणवाचक विशेषण is wrong because a गुणवाचक विशेषण would describe a noun, and और does not describe राम or श्याम."},{"id":"h-case-15","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"«वाह! तुमने अच्छा गाया» में «वाह» क्या है?","options":["समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय","संबंधबोधक अव्यय","विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय","सकर्मक क्रिया"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय because वाह shows a sudden feeling of praise, so it is an exclamatory indeclinable. समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय is wrong because a समुच्चयबोधक would join clauses, and वाह does not join anything. संबंधबोधक अव्यय is wrong because a संबंधबोधक would come after a noun to show relation, and वाह stands alone as a cry. सकर्मक क्रिया is wrong because a सकर्मक क्रिया would have an object, and वाह is not a verb at all."},{"id":"h-case-16","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"«पेड़ के नीचे छाया है» में «के नीचे» क्या है?","options":["क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय","विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय","कर्म कारक का चिह्न","संबंधबोधक अव्यय"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is संबंधबोधक अव्यय because के नीचे comes after पेड़ and shows the relation of the shade to the tree, so it is a postpositional indeclinable. क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय is wrong because नीचे alone can be an adverb, but the phrase के नीचे after a noun is संबंधबोधक. विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय is wrong because a विस्मयादिबोधक would be a cry such as अरे, and के नीचे is not an exclamation. कर्म कारक का चिह्न is wrong because कर्म कारक uses को for an object, and के नीचे does not mark an object."},{"id":"h-case-17","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"जो शब्द लिंग, वचन और कारक से नहीं बदलते, उन्हें क्या कहते हैं?","options":["अव्यय","संज्ञा","विशेषण","सर्वनाम"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is अव्यय because अव्यय is the name for words that keep one form and do not change with gender, number, or case. संज्ञा is wrong because a संज्ञा often changes in plural and with postpositions, such as लड़का and लड़के ने. विशेषण is wrong because a विशेषण can change, such as काला, काली, and काले, so it is not fixed in form. सर्वनाम is wrong because a सर्वनाम changes, such as मैं, मुझे, and मेरा, so it is not an indeclinable."},{"id":"h-case-18","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"«यद्यपि वह थका था तथापि वह दौड़ा» में «यद्यपि» क्या है?","options":["क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय","समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय","विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय","संबोधन का चिह्न"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is समुच्चयबोधक अव्यय because यद्यपि joins the two clauses in an although pattern, together with तथापि, so it is a conjunction. क्रियाविशेषण अव्यय is wrong because a क्रियाविशेषण would tell how he ran, and यद्यपि does not describe the manner of दौड़ा. विस्मयादिबोधक अव्यय is wrong because a विस्मयादिबोधक would show a burst of feeling, and यद्यपि is a linking word. संबोधन का चिह्न is wrong because संबोधन का चिह्न would be हे used to call someone, and यद्यपि does not call anyone."},{"id":"h-case-19","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"हिंदी के कथन के अंत में लगने वाले «।» का क्या नाम है?","options":["अल्प विराम","अर्ध विराम","पूर्ण विराम","प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is पूर्ण विराम because the upright stroke । ends a Hindi statement, and its name is पूर्ण विराम. अल्प विराम is wrong because अल्प विराम is the comma, used for a short pause inside the sentence. अर्ध विराम is wrong because अर्ध विराम is the semicolon, a pause stronger than a comma but not the end of a Hindi statement. प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न is wrong because a प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न is the question mark, used when the sentence asks something."},{"id":"h-case-20","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"प्रश्न वाले वाक्य के अंत में कौन-सा चिह्न लगता है?","options":["पूर्ण विराम","विस्मयादिबोधक चिह्न","योजक चिह्न","प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न because a question closes with the question mark, called प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न. पूर्ण विराम is wrong because पूर्ण विराम closes an ordinary statement, not a question. विस्मयादिबोधक चिह्न is wrong because a विस्मयादिबोधक चिह्न closes an exclamation of feeling, not a question. योजक चिह्न is wrong because a योजक चिह्न is the hyphen that joins words, and it does not end a question."},{"id":"h-case-21","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"वाक्य के अंदर छोटे ठहराव वाला «,» क्या कहलाता है?","options":["अल्प विराम","पूर्ण विराम","अर्ध विराम","उद्धरण चिह्न"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is अल्प विराम because the comma marks a short pause inside a sentence, and that mark is अल्प विराम. पूर्ण विराम is wrong because पूर्ण विराम is the full stop । at the end of a statement. अर्ध विराम is wrong because अर्ध विराम is the semicolon, a longer pause than the comma. उद्धरण चिह्न is wrong because उद्धरण चिह्न are quotation marks used to show someone's exact words."},{"id":"h-case-22","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"किसी के ठीक शब्द दिखाने के लिए कौन-सा चिह्न लगता है?","options":["योजक चिह्न","उद्धरण चिह्न","अर्ध विराम","कोष्ठक चिह्न"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is उद्धरण चिह्न because quotation marks show words exactly as someone said or wrote them, and those marks are उद्धरण चिह्न. योजक चिह्न is wrong because a योजक चिह्न is a hyphen that joins two words, and it does not quote speech. अर्ध विराम is wrong because अर्ध विराम is a semicolon used as a pause, not as a quotation. कोष्ठक चिह्न is wrong because कोष्ठक चिह्न are brackets used to add an extra note, not to quote exact words."},{"id":"h-case-23","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"दो शब्दों को जोड़ने वाली छोटी रेखा का क्या नाम है?","options":["पूर्ण विराम","प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न","योजक चिह्न","अल्प विराम"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is योजक चिह्न because the short joining line is a hyphen, and Hindi grammar calls it योजक चिह्न. पूर्ण विराम is wrong because पूर्ण विराम ends a statement and is a vertical stroke, not a joining line. प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न is wrong because a प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न ends a question and does not join two words. अल्प विराम is wrong because अल्प विराम is a comma for a pause, not a line that joins words."},{"id":"h-case-24","topicId":"h-case","subject":"hindi","stem":"«;» चिह्न का व्याकरण में क्या नाम है?","options":["पूर्ण विराम","अल्प विराम","विस्मयादिबोधक चिह्न","अर्ध विराम"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is अर्ध विराम because the semicolon is called अर्ध विराम, a pause between a comma and a full stop. पूर्ण विराम is wrong because पूर्ण विराम is the Hindi full stop ।, not the semicolon. अल्प विराम is wrong because अल्प विराम is the comma, which is a lighter pause than the semicolon. विस्मयादिबोधक चिह्न is wrong because a विस्मयादिबोधक चिह्न is the exclamation mark, used for strong feeling."},{"id":"h-samas-13","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«माता-पिता» में कौन-सा समास है?","options":["द्वंद्व","तत्पुरुष","कर्मधारय","बहुव्रीहि"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is द्वंद्व because माता and पिता are equal partners joined by and, so the compound is द्वंद्व. तत्पुरुष is wrong because तत्पुरुष would make the second word the only head, and here both parents are equally meant. कर्मधारय is wrong because कर्मधारय would need an adjective describing one noun, and माता is not an adjective of पिता. बहुव्रीहि is wrong because बहुव्रीहि would point to someone other than the two words, and माता-पिता means the parents themselves."},{"id":"h-samas-14","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«दशानन» जब रावण का बोध कराए, तो कौन-सा समास है?","options":["द्वंद्व","बहुव्रीहि","कर्मधारय","तत्पुरुष"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is बहुव्रीहि because दशानन means the one who has ten faces, namely रावण, so neither word is the final meaning. That is बहुव्रीहि. द्वंद्व is wrong because द्वंद्व would mean ten and face as two equal items, and the compound points to a person. कर्मधारय is wrong because कर्मधारय would mean a face that is ten, as if the face itself were the whole meaning. तत्पुरुष is wrong because तत्पुरुष would mean something like the face of ten, with face as the main object, not रावण."},{"id":"h-samas-15","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«नीलकंठ» जब शिव का बोध कराए, तो कौन-सा समास है?","options":["कर्मधारय","द्वंद्व","बहुव्रीहि","अव्ययीभाव"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is बहुव्रीहि because here नीलकंठ means the one whose throat is blue, namely शिव, so it points outside the two words and is बहुव्रीहि. कर्मधारय is wrong because कर्मधारय would mean the throat itself is blue, naming the throat, not शिव. द्वंद्व is wrong because द्वंद्व would join नील and कंठ as equals, and this compound names a person. अव्ययीभाव is wrong because अव्ययीभाव would begin with an indeclinable such as प्रति or यथा, and नीलकंठ does not."},{"id":"h-samas-16","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«देशभक्ति» में कौन-सा समास है?","options":["कर्मधारय","द्वंद्व","बहुव्रीहि","तत्पुरुष"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is तत्पुरुष because देशभक्ति means देश की भक्ति. भक्ति is the main word and की shows the case link, so it is तत्पुरुष. कर्मधारय is wrong because कर्मधारय would need देश to be an adjective describing भक्ति, and देश is a noun in a case relation. द्वंद्व is wrong because द्वंद्व would mean country and devotion as two equal things, and the compound means devotion. बहुव्रीहि is wrong because बहुव्रीहि would name some other person, and देशभक्ति means the devotion itself."},{"id":"t-agriculture-19","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Shifting cultivation becomes more harmful when","options":["the farmer never cuts any tree","the same plot is left unused for a very long recovery","the fallow period becomes too short for the forest to recover","no fire is ever used and the forest is untouched"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is the fallow period becomes too short for the forest to recover because if people return before the vegetation and soil recover, the forest and the land degrade. the farmer never cuts any tree is wrong because never cutting a tree is not shifting cultivation. the same plot is left unused for a very long recovery is wrong because a long recovery is the older pattern that did less harm. no fire is ever used and the forest is untouched is wrong because an untouched forest is not this farming method.\nयाद रखो: झूम तब ज़्यादा नुकसान करती है जब परती समय इतना छोटा हो कि जंगल संभल न पाए।\nगलत मत याद करना: the same plot is left unused for a very long recovery लम्बा आराम जंगल को संभलने देता है।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-20","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Commercial grain farming is associated with","options":["a one-hectare family plot worked only with hand tools for home rice","nomads crossing a desert with camels","picking tea leaves by hand on a hill estate","large farms, machines, and crops such as wheat in temperate grasslands"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is large farms, machines, and crops such as wheat in temperate grasslands because temperate grasslands support big wheat or maize farms that use machinery. a one-hectare family plot worked only with hand tools for home rice is wrong because a tiny family rice plot is intensive subsistence. nomads crossing a desert with camels is wrong because camel nomads are herders, not grain farmers. picking tea leaves by hand on a hill estate is wrong because hand-picked tea is plantation agriculture.\nयाद रखो: वाणिज्यिक अनाज खेती: बड़े खेत, मशीनें, शीतोष्ण घास के मैदानों में गेहूँ जैसी फसल।\nगलत मत याद करना: a one-hectare family plot worked only with hand tools for home rice छोटा घर का चावल यह नहीं।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-21","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Jute grows especially well in","options":["the alluvial lands of the Ganga-Brahmaputra delta","the snowfields of the high Himalaya","the polar tundra","a rainless rocky plateau with no rivers"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is the alluvial lands of the Ganga-Brahmaputra delta because jute wants alluvial soil, high temperature, and heavy rain, which the delta region provides. the snowfields of the high Himalaya is wrong because snowfields are too cold. the polar tundra is wrong because the tundra is too cold and dry for jute. a rainless rocky plateau with no rivers is wrong because a rainless plateau cannot meet jute's need for heavy rainfall.\nयाद रखो: जूट गंगा-ब्रह्मपुत्र डेल्टा की जलोढ़ ज़मीन में खास अच्छा उगता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: the snowfields of the high Himalaya ऊँची बर्फ जूट का खेत नहीं।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-22","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Which of these is a fibre crop?","options":["Rice","Jute","Wheat","Maize"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is Jute because jute is grown for its fibre, the golden fibre. Rice is wrong because rice is a food grain. Wheat is wrong because wheat is a food grain. Maize is wrong because maize is a food grain.\nयाद रखो: जूट रेशा फसल है। चावल, गेहूँ और मक्का अनाज हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Rice चावल रेशा नहीं, अनाज है।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-23","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Tea plantations need a large number of workers mainly because","options":["the bushes are harvested by one person with a single machine in an hour","tea grows without any human care","the tender leaves are picked by hand","the crop is gathered from the ocean"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is the tender leaves are picked by hand because plucking the right leaves is careful hand work, so tea is labour intensive. the bushes are harvested by one person with a single machine in an hour is wrong because tea is not harvested in one hour by one machine in the textbook account. tea grows without any human care is wrong because plantations need labour for plucking and processing. the crop is gathered from the ocean is wrong because tea is a land crop, not an ocean crop.\nयाद रखो: चाय के कोमल पत्ते हाथ से तोड़े जाते हैं, इसलिए बागान में बहुत मज़दूर लगते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the bushes are harvested by one person with a single machine in an hour एक घंटे में एक मशीन पूरा बागान नहीं तोड़ती।"},{"id":"t-agriculture-24","topicId":"t-agriculture","subject":"sst","stem":"Primitive subsistence farming includes","options":["only large wheat estates in the prairies","only information-technology offices","only iron and steel plants","shifting cultivation and nomadic herding"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is shifting cultivation and nomadic herding because the simple, older subsistence forms in this chapter are shifting cultivation and nomadic herding. only large wheat estates in the prairies is wrong because prairie wheat estates are commercial grain farms. only information-technology offices is wrong because offices are not farming. only iron and steel plants is wrong because steel plants are industries.\nयाद रखो: आदिकालीन निर्वाह में झूम और चलवासी पशुचारण आते हैं। प्रेयरी के बड़े गेहूँ खेत नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: only large wheat estates in the prairies प्रेयरी के बड़े खेत वाणिज्यिक अनाज खेती हैं।"},{"id":"t-industries-13","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"TISCO was set up at Jamshedpur in","options":["1907","1757","1857","1947"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is 1907 because the Tata iron and steel works began at Sakchi, now Jamshedpur, in 1907. 1757 is wrong because 1757 is the year of the Battle of Plassey, not of this steel plant. 1857 is wrong because 1857 is the year of the great revolt, not of TISCO. 1947 is wrong because 1947 is the year of Independence, long after the plant had started.\nयाद रखो: टिस्को जमशेदपुर में 1907 में बनी। 1757 प्लासी है, 1857 विद्रोह, 1947 आज़ादी।\nगलत मत याद करना: 1757 1757 प्लासी का साल है, जमशेदपुर के कारखाने का नहीं।"},{"id":"t-industries-14","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"The main mineral inputs of an iron and steel plant are","options":["raw cotton, silk, and jute","iron ore, coal, and limestone","tea, coffee, and cocoa","sea fish, pearls, and seaweed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is iron ore, coal, and limestone because steel-making needs iron ore, coal for fuel, and limestone as a flux. raw cotton, silk, and jute is wrong because cotton, silk, and jute are fibres for textile mills. tea, coffee, and cocoa is wrong because tea, coffee, and cocoa are plantation crops, not steel inputs. sea fish, pearls, and seaweed is wrong because fish and other sea products feed marine-based industries.\nयाद रखो: इस्पात की भट्ठी के तीन खनिज मेहमान: लौह अयस्क, कोयला और चूना पत्थर।\nगलत मत याद करना: raw cotton, silk, and jute कपास, रेशम और जूट कपड़े के हैं, भट्ठी के नहीं।"},{"id":"t-industries-15","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Jamshedpur suited a steel plant mainly because","options":["it lay in a cold desert with no minerals and no river","it had no railway and no source of water","iron ore, coal, other minerals, water, and a railway were available nearby","it was chosen only because tea grew on snowy peaks there"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is iron ore, coal, other minerals, water, and a railway were available nearby because Sakchi was near coal, iron ore, and other minerals, with water from the Subarnarekha and Kharkai rivers and a rail link. it lay in a cold desert with no minerals and no river is wrong because a cold desert without minerals could not feed a steel plant. it had no railway and no source of water is wrong because the site was chosen because water and rail were present, not absent. it was chosen only because tea grew on snowy peaks there is wrong because tea gardens were not the reason for a steel city.\nयाद रखो: जमशेदपुर के पास लौह अयस्क, कोयला, दूसरे खनिज, पानी और रेल थी।\nगलत मत याद करना: it lay in a cold desert with no minerals and no river बिना खनिज ठंडा रेगिस्तान यह जगह नहीं।"},{"id":"t-industries-16","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Pittsburgh is known in this chapter as","options":["the earlier name of Jamshedpur","a cotton-textile city in Japan","a centre of shifting cultivation","an important steel centre in the United States"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is an important steel centre in the United States because Pittsburgh grew as a steel city, with coal nearby and iron ore brought in by the Great Lakes route. the earlier name of Jamshedpur is wrong because Jamshedpur was earlier called Sakchi, not Pittsburgh. a cotton-textile city in Japan is wrong because Osaka, not Pittsburgh, is the Japanese cotton city in this chapter. a centre of shifting cultivation is wrong because shifting cultivation is a kind of farming, not a steel city.\nयाद रखो: पिट्सबर्ग इस अध्याय में अमेरिका का बड़ा इस्पात केंद्र है। जमशेदपुर का पुराना नाम नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the earlier name of Jamshedpur जमशेदपुर की पुरानी साकची है, पिट्सबर्ग नहीं।"},{"id":"t-industries-17","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Ahmedabad became a major centre of","options":["the cotton textile industry","deep-sea fishing as its only work","iron-ore mining in Minnesota","information technology in the year 1600"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is the cotton textile industry because Ahmedabad, on the Sabarmati and close to cotton-growing areas, grew into a great cotton-mill city. deep-sea fishing as its only work is wrong because its fame in this chapter is cloth, not ocean fishing. iron-ore mining in Minnesota is wrong because Minnesota supplied iron ore towards Pittsburgh, and it is not Ahmedabad. information technology in the year 1600 is wrong because information technology is a modern industry, and 1600 is the century of the Company's charter.\nयाद रखो: अहमदाबाद सूती वस्त्र उद्योग का बड़ा केंद्र बना। 1600 की सूचना तकनीक नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: information technology in the year 1600 1600 में अहमदाबाद आईटी शहर नहीं था।"},{"id":"t-industries-18","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Osaka came to be called the Manchester of Japan because of its","options":["gold mines in the Thar Desert","cotton textile industry","polar ice sheets","ban on all cloth making"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is cotton textile industry because Osaka's cotton mills were so important that it was nicknamed the Manchester of Japan. gold mines in the Thar Desert is wrong because the Thar Desert is in India and is not a Japanese textile city. polar ice sheets is wrong because polar ice has no link with Osaka's mills. ban on all cloth making is wrong because Osaka made cloth. It did not ban cloth making.\nयाद रखो: ओसाका को जापान का मैनचेस्टर सूती वस्त्र उद्योग की वजह से कहते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: gold mines in the Thar Desert थार की सोने की खदानें ओसाका नहीं।"},{"id":"t-industries-19","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Bengaluru is a leading Indian centre of","options":["the Tata steel plant started in 1907","marine fishing as its only industry","the information technology industry","the Doctrine of Lapse"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is the information technology industry because Bengaluru, often called the Silicon Valley of India, grew with skilled workers and electronic links rather than heavy ore. the Tata steel plant started in 1907 is wrong because the 1907 Tata steel plant is at Jamshedpur, not Bengaluru. marine fishing as its only industry is wrong because Bengaluru is not a city whose only work is sea fishing. the Doctrine of Lapse is wrong because the Doctrine of Lapse was a Company policy of annexation, not an industry of Bengaluru.\nयाद रखो: बेंगलुरु भारत का बड़ा सूचना तकनीक केंद्र है। 1907 का टाटा इस्पात जमशेदपुर का है।\nगलत मत याद करना: the Tata steel plant started in 1907 टाटा इस्पात 1907 में जमशेदपुर में शुरू हुआ।"},{"id":"t-industries-20","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Silicon Valley, a famous information-technology region, is in","options":["the Thar Desert","the high Himalaya","Antarctica","California in the United States"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is California in the United States because Silicon Valley is in California. Bengaluru is often compared with it. the Thar Desert is wrong because the Thar is a hot desert, not this technology region. the high Himalaya is wrong because the high Himalaya is not Silicon Valley. Antarctica is wrong because Antarctica has no such industrial region.\nयाद रखो: सिलिकॉन वैली अमेरिका के कैलिफोर्निया में है। थार या अंटार्कटिका में नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the Thar Desert थार रेगिस्तान सिलिकॉन वैली नहीं।"},{"id":"t-industries-21","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"The Bhopal gas tragedy of 1984 involved a leak of","options":["methyl isocyanate from a pesticide factory","steam from a household kettle","oxygen given out by trees in a park","clean drinking water from a municipal tap"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is methyl isocyanate from a pesticide factory because in December 1984 methyl isocyanate gas leaked from the Union Carbide pesticide plant at Bhopal and killed and injured many people. steam from a household kettle is wrong because steam from a kettle is not the poisonous gas of that disaster. oxygen given out by trees in a park is wrong because oxygen from trees is not a toxic industrial leak. clean drinking water from a municipal tap is wrong because drinking water was not the substance that escaped.\nयाद रखो: भोपाल 1984 में कीटनाशक कारखाने से मिथाइल आइसोसाइनेट गैस रिस गई।\nगलत मत याद करना: steam from a household kettle घर की केतली की भाप यह त्रासदी नहीं।"},{"id":"t-industries-22","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Careless industry can pollute","options":["nothing at all, because smoke and waste disappear harmlessly","land, air, and water around the factory","only the surface of the Moon","only fossils on another continent"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is land, air, and water around the factory because smoke, chemical waste, and dumping harm the air, the water, and the land nearby. nothing at all, because smoke and waste disappear harmlessly is wrong because waste does not vanish. It pollutes. only the surface of the Moon is wrong because factory pollution acts on the Earth around the plant, not on the Moon. only fossils on another continent is wrong because fossils on another continent are not the victim of a local factory's waste.\nयाद रखो: लापरवाह उद्योग आसपास की ज़मीन, हवा और पानी को गंदा कर सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: nothing at all, because smoke and waste disappear harmlessly धुआँ और कचरा अपने आप गायब नहीं होते।"},{"id":"t-industries-23","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"Iron and steel is called a feeder industry because","options":["it feeds cattle inside the blast furnace","it grows food grains for the workers","its products become raw material for many other industries","it has no link with any other factory"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is its products become raw material for many other industries because machines, buildings, vehicles, and tools need steel, so this industry feeds other industries. it feeds cattle inside the blast furnace is wrong because a blast furnace smelts metal. It does not feed cattle. it grows food grains for the workers is wrong because steel plants do not grow grain. it has no link with any other factory is wrong because the whole point of a feeder industry is its link with other factories.\nयाद रखो: लोहा-इस्पात पोषक उद्योग है क्योंकि उसकी चीज़ें कई और उद्योगों का कच्चा माल बनती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: it feeds cattle inside the blast furnace भट्ठी में गाय नहीं पाली जाती।"},{"id":"t-industries-24","topicId":"t-industries","subject":"sst","stem":"The Chotanagpur plateau became an important industrial region largely because","options":["it is a polar ice cap","it has no minerals and no transport","it lies on the deep floor of the Pacific Ocean","it is rich in minerals such as coal and iron ore"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is it is rich in minerals such as coal and iron ore because coal, iron ore, and other minerals drew mines and factories to this plateau. it is a polar ice cap is wrong because the plateau is in eastern India, not in the polar regions. it has no minerals and no transport is wrong because minerals and transport are present there. Their absence is not the story. it lies on the deep floor of the Pacific Ocean is wrong because it is land in India, not the ocean floor.\nयाद रखो: छोटानागपुर पठार कोयला और लौह अयस्क जैसे खनिजों से समृद्ध है, इसलिए उद्योग बढ़ा।\nगलत मत याद करना: it is a polar ice cap छोटानागपुर ध्रुवीय बर्फ की टोपी नहीं।"},{"id":"t-population-13","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"Fresh water draws settlement because","options":["people need it for drinking, farming, and daily life","deserts are crowded because they lack water","river valleys are always empty","water makes farming impossible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is people need it for drinking, farming, and daily life because towns and villages cluster where drinking and irrigation water can be had. deserts are crowded because they lack water is wrong because lack of water is why deserts are sparse, not crowded. river valleys are always empty is wrong because many river valleys are among the most crowded places. water makes farming impossible is wrong because water makes farming possible.\nयाद रखो: मीठा पानी पीने, खेती और रोज़मर्रा के लिए चाहिए, इसलिए बसावट खिंचती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: deserts are crowded because they lack water पानी की कमी रेगिस्तान को भीड़ नहीं बनाती।"},{"id":"t-population-14","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"Mineral wealth can increase population because","options":["minerals force every person to leave","mines and oilfields create work and draw workers","a mining area can never grow into a town","minerals remove the need for any workers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is mines and oilfields create work and draw workers because people move to places where coal, oil, or other minerals provide jobs. minerals force every person to leave is wrong because minerals attract workers. They do not empty the land by themselves. a mining area can never grow into a town is wrong because mining towns are common around large deposits. minerals remove the need for any workers is wrong because mines need workers. They do not end the need for labour.\nयाद रखो: खदानें और तेल क्षेत्र काम बनाते हैं और मज़दूरों को खींचते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: minerals force every person to leave खनिज हर आदमी को भगाते नहीं।"},{"id":"t-population-15","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"Which of these is a social or historical reason for people to stay in a place?","options":["No one has ever lived there","All houses and roads are forbidden","It has long been a centre of culture, religion, or settled life","It has no past and no community life"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is It has long been a centre of culture, religion, or settled life because places such as Varanasi remain crowded because of a long religious and cultural history, and old settled regions often stay populated. No one has ever lived there is wrong because an empty past does not explain a crowd. All houses and roads are forbidden is wrong because a ban on houses and roads would drive people away. It has no past and no community life is wrong because community life and history are exactly what this factor includes.\nयाद रखो: लंबे समय से संस्कृति, धर्म या बसी ज़िंदगी का केंद्र होना लोगों को वहीं रोके रखता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: No one has ever lived there जहाँ कभी कोई न रहा, वह ऐतिहासिक वजह नहीं।"},{"id":"t-population-16","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"An economic reason for a dense population is that","options":["there is a total absence of work","every factory and every shop is forbidden","people wish to live where nobody is employed","industry and other jobs draw people to cities"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is industry and other jobs draw people to cities because cities such as Mumbai and Osaka grew large because factories and services offered work. there is a total absence of work is wrong because absence of work pushes people away. every factory and every shop is forbidden is wrong because forbidding shops and factories would remove the economic pull. people wish to live where nobody is employed is wrong because people move towards employment, not towards a place with no jobs.\nयाद रखो: उद्योग और दूसरे काम लोगों को शहरों की तरफ खींचते हैं। काम का न होना वजह नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: there is a total absence of work काम का पूरा अभाव भीड़ नहीं लाता।"},{"id":"t-population-17","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"The number of people in a region changes through","options":["births, deaths, and migration","only the renaming of a river","the colour of the national flag","the number of longitudes drawn on a map"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is births, deaths, and migration because babies add people, deaths remove them, and migration moves them in or out. only the renaming of a river is wrong because a new river name does not change how many people live there. the colour of the national flag is wrong because a flag's colour is not a population process. the number of longitudes drawn on a map is wrong because lines of longitude are a map grid, not a cause of population change.\nयाद रखो: इलाके की जनसंख्या जन्म, मृत्यु और प्रवास से बदलती है। झंडे का रंग नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the colour of the national flag झंडा लोगों की गिनती नहीं बदलता।"},{"id":"t-population-18","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"The birth rate is","options":["the number of deaths per 1,000 people in a year","the number of live births per 1,000 people in a year","the number of people leaving a country","the area of a country in square kilometres"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is the number of live births per 1,000 people in a year because birth rate counts live births against each thousand of the population in one year. the number of deaths per 1,000 people in a year is wrong because deaths per thousand are the death rate, not the birth rate. the number of people leaving a country is wrong because people leaving are emigrants, which is migration, not the birth rate. the area of a country in square kilometres is wrong because area is used for density, not for the birth rate.\nयाद रखो: जन्म दर: एक साल में प्रति 1,000 लोगों पर जीवित जन्म। मृत्यु दर इसका उल्टा जुड़वाँ है।\nगलत मत याद करना: the number of deaths per 1,000 people in a year यह मृत्यु दर है, जन्म दर नहीं।"},{"id":"t-population-19","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"The death rate is","options":["the number of live births per 1,000 people in a year","the number of schools in a district","the number of deaths per 1,000 people in a year","the length of the coastline"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is the number of deaths per 1,000 people in a year because death rate counts deaths against each thousand people in one year. the number of live births per 1,000 people in a year is wrong because live births per thousand are the birth rate. the number of schools in a district is wrong because a count of schools is not the death rate. the length of the coastline is wrong because coastline length is a geographic measure, not a population rate.\nयाद रखो: मृत्यु दर: एक साल में प्रति 1,000 लोगों पर मौतें। जन्म दर जीवित बच्चों की है।\nगलत मत याद करना: the number of live births per 1,000 people in a year यह जन्म दर है, मृत्यु दर नहीं।"},{"id":"t-population-20","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"The natural growth rate of population is","options":["the death rate minus the area of the country","only the number of people who migrate","the number of factories added to the number of rivers","the birth rate minus the death rate"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is the birth rate minus the death rate because when births are counted against deaths, the difference is natural growth. Migration is counted separately. the death rate minus the area of the country is wrong because area is not subtracted from the death rate to find natural growth. only the number of people who migrate is wrong because migration changes numbers, but it is not part of natural growth. the number of factories added to the number of rivers is wrong because factories and rivers are not a population formula.\nयाद रखो: प्राकृतिक वृद्धि दर जन्म दर घटा मृत्यु दर है। नदियों में कारखाने जोड़ना नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: only the number of people who migrate सिर्फ प्रवास प्राकृतिक वृद्धि नहीं।"},{"id":"t-population-21","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"Migration means","options":["the movement of people into or out of a place","the birth of a child in a hospital","the weathering of parent rock into soil","the scale printed on a map"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is the movement of people into or out of a place because people who arrive are immigrants and people who leave are emigrants. Both are migration. the birth of a child in a hospital is wrong because a birth is part of the birth rate, not migration. the weathering of parent rock into soil is wrong because weathering is a soil process, not a movement of people. the scale printed on a map is wrong because a map scale compares distances. It is not migration.\nयाद रखो: प्रवास लोगों का किसी जगह आना या जाना है। अस्पताल में जन्म प्रवास नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the birth of a child in a hospital अस्पताल का जन्म प्रवास नहीं कहलाता।"},{"id":"t-population-22","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"A population pyramid with a broad base shows","options":["that almost everyone is over the age of ninety","a large number of young people","that no children have been born","the height of the Himalaya"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is a large number of young people because the base of the pyramid stands for the youngest ages, so a wide base means many children and young people. that almost everyone is over the age of ninety is wrong because the very old appear at the narrow top, not as a wide base. that no children have been born is wrong because a broad base means many births, not none. the height of the Himalaya is wrong because the pyramid is a population diagram, not a mountain height.\nयाद रखो: चौड़ा आधार युवाओं की बड़ी संख्या दिखाता है। नब्बे साल के बुज़ुर्गों की भीड़ नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: that almost everyone is over the age of ninety लगभग सब नब्बे पार हों तो आधार चौड़ा नहीं होता।"},{"id":"t-population-23","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"A narrow top on a population pyramid shows","options":["more babies than any other age group","that the country has no adults at all","fewer people in the oldest age groups","the width of a river"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is fewer people in the oldest age groups because the top stands for the elderly. A narrow top means relatively few people live to old age. more babies than any other age group is wrong because babies are shown at the base, not at the top. that the country has no adults at all is wrong because adults occupy the middle of the pyramid. A narrow top does not erase them. the width of a river is wrong because a river's width is not what the pyramid measures.\nयाद रखो: पतला शीर्ष सबसे बड़ी उम्र के लोगों की कम संख्या दिखाता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: more babies than any other age group ज़्यादा बच्चे आधार को चौड़ा करते हैं, शीर्ष को नहीं।"},{"id":"t-population-24","topicId":"t-population","subject":"sst","stem":"India's population pyramid has a broad base. This means that","options":["India has almost no children","every person in India is elderly","India has no population","India has a large young population"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is India has a large young population because a wide base shows that young people form a large share of India's population. India has almost no children is wrong because a broad base means many children, not almost none. every person in India is elderly is wrong because the elderly are the smaller group at the top. India has no population is wrong because India is one of the world's most populous countries.\nयाद रखो: भारत के पिरामिड का चौड़ा आधार मतलब युवा आबादी बड़ी है। बच्चे गायब नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: India has almost no children लगभग कोई बच्चा नहीं, यह चौड़े आधार का उल्टा है।"},{"id":"m-exponents-21","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 6^2 × 6^1.","options":["6^3","6^2","36^3","6^2 + 6^1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"When the bases are the same, add the powers: 6^2 × 6^1 = 6^3. 6^2 multiplies the powers, which is the rule for a power of a power. 36^3 changes the base. Adding the two powers as terms is not multiplication."},{"id":"m-exponents-22","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (7^4)^2.","options":["7^6","14^4","7^8","7^4"],"answer":2,"explanation":"A power of a power multiplies the indices: (7^4)^2 = 7^8. Adding the indices is for multiplying the same base. 14^4 changes the base. 7^4 drops the outside power."},{"id":"m-exponents-23","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Write 5^−2 with a positive power.","options":["1/5^2","5^2","−5^2","−1/5^2"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A negative power means the reciprocal: 5^−2 = 1/5^2. 5^2 drops the minus in the power. −5^2 and −1/5^2 put a minus sign in front. A negative index does not make the value negative when the base is positive."},{"id":"m-exponents-24","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 2^4 × 2^1.","options":["2^4","4^5","2^5","2^4 + 2^1"],"answer":2,"explanation":"When the bases are the same, add the powers: 2^4 × 2^1 = 2^5. 2^4 multiplies the powers, which is the rule for a power of a power. 4^5 changes the base. Adding the two powers as terms is not multiplication."},{"id":"m-exponents-25","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (6^4)^2.","options":["6^8","6^6","12^4","6^4"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A power of a power multiplies the indices: (6^4)^2 = 6^8. Adding the indices is for multiplying the same base. 12^4 changes the base. 6^4 drops the outside power."},{"id":"m-exponents-26","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 3^2 × 3^1.","options":["3^3","3^2","9^3","3^2 + 3^1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"When the bases are the same, add the powers: 3^2 × 3^1 = 3^3. 3^2 multiplies the powers, which is the rule for a power of a power. 9^3 changes the base. Adding the two powers as terms is not multiplication."},{"id":"m-exponents-27","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify (5^4)^2.","options":["5^6","10^4","5^8","5^4"],"answer":2,"explanation":"A power of a power multiplies the indices: (5^4)^2 = 5^8. Adding the indices is for multiplying the same base. 10^4 changes the base. 5^4 drops the outside power."},{"id":"m-exponents-28","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 4^4 × 4^1.","options":["4^4","16^5","4^5","4^4 + 4^1"],"answer":2,"explanation":"When the bases are the same, add the powers: 4^4 × 4^1 = 4^5. 4^4 multiplies the powers, which is the rule for a power of a power. 16^5 changes the base. Adding the two powers as terms is not multiplication."},{"id":"m-exponents-29","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 5^2 × 5^1.","options":["5^3","5^2","25^3","5^2 + 5^1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"When the bases are the same, add the powers: 5^2 × 5^1 = 5^3. 5^2 multiplies the powers, which is the rule for a power of a power. 25^3 changes the base. Adding the two powers as terms is not multiplication."},{"id":"m-exponents-30","topicId":"m-exponents","subject":"maths","stem":"Simplify 6^4 × 6^1.","options":["6^4","36^5","6^5","6^4 + 6^1"],"answer":2,"explanation":"When the bases are the same, add the powers: 6^4 × 6^1 = 6^5. 6^4 multiplies the powers, which is the rule for a power of a power. 36^5 changes the base. Adding the two powers as terms is not multiplication."},{"id":"m-squares-16","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"The square root of 400 is","options":["20","400","21","40"],"answer":0,"explanation":"√400 = 20, because 20 × 20 = 400. 400 is the square itself. 21 and 40 do not multiply by themselves to give 400."},{"id":"m-squares-17","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"A right triangle has legs 5 cm and 12 cm. The hypotenuse is","options":["17 cm","13 cm","14 cm","60 cm"],"answer":1,"explanation":"By Pythagoras, hypotenuse² = 5² + 12² = 25 + 144 = 169. So the hypotenuse is 13 cm. 17 adds the legs. 14 is the next whole number, whose square is not 169. 60 is the product of the legs, which is related to area, not the hypotenuse."},{"id":"m-squares-18","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"230 lies between the squares of","options":["14 and 15","16 and 17","15 and 17","15 and 16"],"answer":3,"explanation":"15² = 225 and 16² = 256. 230 is greater than 225 and smaller than 256, so it lies between 15 and 16. The other pairs are the neighbouring gaps, and 230 is not in those gaps."},{"id":"m-squares-19","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"The square root of 49 is","options":["49","7","8","14"],"answer":1,"explanation":"√49 = 7, because 7 × 7 = 49. 49 is the square itself. 8 and 14 do not multiply by themselves to give 49."},{"id":"m-squares-20","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"A right triangle has legs 9 cm and 40 cm. The hypotenuse is","options":["49 cm","42 cm","41 cm","360 cm"],"answer":2,"explanation":"By Pythagoras, hypotenuse² = 9² + 40² = 81 + 1600 = 1681. So the hypotenuse is 41 cm. 49 adds the legs. 42 is the next whole number, whose square is not 1681. 360 is the product of the legs, which is related to area, not the hypotenuse."},{"id":"m-squares-21","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"69 lies between the squares of","options":["8 and 9","7 and 8","9 and 10","8 and 10"],"answer":0,"explanation":"8² = 64 and 9² = 81. 69 is greater than 64 and smaller than 81, so it lies between 8 and 9. The other pairs are the neighbouring gaps, and 69 is not in those gaps."},{"id":"m-squares-22","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"The square root of 144 is","options":["144","13","12","24"],"answer":2,"explanation":"√144 = 12, because 12 × 12 = 144. 144 is the square itself. 13 and 24 do not multiply by themselves to give 144."},{"id":"m-squares-23","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"A right triangle has legs 7 cm and 24 cm. The hypotenuse is","options":["31 cm","26 cm","168 cm","25 cm"],"answer":3,"explanation":"By Pythagoras, hypotenuse² = 7² + 24² = 49 + 576 = 625. So the hypotenuse is 25 cm. 31 adds the legs. 26 is the next whole number, whose square is not 625. 168 is the product of the legs, which is related to area, not the hypotenuse."},{"id":"m-squares-24","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"174 lies between the squares of","options":["12 and 13","13 and 14","14 and 15","13 and 15"],"answer":1,"explanation":"13² = 169 and 14² = 196. 174 is greater than 169 and smaller than 196, so it lies between 13 and 14. The other pairs are the neighbouring gaps, and 174 is not in those gaps."},{"id":"m-squares-25","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"The square root of 289 is","options":["289","18","34","17"],"answer":3,"explanation":"√289 = 17, because 17 × 17 = 289. 289 is the square itself. 18 and 34 do not multiply by themselves to give 289."},{"id":"m-squares-26","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"A right triangle has legs 3 cm and 4 cm. The hypotenuse is","options":["5 cm","7 cm","6 cm","12 cm"],"answer":0,"explanation":"By Pythagoras, hypotenuse² = 3² + 4² = 9 + 16 = 25. So the hypotenuse is 5 cm. 7 adds the legs. 6 is the next whole number, whose square is not 25. 12 is the product of the legs, which is related to area, not the hypotenuse."},{"id":"m-squares-27","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"329 lies between the squares of","options":["17 and 18","19 and 20","18 and 19","18 and 20"],"answer":2,"explanation":"18² = 324 and 19² = 361. 329 is greater than 324 and smaller than 361, so it lies between 18 and 19. The other pairs are the neighbouring gaps, and 329 is not in those gaps."},{"id":"m-squares-28","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"The square root of 16 is","options":["4","16","5","8"],"answer":0,"explanation":"√16 = 4, because 4 × 4 = 16. 16 is the square itself. 5 and 8 do not multiply by themselves to give 16."},{"id":"m-squares-29","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"A right triangle has legs 9 cm and 12 cm. The hypotenuse is","options":["21 cm","15 cm","16 cm","108 cm"],"answer":1,"explanation":"By Pythagoras, hypotenuse² = 9² + 12² = 81 + 144 = 225. So the hypotenuse is 15 cm. 21 adds the legs. 16 is the next whole number, whose square is not 225. 108 is the product of the legs, which is related to area, not the hypotenuse."},{"id":"m-squares-30","topicId":"m-squares","subject":"maths","stem":"126 lies between the squares of","options":["10 and 11","12 and 13","11 and 13","11 and 12"],"answer":3,"explanation":"11² = 121 and 12² = 144. 126 is greater than 121 and smaller than 144, so it lies between 11 and 12. The other pairs are the neighbouring gaps, and 126 is not in those gaps."},{"id":"m-cubes-16","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of 6 is","options":["216","36","18","343"],"answer":0,"explanation":"6³ = 6 × 6 × 6 = 216. 36 is the square. 18 is three times the number. 343 is the next cube."},{"id":"m-cubes-17","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube root of 216 is","options":["216","6","36","18"],"answer":1,"explanation":"∛216 = 6, because 6 × 6 × 6 = 216. The cube itself, the square, and three times 6 are different numbers."},{"id":"m-cubes-18","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of -6 is","options":["216","-36","-6","-216"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The cube of a negative number is negative, because three minuses give a minus. (-6)³ = -216. 216 is the cube of the positive number. -36 is the negative square, not the cube. -6 is the number itself."},{"id":"m-cubes-19","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of 7 is","options":["343","49","21","512"],"answer":0,"explanation":"7³ = 7 × 7 × 7 = 343. 49 is the square. 21 is three times the number. 512 is the next cube."},{"id":"m-cubes-20","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube root of 343 is","options":["343","7","49","21"],"answer":1,"explanation":"∛343 = 7, because 7 × 7 × 7 = 343. The cube itself, the square, and three times 7 are different numbers."},{"id":"m-cubes-21","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of -7 is","options":["343","-49","-7","-343"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The cube of a negative number is negative, because three minuses give a minus. (-7)³ = -343. 343 is the cube of the positive number. -49 is the negative square, not the cube. -7 is the number itself."},{"id":"m-cubes-22","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of 8 is","options":["512","64","24","729"],"answer":0,"explanation":"8³ = 8 × 8 × 8 = 512. 64 is the square. 24 is three times the number. 729 is the next cube."},{"id":"m-cubes-23","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube root of 512 is","options":["512","8","64","24"],"answer":1,"explanation":"∛512 = 8, because 8 × 8 × 8 = 512. The cube itself, the square, and three times 8 are different numbers."},{"id":"m-cubes-24","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of -8 is","options":["512","-64","-8","-512"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The cube of a negative number is negative, because three minuses give a minus. (-8)³ = -512. 512 is the cube of the positive number. -64 is the negative square, not the cube. -8 is the number itself."},{"id":"m-cubes-25","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of 9 is","options":["729","81","27","1000"],"answer":0,"explanation":"9³ = 9 × 9 × 9 = 729. 81 is the square. 27 is three times the number. 1000 is the next cube."},{"id":"m-cubes-26","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube root of 729 is","options":["729","9","81","27"],"answer":1,"explanation":"∛729 = 9, because 9 × 9 × 9 = 729. The cube itself, the square, and three times 9 are different numbers."},{"id":"m-cubes-27","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of -9 is","options":["729","-81","-9","-729"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The cube of a negative number is negative, because three minuses give a minus. (-9)³ = -729. 729 is the cube of the positive number. -81 is the negative square, not the cube. -9 is the number itself."},{"id":"m-cubes-28","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of 10 is","options":["1000","100","30","1331"],"answer":0,"explanation":"10³ = 10 × 10 × 10 = 1000. 100 is the square. 30 is three times the number. 1331 is the next cube."},{"id":"m-cubes-29","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube root of 1000 is","options":["1000","10","100","30"],"answer":1,"explanation":"∛1000 = 10, because 10 × 10 × 10 = 1000. The cube itself, the square, and three times 10 are different numbers."},{"id":"m-cubes-30","topicId":"m-cubes","subject":"maths","stem":"The cube of -10 is","options":["1000","-100","-10","-1000"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The cube of a negative number is negative, because three minuses give a minus. (-10)³ = -1000. 1000 is the cube of the positive number. -100 is the negative square, not the cube. -10 is the number itself."},{"id":"m-algebra-16","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (5 + 6)² using an identity.","options":["61","91","22","121"],"answer":3,"explanation":"(x + y)² = x² + 2xy + y². Here x = 5 and y = 6, so the value is 25 + 60 + 36 = 121. 61 drops the middle term 2xy. 91 uses xy instead of 2xy. 22 is the double of the sum, not the square."},{"id":"m-algebra-17","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (5 − 7)².","options":["4","144","-24","74"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(x − y)² = x² − 2xy + y² = 25 − 70 + 49 = 4. 144 is (5 + 7)². -24 is a difference of squares. 74 drops the middle term and also loses the minus."},{"id":"m-algebra-18","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"The value of 5² − 8² is","options":["9","-39","89","41"],"answer":1,"explanation":"5² − 8² = (5 − 8)(5 + 8) = -3 × 13 = -39. 9 expands to a square of a difference, which still has a middle term. 89 adds the squares. The last option adds an extra 2ab onto the correct product."},{"id":"m-algebra-19","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (x + 3)(x + 5).","options":["x² + 15x + 8","x² + 8x + 8","x² + 8x + 15","x² − 8x + 15"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(x + a)(x + b) = x² + (a + b)x + ab. Here a + b = 8 and ab = 15, so the product is x² + 8x + 15. Swapping the sum and the product is the usual slip. A minus in the middle term would fit (x − 3)(x − 5) only if both signs were minus, which they are not."},{"id":"m-algebra-20","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Add 6x + 4 and 4x + 6.","options":["10x + 4","24x + 10","10x + 24","10x + 10"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Add like terms. The x terms are 6x + 4x = 10x. The constants are 4 + 6 = 10. The sum is 10x + 10. The other options multiply coefficients, or they add only one of the constants."},{"id":"m-algebra-21","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (6 + 9)² using an identity.","options":["225","117","171","30"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(x + y)² = x² + 2xy + y². Here x = 6 and y = 9, so the value is 36 + 108 + 81 = 225. 117 drops the middle term 2xy. 171 uses xy instead of 2xy. 30 is the double of the sum, not the square."},{"id":"m-algebra-22","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (6 − 7)².","options":["169","1","-13","85"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(x − y)² = x² − 2xy + y² = 36 − 84 + 49 = 1. 169 is (6 + 7)². -13 is a difference of squares. 85 drops the middle term and also loses the minus."},{"id":"m-algebra-23","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"The value of 6² − 8² is","options":["4","100","-28","68"],"answer":2,"explanation":"6² − 8² = (6 − 8)(6 + 8) = -2 × 14 = -28. 4 expands to a square of a difference, which still has a middle term. 100 adds the squares. The last option adds an extra 2ab onto the correct product."},{"id":"m-algebra-24","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (7 + 9)² using an identity.","options":["130","256","193","32"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(x + y)² = x² + 2xy + y². Here x = 7 and y = 9, so the value is 49 + 126 + 81 = 256. 130 drops the middle term 2xy. 193 uses xy instead of 2xy. 32 is the double of the sum, not the square."},{"id":"m-algebra-25","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (7 − 10)².","options":["289","-51","9","149"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(x − y)² = x² − 2xy + y² = 49 − 140 + 100 = 9. 289 is (7 + 10)². -51 is a difference of squares. 149 drops the middle term and also loses the minus."},{"id":"s-reproduction-27","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"How does transpiration help a tall plant?","options":["It changes the plant into an egg-laying animal","It is the fusion of gametes in the leaf","Water vapour lost from the leaves pulls more water up the xylem","It stores urine in the leaf"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Water vapour lost from the leaves pulls more water up the xylem. Transpiration is the loss of water vapour through stomata. That loss creates a pull which draws water upward through the xylem. It also helps to cool the plant. It changes the plant into an egg-laying animal is wrong because losing water vapour does not turn a plant into an animal. It is the fusion of gametes in the leaf is wrong because fusion of gametes is fertilisation. It stores urine in the leaf is wrong because urine is filtered by animal kidneys, and leaves do not store it.\nयाद रखो: पत्तियों से भाप उड़ती है तो जाइलम में पानी ऊपर खिंचता है। यही वाष्पोत्सर्जन की मदद है।\nगलत मत याद करना: It is the fusion of gametes in the leaf पत्ती में शुक्राणु-अंडा नहीं मिलते।"},{"id":"s-reproduction-28","topicId":"s-reproduction","subject":"science","stem":"Which waste is removed from human blood by the kidneys?","options":["Carbon dioxide, sent out through the larynx","Chlorophyll","Chaff","Urea, dissolved in urine"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Urea, dissolved in urine. Kidneys filter the blood and remove urea, extra salts, and extra water as urine. Ureters carry urine to the urinary bladder. Sweat also removes some water and salts and helps to cool the body. Carbon dioxide, sent out through the larynx is wrong because carbon dioxide leaves mainly through the lungs, and the larynx is the voice box. Chlorophyll is wrong because chlorophyll is a plant pigment and is not a waste filtered by human kidneys. Chaff is wrong because chaff is separated from grain by winnowing.\nयाद रखो: गुर्दे खून से यूरिया छानकर पेशाब बनाते हैं। कार्बन डाइऑक्साइड साँस से बाहर जाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Carbon dioxide, sent out through the larynx फेफड़ों की साँस है, गुर्दे का कचरा नहीं।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-16","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"How many pairs of chromosomes are present in a human body cell?","options":["2 pairs","46 pairs","23 pairs","4 pairs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is 23 pairs. The 23 pairs include the sex chromosomes, XX in a female and XY in a male, while the other pairs occur in both sexes. Genes on these chromosomes carry the inherited instructions. 2 pairs is wrong because there is one pair of sex chromosomes, but the total is 23 pairs. 46 pairs is wrong because there are 46 chromosomes, which means 23 pairs, not 46 pairs. 4 pairs is wrong because four is the number of chambers in the heart, not the number of chromosome pairs.\nयाद रखो: शरीर की कोशिका में 23 जोड़े गुणसूत्र होते हैं। 46 छड़ें हैं, 46 जोड़े नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: 46 pairs छड़ें और जोड़े मिला देने वाली गलती है।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-17","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Which meal pattern best suits a growing adolescent?","options":["A balanced diet of chapati, pulses, milk, fruit, vegetables, and enough iron","Only chips and fizzy drinks at every meal","No meals, because hormones replace food","Only sugar, because insulin turns sugar into height"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is A balanced diet of chapati, pulses, milk, fruit, vegetables, and enough iron. Growth is rapid, so the body needs protein, carbohydrates, fats, vitamins, and minerals. Girls lose iron during menstruation, so leafy vegetables, jaggery, and similar foods are important. Only chips and fizzy drinks at every meal is wrong because packaged snacks do not supply the proteins, vitamins, and minerals needed for fast growth. No meals, because hormones replace food is wrong because hormones do not replace nutrients. Only sugar, because insulin turns sugar into height is wrong because extra sugar is not a balanced diet, and insulin does not build height.\nयाद रखो: बढ़ते किशोर को रोटी, दाल, दूध, फल, सब्जी और काफी लोहा चाहिए। चिप्स अकेले ऊँचाई नहीं देते।\nगलत मत याद करना: Only chips and fizzy drinks at every meal संतुलित थाली नहीं है।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-18","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Which habit supports health during adolescence?","options":["Sharing a needle because friends insist","Never washing, so that oil glands stay blocked","Taking antibiotics for fun","Daily cleanliness, exercise, and refusing drugs"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Daily cleanliness, exercise, and refusing drugs. Sweat and oil glands are more active at puberty, so bathing and clean clothes help. Games and walking keep the body fit. Drugs harm the body and can cause addiction, so the safe reply to pressure is no. Sharing a needle because friends insist is wrong because a shared needle can spread serious infections such as HIV. Never washing, so that oil glands stay blocked is wrong because blocked glands can worsen pimples, and cleanliness is part of health. Taking antibiotics for fun is wrong because antibiotics should be taken only on a doctor's advice.\nयाद रखो: यौवन में नहाना, कसरत और नशीली चीज़ से मना करना शरीर का पहरेदार है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Taking antibiotics for fun दवा का खेल खतरनाक है, आदत नहीं।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-19","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"HIV, the virus that causes AIDS, can spread by...","options":["Hugging an infected friend","Sharing an infected needle or receiving infected blood","Eating from the same plate","Sitting in the same classroom"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Sharing an infected needle or receiving infected blood. HIV can pass by sexual contact with an infected person, by infected blood, by shared syringes, and from an infected mother to her baby. It does not spread by handshakes, hugs, or shared food. Hugging an infected friend is wrong because ordinary touching and hugging do not spread HIV. Eating from the same plate is wrong because sharing a meal is not a route of HIV spread. Sitting in the same classroom is wrong because everyday contact at school does not transmit this virus.\nयाद रखो: HIV संक्रमित सुई या संक्रमित खून से फैल सकता है। गले लगने या एक थाली से नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Hugging an infected friend गले मिलने से एड्स नहीं फैलता।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-20","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Pimples at puberty are linked mainly with...","options":["A sudden loss of all chromosomes","Failure of xylem in the skin","More active oil-secreting sebaceous glands","External fertilisation on the skin"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is More active oil-secreting sebaceous glands. Sebaceous glands secrete oil, and at puberty they become more active so pores may block and acne appears. Washing helps, and the more active sweat glands can also cause body odour if clothes stay dirty. A sudden loss of all chromosomes is wrong because pimples are not caused by chromosomes disappearing. Failure of xylem in the skin is wrong because xylem is a plant tissue, and humans do not have it. External fertilisation on the skin is wrong because external fertilisation is the method used by frogs and fish.\nयाद रखो: यौवन में तेल ग्रंथियाँ ज्यादा तेल छोड़ती हैं, रोम छिद्र बंद होते हैं, मुँहासे निकलते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Failure of xylem in the skin त्वचा में पौधे की पानी-पाइप नहीं होती।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-21","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Why does a boy's voice usually become deep at puberty?","options":["The eardrum turns into the voice box","Estrogen shrinks the voice box of boys","The thyroid gland is removed","The larynx grows and the vocal cords become longer"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is The larynx grows and the vocal cords become longer. The larynx is the voice box at the top of the windpipe. In boys it grows and may show as the Adam's apple. Longer vocal cords vibrate more slowly, so the voice becomes deep and may be hoarse for a while. The eardrum turns into the voice box is wrong because the eardrum receives sound, while the larynx produces the voice. Estrogen shrinks the voice box of boys is wrong because the male voice change is linked with growth of the larynx, not with a shrinking caused by estrogen. The thyroid gland is removed is wrong because the voice change is normal growth, not an operation on the thyroid.\nयाद रखो: लड़के का स्वरयंत्र बढ़ता है, स्वर रज्जु लंबी होती हैं, आवाज़ भारी हो जाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Estrogen shrinks the voice box of boys एस्ट्रोजन लड़कों का आवाज़-सिकोड़ने वाला नहीं।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-22","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"The sharp increase in height at puberty is directed mainly by...","options":["Growth hormone from the pituitary gland","Insulin from the pancreas","A single rush of adrenaline","Haemoglobin alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Growth hormone from the pituitary gland. The pituitary secretes growth hormone, and both height and muscles increase quickly in adolescence. Girls often have their spurt earlier, while many boys continue to gain height for longer. Food must support this growth. Insulin from the pancreas is wrong because insulin regulates blood sugar and is not the height hormone. A single rush of adrenaline is wrong because adrenaline is a short-term stress hormone, not the hormone of the growth spurt. Haemoglobin alone is wrong because haemoglobin carries oxygen, while growth hormone directs the increase in height.\nयाद रखो: यौवन की अचानक ऊँचाई पिट्यूटरी के वृद्धि हार्मोन के इशारे पर आती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Insulin from the pancreas शक्कर संभालता है, अकेले ऊँचाई का सरदार नहीं।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-23","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"A tadpole fails to become a frog if the water has no iodine. Why?","options":["Iodine is the same substance as chlorophyll","The thyroid needs iodine to make thyroxine, which metamorphosis requires","Iodine is another name for testosterone","Without iodine the tadpole becomes a viviparous mammal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is The thyroid needs iodine to make thyroxine, which metamorphosis requires. Thyroxine produced by the thyroid brings about the change from tadpole to frog. The gland can make thyroxine only if iodine is available. This is the same element that iodised salt supplies to humans. Iodine is the same substance as chlorophyll is wrong because chlorophyll is the green pigment of plants, not iodine. Iodine is another name for testosterone is wrong because testosterone is the male hormone made in the testes. Without iodine the tadpole becomes a viviparous mammal is wrong because iodine does not change the way a frog reproduces.\nयाद रखो: टैडपोल को मेंढक बनाने के लिए थायरॉक्सिन चाहिए, और थायरॉक्सिन को आयोडीन।\nगलत मत याद करना: Iodine is another name for testosterone आयोडीन लड़कों का हार्मोन नहीं है।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-24","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Which gland is ductless, so that its secretion goes straight into the blood?","options":["A sweat gland","A salivary gland","An endocrine gland","A seed gland"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is An endocrine gland. Ductless glands are called endocrine glands. Their hormones enter blood capillaries and travel around the body. Salivary glands and sweat glands have ducts, so they are not the hormone glands of this chapter. A sweat gland is wrong because a sweat gland has a duct that opens on the skin. A salivary gland is wrong because saliva travels through a duct into the mouth. A seed gland is wrong because there is no seed gland in the human hormone system.\nयाद रखो: अंतःस्रावी ग्रंथि नलिका रहित है, रस सीधे खून में जाता है। पसीना और लार नलिका से निकलते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: A sweat gland नलिका वाली है, हार्मोन की ग्रंथि नहीं।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-25","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement about drugs is the safe one for an adolescent?","options":["Say no, because drugs harm the body and can cause addiction","Try a drug once to prove courage","Share a needle if it looks clean","Use drugs instead of food and sleep"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Say no, because drugs harm the body and can cause addiction. An addictive drug makes a person crave it. Drugs injure the body and disturb study, and misusing them is unlawful. If friends apply pressure, the healthy decision taught in this chapter is to refuse. Try a drug once to prove courage is wrong because even an early trial can begin harm and craving. Share a needle if it looks clean is wrong because shared needles can transmit HIV and other infections. Use drugs instead of food and sleep is wrong because drugs do not replace meals or rest, and they damage health.\nयाद रखो: नशीली दवा शरीर तोड़ती है और आदत डालती है। किशोर का सुरक्षित जवाब है: नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Try a drug once to prove courage हिम्मत की परीक्षा नहीं, नुकसान की शुरुआत है।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-26","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"The target site of a hormone is...","options":["The school bag that carries the books","The particular organ or cells that the hormone is meant to affect","The field where a rabi crop is growing","The mirror of a microscope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is The particular organ or cells that the hormone is meant to affect. A hormone travels widely in the blood, but it acts on a chosen target. Growth hormone affects growth of the body, and insulin acts on the way cells handle sugar. This matching keeps the messages in order. The school bag that carries the books is wrong because a bag is not a body target of a hormone. The field where a rabi crop is growing is wrong because a crop field is not the target of a human hormone. The mirror of a microscope is wrong because a microscope mirror is not part of the endocrine system.\nयाद रखो: हार्मोन का लक्ष्य वह अंग या कोशिका है जिसे वह बदलने आया है। स्कूल बैग लक्ष्य नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: The school bag that carries the books किताबें ढोता है, हार्मोन का निशाना नहीं।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-27","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Personal hygiene matters more at puberty because...","options":["The heart loses all four of its chambers","Growing bones no longer need minerals","Sweat glands and oil glands become more active","Chromosomes disappear from the nucleus"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Sweat glands and oil glands become more active. More sweat and oil can cause body odour and pimples if skin and clothes are neglected. A daily bath, clean underclothes, and proper care during menstruation are part of staying healthy. The heart loses all four of its chambers is wrong because the heart keeps its four chambers. Growing bones no longer need minerals is wrong because growing bones still need minerals from a balanced diet. Chromosomes disappear from the nucleus is wrong because chromosomes remain in the cells.\nयाद रखो: यौवन में पसीना और तेल की ग्रंथियाँ ज्यादा जागती हैं, इसलिए नहाना और साफ कपड़े ज़रूरी हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: The heart loses all four of its chambers दिल के चार कमरे यौवन में गायब नहीं होते।"},{"id":"s-adolescence-28","topicId":"s-adolescence","subject":"science","stem":"Which pair is matched correctly?","options":["Thyroid and adrenaline","Testes and estrogen","Adrenal gland and thyroxine","Pancreas and insulin"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Pancreas and insulin. Each endocrine gland has its own hormone. The pancreas secretes insulin, the thyroid secretes thyroxine, the adrenals secrete adrenaline, the testes secrete testosterone, and the ovaries secrete estrogen. Thyroid and adrenaline is wrong because adrenaline comes from the adrenal glands, and the thyroid makes thyroxine. Testes and estrogen is wrong because the testes secrete testosterone, while estrogen comes from the ovaries. Adrenal gland and thyroxine is wrong because thyroxine comes from the thyroid, not from the adrenal gland.\nयाद रखो: सही जोड़ी: अग्न्याशय और इंसुलिन। थायरॉइड थायरॉक्सिन देती है, एड्रिनलीन नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Thyroid and adrenaline गलत जोड़ी है: एड्रिनलीन अधिवृक्क ग्रंथि देता है।"},{"id":"s-force-16","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"Liquid rises in a drinking straw when you suck because...","options":["The liquid has no weight","The straw creates a new gravity inside the drink","Pressure inside the straw falls and atmospheric pressure pushes the liquid up","Electrostatic force always pushes the drink downward"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Pressure inside the straw falls and atmospheric pressure pushes the liquid up. Sucking removes some air from the straw, so the pressure inside becomes lower than the pressure outside. The atmosphere pressing on the drink surface pushes liquid up the straw. The liquid has no weight is wrong because the liquid does have weight, and air pressure helps lift it. The straw creates a new gravity inside the drink is wrong because gravity pulls downward and is not made by the straw. Electrostatic force always pushes the drink downward is wrong because the drink rises, and the cause in this activity is atmospheric pressure.\nयाद रखो: स्ट्रॉ में दाब गिरता है, बाहर की हवा पेय को ऊपर धकेलती है। पेय खुद नहीं चढ़ता।\nगलत मत याद करना: The liquid has no weight तरल का वज़न खत्म नहीं हो जाता।"},{"id":"s-force-17","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"Speed is found by...","options":["Dividing the distance travelled by the time taken","Multiplying force by area","Dividing force by area","Multiplying the length of a pendulum by the mass of its bob"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Dividing the distance travelled by the time taken. Speed tells how fast a body moves. If the distance and the time are known, speed equals distance divided by time. The SI unit is the metre per second, written m/s. Multiplying force by area is wrong because force times area is not speed. Dividing force by area is wrong because force divided by area is pressure, not speed. Multiplying the length of a pendulum by the mass of its bob is wrong because that product is not a speed.\nयाद रखो: रफ़्तार का उपनाम: रास्ता बाँटो समय से। बल गुणा क्षेत्र दाब का उल्टा खेल है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Dividing force by area दाब का सूत्र है, रफ़्तार का नहीं।"},{"id":"s-force-18","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"The pressure under a block is 25 Pa and the area is 4 square metres. What force acts on that area?","options":["21 N","25/4 N","29 N","100 N"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is 100 N. Because pressure equals force divided by area, force equals pressure multiplied by area. Here 25 multiplied by 4 is 100, so the force is 100 N. 21 N is wrong because subtracting the area from the pressure is not the link between force and pressure. 25/4 N is wrong because dividing the pressure by the area does not give the force. 29 N is wrong because adding 25 and 4 mixes a pressure with an area."},{"id":"s-force-19","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"A toy car covers equal distances in equal lengths of time. Its motion is...","options":["Non-uniform motion","Uniform motion","Rest, with a speed of zero","Metamorphosis"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Uniform motion. In uniform motion the speed stays the same. A distance-time graph of this motion is a straight line. If the car keeps slowing and speeding up, the motion is non-uniform. Non-uniform motion is wrong because non-uniform motion covers unequal distances in equal times. Rest, with a speed of zero is wrong because equal distances in equal times mean a steady speed, not rest. Metamorphosis is wrong because metamorphosis is a change of body form, as in a frog.\nयाद रखो: बराबर दूरी, बराबर समय: एकसमान गति। ग्राफ सीधी लकीर बनता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Non-uniform motion में दूरी बराबर समय में बराबर नहीं रहती।"},{"id":"s-force-20","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"On a distance-time graph, a steeper straight line means...","options":["The object is at rest","A lower speed than a flatter line","A higher speed","The time period of a pendulum"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is A higher speed. Speed is distance divided by time. A steeper straight line climbs more during the same time, so the object is faster. A horizontal line means the object is not moving. The object is at rest is wrong because rest gives a horizontal line because the distance is not changing. A lower speed than a flatter line is wrong because a steeper line shows more distance in the same time, so the speed is higher. The time period of a pendulum is wrong because this graph describes motion, not the swing of a pendulum.\nयाद रखो: दूरी-समय ग्राफ की खड़ी लकीर तेज़ रफ़्तार है। पड़ी लकीर का मतलब खड़ा आराम।\nगलत मत याद करना: The object is at rest आराम पड़ी लकीर देता है, खड़ी लकीर नहीं।"},{"id":"s-force-21","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"The time period of a simple pendulum is...","options":["The mass of the bob in kilograms","The length of the string, with no time involved","The friction on the bob","The time taken for one complete to and fro swing"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is The time taken for one complete to and fro swing. One oscillation is one complete to and fro motion. The time for that motion is the time period. Students often time 20 oscillations and divide by 20, because one swing is too quick to time well. The mass of the bob in kilograms is wrong because mass is not a time. The length of the string, with no time involved is wrong because length affects the time period, but the time period itself is a time. The friction on the bob is wrong because friction is a force, while the time period is the time for one oscillation.\nयाद रखो: आवर्तकाल एक पूरा आगे-पीछे झूला है। बीस झूले का समय बाँटो बीस से।\nगलत मत याद करना: The mass of the bob in kilograms गोलक का वज़न समय नहीं है।"},{"id":"s-force-22","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"If the length of a simple pendulum is increased, the time period...","options":["Increases","Becomes zero","Stays fixed at one second for every length","Becomes equal to the mass of the bob"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Increases. A longer pendulum takes more time for one oscillation. The time period therefore increases when the length increases. A long swing in a park moves with a slow, large swing for this reason. Becomes zero is wrong because a longer string does not make the time period zero. Stays fixed at one second for every length is wrong because the time period changes when the length changes. Becomes equal to the mass of the bob is wrong because a time is not equal to a mass.\nयाद रखो: लंगर लंबा करो तो एक झूले में ज़्यादा समय लगता है। आवर्तकाल बढ़ता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Becomes zero लंबी डोरी झूले को शून्य समय में नहीं खत्म करती।"},{"id":"s-force-23","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"The length of a simple pendulum is kept the same, but a heavier bob is used. The time period...","options":["Doubles the atmospheric pressure","Stays almost the same","Changes the unit of time from the second to the newton","Stops the bob from ever passing the mean position"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Stays almost the same. Experiments in the motion chapter show that bobs of different mass give nearly the same time period if the length is unchanged. The time period depends on the length. For small swings it also does not depend on how far the bob is pulled aside. Doubles the atmospheric pressure is wrong because the mass of the bob does not set the pressure of the air. Changes the unit of time from the second to the newton is wrong because the second remains the unit of time, and the newton is a unit of force. Stops the bob from ever passing the mean position is wrong because a normal pendulum still swings to and fro about the mean position.\nयाद रखो: डोरी वही रहे तो भारी गोलक भी लगभग उतना ही समय लेता है। वक़्त लंबाई देखता है, वज़न नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Changes the unit of time from the second to the newton गोलक बदलने से इकाई नहीं बदलती।"},{"id":"s-force-24","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"The same force of 60 N acts first on 2 square metres and then on 6 square metres. Which statement is correct?","options":["The pressure on 6 square metres is 30 Pa and the pressure on 2 square metres is 10 Pa","Both pressures equal 60 Pa because the force is the same","The pressure on 2 square metres is 30 Pa, greater than the 10 Pa on 6 square metres","Both pressures equal 4 Pa"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is The pressure on 2 square metres is 30 Pa, greater than the 10 Pa on 6 square metres. Pressure equals force divided by area, so 60 divided by 2 is 30 Pa on the smaller surface and 60 divided by 6 is 10 Pa on the larger surface. The smaller area therefore feels the greater pressure. The pressure on 6 square metres is 30 Pa and the pressure on 2 square metres is 10 Pa is wrong because this swaps the results, because the smaller area gives the larger pressure. Both pressures equal 60 Pa because the force is the same is wrong because the same force on two different areas does not give the same pressure. Both pressures equal 4 Pa is wrong because 4 is not the result of 60 divided by 2 or of 60 divided by 6."},{"id":"s-force-25","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"The attraction between a charged comb and bits of paper is...","options":["A non-contact force","Only a muscular force","Possible only if the comb is an iron magnet","Friction from the floor pushing the paper upward"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is A non-contact force. Electrostatic force can act across a small gap, so it is a non-contact force. Gravity and magnetic force are the other non-contact forces in this chapter. Muscular force and friction need contact. Only a muscular force is wrong because muscles are not pulling the paper; the charged comb is. Possible only if the comb is an iron magnet is wrong because the comb is electrically charged, so the force is electrostatic rather than magnetic. Friction from the floor pushing the paper upward is wrong because friction would oppose a slide along the floor, and it does not lift the bits onto the comb.\nयाद रखो: आवेशित कंघी और कागज़ बिना छुए खिंचते हैं, इसलिए यह असंपर्श बल है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Only a muscular force मांस का धक्का है। कागज़ की पेशियाँ कंघी नहीं खींचतीं।"},{"id":"s-force-26","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"The gravitational force of the Earth...","options":["Acts only when the Earth touches the object with a hand","Pulls objects toward the Earth without needing contact","Is simply another name for friction","Pushes every object away into space"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Pulls objects toward the Earth without needing contact. Objects fall because the Earth attracts them. This attraction is called gravity, and it is a non-contact force. It acts on objects even when nothing is touching them. Acts only when the Earth touches the object with a hand is wrong because gravity acts at a distance, and the Earth does not use a hand. Is simply another name for friction is wrong because friction opposes sliding, while gravity is an attraction. Pushes every object away into space is wrong because Earth's gravity pulls objects toward the Earth.\nयाद रखो: पृथ्वी बिना हाथ लगाए चीज़ों को अपनी तरफ खींचती है। यही गुरुत्व है, असंपर्श बल।\nगलत मत याद करना: Is simply another name for friction गुरुत्व घर्षण का दूसरा नाम नहीं।"},{"id":"s-force-27","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"A simple pendulum completes 20 oscillations in 40 s. What is its time period?","options":["800 s","20 s","2 s","40 s"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is 2 s. The time period is the time for one complete oscillation. Working: time period = total time / number of oscillations = 40 s / 20 = 2 s. 800 s is wrong because 40 multiplied by 20 is 800, and the time period is found by dividing, not multiplying. 20 s is wrong because 20 is the number of oscillations, not the time for one of them. 40 s is wrong because 40 s is the time for all twenty oscillations together."},{"id":"s-force-28","topicId":"s-force","subject":"science","stem":"A girl walks 450 m in 150 s. What is her speed?","options":["67500 m/s","3 m","0.33 m/s","3 m/s"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is 3 m/s. Speed equals distance divided by time. Working: 450 m / 150 s = 3 m/s. 67500 m/s is wrong because 450 multiplied by 150 is 67500, which multiplies distance by time instead of dividing. 3 m is wrong because 3 m is only a distance and does not state per second. 0.33 m/s is wrong because 150 divided by 450 is about 0.33, and that is time divided by distance, not distance divided by time."},{"id":"s-friction-16","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Powder is sprinkled on a carrom board so that...","options":["Friction increases and the striker stops at once","The powder is meant to create static friction and prevent all sliding","Friction decreases and the striker slides easily","The powder raises atmospheric pressure on the coins"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Friction decreases and the striker slides easily. Fine powder fills some of the tiny bumps and behaves a little like a dry lubricant. The striker and the coins then travel farther. Tyre treads do the opposite job, because they are meant to increase grip. Friction increases and the striker stops at once is wrong because the powder lowers friction. The powder is meant to create static friction and prevent all sliding is wrong because the powder helps the striker slide with less opposition. The powder raises atmospheric pressure on the coins is wrong because powder does not change the pressure of the air.\nयाद रखो: कैरम पर पाउडर छोटे दाँत भर देता है, घर्षण घटता है, गोटी दूर तक जाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Friction increases and the striker stops at once पाउडर ब्रेक नहीं है।"},{"id":"s-friction-17","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Bicycle brakes stop the wheel mainly by...","options":["Pressing pads so that friction opposes the spinning rim","Switching gravity off for a moment","Turning the tyres into ball bearings","Increasing the speed of the bicycle"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Pressing pads so that friction opposes the spinning rim. The brake pads rub on a moving part of the wheel. Sliding friction opposes the rotation and the bicycle slows. If the pads are worn smooth, the friction may be too small to stop the bicycle quickly. Switching gravity off for a moment is wrong because brakes do not remove gravity. Turning the tyres into ball bearings is wrong because ball bearings reduce friction in an axle, while brakes use friction to slow the wheel. Increasing the speed of the bicycle is wrong because brakes are used to decrease speed.\nयाद रखो: ब्रेक पैड घूमते रिम पर रगड़ते हैं। घर्षण पहिए की उल्टी दिशा में लगकर साइकिल रोकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Increasing the speed of the bicycle ब्रेक रफ़्तार बढ़ाता नहीं।"},{"id":"s-friction-18","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Which example shows that friction can produce heat?","options":["Holding the palms apart with no rubbing, and calling that friction","Pouring oil on a machine in order to increase heating from friction","Adding a lubricant so that every engine makes more heat on purpose","Rubbing the palms together makes them feel warm"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Rubbing the palms together makes them feel warm. When surfaces rub, some energy changes into heat. Machine parts can become hot and may be damaged if they run dry. This heating is one reason friction can be troublesome. Holding the palms apart with no rubbing, and calling that friction is wrong because heat from friction needs the surfaces to rub. Pouring oil on a machine in order to increase heating from friction is wrong because oil reduces friction and therefore reduces that heating. Adding a lubricant so that every engine makes more heat on purpose is wrong because lubricants are added to cut down friction and unwanted heat.\nयाद रखो: हथेलियाँ रगड़ो तो गर्मी लगती है। घर्षण ऊर्जा का कुछ हिस्सा गर्मी बना देता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Holding the palms apart with no rubbing बिना रगड़ के घर्षण की गर्मी नहीं बनती।"},{"id":"s-friction-19","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Shoe soles wear out mainly because...","options":["Friction is absent while a person walks","Friction rubs them against the ground at every step","The shoe makes a lubricant that dissolves the sole","Rolling friction is larger than sliding friction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Friction rubs them against the ground at every step. Each step scrapes the sole a little, and over months the material is rubbed away. Tyres and machine parts wear for the same reason. Reducing unwanted friction helps parts last longer. Friction is absent while a person walks is wrong because walking uses friction, and that friction slowly wears the sole. The shoe makes a lubricant that dissolves the sole is wrong because ordinary wear is caused by rubbing, not by the shoe producing oil. Rolling friction is larger than sliding friction is wrong because rolling friction is the smaller kind, and a sole usually grips or slides.\nयाद रखो: हर कदम पर तलवा ज़मीन से रगड़ खाता है, इसलिए जूते घिस जाते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Friction is absent while a person walks चलने में घर्षण गायब नहीं होता।"},{"id":"s-friction-20","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Striking a match uses friction in order to...","options":["Cool the tip below freezing","Remove all the oxygen from the room","Heat the tip enough for it to catch fire","Turn the match into a magnet"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Heat the tip enough for it to catch fire. The match head is rubbed on a rough strip, friction produces heat, and the chemicals in the head ignite. That heat is useful here, but the same heating is a problem when it overheats a machine. Cool the tip below freezing is wrong because friction heats the tip. Remove all the oxygen from the room is wrong because the match needs the heat of rubbing, and it does not empty the room of oxygen. Turn the match into a magnet is wrong because striking a match does not magnetise it.\nयाद रखो: माचिस की तीली खुरदरी पट्टी पर रगड़ से इतनी गर्म होती है कि सिर आग पकड़ लेता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Cool the tip below freezing रगड़ ठंडक नहीं, गर्मी लाती है।"},{"id":"s-friction-21","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Which action increases friction?","options":["Oiling a bicycle chain","Fitting ball bearings in a wheel","Sprinkling powder on a carrom board","Rubbing soil on the hands before a kabaddi grip"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Rubbing soil on the hands before a kabaddi grip. Soil makes the palms rougher, so the grip is better. Treads on tyres and grooves on soles also increase friction. Oil, grease, powder, polishing, and ball bearings are used when less friction is wanted. Oiling a bicycle chain is wrong because oil is a lubricant and decreases friction. Fitting ball bearings in a wheel is wrong because ball bearings replace sliding with rolling and decrease friction. Sprinkling powder on a carrom board is wrong because powder decreases friction so that the pieces slide.\nयाद रखो: कबड्डी से पहले मिट्टी मलना हथेली खुरदरी करता है, घर्षण बढ़ता है। तेल उल्टा काम करता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Oiling a bicycle chain स्नेहक है, घर्षण घटाता है।"},{"id":"s-friction-22","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Which action decreases friction?","options":["Putting oil on a squeaky door hinge","Fitting a tyre with deep treads for a wet road","Pressing the brake pads harder on the rim","Choosing a rougher path so that the shoes grip more"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Putting oil on a squeaky door hinge. Oil is a lubricant, and it forms a film on the hinge so the metal parts scrape less. Grease does the same job on many machines, giving less friction, less wear, and less noise. Fitting a tyre with deep treads for a wet road is wrong because treads increase friction and grip. Pressing the brake pads harder on the rim is wrong because a harder press increases the friction that slows the wheel. Choosing a rougher path so that the shoes grip more is wrong because a rougher surface increases friction.\nयाद रखो: कब्जे पर तेल की पतली परत धातु की रगड़ घटाती है, चरचराहट बंद होती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Fitting a tyre with deep treads for a wet road पकड़ बढ़ाने के लिए है, घटाने के लिए नहीं।"},{"id":"s-friction-23","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Drag on a moving body depends on...","options":["Only the colour of the body","Its speed, its shape, and the fluid it moves through","The chromosomes inside the body","Whether the body is a kharif crop"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Its speed, its shape, and the fluid it moves through. A faster body meets more drag, and a blunt shape meets more drag than a streamlined shape. A thick liquid also resists motion more than a thin one, so speed, shape, and the fluid all matter. Only the colour of the body is wrong because colour does not set fluid friction. The chromosomes inside the body is wrong because chromosomes carry genes and do not decide drag. Whether the body is a kharif crop is wrong because the crop season has nothing to do with fluid friction.\nयाद रखो: कर्षण रफ़्तार, आकार और तरल पर निर्भर करता है। रंग और गुणसूत्र इसमें नहीं पड़ते।\nगलत मत याद करना: Only the colour of the body रंग बदलने से पानी की रगड़ नहीं बदलती।"},{"id":"s-friction-24","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"It is easier to roll a heavy drum than to slide it because...","options":["Rolling friction is larger than sliding friction","The drum loses all of its weight as soon as it rolls","Rolling friction is smaller than sliding friction","Sliding friction becomes a non-contact force when the drum is tipped"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Rolling friction is smaller than sliding friction. Sliding means a large face scrapes along the ground. Rolling uses a smaller rolling contact, and rolling friction is smaller. Movers place rollers or wheels under heavy loads for this reason. Rolling friction is larger than sliding friction is wrong because the opposite is true, which is why rolling is easier. The drum loses all of its weight as soon as it rolls is wrong because the weight remains, and the kind of friction changes. Sliding friction becomes a non-contact force when the drum is tipped is wrong because both rolling friction and sliding friction are contact forces.\nयाद रखो: भारी ड्रम सरकाने से लुढ़काना आसान है, क्योंकि लुढ़कन घर्षण सर्पी घर्षण से छोटा है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Rolling friction is larger than sliding friction क्रम उल्टा याद करने की गलती है।"},{"id":"s-friction-25","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement about the direction of friction is correct?","options":["Friction opposes the motion or the attempt to start motion","Friction always points the same way as the applied force","Friction always points vertically upward","Friction points toward the heavier object only after oil is added"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Friction opposes the motion or the attempt to start motion. If a suitcase is pulled toward the east, friction acts toward the west. If the suitcase has not yet moved, static friction still opposes the pull. Friction does not help the relative slide. Friction always points the same way as the applied force is wrong because friction opposes the force that tries to slide the object. Friction always points vertically upward is wrong because friction acts along the two surfaces, opposite the slide. Friction points toward the heavier object only after oil is added is wrong because oil reduces friction, and the direction rule is about opposing motion.\nयाद रखो: घर्षण गति की उल्टी दिशा में लगता है, या चलने की कोशिश की उल्टी दिशा में।\nगलत मत याद करना: Friction always points the same way as the applied force वह धक्के का चेला नहीं, विरोधी है।"},{"id":"s-friction-26","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Machine parts are polished and oiled in order to...","options":["Make them as rough as a tyre tread","Reduce friction, wear, and heating","Increase static friction so the machine cannot start","Change the oil into a hormone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Reduce friction, wear, and heating. Polishing removes some of the irregularities. Oil then separates the remaining bumps with a thin film. The parts turn more easily, last longer, and do not heat up as fast. Make them as rough as a tyre tread is wrong because rough treads are for grip, while most machine parts need less friction. Increase static friction so the machine cannot start is wrong because oil lowers friction so that parts can move. Change the oil into a hormone is wrong because oil is a lubricant, not a hormone.\nयाद रखो: मशीन के पुर्जे चमकाए और तेल लगाए जाते हैं ताकि घर्षण, घिसाव और गर्मी घटें।\nगलत मत याद करना: Make them as rough as a tyre tread टायर की धारियाँ पकड़ बढ़ाती हैं, मशीन को नहीं।"},{"id":"s-friction-27","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"Without friction, which action would become almost impossible?","options":["Letting an already moving object continue on a perfectly smooth surface","Removing atmospheric pressure","Holding a glass of water steadily in the hand","Sending a sound through a vacuum"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Holding a glass of water steadily in the hand. Fingers grip a glass because of friction. Without it the glass would slip out. Walking, writing, tying a knot, and braking a bicycle also depend on friction, so the force is often a help. Letting an already moving object continue on a perfectly smooth surface is wrong because without friction that object would keep moving, so the motion would not become impossible. Removing atmospheric pressure is wrong because atmospheric pressure is not friction. Sending a sound through a vacuum is wrong because sound needs a medium, which is a different rule from the need for friction.\nयाद रखो: बिना घर्षण के गिलास हथेली से फिसल जाएगा। चलना, लिखना और ब्रेक भी इसी पर टिके हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Sending a sound through a vacuum आवाज़ खाली जगह में चलती ही नहीं, घर्षण का सवाल नहीं।"},{"id":"s-friction-28","topicId":"s-friction","subject":"science","stem":"A fish has a streamlined body mainly so that it can...","options":["Increase sliding friction with the water","Produce static friction with air inside the gills","Increase its weight so that it sinks faster","Reduce drag while it swims"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Reduce drag while it swims. Water resists motion, and that resistance is drag. A tapering body moves through water with less opposition. Birds use the same idea in air, and many boats are shaped to cut through water. Increase sliding friction with the water is wrong because more friction would make swimming harder, and the shape reduces drag. Produce static friction with air inside the gills is wrong because the useful effect of the body shape is lower fluid friction in water. Increase its weight so that it sinks faster is wrong because streamlining is about shape and drag, not about making the fish heavier.\nयाद रखो: मछली का धाररेखीय शरीर पानी का कर्षण घटाता है, ताकि तैरना आसान हो।\nगलत मत याद करना: Increase sliding friction with the water पानी से ज़्यादा रगड़ मछली को थका देगी।"},{"id":"s-sound-16","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"Which part of the ear is the thin membrane that vibrates when sound arrives?","options":["The larynx","The pinna, with no membrane farther inside","The eardrum","The retina"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is The eardrum. The outer ear collects sound and guides it along the ear canal. The sound sets the eardrum vibrating. The vibrations are passed inward, and a message goes to the brain, which recognises the sound. The larynx is wrong because the larynx produces sound with the vocal cords and is not the hearing membrane. The pinna, with no membrane farther inside is wrong because the pinna is the outer flap that collects sound, and the vibrating membrane is the eardrum. The retina is wrong because the retina is part of the eye, not the ear.\nयाद रखो: कान का पर्दा पतली झिल्ली है जो आवाज़ आते ही हिलती है। स्वरयंत्र बोलता है, सुनता नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: The larynx आवाज़ बनाता है, कान का हिलता पर्दा नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-17","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"An echo is heard when sound...","options":["Reflects from a surface and comes back to the listener","Is absorbed completely and never returns","Travels through a vacuum and bounces off empty space","Changes into light"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Reflects from a surface and comes back to the listener. Sound can reflect from a cliff, a wall, or a hillside. If the reflected sound returns late enough for the ear to separate it from the original sound, we call it an echo. Soft curtains absorb sound and weaken reflections. Is absorbed completely and never returns is wrong because if nothing returns, there is no echo. Travels through a vacuum and bounces off empty space is wrong because sound cannot travel in a vacuum. Changes into light is wrong because an echo is still a sound, not a beam of light.\nयाद रखो: प्रतिध्वनि तब है जब आवाज़ दीवार या पहाड़ से टकराकर सुनने वाले के पास लौट आए।\nगलत मत याद करना: Travels through a vacuum and bounces off empty space खाली जगह आवाज़ लौटाती नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-18","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"The unit of frequency is the...","options":["Pascal","Decibel","Newton","Hertz"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Hertz. One hertz means one vibration each second, so 200 Hz means 200 vibrations each second, and pitch depends on that frequency. Loudness depends on amplitude instead, and it is expressed in decibels. Pascal is wrong because the pascal is the unit of pressure. Decibel is wrong because the decibel is used for loudness, while frequency is measured in hertz. Newton is wrong because the newton is the unit of force.\nयाद रखो: आवृत्ति की इकाई हर्ट्ज़ है: एक कंपन प्रति सेकंड। डेसिबल ऊँचाई का है, पास्कल दाब का।\nगलत मत याद करना: Pascal दाब की इकाई है, कंपन गिनने की नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-19","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"Ultrasound is sound whose frequency is...","options":["Lower than 20 Hz","Higher than 20,000 Hz","Only between 20 Hz and 20,000 Hz","Exactly zero"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is Higher than 20,000 Hz. Ultra means beyond the hearing range. Humans cannot hear ultrasound, but dogs hear some of it and bats use it to find prey and obstacles. Doctors also use ultrasound to make pictures of organs inside the body. Lower than 20 Hz is wrong because frequencies below 20 Hz are called infrasonic. Only between 20 Hz and 20,000 Hz is wrong because that middle band is the human audible range and is not called ultrasound. Exactly zero is wrong because zero vibrations would not be an ultrasonic wave.\nयाद रखो: पराश्रव्य 20,000 हर्ट्ज़ से ऊपर है। चमगादड़ सुनता है, इंसान नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Lower than 20 Hz अपश्रव्य है, पराश्रव्य नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-20","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"A flute and a violin play the same note at the same loudness, yet they sound different. This difference is called...","options":["An echo","The speed of sound in a vacuum","Quality, or timbre","Noise pollution"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Quality, or timbre. Quality, also called timbre, lets us tell two sounds apart when their pitch and loudness are the same. The pattern of vibration is not the same in every instrument. That is why a flute and a violin can share a note and still sound unlike each other. An echo is wrong because an echo is a reflected repeat, not the difference between two instruments. The speed of sound in a vacuum is wrong because sound has no speed in a vacuum, and that idea does not label the instruments. Noise pollution is wrong because noise pollution is unwanted sound in the surroundings, not the character of one musical note.\nयाद रखो: एक ही तारत्व और ऊँचाई पर बाँसुरी और वायलिन अलग लगें तो वह गुणता या टिम्बर है।\nगलत मत याद करना: An echo दीवार से लौटी आवाज़ है, वाद्य की पहचान नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-21","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"Sound that lingers in a large empty hall because of many reflections is called...","options":["The splitting of white light by a prism","Binary fission","Fertilisation","Reverberation"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Reverberation. In a big bare hall, sound bounces again and again from the walls. The repeated reflections make the sound persist after the source has stopped. Curtains, carpets, and soft panels absorb sound and reduce this reverberation. The splitting of white light by a prism is wrong because a prism splits light, and the lingering of sound is reverberation. Binary fission is wrong because binary fission is the reproduction of Amoeba. Fertilisation is wrong because fertilisation is the fusion of gametes.\nयाद रखो: खाली हॉल में आवाज़ बार-बार टकराकर ठहरी रहे तो उसे अनुनाद या reverberation कहते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Binary fission अमीबा का बँटवारा है, हॉल की गूँज नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-22","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"A clear echo needs a time gap of at least one tenth of a second. If the speed of sound is 340 m/s, what is the least distance to the reflecting wall?","options":["17 m","34 m","68 m","340 m"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is 17 m. Distance equals speed multiplied by time, divided by 2, and the least time is one tenth of a second. 340 multiplied by 1/10 is 34, and 34 divided by 2 is 17, so the wall must be at least 17 m away. 34 m is wrong because 34 is 340 multiplied by one tenth, but the sound must go and return, so that distance is still divided by 2. 68 m is wrong because 68 doubles 34 instead of taking half of the round trip. 340 m is wrong because 340 m is the one-way distance for an echo that takes 2 seconds, not for a gap of one tenth of a second."},{"id":"s-sound-23","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"A louder sound has...","options":["A smaller amplitude","A larger amplitude","A lower frequency and therefore, by itself, a greater loudness","No vibration at all"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is A larger amplitude. If a drum is struck harder, the skin moves farther from its rest position. That larger amplitude sends a louder sound to the ear. A gentle hit gives a small amplitude and a soft sound. A smaller amplitude is wrong because a smaller amplitude makes a softer sound. A lower frequency and therefore, by itself, a greater loudness is wrong because frequency sets pitch, and loudness follows amplitude. No vibration at all is wrong because without vibration there is no sound.\nयाद रखो: ज़ोर की आवाज़ का आयाम बड़ा होता है। ढोल ज़ोर से मारो तो खाल ज़्यादा दूर तक हिलती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A smaller amplitude धीमी आवाज़ देता है, ज़ोर की नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-24","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"A shrill sound differs from a deep sound mainly in...","options":["Loudness only, with no change of frequency","Its speed through a vacuum","Pitch, which rises when the frequency rises","The unit called the pascal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is Pitch, which rises when the frequency rises. A whistle is shrill because it vibrates many times each second, while a deep drum vibrates fewer times, and frequency decides this pitch. Amplitude is a different feature and decides whether the sound is loud or soft. Loudness only, with no change of frequency is wrong because a sound can be shrill whether it is loud or soft, because shrillness is pitch. Its speed through a vacuum is wrong because sound does not travel in a vacuum, and shrillness is not a vacuum speed. The unit called the pascal is wrong because the pascal measures pressure, not pitch.\nयाद रखो: तीखी और भारी आवाज़ का फर्क तारत्व है, और तारत्व आवृत्ति के साथ चढ़ता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Loudness only, with no change of frequency ज़ोर और तीखापन अलग-अलग चीज़ें हैं।"}]},{"id":"mock-2","title":"Full mock 2","kind":"mock","minutes":150,"strict":true,"concept":"Full RMS CET Class 9 paper. 200 questions, 2 hours 30 minutes, no negative marking. English 50, Hindi 20, Social Science 30, Mathematics 50, Science 50. Paper 1 and Paper 2 are marked separately. Each needs 50%.","questions":[{"id":"e-modals-13","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The lights are out and nobody answers, so the speaker is almost certain she is away. Which sentence is correct?","options":["She must to be away","She can to be away","She must is away","She must be away"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She must be away\" because must can show a near certainty based on evidence, and it takes the base form. \"She must to be away\" fails because must is not followed by to. \"She can to be away\" fails because can does not take to, and it would be weaker than this near certainty. \"She must is away\" fails because must is followed by the base form be, not by is."},{"id":"e-modals-14","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Clouds make rain possible, but nobody is certain. Which sentence is correct?","options":["It may rain this afternoon","It must rain this afternoon","It may rains this afternoon","It may to rain this afternoon"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"It may rain this afternoon\" because may shows a real possibility and is followed by the base form. \"It must rain this afternoon\" fails because must would make the rain certain, but the stem says only that it is possible. \"It may rains this afternoon\" fails because may is followed by the base form rain, not rains. \"It may to rain this afternoon\" fails because may is not followed by to."},{"id":"e-modals-15","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"This is a polite request for the time. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Could you to tell me the time, please?","Could you tell me the time, please?","Could you told me the time, please?","Must you tell me the time, please?"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Could you tell me the time, please?\" because could you plus the base form is a polite way to ask someone to do something. \"Could you to tell me the time, please?\" fails because could is not followed by to. \"Could you told me the time, please?\" fails because could takes the base form tell, not told. \"Must you tell me the time, please?\" fails because must you sounds like a complaint about obligation, not a polite request."},{"id":"e-modals-16","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker prefers walking and rejects waiting in the sun. Which sentence is correct?","options":["I would rather to walk than wait in the sun","I would rather walk than to wait in the sun","I would rather walk than wait in the sun","I will rather walk than wait in the sun"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I would rather walk than wait in the sun\" because would rather plus the base form, then than plus another base form, shows preference. \"I would rather to walk than wait in the sun\" fails because would rather is followed by the base form, without to. \"I would rather walk than to wait in the sun\" fails because after than in this pattern, the verb is the base form wait, without to. \"I will rather walk than wait in the sun\" fails because the form is would rather, not will rather."},{"id":"e-modals-17","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker is shocked that someone opened a private letter. Which sentence is correct?","options":["How dare you open my letter?","How dare you to open my letter?","How dares you open my letter?","How dare you opened my letter?"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"How dare you open my letter?\" because how dare you is followed by the base form of the verb. \"How dare you to open my letter?\" fails because dare in this question is followed by the base form, without to. \"How dares you open my letter?\" fails because dare does not take -s before you in this question. \"How dare you opened my letter?\" fails because the verb after dare is the base form open, not opened."},{"id":"e-modals-18","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Wasting food breaks a duty. Which sentence is correct?","options":["You ought not to wasted food","You ought not to waste food","You ought to not wasting food","You must not to waste food"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"You ought not to waste food\" because the negative of ought to is ought not to plus the base form. \"You ought not to wasted food\" fails because after ought not to, the verb is the base form waste. \"You ought to not wasting food\" fails because the negative pattern is ought not to plus the base form, not ought to not wasting. \"You must not to waste food\" fails because must not is a different modal and does not take to."},{"id":"e-modals-19","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The puzzle was too hard for him yesterday. Which sentence is correct?","options":["He cannot solve the puzzle yesterday","He could not solved the puzzle yesterday","He could not solve the puzzle yesterday","He could not to solve the puzzle yesterday"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He could not solve the puzzle yesterday\" because could not is the past negative of can and takes the base form. \"He cannot solve the puzzle yesterday\" fails because cannot is present, but yesterday needs the past form could not. \"He could not solved the puzzle yesterday\" fails because could not is followed by the base form solve. \"He could not to solve the puzzle yesterday\" fails because could not is not followed by to."},{"id":"e-modals-20","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The teacher is refusing permission to leave. Which sentence is correct?","options":["You might not leave before the bell","You may not to leave before the bell","You may not left before the bell","You may not leave before the bell"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"You may not leave before the bell\" because may not can refuse permission. \"You might not leave before the bell\" fails because might not shows a weak possibility, not a refusal of permission. \"You may not to leave before the bell\" fails because may not is followed by the base form, without to. \"You may not left before the bell\" fails because may not takes leave, not left."},{"id":"e-modals-21","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Carrying a raincoat is sensible, but it is not a strict rule. Which sentence is correct?","options":["You must carry a raincoat","You should carry a raincoat","You should to carry a raincoat","You should carries a raincoat"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"You should carry a raincoat\" because should is the modal for advice that is not a strict rule. \"You must carry a raincoat\" fails because must would turn the advice into a strict obligation. \"You should to carry a raincoat\" fails because should is not followed by to. \"You should carries a raincoat\" fails because should takes the base form carry, not carries."},{"id":"e-modals-22","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The question is about what this bird is able to do. Which sentence is correct?","options":["May a penguin fly?","Must a penguin fly?","Can a penguin fly?","Can a penguin flies?"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Can a penguin fly?\" because can is the modal used to ask about ability. \"May a penguin fly?\" fails because may asks about permission or possibility, not about natural ability. \"Must a penguin fly?\" fails because must asks about obligation, not ability. \"Can a penguin flies?\" fails because can is followed by the base form fly, not flies."},{"id":"e-modals-23","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Naina wore no glasses in the past, and that state has changed. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Naina did not used to wear glasses","Naina did not use wear glasses","Naina did not using to wear glasses","Naina did not use to wear glasses"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Naina did not use to wear glasses\" because the negative of used to in this Class 8 pattern is did not use to plus the base form. \"Naina did not used to wear glasses\" fails because after did not, the form is use, not used. \"Naina did not use wear glasses\" fails because to is required in did not use to. \"Naina did not using to wear glasses\" fails because using to is not the negative pattern of used to."},{"id":"e-modals-24","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Running in the corridor is forbidden. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Students must not run in the corridor","Students need not run in the corridor","Students must not to run in the corridor","Students must not ran in the corridor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Students must not run in the corridor\" because must not forbids an action. \"Students need not run in the corridor\" fails because need not would mean running is unnecessary, not that it is forbidden. \"Students must not to run in the corridor\" fails because must not does not take to. \"Students must not ran in the corridor\" fails because must not is followed by the base form run."},{"id":"e-modals-25","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The total matches the check, so the speaker is certain. Which sentence is correct?","options":["This can be the right answer","This must to be the right answer","This must be the right answer","This must is the right answer"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"This must be the right answer\" because must expresses a strong conclusion and is followed by the base form. \"This can be the right answer\" fails because can is only a weak possibility, but the speaker is certain. \"This must to be the right answer\" fails because must is not followed by to. \"This must is the right answer\" fails because must is followed by be, not by is."},{"id":"e-modals-26","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker is asking politely for a drink. Which sentence is correct?","options":["I will like a glass of water","I would like to a glass of water","I would liking a glass of water","I would like a glass of water"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I would like a glass of water\" because would like is a polite way to say what someone wants. \"I will like a glass of water\" fails because will like is not the polite form; the phrase is would like. \"I would like to a glass of water\" fails because would like is followed by the noun here, not by to plus the noun. \"I would liking a glass of water\" fails because would is followed by the base form like, not liking."},{"id":"e-modals-27","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Keeping the room clean is good advice for the class. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We should keep our classroom clean","We should to keep our classroom clean","We should kept our classroom clean","We can kept our classroom clean"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We should keep our classroom clean\" because should plus the base form gives advice. \"We should to keep our classroom clean\" fails because should is not followed by to. \"We should kept our classroom clean\" fails because should takes the base form keep, not kept. \"We can kept our classroom clean\" fails because can also needs the base form, and kept is not that form."},{"id":"e-modals-28","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker is making a very polite request for permission, not asking about a duty. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Might I to ask a question?","Might I ask a question?","Must I ask a question?","Might I asked a question?"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Might I ask a question?\" because might I plus the base form can make a very polite request for permission. \"Might I to ask a question?\" fails because might is not followed by to. \"Must I ask a question?\" fails because must I asks whether the question is obligatory, not for polite permission. \"Might I asked a question?\" fails because might takes the base form ask, not asked."},{"id":"e-modals-29","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker is giving a kind wish, not asking a question about permission. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Might you live long and be happy","May you to live long and be happy","Must you live long and be happy","May you live long and be happy"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"May you live long and be happy\" because may plus the base form can express a wish. \"Might you live long and be happy\" fails because might is not the modal used for this kind of wish. \"May you to live long and be happy\" fails because may in a wish is followed by the base form, without to. \"Must you live long and be happy\" fails because must you would sound like a question of obligation, not a wish."},{"id":"e-modals-30","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"The family no longer lives in the old house, but from there the hills were visible. Which sentence is correct?","options":["From our old house we could see the hills","From our old house we can see the hills","From our old house we could saw the hills","From our old house we could to see the hills"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"From our old house we could see the hills\" because could shows a past ability or past possibility. \"From our old house we can see the hills\" fails because can is present, but the old house belongs to the past. \"From our old house we could saw the hills\" fails because could is followed by the base form see, not saw. \"From our old house we could to see the hills\" fails because could is not followed by to."},{"id":"e-modals-31","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Leaving before the rain is the wiser course, stated with had better. Which sentence is correct?","options":["You had better to leave before the rain starts","You had better leave before the rain starts","You had better left before the rain starts","You have better leave before the rain starts"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"You had better leave before the rain starts\" because had better plus the base form gives strong advice. \"You had better to leave before the rain starts\" fails because had better is followed by the base form, without to. \"You had better left before the rain starts\" fails because had better takes leave, not left. \"You have better leave before the rain starts\" fails because the fixed form is had better, not have better."},{"id":"e-modals-32","topicId":"e-modals","subject":"english","stem":"Apologising to a friend is a duty. Which sentence is correct?","options":["You ought apologise to your friend","You ought to apologises to your friend","You ought to apologise to your friend","You ought to apologised to your friend"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"You ought to apologise to your friend\" because ought to plus the base form expresses duty. \"You ought apologise to your friend\" fails because ought needs to before the base form. \"You ought to apologises to your friend\" fails because after ought to, the verb does not take an -s. \"You ought to apologised to your friend\" fails because apologised is past, but ought to needs the base form."},{"id":"e-errors-13","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The old sailor cannot see with one of his eyes.","options":["The old sailor is blind with one eye","The old sailor is blind from one eye","The old sailor is blind of an one eye","The old sailor is blind in one eye"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The old sailor is blind in one eye\" because blind in one eye is the fixed expression. \"The old sailor is blind with one eye\" fails because the pattern is blind in, not blind with. \"The old sailor is blind from one eye\" fails because from is not the preposition in this description. \"The old sailor is blind of an one eye\" fails because of an one eye is not English; the phrase is blind in one eye."},{"id":"e-errors-14","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The pupils went from outside into the classroom, said without an extra preposition.","options":["The pupils entered the classroom","The pupils entered into the classroom","The pupils entered to the classroom","The pupils entering the classroom"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The pupils entered the classroom\" because enter takes a direct object and does not need into. \"The pupils entered into the classroom\" fails because enter already means go into, so into is not added. \"The pupils entered to the classroom\" fails because enter is not followed by to. \"The pupils entering the classroom\" fails because entering is not a complete past sentence."},{"id":"e-errors-15","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Lata's singing is being praised for its quality.","options":["Lata sings good","Lata sings well","Lata sing well","Lata singing well"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Lata sings well\" because use an adverb, not an adjective, to modify a verb. \"Lata sings good\" fails because a verb such as sings is modified by the adverb well, not by the adjective good. \"Lata sing well\" fails because Lata is third-person singular, so the verb is sings. \"Lata singing well\" fails because singing has no finite verb here."},{"id":"e-errors-16","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The waiting began in the morning and is still going on.","options":["I am waiting here since morning","I have been waiting here from morning","I have been waiting here since morning","I waited here since morning"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I have been waiting here since morning\" because since with a period that reaches the present takes the present perfect or present perfect continuous. \"I am waiting here since morning\" fails because since a starting point that continues to now needs a perfect tense. \"I have been waiting here from morning\" fails because the starting point in this pattern uses since, not from. \"I waited here since morning\" fails because the simple past would mean the waiting is over, but it is still continuing."},{"id":"e-errors-17","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Not one of the two messengers has come.","options":["Neither of the messengers has arrived","Neither of the messengers have arrived","Neither of the messengers are arrived","Neither of the messenger has arrived"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Neither of the messengers has arrived\" because neither of takes a singular verb, and arrive in the perfect uses has arrived. \"Neither of the messengers have arrived\" fails because neither of is singular, so the helper is has, not have. \"Neither of the messengers are arrived\" fails because are arrived is not a present perfect, and neither needs a singular verb. \"Neither of the messenger has arrived\" fails because the noun after neither of must be plural: messengers."},{"id":"e-errors-18","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Vikram is the child of the speaker's uncle or aunt.","options":["Vikram is my cousin brother","Vikram is my cousin","Vikram is my cousin brothers","Vikram are my cousin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Vikram is my cousin\" because say cousin, not cousin brother. \"Vikram is my cousin brother\" fails because cousin already names the relationship, so brother is not added. \"Vikram is my cousin brothers\" fails because brothers is plural and cousin brother is not the correct phrase. \"Vikram are my cousin\" fails because Vikram is singular, so the verb is is, not are."},{"id":"e-errors-19","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The police, treated as a plural body, caught the thief.","options":["The police has arrested the thief","The police is arrested the thief","The police have arrested the thief","The police have arrest the thief"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The police have arrested the thief\" because the noun police is plural and takes have, not has. \"The police has arrested the thief\" fails because police takes a plural verb, so the helper is have, not has. \"The police is arrested the thief\" fails because is arrested is passive and would make the police the people who were arrested. \"The police have arrest the thief\" fails because after have, the present perfect needs the participle arrested."},{"id":"e-errors-20","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Farhan did not make the trip to the fair.","options":["Farhan did not went to the fair","Farhan did not gone to the fair","Farhan did not goes to the fair","Farhan did not go to the fair"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Farhan did not go to the fair\" because did is already the past helper, so the main verb returns to its base form. \"Farhan did not went to the fair\" fails because after did, the verb is the base form go, not went. \"Farhan did not gone to the fair\" fails because gone is a participle and cannot follow did not. \"Farhan did not goes to the fair\" fails because goes adds an -s that must not appear after did."},{"id":"e-errors-21","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Anita spoke to nobody in particular, and at that past moment she was hungry.","options":["Anita told that she was hungry","Anita said that she was hungry","Anita said that she is hungry","Anita told to that she was hungry"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Anita said that she was hungry\" because use said that when there is no listener, and shift the tense after a past reporting verb. \"Anita told that she was hungry\" fails because told needs a listener; without one, the verb is said. \"Anita said that she is hungry\" fails because the hunger belonged to that past moment, so was is the right backshift. \"Anita told to that she was hungry\" fails because told to that is not a reporting pattern."},{"id":"e-errors-22","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Someone should make the lamp start giving light.","options":["Please open the light","Please switch the light","Please switch on the light","Please on the light"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Please switch on the light\" because the verb for a lamp is switch on or turn on, not open. \"Please open the light\" fails because lights are switched on, not opened. \"Please switch the light\" fails because switch needs on or off; switch the light alone is incomplete. \"Please on the light\" fails because on cannot stand as the verb of this request."},{"id":"e-errors-23","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Mother has asked the shop for a sandwich.","options":["Mother has ordered for a sandwich","Mother has ordered to a sandwich","Mother has order a sandwich","Mother has ordered a sandwich"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Mother has ordered a sandwich\" because order is a transitive verb: order a sandwich, not order for a sandwich. \"Mother has ordered for a sandwich\" fails because order takes a direct object and does not need for. \"Mother has ordered to a sandwich\" fails because to is not used between ordered and the thing ordered. \"Mother has order a sandwich\" fails because after has, the participle is ordered, not order."},{"id":"e-errors-24","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The duty belongs to the indefinite person one.","options":["One must do one's duty","One must do his duty","One must do her duty","One must does one's duty"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"One must do one's duty\" because the pronoun one is followed by one's, and must takes the base form. \"One must do his duty\" fails because in this Class 8 pattern, one is matched by one's, not by his. \"One must do her duty\" fails because her changes the indefinite one into a particular gender and breaks the match. \"One must does one's duty\" fails because after must, the verb is the base form do, not does."},{"id":"e-errors-25","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The pony's death happened in an accident, not from a named disease.","options":["The pony died of an accident","The pony died by an accident","The pony died in an accident","The pony was died in an accident"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The pony died in an accident\" because use die in an accident, and do not make die passive. \"The pony died of an accident\" fails because die of is used for a disease, while an accident takes die in. \"The pony died by an accident\" fails because by is not the preposition in this sentence. \"The pony was died in an accident\" fails because die does not form a passive was died."},{"id":"e-errors-26","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The two girls were both in attendance.","options":["The both girls were present","Both of girls were present","Both girl were present","Both girls were present"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Both girls were present\" because say both girls or both of the girls, not the both girls. \"The both girls were present\" fails because the is not placed before both in this pattern. \"Both of girls were present\" fails because both of needs the: both of the girls. \"Both girl were present\" fails because both is followed by a plural noun: girls."},{"id":"e-errors-27","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The speaker locked the cupboard without help, using a proper pronoun.","options":["I locked the cupboard myself","Myself locked the cupboard","Me locked the cupboard myself","I locked the cupboard me"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I locked the cupboard myself\" because the subject is I, and myself can emphasise that the subject did the action. \"Myself locked the cupboard\" fails because myself cannot be the subject of the sentence. \"Me locked the cupboard myself\" fails because the subject pronoun is I, not me. \"I locked the cupboard me\" fails because the emphatic or reflexive pronoun here is myself, not me."},{"id":"e-errors-28","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The doctor recommended rest.","options":["The doctor suggested me to rest","The doctor suggested that I should rest","The doctor suggested me that I should rest","The doctor suggested to rest me"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The doctor suggested that I should rest\" because suggest is followed by a that-clause, not by an object plus to plus a verb. \"The doctor suggested me to rest\" fails because suggest is not followed by a person plus to plus a verb. \"The doctor suggested me that I should rest\" fails because suggest does not take me directly before that. \"The doctor suggested to rest me\" fails because to rest me reverses the meaning and is not the pattern."},{"id":"e-errors-29","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? This cloth is of higher quality than that cloth.","options":["This cloth is superior than that one","This cloth is superior from that one","This cloth is more superior to that one","This cloth is superior to that one"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"This cloth is superior to that one\" because superior, senior, and junior take to, not than, and they are not doubled with more. \"This cloth is superior than that one\" fails because superior is followed by to, not by than. \"This cloth is superior from that one\" fails because from is not the preposition after superior. \"This cloth is more superior to that one\" fails because superior already expresses the higher degree, so more is not added."},{"id":"e-errors-30","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? Captain Sen holds a higher rank than the speaker.","options":["Captain Sen is senior to me","Captain Sen is senior than me","Captain Sen is senior from me","Captain Sen is senior of me"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Captain Sen is senior to me\" because senior to is the correct pattern, just as junior to and superior to are. \"Captain Sen is senior than me\" fails because senior takes to, not than. \"Captain Sen is senior from me\" fails because from is not used after senior. \"Captain Sen is senior of me\" fails because of is not the preposition after senior in this comparison."},{"id":"e-errors-31","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The wish to be on the moon is unreal.","options":["I wish I was on the moon","I wish I were on the moon","I wish I am on the moon","I wish I were be on the moon"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I wish I were on the moon\" because after I wish, an unreal present state uses were for every person, including I. \"I wish I was on the moon\" fails because this Class 8 pattern uses were, not was, after I wish for an unreal desire. \"I wish I am on the moon\" fails because an unreal wish does not stay in the present am. \"I wish I were be on the moon\" fails because were is already the verb, so be must not be added."},{"id":"e-errors-32","topicId":"e-errors","subject":"english","stem":"Which sentence is correct? The witness told what the lane looked like, without an extra preposition.","options":["The witness described about the lane","The witness described of the lane","The witness described the lane","The witness describing the lane"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The witness described the lane\" because describe is transitive: describe the lane, not describe about the lane. \"The witness described about the lane\" fails because describe takes a direct object and does not need about. \"The witness described of the lane\" fails because of is not used after describe in this sentence. \"The witness describing the lane\" fails because describing is not a complete verb for this past report."},{"id":"e-jumbled-13","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: he / worked / hard / and / passed / the / test?","options":["He worked and hard passed the test","He hard worked and the test passed","Worked he hard and passed the test","He worked hard and passed the test"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He worked hard and passed the test\" because and joins two matching actions, with each object or adverb next to its own verb. \"He worked and hard passed the test\" fails because hard must stay with worked, and and must join the two verb phrases. \"He hard worked and the test passed\" fails because hard should follow worked, and the test should follow passed. \"Worked he hard and passed the test\" fails because the subject he must come before worked."},{"id":"e-jumbled-14","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: the / teacher / told / us / to / sit / down?","options":["The teacher told us to sit down","The teacher told to us sit down","Told the teacher us to sit down","The teacher us told to sit down"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The teacher told us to sit down\" because told is followed by the person and then by to plus the base verb. \"The teacher told to us sit down\" fails because told is followed by us and then by to sit, not by to us sit. \"Told the teacher us to sit down\" fails because the statement cannot begin with told before the subject. \"The teacher us told to sit down\" fails because us cannot stand between the subject and told."},{"id":"e-jumbled-15","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: we / saw / three / elephants / in / the / forest?","options":["We saw elephants three in the forest","We saw three elephants in the forest","Saw we three elephants in the forest","We saw three in elephants the forest"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We saw three elephants in the forest\" because the number comes before the noun, and the place phrase keeps its preposition next to its noun. \"We saw elephants three in the forest\" fails because the number three must come before elephants. \"Saw we three elephants in the forest\" fails because the subject we must come before the verb. \"We saw three in elephants the forest\" fails because in the forest must stay together as the place phrase."},{"id":"e-jumbled-16","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: please / give / me / a / glass / of / water?","options":["Give please me a glass of water","Please me give a glass of water","Please give me a glass of water","Please give a me glass of water"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Please give me a glass of water\" because please plus the base verb is followed by the indirect object and then the direct object. \"Give please me a glass of water\" fails because please should come before the request, not between give and me. \"Please me give a glass of water\" fails because the verb give must come before the person me. \"Please give a me glass of water\" fails because a must come before glass, and me should follow give directly."},{"id":"e-jumbled-17","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: honesty / is / the / best / policy?","options":["Honesty is the best policy","Honesty the best is policy","The best honesty is policy","Honesty is best the policy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Honesty is the best policy\" because a complement follows the linking verb, and the comes before a superlative adjective. \"Honesty the best is policy\" fails because is must come before the complement the best policy. \"The best honesty is policy\" fails because the best must describe policy, not honesty. \"Honesty is best the policy\" fails because the must come before the superlative best."},{"id":"e-jumbled-18","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: she / speaks / English / very / well?","options":["She speaks very English well","She speaks English very well","Speaks she English very well","She very speaks English well"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She speaks English very well\" because the object follows the verb, and very comes immediately before the adverb well. \"She speaks very English well\" fails because very must modify well, not sit between speaks and English. \"Speaks she English very well\" fails because the subject must come before the verb. \"She very speaks English well\" fails because very does not modify the verb speaks; it belongs with well."},{"id":"e-jumbled-19","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: I / have / never / seen / the / sea?","options":["I have seen never the sea","I seen have never the sea","I have never seen the sea","Have I seen the never sea"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I have never seen the sea\" because in the present perfect, never usually comes after have or has and before the past participle. \"I have seen never the sea\" fails because never stands between have and the past participle, not after seen. \"I seen have never the sea\" fails because have must come before seen. \"Have I seen the never sea\" fails because never cannot sit inside the noun phrase the sea."},{"id":"e-jumbled-20","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: he / put / the / books / on / the / shelf?","options":["He put on the books the shelf","Put he the books on the shelf","He the books put on the shelf","He put the books on the shelf"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He put the books on the shelf\" because the object follows the verb, and the place phrase begins with on. \"He put on the books the shelf\" fails because on the shelf must stay together after the object. \"Put he the books on the shelf\" fails because the subject must come before the verb. \"He the books put on the shelf\" fails because the object should follow put, not come before it."},{"id":"e-jumbled-21","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: the / captain / of / our / team / scored / a / goal?","options":["The captain scored of our team a goal","The captain of our team scored a goal","The of captain our team scored a goal","Scored the captain of our team a goal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The captain of our team scored a goal\" because a phrase such as of our team follows the noun it describes, and the object follows the verb. \"The captain scored of our team a goal\" fails because of our team must stay with captain, not follow scored. \"The of captain our team scored a goal\" fails because of is in the wrong place, so the noun phrase is broken. \"Scored the captain of our team a goal\" fails because the statement should not begin with the verb."},{"id":"e-jumbled-22","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: they / are / going / to / the / market / now?","options":["They going are to the market now","They are to going the market now","They are going to the market now","Going they are to the market now"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"They are going to the market now\" because the present continuous places are before the -ing form, and to the market is the place phrase. \"They going are to the market now\" fails because are must come before going. \"They are to going the market now\" fails because to the market must stay together, and going comes before that phrase. \"Going they are to the market now\" fails because the subject should begin this statement."},{"id":"h-samas-17","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«सुख-दुख» में कौन-सा समास है?","options":["द्वंद्व","तत्पुरुष","बहुव्रीहि","कर्मधारय"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is द्वंद्व because सुख and दुख are both equally present, joy and sorrow together, so the compound is द्वंद्व. तत्पुरुष is wrong because तत्पुरुष would make दुख the only head with a case relation, and both words stay equal. बहुव्रीहि is wrong because बहुव्रीहि would point to a third thing, and सुख-दुख means the joy and the sorrow themselves. कर्मधारय is wrong because कर्मधारय would need one word to describe the other, and सुख is not an adjective of दुख."},{"id":"h-samas-18","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«विद्या + आलय» की सही संधि कौन-सी है?","options":["विद्यआलय","विद्यालय","विद्यायलय","विद्यलय"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is विद्यालय because विद्या ends in आ and आलय begins with आ. आ plus आ becomes आ, so the join is विद्यालय. विद्यआलय is wrong because विद्यआलय keeps both vowels side by side and does not make the required long-vowel sandhi. विद्यायलय is wrong because विद्यायलय inserts an extra य that this आ plus आ join does not need. विद्यलय is wrong because विद्यलय drops a necessary आ and is not the sandhi of these two words."},{"id":"h-samas-19","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«सूर्य + उदय» की सही संधि कौन-सी है?","options":["सूर्यउदय","सूर्यादय","सूर्योदय","सूर्युदय"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is सूर्योदय because सूर्य ends in अ and उदय begins with उ. अ plus उ becomes ओ, so the word is सूर्योदय. सूर्यउदय is wrong because सूर्यउदय leaves the two vowels unjoined. सूर्यादय is wrong because सूर्यादय would be the result of अ plus आ, which is not the vowel at the start of उदय. सूर्युदय is wrong because सूर्युदय uses उ instead of the गुण vowel ओ required by अ plus उ."},{"id":"h-samas-20","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«नदी + ईश» की सही संधि कौन-सी है?","options":["नदीईश","नदेश","नदीयश","नदीश"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is नदीश because नदी ends in ई and ईश begins with ई. ई plus ई becomes ई, so the join is नदीश. नदीईश is wrong because नदीईश keeps both ई vowels separate and misses the sandhi. नदेश is wrong because नदेश changes the first vowel and drops the long ई of नदी. नदीयश is wrong because नदीयश adds a य and changes ईश into यश, which this sandhi does not do."},{"id":"h-samas-21","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«हिम + आलय» की सही संधि कौन-सी है?","options":["हिमालय","हिमाआलय","हिमालय्य","हिमाल्य"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is हिमालय because हिम ends in अ and आलय begins with आ. अ plus आ becomes आ, so the word is हिमालय. हिमाआलय is wrong because हिमाआलय writes both vowels instead of joining them into one आ. हिमालय्य is wrong because हिमालय्य adds an extra य at the end that the two words do not have. हिमाल्य is wrong because हिमाल्य drops the final अ of आलय and shortens the word wrongly."},{"id":"h-samas-22","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«महा + ईश» की सही संधि कौन-सी है?","options":["महाईश","महेश","महीश","महोश"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is महेश because महा ends in आ and ईश begins with ई. आ plus ई becomes ए, so the word is महेश. महाईश is wrong because महाईश leaves आ and ई unjoined. महीश is wrong because महीश would come from a different vowel change, not from आ plus ई. महोश is wrong because महोश would be the join of आ plus उ, and ईश begins with ई, not उ."},{"id":"h-samas-23","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«सु + आगत» की सही संधि कौन-सी है?","options":["सुआगत","सौगत","स्वागत","स्वागात"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is स्वागत because सु ends in उ and आगत begins with आ. उ plus आ becomes वा, so the word is स्वागत. सुआगत is wrong because सुआगत leaves the two vowels side by side and does not make the यण sandhi. सौगत is wrong because सौगत uses औ, which would be a different vowel join, not उ plus आ. स्वागात is wrong because स्वागात moves the vowels and does not match सु plus आगत."},{"id":"h-samas-24","topicId":"h-samas","subject":"hindi","stem":"«महा + उत्सव» की सही संधि कौन-सी है?","options":["महाउत्सव","महौत्सव","महुत्सव","महोत्सव"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is महोत्सव because महा ends in आ and उत्सव begins with उ. आ plus उ becomes ओ, so the word is महोत्सव. महाउत्सव is wrong because महाउत्सव keeps आ and उ separate instead of joining them. महौत्सव is wrong because महौत्सव uses औ, and आ plus उ does not become औ. महुत्सव is wrong because महुत्सव keeps उ and drops the required ओ from आ plus उ."},{"id":"h-idioms-13","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«आग में घी डालना» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["झगड़े को और बढ़ाना","भोजन को स्वादिष्ट बनाना","जलती आग को बुझाना","सर्दी में शरीर तपाना"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is झगड़े को और बढ़ाना because adding ghee to a fire makes it flare up, and the idiom means to make a quarrel worse. भोजन को स्वादिष्ट बनाना is wrong because भोजन को स्वादिष्ट बनाना is the literal kitchen use of ghee, not the idiom. जलती आग को बुझाना is wrong because जलती आग को बुझाना is the opposite of feeding a fire. सर्दी में शरीर तपाना is wrong because सर्दी में शरीर तपाना is about getting warm, and the idiom is about worsening a conflict."},{"id":"h-idioms-14","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«आस्तीन का साँप» किसे कहते हैं?","options":["जंगल में रहने वाला साँप","अपनों में छिपा शत्रु","बहादुर सैनिक","सीधा-सादा मित्र"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is अपनों में छिपा शत्रु because a snake kept in the sleeve is an enemy who stays close and then harms you. जंगल में रहने वाला साँप is wrong because जंगल में रहने वाला साँप is only a literal snake and not a traitor in one's own circle. बहादुर सैनिक is wrong because बहादुर सैनिक is a brave fighter, not a hidden enemy. सीधा-सादा मित्र is wrong because सीधा-सादा मित्र is a simple honest friend, the opposite of this idiom."},{"id":"h-idioms-15","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«नाक में दम करना» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["सुगंध से प्रसन्न होना","नाक ऊँची रखना","बहुत तंग करना","गहरी साँस लेना"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is बहुत तंग करना because नाक में दम करना means to pester someone until that person is fed up. सुगंध से प्रसन्न होना is wrong because सुगंध से प्रसन्न होना is about enjoying a fragrance, not about harassment. नाक ऊँची रखना is wrong because नाक ऊँची रखना suggests pride, and this idiom is about annoying someone. गहरी साँस लेना is wrong because गहरी साँस लेना is ordinary breathing and not the idiom."},{"id":"h-idioms-16","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«दाँतों तले उँगली दबाना» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["दाँत साफ करना","चुपचाप भोजन करना","गुस्सा दिखाकर चिल्लाना","बहुत चकित होना"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is बहुत चकित होना because pressing a finger under the teeth is the picture of great surprise. दाँत साफ करना is wrong because दाँत साफ करना is brushing the teeth and misses the idiomatic surprise. चुपचाप भोजन करना is wrong because चुपचाप भोजन करना is eating quietly, and the idiom is not about a meal. गुस्सा दिखाकर चिल्लाना is wrong because गुस्सा दिखाकर चिल्लाना is anger, whereas this idiom is astonishment."},{"id":"h-idioms-17","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«नाच न जाने आँगन टेढ़ा» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["अपनी कमी का दोष दूसरे पर लगाना","आँगन को समतल कर देना","बहुत अच्छा नृत्य करना","मेहमान का स्वागत करना"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is अपनी कमी का दोष दूसरे पर लगाना because a person who cannot dance blames the courtyard, so the proverb means shifting the blame for one's own lack of skill. आँगन को समतल कर देना is wrong because आँगन को समतल कर देना takes the courtyard literally and misses the lesson. बहुत अच्छा नृत्य करना is wrong because बहुत अच्छा नृत्य करना is the opposite of not knowing how to dance. मेहमान का स्वागत करना is wrong because मेहमान का स्वागत करना is hospitality and not this proverb."},{"id":"h-idioms-18","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«नीम हकीम खतरे जान» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["नीम की पत्तियाँ सदा लाभ करती हैं","अधूरा वैद्य जीवन के लिए खतरनाक होता है","अच्छा चिकित्सक रोगी बचाता है","हकीम केवल बाजार में बैठता है"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is अधूरा वैद्य जीवन के लिए खतरनाक होता है because a half-trained healer can put a life in danger, which is the meaning of this proverb. नीम की पत्तियाँ सदा लाभ करती हैं is wrong because नीम की पत्तियाँ सदा लाभ करती हैं talks about the neem plant as medicine and misses the warning. अच्छा चिकित्सक रोगी बचाता है is wrong because अच्छा चिकित्सक रोगी बचाता है describes a skilled doctor, not a quack. हकीम केवल बाजार में बैठता है is wrong because हकीम केवल बाजार में बैठता है describes a place of work and not the danger of poor skill."},{"id":"h-idioms-19","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«अपने पैरों पर कुल्हाड़ी मारना» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["जंगल में लकड़ी काटना","बहुत तेज दौड़ना","स्वयं अपनी हानि कर लेना","परिश्रम से सफलता पाना"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is स्वयं अपनी हानि कर लेना because striking one's own feet with an axe means harming one's own interest. जंगल में लकड़ी काटना is wrong because जंगल में लकड़ी काटना is literal woodcutting and not self-harm. बहुत तेज दौड़ना is wrong because बहुत तेज दौड़ना is running fast, and the idiom is not about speed. परिश्रम से सफलता पाना is wrong because परिश्रम से सफलता पाना is a good result, while the idiom is about causing one's own loss."},{"id":"h-idioms-20","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«ऊँट के मुँह में जीरा» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["ऊँट के लिए पूरा चारा","बहुत स्वादिष्ट दावत","बड़ी रकम की बचत","जरूरत की तुलना में बहुत कम चीज"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is जरूरत की तुलना में बहुत कम चीज because a pinch of cumin in a camel's mouth is far too little for the need. ऊँट के लिए पूरा चारा is wrong because ऊँट के लिए पूरा चारा would be enough fodder, the opposite of a tiny amount. बहुत स्वादिष्ट दावत is wrong because बहुत स्वादिष्ट दावत is a rich feast, not a hopelessly small portion. बड़ी रकम की बचत is wrong because बड़ी रकम की बचत is a large saving, and the proverb is about something too small."},{"id":"h-idioms-21","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«मुँह में राम, बगल में छूरी» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["ऊपर से भला और अंदर से घातक","भक्ति में लीन साधु","रसोई में व्यस्त रसोइया","रणभूमि का साहसी योद्धा"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is ऊपर से भला और अंदर से घातक because the name of Ram is on the lips while a knife is hidden under the arm, so the person looks good and means harm. भक्ति में लीन साधु is wrong because भक्ति में लीन साधु would be a genuinely devout person, and the proverb is about hypocrisy. रसोई में व्यस्त रसोइया is wrong because रसोई में व्यस्त रसोइया takes the knife as a kitchen tool and misses the hidden harm. रणभूमि का साहसी योद्धा is wrong because रणभूमि का साहसी योद्धा is open bravery, not a friendly face hiding a weapon."},{"id":"h-idioms-22","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«खोदा पहाड़ निकली चुहिया» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["पहाड़ पर चूहों का बसेरा","बहुत मेहनत का बहुत छोटा परिणाम","कड़ी मेहनत का बहुत बड़ा लाभ","खेत में चूहों का उपद्रव"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is बहुत मेहनत का बहुत छोटा परिणाम because digging up a whole mountain and finding only a mouse means a huge effort with a tiny result. पहाड़ पर चूहों का बसेरा is wrong because पहाड़ पर चूहों का बसेरा is a literal nest of mice and not the proverb. कड़ी मेहनत का बहुत बड़ा लाभ is wrong because कड़ी मेहनत का बहुत बड़ा लाभ is the opposite outcome, a large reward. खेत में चूहों का उपद्रव is wrong because खेत में चूहों का उपद्रव is a farming problem, not the lesson about wasted effort."},{"id":"h-idioms-23","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"इनमें कौन-सी पंक्ति लोकोक्ति है?","options":["आँखों का तारा","नौ दो ग्यारह होना","जैसे को तैसा","नाक में दम करना"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is जैसे को तैसा because जैसे को तैसा is a complete saying with its own lesson, so it is a लोकोक्ति. आँखों का तारा is wrong because आँखों का तारा is a मुहावरा and needs to be placed inside a sentence, such as वह आँखों का तारा है. नौ दो ग्यारह होना is wrong because नौ दो ग्यारह होना is a मुहावरा for fleeing, not a full proverb by itself. नाक में दम करना is wrong because नाक में दम करना is a मुहावरा meaning to pester, and it is completed only inside a sentence."},{"id":"h-idioms-24","topicId":"h-idioms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«कान भरना» मुहावरे का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["कान में तेल डालना","ध्यान से बात सुनना","ऊँची आवाज में बोलना","किसी के विरुद्ध चुगली करना"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is किसी के विरुद्ध चुगली करना because कान भरना means to poison someone's ears by backbiting against another person. कान में तेल डालना is wrong because कान में तेल डालना is a literal home remedy and not the idiom. ध्यान से बात सुनना is wrong because ध्यान से बात सुनना is careful listening, whereas the idiom is instigation. ऊँची आवाज में बोलना is wrong because ऊँची आवाज में बोलना is speaking loudly and does not mean carrying tales."},{"id":"t-constitution-13","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"The Right to Constitutional Remedies allows a citizen to","options":["move the courts if a Fundamental Right is violated","cancel the Constitution by a private letter","appoint the Prime Minister alone","close the Supreme Court"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is move the courts if a Fundamental Right is violated because this right lets a person ask the courts to enforce the other Fundamental Rights. Dr Ambedkar called it the heart and soul of the Constitution. cancel the Constitution by a private letter is wrong because a private letter cannot cancel the Constitution. appoint the Prime Minister alone is wrong because the Prime Minister is chosen through the parliamentary majority, not by one citizen's letter. close the Supreme Court is wrong because the remedy uses the courts. It does not close them.\nयाद रखो: संवैधानिक उपचार: मूल अधिकार टूटे तो नागरिक अदालत जा सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: cancel the Constitution by a private letter निजी चिट्ठी से संविधान रद्द नहीं होता।"},{"id":"t-constitution-14","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"Directive Principles differ from Fundamental Rights because they","options":["are the only rules a court is allowed to enforce","guide the government but are not directly enforceable by a court in the same way","were issued by the East India Company in 1757","replace the Constitution"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is guide the government but are not directly enforceable by a court in the same way because Directive Principles are instructions for governance. A citizen cannot enforce them in court as Fundamental Rights are enforced. are the only rules a court is allowed to enforce is wrong because it is the Fundamental Rights, not the Directive Principles, that the courts directly enforce. were issued by the East India Company in 1757 is wrong because they are part of the Indian Constitution, not a Company order of 1757. replace the Constitution is wrong because they sit inside the Constitution. They do not replace it.\nयाद रखो: नीति निर्देशक सिद्धांत सरकार का मार्गदर्शन करते हैं, अदालत से मूल अधिकारों की तरह सीधे लागू नहीं होते।\nगलत मत याद करना: are the only rules a court is allowed to enforce अदालत सीधे मूल अधिकार लागू करती है, सिर्फ निर्देशक सिद्धांत नहीं।"},{"id":"t-constitution-15","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"The Indian Constitution came into effect on","options":["15 August 1947","26 January 1930","26 January 1950","10 May 1857"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is 26 January 1950 because 26 January 1950 is the day the Constitution commenced, which is why it is celebrated as Republic Day. 15 August 1947 is wrong because 15 August 1947 is Independence Day, when British rule ended, not the day the Constitution came into effect. 26 January 1930 is wrong because 26 January 1930 was an earlier independence pledge, not the commencement of this Constitution. 10 May 1857 is wrong because 10 May 1857 is the start of the Meerut rising.\nयाद रखो: संविधान लागू 26 जनवरी 1950 को हुआ। 15 अगस्त 1947 आज़ादी है, गणतंत्र दिवस नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: 15 August 1947 पंद्रह अगस्त आज़ादी है। संविधान की ताकत 26 जनवरी 1950 को आई।"},{"id":"t-constitution-16","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"The Constituent Assembly adopted the Constitution on","options":["26 January 1950","13 April 1919","12 March 1930","26 November 1949"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is 26 November 1949 because the Assembly adopted the Constitution on 26 November 1949, and it came into effect later, on 26 January 1950. 26 January 1950 is wrong because 26 January 1950 is the date it came into force, not the date it was adopted. 13 April 1919 is wrong because 13 April 1919 is the date of the Jallianwala Bagh firing. 12 March 1930 is wrong because 12 March 1930 is the day the Salt March began.\nयाद रखो: संविधान सभा ने संविधान 26 नवम्बर 1949 को अंगीकृत किया। लागू 26 जनवरी 1950 को हुआ।\nगलत मत याद करना: 26 January 1950 यह लागू होने का दिन है, अंगीकार का नहीं।"},{"id":"t-constitution-17","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"Dr B.R. Ambedkar was","options":["Chairman of the Drafting Committee of the Constitution","the first Viceroy of India","the Nawab of Bengal defeated at Plassey","the founder of the East India Company"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is Chairman of the Drafting Committee of the Constitution because the Constituent Assembly appointed Dr Ambedkar to chair the committee that drafted the Constitution. the first Viceroy of India is wrong because Lord Canning became the first Viceroy in 1858. the Nawab of Bengal defeated at Plassey is wrong because Siraj-ud-daulah was the Nawab defeated at Plassey. the founder of the East India Company is wrong because the Company received its charter in 1600, long before Ambedkar.\nयाद रखो: डॉ. आंबेडकर संविधान की प्रारूप समिति के अध्यक्ष थे। पहला वायसराय कैनिंग था।\nगलत मत याद करना: the first Viceroy of India पहला वायसराय लॉर्ड कैनिंग बना, आंबेडकर नहीं।"},{"id":"t-constitution-18","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"Dr Rajendra Prasad is remembered here as","options":["Chairman of the Drafting Committee","President of the Constituent Assembly","the general who ordered the firing at Jallianwala Bagh","the Mughal emperor exiled after 1857"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is President of the Constituent Assembly because Dr Rajendra Prasad presided over the Constituent Assembly. He should not be confused with Dr Ambedkar, who chaired the Drafting Committee. Chairman of the Drafting Committee is wrong because the Drafting Committee was chaired by Dr B.R. Ambedkar. the general who ordered the firing at Jallianwala Bagh is wrong because General Dyer ordered the firing at Jallianwala Bagh. the Mughal emperor exiled after 1857 is wrong because Bahadur Shah Zafar was the emperor exiled to Rangoon.\nयाद रखो: डॉ. राजेंद्र प्रसाद संविधान सभा के अध्यक्ष थे। प्रारूप समिति आंबेडकर की थी।\nगलत मत याद करना: Chairman of the Drafting Committee प्रारूप समिति की कुर्सी आंबेडकर की थी, प्रसाद की नहीं।"},{"id":"t-constitution-19","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"A law that violates Fundamental Rights can be","options":["placed above the Constitution","hidden from every judge","struck down by the courts","turned automatically into a Fundamental Right"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is struck down by the courts because judicial review allows the courts to declare such a law void because the Constitution is higher than an ordinary law. placed above the Constitution is wrong because no ordinary law stands above the Constitution. hidden from every judge is wrong because courts exist to examine laws. They are not barred from seeing them. turned automatically into a Fundamental Right is wrong because a law that breaks a right is invalid. It does not become a right.\nयाद रखो: जो कानून मूल अधिकार तोड़े, अदालत उसे रद्द कर सकती है। संविधान से ऊपर कोई साधारण कानून नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: placed above the Constitution साधारण कानून संविधान के सिंहासन पर नहीं बैठता।"},{"id":"t-constitution-20","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"Secularism, as a feature of this Constitution, means that","options":["the state must promote only one faith","all religious belief is banned","only soldiers may worship","the state does not set up any one religion as the official religion"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is the state does not set up any one religion as the official religion because the Indian state has no official religion and must treat citizens of every faith as equals. the state must promote only one faith is wrong because promoting one faith as the state religion would contradict secularism. all religious belief is banned is wrong because secularism is not a ban on belief. only soldiers may worship is wrong because freedom of religion belongs to the people, not only to soldiers.\nयाद रखो: पंथनिरपेक्षता: राज्य किसी एक धर्म को राजधर्म नहीं बनाता। विश्वास पर रोक नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: all religious belief is banned सारा धार्मिक विश्वास मना करना पंथनिरपेक्षता नहीं।"},{"id":"t-constitution-21","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"The Preamble of the Constitution opens with the words","options":["We, the People of India","By order of the East India Company","Doctrine of Lapse","Swaraj is my birthright"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is We, the People of India because the Preamble begins 'We, the People of India', showing that the authority of the Constitution comes from the people. By order of the East India Company is wrong because the Company did not issue the Preamble. Doctrine of Lapse is wrong because the Doctrine of Lapse was a colonial annexation policy. Swaraj is my birthright is wrong because Tilak's line belongs to the national movement, not to the opening of the Preamble.\nयाद रखो: प्रस्तावना के पहले शब्द हैं: हम, भारत के लोग। कंपनी का आदेश नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: By order of the East India Company ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी का हुक्म प्रस्तावना नहीं खोलता।"},{"id":"t-constitution-22","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"Which pairing of organs is correct?","options":["The judiciary collects the land revenue of Bengal","The legislature makes laws, and the judiciary interprets them","The executive carves Ashoka's edicts","The legislature commands the sepoys at Meerut"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is The legislature makes laws, and the judiciary interprets them because Parliament and the state legislatures make laws, while courts interpret the laws and the Constitution. The judiciary collects the land revenue of Bengal is wrong because collecting Bengal's revenue was the Company's Diwani, not the work of today's judiciary. The executive carves Ashoka's edicts is wrong because Ashoka's edicts are ancient inscriptions, not the job of the modern executive. The legislature commands the sepoys at Meerut is wrong because the Meerut sepoys belong to the revolt of 1857, not to the legislature.\nयाद रखो: विधायिका कानून बनाती है, न्यायपालिका उनका अर्थ लगाती है। दीवानी राजस्व अदालत नहीं वसूलती।\nगलत मत याद करना: The judiciary collects the land revenue of Bengal बंगाल की दीवानी आज की अदालत का काम नहीं।"},{"id":"t-constitution-23","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"Fundamental Rights matter in daily life because","options":["they are secret notes with no legal force","they apply only inside one princely state of the 1840s","the courts can enforce them when they are broken","they allow the practice of untouchability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is the courts can enforce them when they are broken because a citizen can approach a court, especially under the Right to Constitutional Remedies, if a Fundamental Right is violated. they are secret notes with no legal force is wrong because these rights are public constitutional guarantees, not secret notes. they apply only inside one princely state of the 1840s is wrong because they protect people throughout India today, not one old princely state. they allow the practice of untouchability is wrong because Article 17 abolishes untouchability, so the rights do not allow it.\nयाद रखो: मूल अधिकार रोज़मर्रा में इसलिए मायने रखते हैं क्योंकि टूटने पर अदालत उन्हें लागू कर सकती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: they allow the practice of untouchability अस्पृश्यता ये अधिकार नहीं देते। अनुच्छेद 17 उसे मिटाता है।"},{"id":"t-constitution-24","topicId":"t-constitution","subject":"sst","stem":"The Indian Constitution was framed by","options":["the English East India Company in 1600","General Dyer in 1919","the Viceroy alone, with no Indian members","the Constituent Assembly"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is the Constituent Assembly because a Constituent Assembly of Indian representatives drafted the Constitution between 1946 and 1949. the English East India Company in 1600 is wrong because the Company of 1600 was a trading corporation, not the maker of this Constitution. General Dyer in 1919 is wrong because General Dyer ordered the Jallianwala Bagh firing. He did not frame the Constitution. the Viceroy alone, with no Indian members is wrong because Indians in the Assembly, including the Drafting Committee, wrote it. It was not the Viceroy's solo work.\nयाद रखो: भारतीय संविधान संविधान सभा ने बनाया। 1600 की कंपनी या जनरल डायर ने नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: General Dyer in 1919 जनरल डायर 1919 जलियाँवाला बाग के हैं, संविधान के लेखक नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-13","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Indian secularism also tries to stop domination","options":["inside a religion, as when untouchability was banned","of pupils who study mathematics","of farmers who plough along the contour","of judges who hear a civil dispute"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is inside a religion, as when untouchability was banned because the ban on untouchability protects people inside a religious community from oppression by others of the same broad tradition. of pupils who study mathematics is wrong because mathematics is not a religious domination. of farmers who plough along the contour is wrong because contour ploughing is a soil method. of judges who hear a civil dispute is wrong because a civil judge's work is not this kind of religious domination.\nयाद रखो: हावी होना धर्म के अंदर भी रोका जाता है, जैसे अस्पृश्यता पर रोक।\nगलत मत याद करना: of pupils who study mathematics गणित पढ़ने वाले विद्यार्थी इस हावी होने की मिसाल नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-14","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"In a secular state the majority community","options":["has a right to make its faith the official religion","must not use the state to impose its religion on others","alone may be recruited to public jobs","stands above the Constitution"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is must not use the state to impose its religion on others because numbers do not give a community the right to capture the state for its own faith. has a right to make its faith the official religion is wrong because an official religion would contradict Indian secularism. alone may be recruited to public jobs is wrong because public employment is open across religions. stands above the Constitution is wrong because every community is under the Constitution.\nयाद रखो: पंथनिरपेक्ष राज्य में बहुसंख्यक अपनी आस्था दूसरों पर राज्य से नहीं थोप सकते।\nगलत मत याद करना: has a right to make its faith the official religion अपनी आस्था को राजधर्म बनाने का हक नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-15","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"A person of any faith has the right to","options":["be punished merely for holding it","be refused a public school only because of it","follow and practise that faith","lose the vote because of a place of worship"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is follow and practise that faith because freedom of religion protects the practice of faith for every community. be punished merely for holding it is wrong because punishing belief itself would destroy that freedom. be refused a public school only because of it is wrong because a public school may not shut its door on religious grounds. lose the vote because of a place of worship is wrong because the vote is not taken away because of a place of worship.\nयाद रखो: किसी भी आस्था का व्यक्ति उस आस्था को मान और उसका आचरण कर सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: be punished merely for holding it सिर्फ आस्था रखने पर सज़ा यह अधिकार नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-16","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Which action fits Indian secularism?","options":["The state chooses one official religion","The state shuts every place of worship forever","The state gives government jobs to only one community","The state stops a religious practice that violates fundamental rights"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is The state stops a religious practice that violates fundamental rights because intervention is allowed when a practice, such as untouchability, breaks fundamental rights. The state chooses one official religion is wrong because choosing an official religion abandons secularism. The state shuts every place of worship forever is wrong because closing every place of worship would be hostility to religion. The state gives government jobs to only one community is wrong because jobs reserved for one religion are discrimination.\nयाद रखो: जो प्रथा मूल अधिकार तोड़े, राज्य उसे रोके। यही भारतीय पंथनिरपेक्षता में बैठता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: The state chooses one official religion एक राजधर्म चुनना इस विचार में नहीं बैठता।"},{"id":"t-secularism-17","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Which action does not fit Indian secularism?","options":["Hostility that tries to wipe out all religious belief","Equal respect for people of every religion","A legal ban on untouchability","State support for a minority school"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is Hostility that tries to wipe out all religious belief because Indian secularism is not an attack on faith itself. Equal respect for people of every religion is wrong because equal respect is the heart of this idea. A legal ban on untouchability is wrong because the ban on untouchability is an accepted intervention. State support for a minority school is wrong because support for a minority school is part of the Indian approach.\nयाद रखो: जो दुश्मनी सारा धार्मिक विश्वास मिटाना चाहे, वह भारतीय पंथनिरपेक्षता में नहीं बैठती।\nगलत मत याद करना: Equal respect for people of every religion हर धर्म के लोगों का समान सम्मान इसमें बैठता है।"},{"id":"t-secularism-18","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Government offices should","options":["display the rites of only one faith as the state faith","not be used to promote one religion","refuse entry to people of a minority religion","collect a special tax from people who pray"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is not be used to promote one religion because law courts, police stations, and government offices must not become advertisements for one religion. display the rites of only one faith as the state faith is wrong because promoting one faith as the state faith breaks secularism. refuse entry to people of a minority religion is wrong because entry to a public office cannot depend on religion. collect a special tax from people who pray is wrong because a prayer tax would discriminate on the ground of religion.\nयाद रखो: सरकारी दफ्तर एक धर्म का प्रचार करने के लिए इस्तेमाल नहीं होने चाहिए।\nगलत मत याद करना: display the rites of only one faith as the state faith एक आस्था को राजधर्म की तरह दिखाना दफ्तर का काम नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-19","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Principled distance means that the state","options":["merges itself with one religion","bans every private belief","stays apart from religion without becoming the enemy of faith","lets one shrine write the criminal law"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is stays apart from religion without becoming the enemy of faith because the state neither runs a religion nor persecutes religious people. merges itself with one religion is wrong because merging with one religion would create a state religion. bans every private belief is wrong because private belief remains free. lets one shrine write the criminal law is wrong because criminal law is made by the legislature under the Constitution, not by a shrine.\nयाद रखो: सिद्धांत की दूरी: राज्य धर्म से अलग रहे, पर आस्था का दुश्मन न बने।\nगलत मत याद करना: merges itself with one religion एक धर्म में मिल जाना दूरी नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-20","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Opening public jobs to people of every religion supports","options":["the rule that only one religion may serve the government","the Doctrine of Lapse","the practice of untouchability","equality of citizens regardless of faith"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is equality of citizens regardless of faith because equal access to public employment is part of not discriminating on the ground of religion. the rule that only one religion may serve the government is wrong because limiting jobs to one religion would be discrimination. the Doctrine of Lapse is wrong because the Doctrine of Lapse was a colonial annexation policy. the practice of untouchability is wrong because untouchability is abolished and is not supported by equal jobs.\nयाद रखो: हर धर्म के लोगों के लिए सार्वजनिक नौकरियाँ नागरिकों की समानता को सहारा देती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the practice of untouchability अस्पृश्यता समानता नहीं, वह मिटाई गई है।"},{"id":"t-secularism-21","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Freedom of religion does not allow a community to","options":["violate the fundamental rights of other people","celebrate its own festival in peace","run a school for its children within the law","pray in its own place of worship"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is violate the fundamental rights of other people because religious freedom stops where another person's fundamental rights begin. celebrate its own festival in peace is wrong because a peaceful festival is protected. run a school for its children within the law is wrong because a lawful school is part of educational freedom. pray in its own place of worship is wrong because worship in one's own place is part of freedom of religion.\nयाद रखो: धर्म की आज़ादी किसी समुदाय को दूसरों के मूल अधिकार तोड़ने की छूट नहीं देती।\nगलत मत याद करना: celebrate its own festival in peace शांति से अपना त्योहार मनाना मना नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-22","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"If a custom humiliates a group of people, the secular state","options":["must defend the custom because no custom can ever be questioned","may step in to protect their fundamental rights","must adopt that custom as the official religion","must punish the victims instead of the humiliation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is may step in to protect their fundamental rights because the ban on untouchability shows that the state can interfere to stop a humiliating religious custom. must defend the custom because no custom can ever be questioned is wrong because customs are not above fundamental rights. must adopt that custom as the official religion is wrong because adopting the custom as a state religion would spread the harm. must punish the victims instead of the humiliation is wrong because the victims are the people the law protects.\nयाद रखो: जो रिवाज़ लोगों को अपमानित करे, पंथनिरपेक्ष राज्य उनके मूल अधिकार बचाने दखल दे सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: must defend the custom because no custom can ever be questioned कोई रिवाज़ सवाल से ऊपर नहीं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-23","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"Minority educational institutions have a place in Indian secularism because","options":["minorities are forbidden to open any school","only the largest community may run a school","communities are allowed to preserve their culture and education","schooling is reserved for one religion"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is communities are allowed to preserve their culture and education because cultural and educational rights let minorities establish institutions, and the state may support that freedom. minorities are forbidden to open any school is wrong because minorities are not forbidden to open schools. only the largest community may run a school is wrong because schooling is not a monopoly of the largest community. schooling is reserved for one religion is wrong because education is not reserved for a single religion.\nयाद रखो: अल्पसंख्यक शिक्षण संस्थाएँ इसलिए हैं कि समुदाय अपनी संस्कृति और शिक्षा बचा सकें।\nगलत मत याद करना: minorities are forbidden to open any school अल्पसंख्यकों के लिए स्कूल मना नहीं हैं।"},{"id":"t-secularism-24","topicId":"t-secularism","subject":"sst","stem":"The best short description of Indian secularism is","options":["one official religion for the whole country","a ban on every form of religious belief","rule by the priests of the largest community","equal respect for all religions, with room to stop a practice that breaks fundamental rights"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is equal respect for all religions, with room to stop a practice that breaks fundamental rights because the state treats faiths equally and still intervenes against a practice such as untouchability. one official religion for the whole country is wrong because one official religion would undo secularism. a ban on every form of religious belief is wrong because belief is not banned. rule by the priests of the largest community is wrong because priests of one community do not rule the state.\nयाद रखो: सब धर्मों का समान सम्मान, और मूल अधिकार तोड़ने वाली प्रथा रोकने की जगह।\nगलत मत याद करना: one official religion for the whole country पूरे देश का एक राजधर्म यह वर्णन नहीं।"},{"id":"t-parliament-13","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"The Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act is a useful example because","options":["Parliament passed it after years of public demand, especially from women's groups","the East India Company issued it in 1600","it made criticism of every law a crime","it said that violence at home is not a legal concern"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is Parliament passed it after years of public demand, especially from women's groups because the 2005 law shows how campaigns can push Parliament to protect people inside the home. the East India Company issued it in 1600 is wrong because 1600 is the year of the Company's charter, not of this Act. it made criticism of every law a crime is wrong because the Act responded to criticism. It did not ban criticism. it said that violence at home is not a legal concern is wrong because the Act treats domestic violence as a legal wrong.\nयाद रखो: घरेलू हिंसा से महिलाओं का संरक्षण कानून जनमाँग, खासकर महिला समूहों, के सालों बाद संसद ने पास किया।\nगलत मत याद करना: the East India Company issued it in 1600 1600 की कंपनी ने यह कानून नहीं निकाला।"},{"id":"t-parliament-14","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"An unconstitutional law can be","options":["hidden from judges for ever","struck down by the courts","made stronger than the Constitution by a speech","enforced even when it destroys Fundamental Rights"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is struck down by the courts because if a law breaks the Constitution, the courts may declare it void. hidden from judges for ever is wrong because judges are entitled to examine a law. made stronger than the Constitution by a speech is wrong because a speech cannot lift a statute above the Constitution. enforced even when it destroys Fundamental Rights is wrong because a law that destroys Fundamental Rights is open to being struck down.\nयाद रखो: जो कानून संविधान तोड़े, अदालत उसे रद्द कर सकती है। भाषण से संविधान से ऊपर नहीं हो जाता।\nगलत मत याद करना: made stronger than the Constitution by a speech एक भाषण कानून को संविधान से बड़ा नहीं करता।"},{"id":"t-parliament-15","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"The opposition in Parliament","options":["is forbidden to speak","commands the army","questions the government and points out its failures","grants the Diwani of Bengal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is questions the government and points out its failures because parties that are not in office use questions and debate to check the government. is forbidden to speak is wrong because opposition members have the right to speak. commands the army is wrong because the army is not commanded from the opposition benches. grants the Diwani of Bengal is wrong because the Diwani was granted to the Company in 1765.\nयाद रखो: संसद में विपक्ष सरकार से सवाल करता है और उसकी असफलताएँ दिखाता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: is forbidden to speak विपक्ष का मुँह बंद करना उसका काम नहीं।"},{"id":"t-parliament-16","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"A coalition is needed when","options":["every party refuses to take its seats","the group with no seats rules alone","the Constitution has been dissolved","no single party has a majority, so parties join together to govern"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is no single party has a majority, so parties join together to govern because two or more parties can combine their seats to cross the majority mark. every party refuses to take its seats is wrong because refusing seats does not create a government. the group with no seats rules alone is wrong because a group with no seats has no majority. the Constitution has been dissolved is wrong because forming a coalition does not dissolve the Constitution.\nयाद रखो: गठबंधन तब चाहिए जब किसी एक दल के पास बहुमत न हो, इसलिए दल मिलकर शासन करें।\nगलत मत याद करना: the group with no seats rules alone बिना सीट का समूह अकेला शासन नहीं करता।"},{"id":"t-parliament-17","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"Universal adult franchise in elections to the Lok Sabha means that","options":["citizens who are 18 or older have the right to vote","only men who own large estates may vote","only people above 80 may vote","the vote is limited to one religion"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is citizens who are 18 or older have the right to vote because every adult citizen has one vote, without a property, gender, or religious qualification. only men who own large estates may vote is wrong because property and gender limits belonged to older, unfair franchises. only people above 80 may vote is wrong because the age is 18, not 80. the vote is limited to one religion is wrong because religion does not decide who may vote.\nयाद रखो: लोकसभा के चुनाव में सार्वभौमिक वयस्क मताधिकार: 18 साल या उससे बड़े नागरिकों को वोट का हक।\nगलत मत याद करना: only men who own large estates may vote सिर्फ बड़े ज़मींदार पुरुषों का वोट यह अधिकार नहीं।"},{"id":"t-parliament-18","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"The Prime Minister and the Council of Ministers are","options":["free of any duty to explain their actions","answerable to the Lok Sabha","a branch of a district police station only","appointed by the Nawab of Bengal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is answerable to the Lok Sabha because the executive must keep the confidence of the directly elected house and answer its questions. free of any duty to explain their actions is wrong because answerability is the point of parliamentary government. a branch of a district police station only is wrong because ministers are not a local police post. appointed by the Nawab of Bengal is wrong because the Nawab of Bengal does not appoint the Union Council of Ministers.\nयाद रखो: प्रधानमंत्री और मंत्रिपरिषद लोकसभा के प्रति उत्तरदायी हैं। बहुमत वहीं सरकार बनाता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: free of any duty to explain their actions जवाब देने की ड्यूटी से आज़ाद मंत्रिपरिषद नहीं होती।"},{"id":"m-algebra-26","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"The value of 7² − 8² is","options":["1","113","97","-15"],"answer":3,"explanation":"7² − 8² = (7 − 8)(7 + 8) = -1 × 15 = -15. 1 expands to a square of a difference, which still has a middle term. 113 adds the squares. The last option adds an extra 2ab onto the correct product."},{"id":"m-algebra-27","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (8 + 9)² using an identity.","options":["145","217","289","34"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(x + y)² = x² + 2xy + y². Here x = 8 and y = 9, so the value is 64 + 144 + 81 = 289. 145 drops the middle term 2xy. 217 uses xy instead of 2xy. 34 is the double of the sum, not the square."},{"id":"m-algebra-28","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (8 − 10)².","options":["324","-36","164","4"],"answer":3,"explanation":"(x − y)² = x² − 2xy + y² = 64 − 160 + 100 = 4. 324 is (8 + 10)². -36 is a difference of squares. 164 drops the middle term and also loses the minus."},{"id":"m-algebra-29","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"The value of 8² − 11² is","options":["-57","9","185","119"],"answer":0,"explanation":"8² − 11² = (8 − 11)(8 + 11) = -3 × 19 = -57. 9 expands to a square of a difference, which still has a middle term. 185 adds the squares. The last option adds an extra 2ab onto the correct product."},{"id":"m-algebra-30","topicId":"m-algebra","subject":"maths","stem":"Expand (9 + 12)² using an identity.","options":["225","333","42","441"],"answer":3,"explanation":"(x + y)² = x² + 2xy + y². Here x = 9 and y = 12, so the value is 81 + 216 + 144 = 441. 225 drops the middle term 2xy. 333 uses xy instead of 2xy. 42 is the double of the sum, not the square."},{"id":"m-factorisation-16","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 5x² + 25x.","options":["5(x² + 5)","x(5 + 5)","5x(x + 25)","5x(x + 5)"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Both terms have 5x. 5x² + 25x = 5x(x + 5). 5(x² + 5) leaves the second term short of an x. x(5 + 5) is linear. 5x(x + 25) puts the common factor back into the bracket."},{"id":"m-factorisation-17","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 6x + 12.","options":["6(x + 2)","6(x + 12)","x(6 + 2)","6x(1 + 2)"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The common factor is 6. 6x + 12 = 6(x + 2). 6(x + 12) would expand to 6x + 72, which has an extra 6. x(6 + 2) expands to 6x + 2x, not a constant term. 6x(1 + 2) expands to 6x + 12x, so the second term still has x."},{"id":"m-factorisation-18","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise x² + 9x + 18.","options":["(x + 18)(x + 1)","(x + 6)(x + 3)","(x − 6)(x − 3)","(x + 6)(x − 3)"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Look for two numbers that add to 9 and multiply to 18. They are 6 and 3, so the factors are (x + 6)(x + 3). (x − 6)(x − 3) gives a plus middle term only if you expand carefully: the middle term is negative. (x + 6)(x − 3) gives a middle term 3, not 9."},{"id":"m-factorisation-19","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise x² − 36.","options":["(x − 6)²","(x + 6)²","(x − 6)(x + 6)","(x − 36)(x + 1)"],"answer":2,"explanation":"x² − 36 is a difference of squares: x² − 6² = (x − 6)(x + 6). (x − 6)² = x² − 12x + 36, which has a middle term. (x + 6)² adds the squares. The last option does not multiply back to x² − 36."},{"id":"m-factorisation-20","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 6x² + 30x.","options":["6(x² + 5)","x(6 + 5)","6x(x + 30)","6x(x + 5)"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Both terms have 6x. 6x² + 30x = 6x(x + 5). 6(x² + 5) leaves the second term short of an x. x(6 + 5) is linear. 6x(x + 30) puts the common factor back into the bracket."},{"id":"m-factorisation-21","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 7x + 14.","options":["7(x + 2)","7(x + 14)","x(7 + 2)","7x(1 + 2)"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The common factor is 7. 7x + 14 = 7(x + 2). 7(x + 14) would expand to 7x + 98, which has an extra 7. x(7 + 2) expands to 7x + 2x, not a constant term. 7x(1 + 2) expands to 7x + 14x, so the second term still has x."},{"id":"m-factorisation-22","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise x² + 10x + 21.","options":["(x + 21)(x + 1)","(x + 7)(x + 3)","(x − 7)(x − 3)","(x + 7)(x − 3)"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Look for two numbers that add to 10 and multiply to 21. They are 7 and 3, so the factors are (x + 7)(x + 3). (x − 7)(x − 3) gives a plus middle term only if you expand carefully: the middle term is negative. (x + 7)(x − 3) gives a middle term 4, not 10."},{"id":"m-factorisation-23","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise x² − 49.","options":["(x − 7)²","(x + 7)²","(x − 7)(x + 7)","(x − 49)(x + 1)"],"answer":2,"explanation":"x² − 49 is a difference of squares: x² − 7² = (x − 7)(x + 7). (x − 7)² = x² − 14x + 49, which has a middle term. (x + 7)² adds the squares. The last option does not multiply back to x² − 49."},{"id":"m-factorisation-24","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 7x² + 35x.","options":["7(x² + 5)","x(7 + 5)","7x(x + 35)","7x(x + 5)"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Both terms have 7x. 7x² + 35x = 7x(x + 5). 7(x² + 5) leaves the second term short of an x. x(7 + 5) is linear. 7x(x + 35) puts the common factor back into the bracket."},{"id":"m-factorisation-25","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 8x + 16.","options":["8(x + 2)","8(x + 16)","x(8 + 2)","8x(1 + 2)"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The common factor is 8. 8x + 16 = 8(x + 2). 8(x + 16) would expand to 8x + 128, which has an extra 8. x(8 + 2) expands to 8x + 2x, not a constant term. 8x(1 + 2) expands to 8x + 16x, so the second term still has x."},{"id":"m-factorisation-26","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise x² + 11x + 24.","options":["(x + 24)(x + 1)","(x + 8)(x + 3)","(x − 8)(x − 3)","(x + 8)(x − 3)"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Look for two numbers that add to 11 and multiply to 24. They are 8 and 3, so the factors are (x + 8)(x + 3). (x − 8)(x − 3) gives a plus middle term only if you expand carefully: the middle term is negative. (x + 8)(x − 3) gives a middle term 5, not 11."},{"id":"m-factorisation-27","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise x² − 64.","options":["(x − 8)²","(x + 8)²","(x − 8)(x + 8)","(x − 64)(x + 1)"],"answer":2,"explanation":"x² − 64 is a difference of squares: x² − 8² = (x − 8)(x + 8). (x − 8)² = x² − 16x + 64, which has a middle term. (x + 8)² adds the squares. The last option does not multiply back to x² − 64."},{"id":"m-factorisation-28","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 8x² + 40x.","options":["8(x² + 5)","x(8 + 5)","8x(x + 40)","8x(x + 5)"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Both terms have 8x. 8x² + 40x = 8x(x + 5). 8(x² + 5) leaves the second term short of an x. x(8 + 5) is linear. 8x(x + 40) puts the common factor back into the bracket."},{"id":"m-factorisation-29","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise 9x + 18.","options":["9(x + 2)","9(x + 18)","x(9 + 2)","9x(1 + 2)"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The common factor is 9. 9x + 18 = 9(x + 2). 9(x + 18) would expand to 9x + 162, which has an extra 9. x(9 + 2) expands to 9x + 2x, not a constant term. 9x(1 + 2) expands to 9x + 18x, so the second term still has x."},{"id":"m-factorisation-30","topicId":"m-factorisation","subject":"maths","stem":"Factorise x² + 12x + 27.","options":["(x + 27)(x + 1)","(x + 9)(x + 3)","(x − 9)(x − 3)","(x + 9)(x − 3)"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Look for two numbers that add to 12 and multiply to 27. They are 9 and 3, so the factors are (x + 9)(x + 3). (x − 9)(x − 3) gives a plus middle term only if you expand carefully: the middle term is negative. (x + 9)(x − 3) gives a middle term 6, not 12."},{"id":"m-equations-16","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 2x + 4 = 18.","options":["14","8","18","7"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Subtract 4 from both sides: 2x = 18 − 4 = 14. Then divide by 2: x = 7. 14 is the value of 2x before dividing. 8 is one more than the solution. 18 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-equations-17","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"A boy is 7 years younger than his sister. Their ages add up to 21. The boy's age is","options":["7","14","10","21"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Let the boy's age be y. Then the sister is y + 7, and y + (y + 7) = 21. So 2y = 14 and y = 7. 14 is the sister's age. 14 forgets that the sister is older than the boy by 7, not that her age is 7. Half of 21 ignores the age gap."},{"id":"m-equations-18","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 5x + 3 = 43.","options":["40","9","8","43"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Subtract 3 from both sides: 5x = 43 − 3 = 40. Then divide by 5: x = 8. 40 is the value of 5x before dividing. 9 is one more than the solution. 43 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-equations-19","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"A boy is 4 years younger than his sister. Their ages add up to 20. The boy's age is","options":["12","16","10","8"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Let the boy's age be y. Then the sister is y + 4, and y + (y + 4) = 20. So 2y = 16 and y = 8. 12 is the sister's age. 16 forgets that the sister is older than the boy by 4, not that her age is 4. Half of 20 ignores the age gap."},{"id":"m-equations-20","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 3x + 2 = 29.","options":["27","9","10","29"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Subtract 2 from both sides: 3x = 29 − 2 = 27. Then divide by 3: x = 9. 27 is the value of 3x before dividing. 10 is one more than the solution. 29 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-equations-21","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"A boy is 7 years younger than his sister. Their ages add up to 25. The boy's age is","options":["16","18","9","12"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Let the boy's age be y. Then the sister is y + 7, and y + (y + 7) = 25. So 2y = 18 and y = 9. 16 is the sister's age. 18 forgets that the sister is older than the boy by 7, not that her age is 7. Half of 25 ignores the age gap."},{"id":"m-equations-22","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 6x + 1 = 61.","options":["10","60","11","61"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Subtract 1 from both sides: 6x = 61 − 1 = 60. Then divide by 6: x = 10. 60 is the value of 6x before dividing. 11 is one more than the solution. 61 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-equations-23","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"A boy is 4 years younger than his sister. Their ages add up to 24. The boy's age is","options":["14","10","20","12"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Let the boy's age be y. Then the sister is y + 4, and y + (y + 4) = 24. So 2y = 20 and y = 10. 14 is the sister's age. 20 forgets that the sister is older than the boy by 4, not that her age is 4. Half of 24 ignores the age gap."},{"id":"m-equations-24","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 4x + 4 = 48.","options":["44","12","48","11"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Subtract 4 from both sides: 4x = 48 − 4 = 44. Then divide by 4: x = 11. 44 is the value of 4x before dividing. 12 is one more than the solution. 48 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-equations-25","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"A boy is 7 years younger than his sister. Their ages add up to 29. The boy's age is","options":["11","18","22","14"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Let the boy's age be y. Then the sister is y + 7, and y + (y + 7) = 29. So 2y = 22 and y = 11. 18 is the sister's age. 22 forgets that the sister is older than the boy by 7, not that her age is 7. Half of 29 ignores the age gap."},{"id":"m-equations-26","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 2x + 3 = 27.","options":["24","13","12","27"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Subtract 3 from both sides: 2x = 27 − 3 = 24. Then divide by 2: x = 12. 24 is the value of 2x before dividing. 13 is one more than the solution. 27 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-equations-27","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"A boy is 4 years younger than his sister. Their ages add up to 28. The boy's age is","options":["16","24","14","12"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Let the boy's age be y. Then the sister is y + 4, and y + (y + 4) = 28. So 2y = 24 and y = 12. 16 is the sister's age. 24 forgets that the sister is older than the boy by 4, not that her age is 4. Half of 28 ignores the age gap."},{"id":"m-equations-28","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 5x + 2 = 67.","options":["65","13","14","67"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Subtract 2 from both sides: 5x = 67 − 2 = 65. Then divide by 5: x = 13. 65 is the value of 5x before dividing. 14 is one more than the solution. 67 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-equations-29","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"A boy is 7 years younger than his sister. Their ages add up to 33. The boy's age is","options":["20","26","13","16"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Let the boy's age be y. Then the sister is y + 7, and y + (y + 7) = 33. So 2y = 26 and y = 13. 20 is the sister's age. 26 forgets that the sister is older than the boy by 7, not that her age is 7. Half of 33 ignores the age gap."},{"id":"m-equations-30","topicId":"m-equations","subject":"maths","stem":"Solve 3x + 1 = 43.","options":["14","42","15","43"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Subtract 1 from both sides: 3x = 43 − 1 = 42. Then divide by 3: x = 14. 42 is the value of 3x before dividing. 15 is one more than the solution. 43 is the right-hand side, not the value of x."},{"id":"m-comparing-16","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"Compound interest on ₹1500 at 10% per year for 2 years, added yearly, gives an amount of","options":["₹1800","₹1650.0000000000002","₹1500","₹1815"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Amount after 2 years at 10% is P × (1.1)² = P × 1.21 = ₹1815. ₹1800 is two years of simple interest at 10%. ₹1650.0000000000002 is only one year. ₹1800 is the same simple-interest amount written another way."},{"id":"m-comparing-17","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"The ratio of boys to girls is 4 : 6. Boys are what fraction of the total children?","options":["2/5","2/3","3/5","4/7"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total parts = 4 + 6 = 10. Boys are 4 of those parts, so the fraction is 2/5. 2/3 compares boys with girls, not with the total. 3/5 is the girls' share."},{"id":"m-comparing-18","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"A price of ₹60 increases by 10%. The new price is","options":["₹70","₹66","₹6","₹54"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Increase = 10% of 60 = ₹6. New price = ₹66. ₹70 adds 10 rupees. The middle option is only the increase. The last option is a 10% decrease."},{"id":"m-comparing-19","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"A shopkeeper buys an item for ₹500 and wants a profit of 20%. The selling price is","options":["₹520","₹100","₹600","₹400"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Profit = 20% of 500 = ₹100. Selling price = cost + profit = ₹600. ₹520 adds the percent number itself, not the percent of the cost. ₹100 is only the profit. The last option subtracts the profit, which would be a loss."},{"id":"m-comparing-20","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"A marked price of ₹350 is discounted by 10%. The sale price is","options":["₹340","₹35","₹385","₹315"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Discount = 10% of 350 = ₹35. Sale price = 350 − that discount = ₹315. ₹340 subtracts 10 rupees, not 10 percent. The middle option is only the discount. Adding the discount would raise the price."},{"id":"m-comparing-21","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"Simple interest on ₹4000 at 5% per year for 4 years is","options":["₹800","₹200","₹4800","₹160"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Simple interest = PRT/100 = 4000 × 5 × 4 / 100 = ₹800. ₹200 is the interest for one year only. ₹4800 is the amount, not the interest. ₹160 drops the rate."},{"id":"m-comparing-22","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"Compound interest on ₹2000 at 10% per year for 2 years, added yearly, gives an amount of","options":["₹2400","₹2420","₹2200","₹2000"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Amount after 2 years at 10% is P × (1.1)² = P × 1.21 = ₹2420. ₹2400 is two years of simple interest at 10%. ₹2200 is only one year. ₹2400 is the same simple-interest amount written another way."},{"id":"m-comparing-23","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"The ratio of boys to girls is 5 : 7. Boys are what fraction of the total children?","options":["5/7","7/12","5/12","5/8"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Total parts = 5 + 7 = 12. Boys are 5 of those parts, so the fraction is 5/12. 5/7 compares boys with girls, not with the total. 7/12 is the girls' share."},{"id":"m-comparing-24","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"A price of ₹70 increases by 10%. The new price is","options":["₹80","₹7","₹63","₹77"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Increase = 10% of 70 = ₹7. New price = ₹77. ₹80 adds 10 rupees. The middle option is only the increase. The last option is a 10% decrease."},{"id":"m-comparing-25","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"A shopkeeper buys an item for ₹600 and wants a profit of 25%. The selling price is","options":["₹750","₹625","₹150","₹450"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Profit = 25% of 600 = ₹150. Selling price = cost + profit = ₹750. ₹625 adds the percent number itself, not the percent of the cost. ₹150 is only the profit. The last option subtracts the profit, which would be a loss."},{"id":"m-comparing-26","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"A marked price of ₹400 is discounted by 10%. The sale price is","options":["₹390","₹360","₹40","₹440"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Discount = 10% of 400 = ₹40. Sale price = 400 − that discount = ₹360. ₹390 subtracts 10 rupees, not 10 percent. The middle option is only the discount. Adding the discount would raise the price."},{"id":"m-comparing-27","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"Simple interest on ₹5000 at 5% per year for 4 years is","options":["₹250","₹6000","₹1000","₹200"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Simple interest = PRT/100 = 5000 × 5 × 4 / 100 = ₹1000. ₹250 is the interest for one year only. ₹6000 is the amount, not the interest. ₹200 drops the rate."},{"id":"m-comparing-28","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"Compound interest on ₹2500 at 10% per year for 2 years, added yearly, gives an amount of","options":["₹3000","₹2750","₹2500","₹3025"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Amount after 2 years at 10% is P × (1.1)² = P × 1.21 = ₹3025. ₹3000 is two years of simple interest at 10%. ₹2750 is only one year. ₹3000 is the same simple-interest amount written another way."},{"id":"m-comparing-29","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"The ratio of boys to girls is 6 : 8. Boys are what fraction of the total children?","options":["3/7","3/4","4/7","2/3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Total parts = 6 + 8 = 14. Boys are 6 of those parts, so the fraction is 3/7. 3/4 compares boys with girls, not with the total. 4/7 is the girls' share."},{"id":"m-comparing-30","topicId":"m-comparing","subject":"maths","stem":"A price of ₹80 increases by 10%. The new price is","options":["₹90","₹88","₹8","₹72"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Increase = 10% of 80 = ₹8. New price = ₹88. ₹90 adds 10 rupees. The middle option is only the increase. The last option is a 10% decrease."},{"id":"s-sound-25","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"Which step helps to reduce noise pollution?","options":["Planting trees along a busy road","Bursting more crackers beside a hospital","Removing the silencers from motorbikes","Playing loudspeakers at full volume all night"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct answer is Planting trees along a busy road. Trees soften and absorb some of the sound. Silencers on vehicles, covers on noisy machines, and limits on loudspeakers also help. Keeping a television or music system at a low volume protects hearing. Bursting more crackers beside a hospital is wrong because crackers add noise, and a hospital needs quiet. Removing the silencers from motorbikes is wrong because silencers reduce noise, so taking them off makes the problem worse. Playing loudspeakers at full volume all night is wrong because that adds unwanted sound and disturbs sleep.\nयाद रखो: सड़क किनारे पेड़ कुछ शोर सोख लेते हैं। पटाखे और बिना साइलेंसर वाली बाइक शोर बढ़ाती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Bursting more crackers beside a hospital अस्पताल के पास शोर घटाने का तरीका नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-26","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"In a sound wave, a compression and a rarefaction are...","options":["Two names for the eardrum","A region where particles are crowded and a region where they are spread apart","The north and south poles of a magnet","The kharif season and the rabi season"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct answer is A region where particles are crowded and a region where they are spread apart. A vibrating body pushes nearby particles together and makes a compression. When it moves back, it leaves a rarefaction, where the particles are farther apart. These regions travel outward, while each particle only vibrates about its mean position. Two names for the eardrum is wrong because the eardrum is a membrane, not the two regions of the wave. The north and south poles of a magnet is wrong because magnetic poles are not parts of a sound wave. The kharif season and the rabi season is wrong because crop seasons are not parts of a wave.\nयाद रखो: संपीडन में कण भीड़ में हैं, विरलन में कण फैले हैं। दोनों मिलकर ध्वनि तरंग चलती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: The north and south poles of a magnet चुंबक के सिरे हैं, हवा के कणों की भीड़ नहीं।"},{"id":"s-sound-27","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"A bat flying in the dark uses ultrasound. This works because...","options":["The bat sends only infrasound, which people hear as music","The calls travel through a vacuum","The bat sends out very high-frequency sound and listens for the reflection","The bat sees colours called decibels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct answer is The bat sends out very high-frequency sound and listens for the reflection. Ultrasound has a frequency above 20,000 Hz. Echoes from insects and walls return to the bat, and the timing of those echoes shows where things are. People cannot hear the calls, but the method is still the reflection of sound. The bat sends only infrasound, which people hear as music is wrong because bats use ultrasound above the human range, and people do not hear it as music. The calls travel through a vacuum is wrong because a vacuum cannot carry sound, and air carries the bat's calls. The bat sees colours called decibels is wrong because the decibel is a unit of loudness, not a colour of light.\nयाद रखो: चमगादड़ बहुत ऊँची आवृत्ति की आवाज़ फेंकता है और उसकी प्रतिध्वनि सुनकर रास्ता देखता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: The calls travel through a vacuum खाली जगह में न पुकार जाती है, न प्रतिध्वनि लौटती है।"},{"id":"s-sound-28","topicId":"s-sound","subject":"science","stem":"An alarm clock is seen ringing inside a jar while the air is pumped out, yet the sound fades. What does this show?","options":["Light needs air, because the clock vanishes","Sound travels best of all in a vacuum","The thick glass forces the frequency below 1 Hz","Sound needs a medium and cannot travel through a vacuum"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct answer is Sound needs a medium and cannot travel through a vacuum. The alarm is still vibrating, which is why it can be seen. As the air is removed, the medium that should carry the vibration is lost, so the sound grows faint. Letting the air back in brings the sound back. Light needs air, because the clock vanishes is wrong because the clock is still seen, so light is crossing the jar while the sound fades. Sound travels best of all in a vacuum is wrong because the fading sound shows the opposite. The thick glass forces the frequency below 1 Hz is wrong because the point of the experiment is the missing air, not a new frequency caused by the glass.\nयाद रखो: घड़ी दिखती है पर आवाज़ खो जाती है, क्योंकि आवाज़ को हवा चाहिए। निर्वात उसे नहीं ढोता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Sound travels best of all in a vacuum खाली जगह सबसे अच्छी सड़क नहीं, बंद गली है।"},{"id":"s-light-16","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"Which structure carries the message from the retina to the brain?","options":["Cornea","Pupil","Optic nerve","Lens"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Optic nerve\". After rods and cones detect the image, the optic nerve takes the signals to the brain. \"Cornea\" is wrong because the cornea lets light in and does not carry a nerve message. \"Pupil\" is wrong because the pupil is an opening that controls the amount of light. \"Lens\" is wrong because the lens focuses light and does not carry the message to the brain.\nयाद रखो: रेटिना का संदेश मस्तिष्क तक दृक् तंत्रिका (optic nerve) ले जाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Pupil सिर्फ छेद है, तार नहीं।"},{"id":"s-light-17","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"Visually challenged people can read by touching patterns of raised dots. What is this system called?","options":["Braille","Morse ink writing that must be seen","Kaleidoscope script","Lateral inversion printing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Braille\". Braille uses raised dots so that reading is done by touch. \"Morse ink writing that must be seen\" is wrong because Morse ink has to be looked at, so it is not the touch system of raised dots. \"Kaleidoscope script\" is wrong because a kaleidoscope makes coloured patterns and is not a reading system. \"Lateral inversion printing\" is wrong because lateral inversion is a mirror effect, not a touch alphabet.\nयाद रखो: उभरे बिंदुओं को छूकर पढ़ना ब्रेल है। आँख से देखना ज़रूरी नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Morse ink writing that must be seen स्याही देखनी पड़ती है, ब्रेल छूनी पड़ती है।"},{"id":"s-light-18","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"Which set of words best describes the image in a plane mirror?","options":["Real, inverted, and smaller than the object","Real, erect, and larger than the object","Virtual, erect, and the same size as the object","Virtual, inverted, and formed on a screen in front of the mirror"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Virtual, erect, and the same size as the object\". A plane mirror forms a virtual erect image that matches the object in size and is as far behind the mirror as the object is in front. \"Real, inverted, and smaller than the object\" is wrong because a plane-mirror image is not real, not inverted, and not smaller. \"Real, erect, and larger than the object\" is wrong because the image cannot be caught on a screen and is not enlarged. \"Virtual, inverted, and formed on a screen in front of the mirror\" is wrong because the image is erect and virtual, so it is not formed on a screen in front.\nयाद रखो: समतल दर्पण की छवि आभासी, सीधी और वस्तु जितनी बड़ी होती है। पर्दे पर उलटी असली नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Real, inverted, and smaller than the object यह कैमरे या लेंस की उलटी छवि जैसी बात है।"},{"id":"s-light-19","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"AMBULANCE is often painted in reverse on the front of the vehicle. Why can a driver ahead read it in a rear-view mirror?","options":["The mirror disperses the letters into seven colours that spell the word","A plane mirror shows lateral inversion, so the reversed letters look normal in the mirror","The mirror makes the letters larger but does not change their order","The mirror reflects the word only at night"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A plane mirror shows lateral inversion, so the reversed letters look normal in the mirror\". Left and right are swapped in a plane mirror, which is called lateral inversion. \"The mirror disperses the letters into seven colours that spell the word\" is wrong because a mirror does not disperse paint into a spectrum in order to spell a word. \"The mirror makes the letters larger but does not change their order\" is wrong because size is unchanged, and the useful change is the left-right swap. \"The mirror reflects the word only at night\" is wrong because a rear-view mirror works in daylight as well as at night.\nयाद रखो: समतल दर्पण दाएँ-बाएँ उलटता है। एम्बुलेंस उल्टा लिखा होता है ताकि शीशे में सीधा पढ़ो।\nगलत मत याद करना: The mirror disperses the letters into seven colours अक्षर इंद्रधनुष नहीं बनते।"},{"id":"s-light-20","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"The angle of incidence is the angle between which two lines?","options":["The incident ray and the mirror surface","The reflected ray and the object","The two sides of a prism","The incident ray and the normal"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"The incident ray and the normal\". The normal is the line drawn at 90 degrees to the mirror at the point where the ray hits. \"The incident ray and the mirror surface\" is wrong because the angle with the mirror surface is not the angle of incidence. \"The reflected ray and the object\" is wrong because the object is not one of the two lines that define this angle. \"The two sides of a prism\" is wrong because a prism is used in dispersion, and this angle is defined at a mirror.\nयाद रखो: आपतन कोण आपतित किरण और अभिलम्ब के बीच है, दर्पण की सतह के बीच नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: The incident ray and the mirror surface सतह वाला कोण आपतन कोण नहीं कहलाता।"},{"id":"s-light-21","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"A ray strikes a plane mirror with an angle of incidence of 40 degrees. What is the angle of reflection?","options":["50 degrees","40 degrees","20 degrees","80 degrees"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"40 degrees\". The angle of reflection equals the angle of incidence, so both are 40 degrees. \"50 degrees\" is wrong because 50 degrees would be the angle with the mirror if someone confused it with the normal, but the reflection angle equals 40 degrees. \"20 degrees\" is wrong because the reflected angle is not half of the incident angle. \"80 degrees\" is wrong because the reflected angle is not double the incident angle.\nयाद रखो: नियम छोटा है: आने का कोण लौटने के कोण के बराबर। चालीस गया तो चालीस लौटा।\nगलत मत याद करना: 80 degrees कोण को दुगना करने की गलती है। बराबर ही बराबर।"},{"id":"s-light-22","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"The angle of incidence at a plane mirror is 30 degrees. What is the angle between the incident ray and the reflected ray?","options":["30 degrees","90 degrees","15 degrees","60 degrees"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"60 degrees\". Each ray makes 30 degrees with the normal, so the rays are 30 + 30 = 60 degrees apart. \"30 degrees\" is wrong because 30 degrees is the angle with the normal, not the angle between the two rays. \"90 degrees\" is wrong because 90 degrees would need each ray to be 45 degrees from the normal. \"15 degrees\" is wrong because 15 degrees is half of 30, and the rays are separated by the sum of the two equal angles."},{"id":"s-light-23","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"A film is many still pictures shown quickly, yet the scene looks continuous. Which fact about the eye explains this?","options":["The cornea stores each picture for one full minute","The pupil reflects pictures back onto the screen","The impression of an image stays on the retina for about 1/16 of a second","Rods split each picture into seven colours"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"The impression of an image stays on the retina for about 1/16 of a second\". This lingering impression is called persistence of vision. \"The cornea stores each picture for one full minute\" is wrong because the cornea does not store pictures, and the time is about 1/16 of a second, not a minute. \"The pupil reflects pictures back onto the screen\" is wrong because the pupil is an opening and does not reflect stored pictures. \"Rods split each picture into seven colours\" is wrong because splitting into colours is dispersion, not persistence of vision.\nयाद रखो: चित्र रेटिना पर लगभग एक बटे सोलह सेकंड टिका रहता है, इसलिए फिल्म चलती हुई लगती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: The cornea stores each picture for one full minute कॉर्निया एक मिनट की अलमारी नहीं।"},{"id":"s-light-24","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"Trouble in seeing in dim light is linked in this chapter to a shortage of which nutrient?","options":["Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Iodine","Calcium"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Vitamin A\". A shortage of vitamin A is a common cause of night blindness. \"Vitamin C\" is wrong because vitamin C is not the nutrient named for night blindness in this chapter. \"Iodine\" is wrong because iodine is linked with the thyroid, not with this eye trouble. \"Calcium\" is wrong because calcium is important for bones and is not the nutrient named here for dim-light vision.\nयाद रखो: मंद रोशनी में कम दिखना विटामिन A की कमी से जुड़ा है। आयोडीन घेंघा का है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Iodine थायरॉइड का तत्व है, रात की आँख का विटामिन नहीं।"},{"id":"s-light-25","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"In old age the eye lens may become cloudy and vision foggy. What is this condition, and what can be done?","options":["It is dispersion, and it is treated with a glass prism","It is night blindness, and no treatment exists","It is cataract, and the cloudy lens can be removed and replaced","It is lateral inversion, and it is treated with two mirrors"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"It is cataract, and the cloudy lens can be removed and replaced\". Cataract is clouding of the eye lens, and surgery can replace that lens. \"It is dispersion, and it is treated with a glass prism\" is wrong because dispersion is the splitting of light, not a cloudy lens. \"It is night blindness, and no treatment exists\" is wrong because night blindness is a different trouble, linked with vitamin A, and cataract can be treated. \"It is lateral inversion, and it is treated with two mirrors\" is wrong because lateral inversion is a mirror effect, not a disease of the lens.\nयाद रखो: बुढ़ापे में लेंस धुंधला हो तो मोतियाबिंद है। धुंधला लेंस निकालकर नया लगाया जा सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: It is night blindness, and no treatment exists रात का अँधापन विटामिन A की बात है।"},{"id":"s-light-26","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"Which habit protects the eyes, as advised in the Light chapter?","options":["Do not look directly at the Sun or any powerful light","Read for long hours in a moving vehicle every day","Rub the eyes hard whenever a little dust enters","Always read very small print in a very dim room"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Do not look directly at the Sun or any powerful light\". Strong light can damage the eyes, so it should not be stared at. \"Read for long hours in a moving vehicle every day\" is wrong because reading in a moving vehicle strains the eyes. \"Rub the eyes hard whenever a little dust enters\" is wrong because hard rubbing can injure the eye, so dust should not be rubbed in. \"Always read very small print in a very dim room\" is wrong because dim light and tiny print strain the eyes.\nयाद रखो: आँख बचाओ: सूरज या तेज़ रोशनी में सीधे मत घूरो। मंद कमरे में महीन अक्षर आँख थकाते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Always read very small print in a very dim room किताब की सलाह का उल्टा है।"},{"id":"s-light-27","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"An owl sees well at night. Which eye feature explains this?","options":["Its retina has only cones and no rods","Its cornea is opaque and blocks extra light","Its optic nerve forms the picture without a retina","Its retina has a large number of rods"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Its retina has a large number of rods\". Rods are sensitive to dim light, and an owl has many of them. \"Its retina has only cones and no rods\" is wrong because cones work in bright light, and an owl is not limited to cones. \"Its cornea is opaque and blocks extra light\" is wrong because an opaque cornea would block sight, and the owl cornea lets light in. \"Its optic nerve forms the picture without a retina\" is wrong because the picture is formed on the retina, and the nerve only carries signals.\nयाद रखो: उल्लू की रेटिना में शलाकाएँ बहुत हैं, इसलिए रात में देख लेता है। शंकु अकेले काफी नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Its retina has only cones and no rods शंकु रंग और तेज़ रोशनी के हैं, रात के नहीं।"},{"id":"s-light-28","topicId":"s-light","subject":"science","stem":"How does a simple periscope help someone see over a wall or from a submarine?","options":["One prism splits the view into seven colours","Two plane mirrors are fixed parallel to each other in a tube","A single mirror lies flat and forms only a real image on a screen","Three mirrors join as a triangle to make coloured patterns"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Two plane mirrors are fixed parallel to each other in a tube\". Each mirror is set at 45 degrees, so light from above is turned down the tube and then out to the eye. \"One prism splits the view into seven colours\" is wrong because a prism disperses light, and a simple periscope uses two mirrors. \"A single mirror lies flat and forms only a real image on a screen\" is wrong because one flat mirror cannot bend the view down a tube, and its image is virtual. \"Three mirrors join as a triangle to make coloured patterns\" is wrong because that arrangement is a kaleidoscope, not a periscope.\nयाद रखो: पेरिस्कोप की नलिका में दो समतल दर्पण एक-दूसरे के समान्तर लगे होते हैं, दीवार के पार दिखता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Three mirrors join as a triangle to make coloured patterns कैलिडोस्कोप का खेल है।"},{"id":"s-current-16","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"Why is a tin layer useful on an iron food can?","options":["Tin makes the iron react faster with the food","Tin is kept in kerosene, so the food stays dry","Tin turns the food into an acid","Tin protects the iron and is suitable for contact with food"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Tin protects the iron and is suitable for contact with food\". Tin is less reactive than iron, so the food is not left against bare iron. \"Tin makes the iron react faster with the food\" is wrong because the coat is added to slow damage, not to speed a reaction with food. \"Tin is kept in kerosene, so the food stays dry\" is wrong because kerosene storage is for sodium and potassium, not for a tin-coated can. \"Tin turns the food into an acid\" is wrong because the tin layer does not convert food into an acid.\nयाद रखो: टिन लोहे को बचाता है और खाने के संपर्क में ठीक रहता है। खाने को अम्ल नहीं बनाता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Tin makes the iron react faster with the food टिन रफ़्तार बढ़ाने नहीं, रोकने आता है।"},{"id":"s-current-17","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"Which careful practice belongs with electroplating solutions?","options":["Used solutions are pure drinking water and may be poured into a river","Used solutions can pollute water and must be disposed of as directed","The solution should be burnt in an open yard","The solution becomes harmless soil by itself"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Used solutions can pollute water and must be disposed of as directed\". The conducting solutions from plating are chemical wastes. \"Used solutions are pure drinking water and may be poured into a river\" is wrong because these solutions contain metal salts and are not drinking water. \"The solution should be burnt in an open yard\" is wrong because burning is not the safe disposal taught for these liquids. \"The solution becomes harmless soil by itself\" is wrong because it does not turn into soil, and careless dumping pollutes water.\nयाद रखो: इलेक्ट्रोप्लेटिंग का इस्तेमाल घोल पानी गंदा कर सकता है। जहाँ कहा जाए, वहीं फेंको।\nगलत मत याद करना: Used solutions are pure drinking water and may be poured into a river घोल पीने का पानी नहीं।"},{"id":"s-current-18","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"Vinegar conducts electricity. Which general rule explains this?","options":["Every colourless liquid conducts, including distilled water","Only the liquid metal mercury can conduct","Oils conduct better than salt solutions","Solutions of acids, bases, and salts usually conduct"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Solutions of acids, bases, and salts usually conduct\". Vinegar contains acetic acid, so its solution can carry a current. \"Every colourless liquid conducts, including distilled water\" is wrong because distilled water is colourless and still a poor conductor. \"Only the liquid metal mercury can conduct\" is wrong because many acid, base, and salt solutions conduct, not only mercury. \"Oils conduct better than salt solutions\" is wrong because oils are poor conductors compared with salt solutions.\nयाद रखो: सिरका इसलिए चलाता है क्योंकि अम्ल, क्षार और लवण के घोल आमतौर पर चालक होते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Oils conduct better than salt solutions तेल नमक के घोल से अच्छा चालक नहीं।"},{"id":"s-current-19","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"The free ends of a tester are separated by air, and the bulb stays off. What does this show?","options":["Air is a salt solution","Air electroplates the bulb with copper","Air is a poor conductor of electricity","Air is the anode of the cell"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Air is a poor conductor of electricity\". The air gap breaks the circuit because air does not let the current pass. \"Air is a salt solution\" is wrong because air is a gas, not a solution of salt. \"Air electroplates the bulb with copper\" is wrong because an air gap does not deposit copper. \"Air is the anode of the cell\" is wrong because the anode is an electrode joined to the positive terminal, not the air in the gap.\nयाद रखो: हवा खराब चालक है, इसलिए खुले सिरों पर बल्ब नहीं जलता। हवा नमक का घोल नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Air is a salt solution हवा को नमकीन घोल मत समझ बैठना।"},{"id":"s-current-20","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"A compass needle near the tester wire deflects slightly, but the bulb stays dark. What does the deflection show?","options":["A weak current is passing through the liquid","The liquid is distilled water and no current flows at all","The compass itself is being electroplated","The liquid has opened the circuit completely"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A weak current is passing through the liquid\". Even a small current can deflect the compass, which is why it is used when the bulb does not glow. \"The liquid is distilled water and no current flows at all\" is wrong because a deflection means a current is present. \"The compass itself is being electroplated\" is wrong because the compass is only a detector here, not the object being plated. \"The liquid has opened the circuit completely\" is wrong because an open circuit would not deflect the compass.\nयाद रखो: बल्ब अँधेरा हो और कंपास की सुई हिले, तो तरल में कमज़ोर धारा बह रही है।\nगलत मत याद करना: The liquid is distilled water and no current flows at all सुई हिली तो धारा शून्य नहीं।"},{"id":"s-current-21","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"Which pairing of electrode and terminal is correct?","options":["Anode with the negative terminal, and cathode with the positive terminal","Both anode and cathode with the positive terminal","Anode with the positive terminal, and cathode with the negative terminal","Both electrodes with no battery at all"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Anode with the positive terminal, and cathode with the negative terminal\". That is how the two electrodes are named in this chapter. \"Anode with the negative terminal, and cathode with the positive terminal\" is wrong because that swaps the names. \"Both anode and cathode with the positive terminal\" is wrong because the two electrodes are joined to opposite terminals. \"Both electrodes with no battery at all\" is wrong because without a battery there is no positive or negative electrode in the circuit.\nयाद रखो: एनोड धन टर्मिनल के साथ, कैथोड ऋण टर्मिनल के साथ। जोड़ी उल्टी मत जोड़ना।\nगलत मत याद करना: Anode with the negative terminal, and cathode with the positive terminal दोनों नाम उल्टे हैं।"},{"id":"s-current-22","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"A cheap metal ornament is covered with a very thin layer of gold. Which process is this?","options":["Electroplating","Carbonisation of coal","Dispersion of light","Crystallisation of sugar"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Electroplating\". Electroplating deposits a thin layer of a desired metal by using current. \"Carbonisation of coal\" is wrong because carbonisation changes vegetation into coal and does not coat jewellery. \"Dispersion of light\" is wrong because dispersion splits light into colours. \"Crystallisation of sugar\" is wrong because crystallisation separates a solid from a solution and is not gold coating.\nयाद रखो: सस्ते गहने पर सोने की पतली परत विद्युत-लेपन है। कोयला बनना अलग कहानी है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Carbonisation of coal मृत पौधों से कोयला बनने की प्रक्रिया है।"},{"id":"s-current-23","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"Which observation is a chemical effect of current, rather than only a way of detecting current?","options":["A bulb glows in a wire circuit","A compass needle turns near a wire","An LED lights when connected the proper way","A metal layer is deposited on an object from a salt solution"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A metal layer is deposited on an object from a salt solution\". Deposition of metal is a chemical change caused by the current. \"A bulb glows in a wire circuit\" is wrong because a glowing bulb shows that current flows, but the glow itself is not the chemical effect. \"A compass needle turns near a wire\" is wrong because the turn detects current and is not a chemical change in the liquid. \"An LED lights when connected the proper way\" is wrong because the LED is a detector of current, not the chemical change.\nयाद रखो: नमक के घोल से वस्तु पर धातु की परत जमना धारा का रासायनिक प्रभाव है। बल्ब का जलना पहचान का तरीका है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A bulb glows in a wire circuit धारा दिखाने का तरीका है, रासायनिक बदलाव नहीं।"},{"id":"s-current-24","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"Sugar dissolved in distilled water does not light the bulb. Why?","options":["Sugar is a metal and blocks current by conducting too well","A sugar solution is not a conducting solution of an acid, a base, or a salt","Sugar turns the water into chromium","Sugar electroplates the beaker with tin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A sugar solution is not a conducting solution of an acid, a base, or a salt\". The dissolved sugar does not make the water conduct the way salt does. \"Sugar is a metal and blocks current by conducting too well\" is wrong because sugar is not a metal, and the bulb stays dark because the solution conducts poorly. \"Sugar turns the water into chromium\" is wrong because sugar does not become chromium. \"Sugar electroplates the beaker with tin\" is wrong because no plating metal is being deposited in this test.\nयाद रखो: चीनी का घोल अम्ल, क्षार या लवण का चालक घोल नहीं, इसलिए बल्ब नहीं जलता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Sugar is a metal and blocks current by conducting too well चीनी धातु नहीं है।"},{"id":"s-current-25","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"What is the job of a fuse wire in a household circuit?","options":["It reflects light so that every switch stays cool","It is a thick copper bar meant to raise the current","It stores distilled water for the wires","It melts and breaks the circuit when the current is too large"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"It melts and breaks the circuit when the current is too large\". A fuse has a low melting point and is joined in series. Extra current heats it until it melts and opens the circuit. This is a use of the heating effect of current. \"It reflects light so that every switch stays cool\" is wrong because a fuse works by melting, not by reflecting light. \"It is a thick copper bar meant to raise the current\" is wrong because a fuse is meant to stop a dangerous current, not to increase it. \"It stores distilled water for the wires\" is wrong because a fuse is a short piece of wire, not a water store.\nयाद रखो: फ्यूज का तार बहुत धारा पर पिघलकर परिपथ तोड़ देता है। वह मोटा ताँबा नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: It is a thick copper bar meant to raise the current फ्यूज धारा बढ़ाने की छड़ नहीं।"},{"id":"s-current-26","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"A coil of insulated wire is wound on an iron nail and joined to a cell. When does this electromagnet attract iron pins?","options":["Only after the cell is removed and the current has stopped","Only while current flows in the coil","Only when the nail is kept under kerosene","Never, because a coil cannot magnetise an iron nail"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Only while current flows in the coil\". The iron nail becomes a magnet for as long as the current flows, and it loses that magnetism when the current stops. More turns or a stronger current make the electromagnet stronger. Electric bells use this effect. \"Only after the cell is removed and the current has stopped\" is wrong because stopping the current stops the magnetism. \"Only when the nail is kept under kerosene\" is wrong because kerosene is not needed to make the electromagnet. \"Never, because a coil cannot magnetise an iron nail\" is wrong because the iron core inside a current-carrying coil does attract iron.\nयाद रखो: लोहे की कील पर लपेटी कुंडली चुंबक तभी बनती है जब धारा बह रही हो। सेल हटाओ, पिन गिरें।\nगलत मत याद करना: Only after the cell is removed and the current has stopped धारा रुकते ही चुंबक सो जाता है।"},{"id":"s-current-27","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"An electric iron becomes hot when it is switched on. Which effect of current is being used?","options":["The heating effect of an electric current","Only the splitting of white light by a prism","Only a chemical change inside a cut potato","Lateral inversion of a word in a mirror"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"The heating effect of an electric current\". A current can make a wire hot. An electric iron, a room heater, and the filament of a bulb all use this heating effect. \"Only the splitting of white light by a prism\" is wrong because a prism disperses light and does not heat the iron. \"Only a chemical change inside a cut potato\" is wrong because the iron gets hot by the heating effect, not by the potato test. \"Lateral inversion of a word in a mirror\" is wrong because lateral inversion is a mirror effect, not the reason an iron becomes hot.\nयाद रखो: बिजली का इस्तरी गर्म होता है क्योंकि धारा का तापीय प्रभाव काम कर रहा है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Only the splitting of white light by a prism प्रिज्म का खेल इस्तरी नहीं गरम करता।"},{"id":"s-current-28","topicId":"s-current","subject":"science","stem":"Which liquid should be used to show that a little acid can make water conduct?","options":["Kerosene with a few drops of oil","Melted plastic","Distilled water with a few drops of dilute acid","Dry sand"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Distilled water with a few drops of dilute acid\". Distilled water conducts poorly, and adding acid makes a conducting solution. \"Kerosene with a few drops of oil\" is wrong because mixing oils does not make a conducting acid solution. \"Melted plastic\" is wrong because plastic is an insulator and is not the liquid in this test. \"Dry sand\" is wrong because dry sand is not a solution of an acid in water.\nयाद रखो: थोड़ा तनु अम्ल मिला आसुत जल दिखाता है कि अम्ल पानी को चालक बना सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Kerosene with a few drops of oil तेल में तेल मिलाना चालक प्रयोग नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-16","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"A copper wire is left in zinc sulphate solution. What is expected?","options":["No displacement, because copper is less reactive than zinc","Copper displaces zinc and a grey coat of zinc covers the wire","The solution becomes blue copper sulphate at once","Both metals vanish and leave pure water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"No displacement, because copper is less reactive than zinc\". Only a more reactive metal displaces a less reactive one from a salt solution. \"Copper displaces zinc and a grey coat of zinc covers the wire\" is wrong because copper cannot displace zinc. \"The solution becomes blue copper sulphate at once\" is wrong because copper does not pass into the solution in this pairing. \"Both metals vanish and leave pure water\" is wrong because no such change to pure water occurs.\nयाद रखो: ताँबा जस्ते से कम क्रियाशील है, इसलिए जिंक सल्फेट से जस्ता नहीं हटाता। कोई विस्थापन नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Copper displaces zinc and a grey coat of zinc covers the wire कमज़ोर ताँबा जस्ते को नहीं धकेलता।"},{"id":"s-metals-17","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Which reaction is a displacement reaction?","options":["Ice melting to water","Tearing paper into bits","Zinc reacting with copper sulphate to form zinc sulphate and copper","Light reflecting from a mirror"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Zinc reacting with copper sulphate to form zinc sulphate and copper\". Zinc takes the place of copper in the salt. \"Ice melting to water\" is wrong because melting is a physical change of state. \"Tearing paper into bits\" is wrong because tearing changes size and shape only. \"Light reflecting from a mirror\" is wrong because reflection is not a chemical displacement.\nयाद रखो: जस्ता कॉपर सल्फेट से ताँबा निकाल देता है। यह विस्थापन है। बर्फ पिघलना सिर्फ अवस्था बदलना है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Ice melting to water नया पदार्थ नहीं बनता, विस्थापन नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-18","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Copper sulphate crystals separate from solution, and the solid is still copper sulphate. What kind of change is this crystallisation?","options":["A physical change, because no new substance is formed","A chemical change like the rusting of iron","A chemical change like the burning of magnesium","A displacement that produces hydrogen gas"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A physical change, because no new substance is formed\". Crystallisation separates the same copper sulphate as pure crystals. \"A chemical change like the rusting of iron\" is wrong because rusting makes a new brown substance, and these crystals are still copper sulphate. \"A chemical change like the burning of magnesium\" is wrong because burning makes magnesium oxide, a new substance. \"A displacement that produces hydrogen gas\" is wrong because no metal is displacing another metal and no hydrogen is released.\nयाद रखो: क्रिस्टलीकरण में कॉपर सल्फेट कॉपर सल्फेट ही रहता है। नया पदार्थ नहीं, इसलिए भौतिक परिवर्तन।\nगलत मत याद करना: A chemical change like the rusting of iron जंग में नया भूरा पदार्थ बनता है।"},{"id":"s-metals-19","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"A sheet of paper is torn into small pieces. Why is this a physical change?","options":["Tearing produces hydrogen gas","The paper becomes ash","A new element is formed, so the pieces are no longer paper","Only the size and shape change, and no new substance is formed"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Only the size and shape change, and no new substance is formed\". The pieces are still paper. \"Tearing produces hydrogen gas\" is wrong because no hydrogen is released by tearing. \"The paper becomes ash\" is wrong because ash would mean burning, which is a chemical change. \"A new element is formed, so the pieces are no longer paper\" is wrong because the pieces are still the same paper.\nयाद रखो: कागज़ फाड़ने पर सिर्फ आकार बदलता है, कागज़ कागज़ ही रहता है। इसलिए भौतिक परिवर्तन।\nगलत मत याद करना: The paper becomes ash राख तो जलने पर बनती है, फाड़ने पर नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-20","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"An iron gate in moist air develops a brown flaky coat. What is this change?","options":["A physical change like melting ice","A chemical change called rusting","Only a change of state from solid iron to iron gas","Crystallisation of pure iron"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A chemical change called rusting\". Rust is a new substance formed from iron, oxygen, and moisture. \"A physical change like melting ice\" is wrong because melting does not produce a new brown substance. \"Only a change of state from solid iron to iron gas\" is wrong because the gate does not boil away, and rust is a new solid. \"Crystallisation of pure iron\" is wrong because crystallisation would purify a substance, and rusting damages the iron.\nयाद रखो: नम हवा में लोहे का भूरा परतदार कोट जंग है, रासायनिक परिवर्तन। बर्फ पिघलना ऐसा नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: A physical change like melting ice बर्फ पानी बनकर वापस जम सकती है, जंग नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-21","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Milk sets into curd. Why is this a chemical change?","options":["Only the temperature changes, and the milk remains the same substance","The milk is torn like paper","Curd and milk differ only in the shape of the container","A new substance, curd, is formed"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A new substance, curd, is formed\". The taste and composition change, so this is not only a change of shape. \"Only the temperature changes, and the milk remains the same substance\" is wrong because curd is not the same substance as milk. \"The milk is torn like paper\" is wrong because setting curd is a chemical change, not tearing. \"Curd and milk differ only in the shape of the container\" is wrong because the container shape is irrelevant, and a new substance has formed.\nयाद रखो: दूध से दही नया पदार्थ है, इसलिए रासायनिक परिवर्तन। सिर्फ बर्तन का आकार नहीं बदला।\nगलत मत याद करना: Only the temperature changes, and the milk remains the same substance दही दूध नहीं रहता।"},{"id":"s-metals-22","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Which condition is needed for iron to rust?","options":["The iron must be covered with kerosene","Both oxygen and water, or moisture, must be present","The iron must be kept in a vacuum with no air and no water","Rusting needs a prism and seven colours of light"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Both oxygen and water, or moisture, must be present\". Iron does not rust if either air or moisture is absent. \"The iron must be covered with kerosene\" is wrong because kerosene is used to store sodium and potassium, not to make iron rust. \"The iron must be kept in a vacuum with no air and no water\" is wrong because a vacuum removes the oxygen and moisture that rusting needs. \"Rusting needs a prism and seven colours of light\" is wrong because rusting is a chemical reaction with air and moisture, not an effect of a spectrum.\nयाद रखो: जंग के लिए ऑक्सीजन और पानी दोनों चाहिए। निर्वात में बिना हवा-पानी जंग नहीं लगता।\nगलत मत याद करना: The iron must be kept in a vacuum with no air and no water वहाँ जंग रुक जाता है, शुरू नहीं होता।"},{"id":"s-metals-23","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Which method protects iron by coating it with zinc?","options":["Galvanisation","Storing the iron under water like phosphorus","Painting the iron with lemon juice","Leaving the iron in copper sulphate solution"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Galvanisation\". The zinc layer keeps air and moisture away from the iron. \"Storing the iron under water like phosphorus\" is wrong because water would help iron rust, and that storage method is for phosphorus. \"Painting the iron with lemon juice\" is wrong because lemon juice is acidic and is not a zinc coating. \"Leaving the iron in copper sulphate solution\" is wrong because that displaces copper onto iron and does not galvanise it.\nयाद रखो: लोहे पर जस्ते की परत चढ़ाना यशद-लेपन या गैल्वेनीकरण है। फॉस्फोरस वाला पानी अलग कहानी है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Storing the iron under water like phosphorus फॉस्फोरस का तरीका लोहे की सुरक्षा नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-24","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Which non-metal is a liquid at room temperature?","options":["Copper","Iron","Bromine","Graphite"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Bromine\". Bromine is the non-metal that is liquid at room temperature. \"Copper\" is wrong because copper is a solid metal. \"Iron\" is wrong because iron is a solid metal. \"Graphite\" is wrong because graphite is a solid non-metal, not a liquid metal.\nयाद रखो: कमरे के ताप पर तरल अधातु ब्रोमीन है। तरल धातु पारा है। दोनों को एक मत समझना।\nगलत मत याद करना: Copper ठोस धातु है, तरल अधातु नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-25","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement matches the behaviour of copper, gold, and silver in moist air?","options":["Copper gets a green coat, and gold and silver are less reactive","Gold rusts faster than iron, and copper stays bright forever","Silver forms the green coat of basic copper carbonate","Copper is stored in kerosene because it catches fire in air"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Copper gets a green coat, and gold and silver are less reactive\". Moist air gives copper a green layer of basic copper carbonate. Gold and silver lie lower in the reactivity order than iron, so they do not rust. Silver may turn black by forming silver sulphide, but it is still much less reactive than sodium or iron. \"Gold rusts faster than iron, and copper stays bright forever\" is wrong because gold does not rust like iron, and copper does develop a green coat. \"Silver forms the green coat of basic copper carbonate\" is wrong because that green coat belongs to copper, not silver. \"Copper is stored in kerosene because it catches fire in air\" is wrong because kerosene storage is for sodium and potassium, not for copper.\nयाद रखो: ताँबे पर नम हवा में हरी परत चढ़ती है। सोना और चाँदी कम क्रियाशील हैं, आसानी से नहीं बदलते।\nगलत मत याद करना: Gold rusts faster than iron, and copper stays bright forever सोना लोहे से तेज़ नहीं जंग खाता।"},{"id":"s-metals-26","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Copper does not give hydrogen with dilute hydrochloric acid. Why?","options":["Copper is more reactive than potassium","Copper is a non-metal","Copper is less reactive than hydrogen and does not displace it from the acid","Dilute acids never react with any metal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Copper is less reactive than hydrogen and does not displace it from the acid\". Metals below hydrogen in the reactivity order do not release hydrogen from dilute acids. \"Copper is more reactive than potassium\" is wrong because potassium is far more reactive than copper. \"Copper is a non-metal\" is wrong because copper is a metal. \"Dilute acids never react with any metal\" is wrong because zinc and iron do react with dilute acids to give hydrogen.\nयाद रखो: ताँबा हाइड्रोजन से भी कम क्रियाशील है, इसलिए तनु अम्ल से हाइड्रोजन नहीं छीनता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Copper is more reactive than potassium पोटैशियम सबसे गुस्सैल में है, ताँबा नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-27","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Which list is in order of decreasing reactivity?","options":["Copper, iron, zinc, sodium","Sodium, zinc, iron, copper","Iron, copper, sodium, zinc","Zinc, sodium, copper, iron"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Sodium, zinc, iron, copper\". Sodium is more reactive than zinc, zinc more than iron, and iron more than copper. \"Copper, iron, zinc, sodium\" is wrong because that is nearly the reverse order. \"Iron, copper, sodium, zinc\" is wrong because sodium is the most reactive of these four, so it cannot sit third. \"Zinc, sodium, copper, iron\" is wrong because sodium is more reactive than zinc, and iron is more reactive than copper.\nयाद रखो: घटना क्रम: सोडियम सबसे गुस्सा, फिर जस्ता, फिर लोहा, ताँबा सबसे शांत।\nगलत मत याद करना: Copper, iron, zinc, sodium यह सूची उल्टी चढ़ाई है, घटती क्रिया नहीं।"},{"id":"s-metals-28","topicId":"s-metals","subject":"science","stem":"Burning a magnesium ribbon to white ash is which kind of change?","options":["A physical change, because only the shape of the ribbon changes","A change of state like ice to water","Lateral inversion","A chemical change, because magnesium oxide, a new substance, is formed"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A chemical change, because magnesium oxide, a new substance, is formed\". The white ash is not still magnesium metal. \"A physical change, because only the shape of the ribbon changes\" is wrong because a new substance forms, so the change is chemical. \"A change of state like ice to water\" is wrong because the ribbon is burning, not merely melting. \"Lateral inversion\" is wrong because lateral inversion is a mirror effect, not burning.\nयाद रखो: मैग्नीशियम जलकर सफेद मैग्नीशियम ऑक्साइड बनाता है। नया पदार्थ है, इसलिए रासायनिक परिवर्तन।\nगलत मत याद करना: A physical change, because only the shape of the ribbon changes रिबन सिर्फ आकार नहीं बदलता।"},{"id":"s-acids-16","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"If soil is too basic, which treatment does the chapter suggest?","options":["Add more slaked lime","Add organic matter, which releases acids","Add sodium hydroxide","Add large amounts of milk of magnesia"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Add organic matter, which releases acids\". Those acids neutralise the basic nature of the soil. \"Add more slaked lime\" is wrong because slaked lime is a base and is used when soil is too acidic. \"Add sodium hydroxide\" is wrong because sodium hydroxide is a strong base. \"Add large amounts of milk of magnesia\" is wrong because milk of magnesia is also a base.\nयाद रखो: मिट्टी बहुत क्षारीय हो तो जैविक पदार्थ डालो। वह अम्ल छोड़कर मिट्टी संतुलित करता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Add more slaked lime चूना क्षार है, क्षारीय मिट्टी को और क्षार बनाएगा।"},{"id":"s-acids-17","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Rain mixes with sulphur dioxide and nitrogen dioxide from polluted air. What problem can this cause?","options":["The rain becomes a strong base like soap","The rain turns into milk of magnesia","The gases make the rain unable to wet soil at all","Acid rain, which can damage buildings, plants, and animals"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Acid rain, which can damage buildings, plants, and animals\". These gases form acids in rainwater. \"The rain becomes a strong base like soap\" is wrong because the dissolved gases make acids, not a soapy base. \"The rain turns into milk of magnesia\" is wrong because milk of magnesia is a prepared base, not polluted rain. \"The gases make the rain unable to wet soil at all\" is wrong because acid rain still falls as rain, and its problem is the acid, not a failure to wet soil.\nयाद रखो: प्रदूषित हवा की सल्फर डाइऑक्साइड और नाइट्रोजन डाइऑक्साइड बारिश को अम्लीय वर्षा बना सकती हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: The rain becomes a strong base like soap साबुन नहीं बनता, अम्ल बनता है।"},{"id":"s-acids-18","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Which acid is present in vinegar?","options":["Formic acid as the main acid of vinegar","Acetic acid","Sodium hydroxide","Calcium hydroxide"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Acetic acid\". Vinegar contains acetic acid. \"Formic acid as the main acid of vinegar\" is wrong because formic acid is the acid of an ant sting. \"Sodium hydroxide\" is wrong because sodium hydroxide is a base. \"Calcium hydroxide\" is wrong because calcium hydroxide is lime water, a base.\nयाद रखो: सिरके में ऐसीटिक अम्ल है। फॉर्मिक अम्ल चींटी के डंक का है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Formic acid as the main acid of vinegar चींटी वाले अम्ल को सिरके की बोतल मत बना देना।"},{"id":"s-acids-19","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Citric acid is found in which foods?","options":["Citrus fruits such as lemons and oranges","Milk of magnesia","Window cleaner","Lime water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Citrus fruits such as lemons and oranges\". The sour taste of these fruits comes largely from citric acid. \"Milk of magnesia\" is wrong because milk of magnesia is a base, not a food acid. \"Window cleaner\" is wrong because window cleaner contains ammonium hydroxide, a base. \"Lime water\" is wrong because lime water is a base.\nयाद रखो: सिट्रिक अम्ल नींबू और संतरे जैसे खट्टे फलों में है। चूने का पानी क्षार है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Lime water खिड़की नहीं, क्षारीय पानी है। सिट्रिक अम्ल वहाँ नहीं रहता।"},{"id":"s-acids-20","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Lactic acid is the acid linked with which food?","options":["Tamarind","An ant sting","Curd","Soap"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Curd\". Curd contains lactic acid. \"Tamarind\" is wrong because the acid of tamarind is tartaric acid. \"An ant sting\" is wrong because the acid of an ant sting is formic acid. \"Soap\" is wrong because soap is basic.\nयाद रखो: लैक्टिक अम्ल दही के साथ जुड़ा है। इमली में टार्टरिक अम्ल है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Tamarind इमली है, उसमें लैक्टिक नहीं, टार्टरिक अम्ल है।"},{"id":"s-acids-21","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Tartaric acid is present in which of these?","options":["Tamarind","Window cleaner","Milk of magnesia","Calamine lotion as its main substance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Tamarind\". Tamarind, grapes, and unripe mangoes contain tartaric acid. \"Window cleaner\" is wrong because window cleaner is basic. \"Milk of magnesia\" is wrong because milk of magnesia is a base. \"Calamine lotion as its main substance\" is wrong because calamine contains zinc carbonate, a base.\nयाद रखो: टार्टरिक अम्ल इमली में है। पालक में ऑक्सैलिक, दही में लैक्टिक।\nगलत मत याद करना: Milk of magnesia क्षार है, इमली का अम्ल नहीं।"},{"id":"s-acids-22","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Oxalic acid is found in which plant food named in the chapter?","options":["Table salt","Baking soda","Spinach","Quicklime"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Spinach\". Spinach contains oxalic acid. \"Table salt\" is wrong because table salt is sodium chloride, a salt, not oxalic acid. \"Baking soda\" is wrong because baking soda is a mild base. \"Quicklime\" is wrong because quicklime is calcium oxide, a base.\nयाद रखो: ऑक्सैलिक अम्ल पालक में है। बेकिंग सोडा और बिना बुझा चूना क्षार हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Quicklime बिना बुझा चूना क्षार है, पालक का अम्ल नहीं।"}]},{"id":"mock-3","title":"Full mock 3","kind":"mock","minutes":150,"strict":true,"concept":"Full RMS CET Class 9 paper. 200 questions, 2 hours 30 minutes, no negative marking. English 50, Hindi 20, Social Science 30, Mathematics 50, Science 50. Paper 1 and Paper 2 are marked separately. Each needs 50%.","questions":[{"id":"e-jumbled-23","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: the / book / on / the / desk / is / mine?","options":["The book is on the desk mine","On the book the desk is mine","The book on the desk mine is","The book on the desk is mine"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The book on the desk is mine\" because a describing phrase follows its noun, and the linking verb is comes before the complement. \"The book is on the desk mine\" fails because mine is the complement of is and should come at the end, while on the desk describes book. \"On the book the desk is mine\" fails because on the desk is split, so the noun phrase is nonsense. \"The book on the desk mine is\" fails because is must come before the complement mine."},{"id":"e-jumbled-24","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: I / met / a / boy / with / blue / shoes?","options":["I met a boy with blue shoes","I met a with boy blue shoes","Met I a boy with blue shoes","I a boy met with blue shoes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I met a boy with blue shoes\" because the object follows the verb, and with plus a noun phrase describes that object. \"I met a with boy blue shoes\" fails because with blue shoes must follow boy, not split a and boy. \"Met I a boy with blue shoes\" fails because the subject I must come before the verb. \"I a boy met with blue shoes\" fails because the object should follow met, not come before it."},{"id":"e-jumbled-25","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"The bell rang first, and only then did the pupils leave. Which order states that correctly?","options":["After the pupils left, the bell rang","After rang the bell the pupils left","After the bell rang, the pupils left","Left the pupils after the bell rang"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"After the bell rang, the pupils left\" because after introduces the earlier event, and the main clause states what happened next. \"After the pupils left, the bell rang\" fails because this says the pupils left before the bell, which reverses the stated order. \"After rang the bell the pupils left\" fails because the clause after the bell rang needs the subject before the verb. \"Left the pupils after the bell rang\" fails because the result clause should not begin with the verb left."},{"id":"e-jumbled-26","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: although / he / was / ill / he / came / to / school?","options":["Although he ill was, he came to school","He came although to school he was ill","Although was he ill, he came to school","Although he was ill, he came to school"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Although he was ill, he came to school\" because although begins the contrast clause, with normal subject-verb order inside it. \"Although he ill was, he came to school\" fails because was must come before the complement ill. \"He came although to school he was ill\" fails because although must introduce its own clause, not sit inside came to school. \"Although was he ill, he came to school\" fails because the subject he must come before was in the although-clause."},{"id":"e-jumbled-27","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: the / girl / who / won / the / prize / is / my / cousin?","options":["The girl who won the prize is my cousin","The girl who the prize won is my cousin","Who the girl won the prize is my cousin","The girl won who the prize is my cousin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The girl who won the prize is my cousin\" because a relative clause follows the noun it describes, and the main verb is comes after that clause. \"The girl who the prize won is my cousin\" fails because won must come before its object the prize. \"Who the girl won the prize is my cousin\" fails because who cannot replace the at the start of the main noun phrase. \"The girl won who the prize is my cousin\" fails because the relative clause who won the prize must stay together after girl."},{"id":"e-jumbled-28","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Darkness caused them to carry a lamp. Which order states that cause correctly?","options":["Because we carried a lamp, the road was dark","Because the road was dark, we carried a lamp","Because the road dark was, we carried a lamp","The road because was dark we carried a lamp"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Because the road was dark, we carried a lamp\" because because introduces the cause, and the main clause states the result. \"Because we carried a lamp, the road was dark\" fails because this reverses cause and effect, but the darkness caused the lamp, not the other way round. \"Because the road dark was, we carried a lamp\" fails because was must come before dark. \"The road because was dark we carried a lamp\" fails because because must begin its clause, not sit inside the noun phrase."},{"id":"e-jumbled-29","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"The rain stopped first, and then the children ran outside. Which order states that correctly?","options":["When the children ran outside, the rain stopped","Stopped the rain when the children ran outside","When the rain the children stopped ran outside","When the rain stopped, the children ran outside"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"When the rain stopped, the children ran outside\" because when introduces the earlier event, and the main clause says what happened after it. \"When the children ran outside, the rain stopped\" fails because this makes the running come before the end of the rain, which reverses the stated order. \"Stopped the rain when the children ran outside\" fails because the when-clause should not begin with the verb. \"When the rain the children stopped ran outside\" fails because the two clauses are tangled, so neither has its own subject and verb in order."},{"id":"e-jumbled-30","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Which is the correct order of these words: the / dog / that / barked / at / us / is / ours?","options":["The dog that barked at us is ours","The dog that us barked at is ours","That the dog barked at us is ours","The dog barked that at us is ours"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The dog that barked at us is ours\" because the relative clause follows dog, and the main verb is comes after the whole subject. \"The dog that us barked at is ours\" fails because barked must come before the phrase at us. \"That the dog barked at us is ours\" fails because that cannot take the place of the at the beginning of the sentence. \"The dog barked that at us is ours\" fails because the relative clause that barked at us must stay together after dog."},{"id":"e-jumbled-31","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"Rain would make them stay indoors. Which grammatical order states that condition?","options":["If we will stay indoors, it rains","If it rains, we will stay indoors","If rains it, we will stay indoors","Rains if it we will stay indoors"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If it rains, we will stay indoors\" because if is followed by a present-tense condition, and will stands in the result clause. \"If we will stay indoors, it rains\" fails because will does not belong in the if-clause, and this order also reverses the condition and the result. \"If rains it, we will stay indoors\" fails because the subject it must come before rains. \"Rains if it we will stay indoors\" fails because the if-clause is broken and cannot begin with rains."},{"id":"e-jumbled-32","topicId":"e-jumbled","subject":"english","stem":"The flood caused the bus to turn back. Which order states that cause correctly?","options":["Because the bus turned back, the road was flooded","The road because was flooded the bus turned back","Because the road was flooded, the bus turned back","Flooded the road was because the bus turned back"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Because the road was flooded, the bus turned back\" because because introduces the cause, and the main clause gives the result. \"Because the bus turned back, the road was flooded\" fails because this reverses cause and effect; the flood caused the bus to turn, not the opposite. \"The road because was flooded the bus turned back\" fails because because must open the cause clause instead of sitting after the road. \"Flooded the road was because the bus turned back\" fails because the cause clause cannot begin with the participle flooded in this pattern."},{"id":"e-vocab-13","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"My uncle visits us once in a blue moon. What does the idiom mean?","options":["On every full moon","Once each afternoon","Wearing blue clothes","Very rarely"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Very rarely\" because once in a blue moon means very rarely. \"On every full moon\" fails because the idiom is not about a real moon in the sky. \"Once each afternoon\" fails because the visits are rare, not daily. \"Wearing blue clothes\" fails because blue moon is not about the colour of clothing."},{"id":"e-vocab-14","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"The first sum was a piece of cake for Meera. What does the idiom mean?","options":["Very easy","A sweet snack","Too difficult to finish","Written on paper"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Very easy\" because a piece of cake means something is very easy. \"A sweet snack\" fails because the idiom is not about real food. \"Too difficult to finish\" fails because a piece of cake means the opposite of difficult. \"Written on paper\" fails because the phrase says nothing about paper."},{"id":"e-vocab-15","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Before the test, Rohan had to burn the midnight oil. What does the idiom mean?","options":["Light a lamp in a field","Work late into the night","Waste fuel at school","Sleep before sunset"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Work late into the night\" because burn the midnight oil means to work or study very late. \"Light a lamp in a field\" fails because the idiom is not about a real oil lamp outdoors. \"Waste fuel at school\" fails because it does not mean wasting fuel. \"Sleep before sunset\" fails because sleeping early is the opposite of this idiom."},{"id":"e-vocab-16","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Nobody should spill the beans about the surprise. What does the idiom mean?","options":["Drop real beans","Cook a new dish","Reveal a secret","Plant a garden"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Reveal a secret\" because spill the beans means to tell something that was meant to stay secret. \"Drop real beans\" fails because the idiom is not about food falling on the floor. \"Cook a new dish\" fails because cooking is not the meaning. \"Plant a garden\" fails because planting is not the meaning of this fixed phrase."},{"id":"e-vocab-17","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"After the journey, Grandmother felt under the weather. What does the idiom mean?","options":["Slightly ill","Standing in the rain","Very cheerful","Ready to travel"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Slightly ill\" because under the weather means slightly unwell. \"Standing in the rain\" fails because the idiom is not about being outdoors in bad weather. \"Very cheerful\" fails because cheerful is not the meaning; she felt unwell. \"Ready to travel\" fails because the phrase does not mean ready for another trip."},{"id":"e-vocab-18","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"The rescue team arrived at the eleventh hour. What does the idiom mean?","options":["At eleven o'clock exactly","At the last moment","Eleven hours late","Early in the morning"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"At the last moment\" because at the eleventh hour means at the last possible moment. \"At eleven o'clock exactly\" fails because the idiom is not a precise clock time. \"Eleven hours late\" fails because it does not measure eleven hours. \"Early in the morning\" fails because the last moment is not the same as early morning."},{"id":"e-vocab-19","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correctly spelled word.","options":["Neccessary","Necessery","Necessary","Necesarry"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Necessary\" because the standard spelling is necessary: one c, then e, then two s letters, then -ary. \"Neccessary\" fails because necessary has one c and two s letters, not two c letters. \"Necessery\" fails because the ending is -ary, not -ery. \"Necesarry\" fails because the middle vowels and the single c are missing in this spelling."},{"id":"e-vocab-20","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correctly spelled word for getting something that is sent to you.","options":["Recieve","Receeve","Recive","Receive"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Receive\" because receive is spelled with ei after c. \"Recieve\" fails because the rule i before e except after c makes the spelling receive, not recieve. \"Receeve\" fails because the vowel letters are ei, not ee. \"Recive\" fails because the word needs the e after c and before i."},{"id":"e-vocab-21","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correctly spelled word meaning to keep things apart.","options":["Seperate","Separate","Seprate","Separite"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Separate\" because separate has the vowel pattern a in the second syllable. \"Seperate\" fails because the second vowel is a, so the spelling is separate, not seperate. \"Seprate\" fails because the second syllable needs the letter a. \"Separite\" fails because the ending is -ate, not -ite."},{"id":"e-vocab-22","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correctly spelled word for a chart of the months.","options":["Calender","Calandar","Calendar","Calander"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Calendar\" because calendar ends in -ar and has e in the second syllable. \"Calender\" fails because the ending is -ar, not -er. \"Calandar\" fails because the second vowel is e, not a. \"Calander\" fails because both the middle vowel and the ending are wrong."},{"id":"e-vocab-23","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correctly spelled word for the position after eleventh.","options":["Twelth","Twelveth","Twelfeth","Twelfth"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Twelfth\" because twelfth keeps the f of twelve and adds th. \"Twelth\" fails because the f after the l is required: twelfth. \"Twelveth\" fails because there is no extra e before the final th. \"Twelfeth\" fails because the consonant order is lf, and there is no extra e."},{"id":"e-vocab-24","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Choose the correctly spelled word for the natural world around us.","options":["Environment","Enviroment","Enviornment","Environmant"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Environment\" because environment has n after enviro and ends in -ment. \"Enviroment\" fails because the letter n after o is missing in enviroment. \"Enviornment\" fails because the letters ro have been swapped. \"Environmant\" fails because the ending is -ment, not -mant."},{"id":"e-vocab-25","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Sleep can change how well you remember. Which sentence uses the verb correctly?","options":["Lack of sleep will effect your memory","Lack of sleep will affects your memory","Lack of sleep will affect your memory","Lack of sleep will effective your memory"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Lack of sleep will affect your memory\" because affect is the verb that means to influence something. \"Lack of sleep will effect your memory\" fails because effect is normally a noun here, while the verb meaning to influence is affect. \"Lack of sleep will affects your memory\" fails because after will, the verb stays in the base form affect. \"Lack of sleep will effective your memory\" fails because effective is an adjective and cannot take your memory as a verb would."},{"id":"e-vocab-26","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"The storm left a clear result. Which sentence uses the noun correctly?","options":["The affect of the storm was serious","The effective of the storm was serious","The effecting of the storm was serious","The effect of the storm was serious"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The effect of the storm was serious\" because effect is the noun that means a result. \"The affect of the storm was serious\" fails because affect is the verb; the noun for a result is effect. \"The effective of the storm was serious\" fails because effective is an adjective, not the noun for a result. \"The effecting of the storm was serious\" fails because effecting is not the ordinary noun for a result."},{"id":"e-vocab-27","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"The head of the school spoke to the pupils. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The principal addressed the school","The principle addressed the school","The principally addressed the school","The principal address the school"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The principal addressed the school\" because principal can mean the head of a school; principle means a rule or belief. \"The principle addressed the school\" fails because principle means a rule, while the head of a school is the principal. \"The principally addressed the school\" fails because principally is an adverb and cannot be the person who spoke. \"The principal address the school\" fails because the past form addressed is needed for this finished speech."},{"id":"e-vocab-28","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Fair play is a rule the team respects. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Honesty is an important principal","Honesty is an important principle","Honesty is an important principally","Honesty is a important principle"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Honesty is an important principle\" because principle means a rule or belief, and a vowel sound before important takes an. \"Honesty is an important principal\" fails because principal would name a person or a main thing, not the rule itself. \"Honesty is an important principally\" fails because principally is an adverb and cannot follow important as a noun. \"Honesty is a important principle\" fails because important begins with a vowel sound, so the article is an, not a."},{"id":"e-vocab-29","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"The bus was standing still at the stop. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The bus was stationery at the stop","The bus was stationarily at the stop","The bus were stationary at the stop","The bus was stationary at the stop"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The bus was stationary at the stop\" because stationary means not moving; stationery means paper, pens, and similar goods. \"The bus was stationery at the stop\" fails because stationery means writing materials, while still and not moving is stationary. \"The bus was stationarily at the stop\" fails because stationarily is not the adjective needed after was. \"The bus were stationary at the stop\" fails because bus is singular, so the verb is was, not were."},{"id":"e-vocab-30","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Pens, pencils, and paper are needed for class. Which sentence is correct?","options":["I need stationery for the drawing class","I need stationary for the drawing class","I need stationeries for the drawing class","I need a stationery for the drawing class"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"I need stationery for the drawing class\" because stationery, spelled with an e, means writing materials. \"I need stationary for the drawing class\" fails because stationary means not moving, while writing materials are stationery. \"I need stationeries for the drawing class\" fails because stationery is normally uncountable and does not take this plural. \"I need a stationery for the drawing class\" fails because a is not used before the uncountable noun stationery in this sentence."},{"id":"e-vocab-31","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Camels travel across hot, dry land. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Camels cross the hot dessert","Camels cross the hot desert","Camels cross the hot deserted","Camels crosses the hot desert"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Camels cross the hot desert\" because a desert is dry land; a dessert is sweet food, and the plural camels takes cross. \"Camels cross the hot dessert\" fails because dessert is a sweet course, while dry land is a desert. \"Camels cross the hot deserted\" fails because deserted is a different adjective and does not name the land here. \"Camels crosses the hot desert\" fails because camels is plural, so the verb is cross, not crosses."},{"id":"e-vocab-32","topicId":"e-vocab","subject":"english","stem":"Fruit was the sweet course at the end of the meal. Which sentence is correct?","options":["We ate fruit for desert","We ate fruit for deserted","We ate fruit for dessert","We ate fruit for desserting"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"We ate fruit for dessert\" because dessert, with a double s, is the sweet course eaten at the end of a meal. \"We ate fruit for desert\" fails because desert is dry land, while the sweet course is dessert. \"We ate fruit for deserted\" fails because deserted does not name a course of a meal. \"We ate fruit for desserting\" fails because desserting is not a noun for the sweet course."},{"id":"e-tags-13","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"This states a scientific fact that is always true. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If you will heat ice, it melts","If you heat ice, it melted","If you heated ice, it will melt","If you heat ice, it melts"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If you heat ice, it melts\" because the zero conditional uses the simple present in both clauses for a fact that is always true. \"If you will heat ice, it melts\" fails because will does not belong in the if-clause of a general fact. \"If you heat ice, it melted\" fails because a fact that is always true stays in the present, so melted is the wrong tense. \"If you heated ice, it will melt\" fails because this mixes a past if-clause with will, which is not the zero conditional."},{"id":"e-tags-14","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Boiling at one hundred degrees is a fact of nature. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If water reaches one hundred degrees, it boils","If water will reach one hundred degrees, it boils","If water reached one hundred degrees, it boils","If water reaches one hundred degrees, it boiled"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If water reaches one hundred degrees, it boils\" because a zero conditional about a scientific fact uses the simple present in the if-clause and in the result. \"If water will reach one hundred degrees, it boils\" fails because the if-clause of a fact uses the present, not will. \"If water reached one hundred degrees, it boils\" fails because reached is past, but this general fact needs the present in both clauses. \"If water reaches one hundred degrees, it boiled\" fails because boiled is past and does not state a permanent fact."},{"id":"e-tags-15","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Rain tomorrow is possible, and the picnic plan depends on it. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If it will rain tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic","If it rains tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic","If it rains tomorrow, we would cancel the picnic","If it rained tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If it rains tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic\" because the first conditional uses the simple present in the if-clause and will in the result. \"If it will rain tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic\" fails because will is not used in the if-clause of a first conditional. \"If it rains tomorrow, we would cancel the picnic\" fails because a real future result uses will, not would. \"If it rained tomorrow, we will cancel the picnic\" fails because rained would make the condition unreal, and it clashes with will."},{"id":"e-tags-16","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Daily practice is a real plan that can lead to improvement. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If you will practise daily, you will improve","If you practise daily, you would improve","If you practise daily, you will improve","If you practised daily, you will improve"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If you practise daily, you will improve\" because a likely future condition uses if plus the present, and will in the main clause. \"If you will practise daily, you will improve\" fails because the if-clause should use the present practise, not will practise. \"If you practise daily, you would improve\" fails because would belongs to an unreal conditional, not to this likely future. \"If you practised daily, you will improve\" fails because the past practised does not match will in a first conditional."},{"id":"e-tags-17","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker is not a bird. This is only imagination. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If I were a bird, I would fly","If I were a bird, I will fly","If I am a bird, I would fly","If I were a bird, I would flew"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If I were a bird, I would fly\" because the second conditional uses were for an unreal present and would plus the base form in the result. \"If I were a bird, I will fly\" fails because an unreal result uses would, not will. \"If I am a bird, I would fly\" fails because an unreal present uses were, not the present am. \"If I were a bird, I would flew\" fails because would is followed by the base form fly, not flew."},{"id":"e-tags-18","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker is giving unreal advice, imagining that he is the listener. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If I was you, I would tell the truth","If I were you, I would tell the truth","If I were you, I will tell the truth","If I am you, I would tell the truth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If I were you, I would tell the truth\" because If I were you is the second conditional, and the result uses would. \"If I was you, I would tell the truth\" fails because this Class 8 unreal pattern uses were for every person, including I, not was. \"If I were you, I will tell the truth\" fails because the unreal result needs would, not will. \"If I am you, I would tell the truth\" fails because am is present and real, but the sentence is only imagined."},{"id":"e-tags-19","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"She is not the captain. Imagine that she is. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If she was the captain, she will change the rule","If she is the captain, she would change the rule","If she were the captain, she would change the rule","If she were the captain, she will change the rule"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If she were the captain, she would change the rule\" because an imagined present uses were in the if-clause and would in the result. \"If she was the captain, she will change the rule\" fails because the unreal if-clause uses were, and the result uses would, not will. \"If she is the captain, she would change the rule\" fails because is would make the condition real, but she is not the captain. \"If she were the captain, she will change the rule\" fails because will does not match the unreal were-clause."},{"id":"e-tags-20","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"The speaker has no ticket, so going to the fair is only imagined. Which sentence is correct?","options":["If I have a ticket, I would go to the fair","If I had a ticket, I will go to the fair","If I had a ticket, I would went to the fair","If I had a ticket, I would go to the fair"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"If I had a ticket, I would go to the fair\" because the second conditional uses a past form in the if-clause and would plus the base verb in the result. \"If I have a ticket, I would go to the fair\" fails because have is present, but this unreal condition needs the past form had. \"If I had a ticket, I will go to the fair\" fails because an unreal result uses would, not will. \"If I had a ticket, I would went to the fair\" fails because would takes the base form go, not went."},{"id":"e-tags-21","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"The manner of speaking to the baby is gentle. Which sentence is correct?","options":["She speaks soft to the baby","She speaks softly to the baby","She speaks softy to the baby","She speaking softly to the baby"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She speaks softly to the baby\" because an adverb, often ending in -ly, modifies a verb. \"She speaks soft to the baby\" fails because speaks needs the adverb softly, not the adjective soft. \"She speaks softy to the baby\" fails because softy is not the adverb; the adverb is softly. \"She speaking softly to the baby\" fails because speaking has no finite verb in this sentence."},{"id":"e-tags-22","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Tastes works as a linking verb and describes the soup. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The soup tastes deliciously","The soup taste delicious","The soup tastes delicious","The soup is tasting deliciously"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The soup tastes delicious\" because linking verbs such as taste, look, and smell take an adjective, not an adverb. \"The soup tastes deliciously\" fails because a linking verb is followed by an adjective, not by the adverb deliciously. \"The soup taste delicious\" fails because soup is singular, so the verb is tastes. \"The soup is tasting deliciously\" fails because the continuous is unnecessary, and deliciously is the wrong form after a linking idea."},{"id":"e-tags-23","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"The porters used great effort all morning. Hard means with effort, not almost not. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The porters worked hardly all morning","The porters worked hardlier all morning","The porters working hard all morning","The porters worked hard all morning"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The porters worked hard all morning\" because hard can be an adverb meaning with great effort, while hardly means almost not. \"The porters worked hardly all morning\" fails because hardly means almost not, but the stem means they worked with effort. \"The porters worked hardlier all morning\" fails because hard does not take the comparative hardlier. \"The porters working hard all morning\" fails because working is not a complete verb here."},{"id":"e-tags-24","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"He wrote almost nothing, and the page stayed blank. Which sentence is correct?","options":["He hardly wrote a line, so the page was blank","He hard wrote a line, so the page was blank","He hardly written a line, so the page was blank","He hardly write a line, so the page was blank"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"He hardly wrote a line, so the page was blank\" because hardly means almost not and is followed by the correct form of the verb. \"He hard wrote a line, so the page was blank\" fails because hard would mean with effort, but the blank page shows he wrote almost nothing. \"He hardly written a line, so the page was blank\" fails because hardly is followed by the past form wrote, not the participle written. \"He hardly write a line, so the page was blank\" fails because the past sentence needs wrote, not the base form write."},{"id":"e-tags-25","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Looks describes her appearance, not the manner of an action. Which sentence is correct?","options":["She looks happily today","She look happy today","She looks happy today","She is looking happily today"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"She looks happy today\" because after a linking verb, use an adjective to describe the subject. \"She looks happily today\" fails because looks as a linking verb takes the adjective happy, not the adverb happily. \"She look happy today\" fails because she needs the singular verb looks. \"She is looking happily today\" fails because happily would modify an action, but the sentence describes her appearance."},{"id":"e-tags-26","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"The team's playing is being praised. Which sentence is correct?","options":["The team played good and won","The team played welly and won","The team playing well and won","The team played well and won"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"The team played well and won\" because well is the adverb that matches the adjective good. \"The team played good and won\" fails because played needs the adverb well, not the adjective good. \"The team played welly and won\" fails because the adverb is well, not welly. \"The team playing well and won\" fails because playing cannot replace the finite verb played."},{"id":"e-tags-27","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Compare the two ropes. Which sentence is correct?","options":["This rope is longer than that rope","This rope is more longer than that rope","This rope is longer then that rope","This rope is long than that rope"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"This rope is longer than that rope\" because a comparative adjective is followed by than, and it is not doubled with more. \"This rope is more longer than that rope\" fails because longer is already comparative, so more must not be added. \"This rope is longer then that rope\" fails because the comparison word is than, not then. \"This rope is long than that rope\" fails because the comparative longer is required before than, not the positive long."},{"id":"e-tags-28","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"There are many girls in the class, and Khushboo is taller than all the others. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Khushboo is the taller girl in the class","Khushboo is the tallest girl in the class","Khushboo is the most tallest girl in the class","Khushboo is tallest girl in the class"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Khushboo is the tallest girl in the class\" because use the superlative, with the, when one person or thing is compared with a whole group. \"Khushboo is the taller girl in the class\" fails because taller compares two, while a whole class needs the superlative tallest. \"Khushboo is the most tallest girl in the class\" fails because tallest should not be combined with most. \"Khushboo is tallest girl in the class\" fails because the superlative needs the article the."},{"id":"e-tags-29","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"The two puzzles are equal in difficulty. Which sentence is correct?","options":["This puzzle is as easier as that one","This puzzle is so easy as that one","This puzzle is as easy than that one","This puzzle is as easy as that one"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"This puzzle is as easy as that one\" because equal comparison uses as plus the positive adjective plus as. \"This puzzle is as easier as that one\" fails because as...as uses the positive degree easy, not the comparative easier. \"This puzzle is so easy as that one\" fails because in this positive comparison the pair is as...as, not so...as. \"This puzzle is as easy than that one\" fails because as is completed by as, not by than."},{"id":"e-tags-30","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Only two paths are being compared. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Of the two paths, this is the shorter one","Of the two paths, this is the shortest one","Of the two paths, this is the more shorter one","Of the two paths, this is shorter one"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Of the two paths, this is the shorter one\" because when two things are compared, use the comparative with the, not the superlative. \"Of the two paths, this is the shortest one\" fails because shortest is for more than two, while two items take the comparative shorter. \"Of the two paths, this is the more shorter one\" fails because more and shorter together make a double comparative. \"Of the two paths, this is shorter one\" fails because the comparative of two usually takes the: the shorter one."},{"id":"e-tags-31","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Compare the two examples of handwriting. Which sentence is correct?","options":["His handwriting is more better than mine","His handwriting is better than mine","His handwriting is best than mine","His handwriting is good than mine"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"His handwriting is better than mine\" because good, better, and best are irregular, and better is the form used with than. \"His handwriting is more better than mine\" fails because better is already the comparative of good, so more is not added. \"His handwriting is best than mine\" fails because best is the superlative and is not followed by than. \"His handwriting is good than mine\" fails because than needs the comparative better, not the positive good."},{"id":"e-tags-32","topicId":"e-tags","subject":"english","stem":"Compare the usefulness of the two metals. Which sentence is correct?","options":["Iron is usefuler than gold","Iron is more usefuler than gold","Iron is more useful than gold","Iron is most useful than gold"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is \"Iron is more useful than gold\" because adjectives of more than two syllables usually take more before the positive form. \"Iron is usefuler than gold\" fails because a longer adjective such as useful forms its comparative with more, not with -er. \"Iron is more usefuler than gold\" fails because more and -er must not be used together. \"Iron is most useful than gold\" fails because most is superlative, and than needs the comparative more useful."},{"id":"h-synonyms-13","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«उन्नति» का विलोम कौन-सा है?","options":["अवनति","प्रगति","वृद्धि","उत्थान"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is अवनति because अवनति means decline and is the opposite of उन्नति, progress. प्रगति is wrong because प्रगति means progress, so it is similar to उन्नति. वृद्धि is wrong because वृद्धि means increase, not decline. उत्थान is wrong because उत्थान means rising up, which is close to उन्नति, not opposite."},{"id":"h-synonyms-14","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"किस वाक्य में «फल» का अर्थ परिणाम है?","options":["बच्चे ने पेड़ से फल तोड़ा","मेहनत का फल उसे मिला","बाजार में फल बिक रहे हैं","उसने आम का रस पिया"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is मेहनत का फल उसे मिला because मेहनत का फल means the result of hard work, so फल here means result. बच्चे ने पेड़ से फल तोड़ा is wrong because बच्चे ने पेड़ से फल तोड़ा uses फल for fruit picked from a tree. बाजार में फल बिक रहे हैं is wrong because बाजार में फल बिक रहे हैं uses फल for fruit on sale. उसने आम का रस पिया is wrong because उसने आम का रस पिया is about mango juice and does not use फल to mean a result. The sentence does not even use the result sense."},{"id":"h-synonyms-15","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"किस वाक्य में «हार» का अर्थ गले का आभूषण है?","options":["टीम को हार का दुख हुआ","वह हार मानकर बैठ गया","माँ ने सोने की हार पहनी","खिलाड़ी अपनी हार से उदास था"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is माँ ने सोने की हार पहनी because सोने की हार पहनी means she wore a golden necklace, so हार is jewellery. टीम को हार का दुख हुआ is wrong because टीम को हार का दुख हुआ uses हार for a defeat in a match. वह हार मानकर बैठ गया is wrong because वह हार मानकर बैठ गया uses हार मानना for accepting defeat. खिलाड़ी अपनी हार से उदास था is wrong because खिलाड़ी अपनी हार से उदास था again uses हार as defeat, not as a necklace."},{"id":"h-synonyms-16","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«संपादक ने आज का पत्र छापा» में «पत्र» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["पेड़ का पत्ता","मित्र को लिखी चिट्ठी","सोने का सिक्का","समाचार-पत्र"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is समाचार-पत्र because an editor printing today's पत्र means the newspaper, one meaning of this अनेकार्थी word. पेड़ का पत्ता is wrong because पेड़ का पत्ता is another meaning of पत्र, but an editor does not print a leaf as आज का पत्र. मित्र को लिखी चिट्ठी is wrong because मित्र को लिखी चिट्ठी is a personal letter, and today's printed issue from an editor is the newspaper. सोने का सिक्का is wrong because सोने का सिक्का is not a meaning of पत्र at all."},{"id":"h-synonyms-17","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«रीता कल विद्यालय गई थी» में «कल» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["बीता हुआ दिन","आने वाला दिन","मशीन का पुर्जा","नदी का किनारा"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is बीता हुआ दिन because गई थी is past, so कल in this sentence means yesterday, the day already gone. आने वाला दिन is wrong because आने वाला दिन would fit a future verb such as जाएगी, and this verb is past. मशीन का पुर्जा is wrong because मशीन का पुर्जा is another meaning of कल, but this sentence is about going to school, not about a machine. नदी का किनारा is wrong because नदी का किनारा is not a meaning of कल."},{"id":"h-synonyms-18","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«मैं कल यात्रा करूँगा» में «कल» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["बीता हुआ दिन","आने वाला दिन","आकाश","पर्वत"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is आने वाला दिन because करूँगा is future, so कल here means tomorrow, the day that is coming. बीता हुआ दिन is wrong because बीता हुआ दिन would need a past verb such as गया था, and this verb looks ahead. आकाश is wrong because आकाश is not a meaning of कल. पर्वत is wrong because पर्वत is not a meaning of कल."},{"id":"h-synonyms-19","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«कक्षा में गुरु पाठ पढ़ा रहे हैं» में «गुरु» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["बृहस्पति ग्रह","भारी पत्थर","शिक्षक","समुद्र"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is शिक्षक because in a classroom, गुरु means the teacher who is reading the lesson. बृहस्पति ग्रह is wrong because बृहस्पति ग्रह is another meaning of गुरु, the planet Jupiter, and this sentence is about a class. भारी पत्थर is wrong because भारी पत्थर uses the sense heavy, and गुरु here is a person teaching, not a weight. समुद्र is wrong because समुद्र is not a meaning of गुरु."},{"id":"h-synonyms-20","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«नीला अंबर देखकर कवि मुसकुराया» में «अंबर» का अर्थ क्या है?","options":["रेशमी कपड़ा","सोना","नदी","आकाश"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is आकाश because नीला अंबर in a poem is the blue sky, a common meaning of अंबर. रेशमी कपड़ा is wrong because रेशमी कपड़ा is the other meaning, cloth, but नीला अंबर here is the sky the poet sees. सोना is wrong because सोना is not a meaning of अंबर. नदी is wrong because नदी is not a meaning of अंबर."},{"id":"h-synonyms-21","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"शुद्ध वर्तनी कौन-सी है?","options":["परीक्षा","परिक्षा","परीक्शा","परिक्शा"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is परीक्षा because the accepted spelling is परीक्षा, with a long ई and the conjunct क्ष. परिक्षा is wrong because परिक्षा uses a short इ and is the common wrong spelling. परीक्शा is wrong because परीक्शा writes श instead of the ष inside क्ष. परिक्शा is wrong because परिक्शा both shortens the vowel and breaks the consonant cluster."},{"id":"h-synonyms-22","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"बहुत चमकदार के अर्थ में शुद्ध वर्तनी कौन-सी है?","options":["उज्वल","उज्ज्वल","उजवल","उज्जवल"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is उज्ज्वल because the standard spelling is उज्ज्वल, with the double ज्ज्व cluster. उज्वल is wrong because उज्वल drops one ज and is the usual misspelling. उजवल is wrong because उजवल uses व without the required conjunct and drops a ज. उज्जवल is wrong because उज्जवल keeps two ज letters but misses the ज्व conjunct of the standard form."},{"id":"h-synonyms-23","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"शुद्ध वर्तनी वाला शब्द चुनो।","options":["आर्शीवाद","आशिर्वाद","आशीर्वाद","आशीर्वाड"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is आशीर्वाद because आशीर्वाद is the accepted spelling of blessing, with शी and a final द. आर्शीवाद is wrong because आर्शीवाद swaps the place of र् and is not correct. आशिर्वाद is wrong because आशिर्वाद uses a short इ in शि instead of the long शी. आशीर्वाड is wrong because आशीर्वाड ends in ड, and the word ends in द."},{"id":"h-synonyms-24","topicId":"h-synonyms","subject":"hindi","stem":"«अति + अधिक» से बनी सही वर्तनी कौन-सी है?","options":["अत्याधिक","अत्यधीक","अतियधिक","अत्यधिक"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is अत्यधिक because अति ends in इ and अधिक begins with अ. इ plus अ becomes य, so the spelling is अत्यधिक. अत्याधिक is wrong because अत्याधिक inserts या and is the common wrong spelling. अत्यधीक is wrong because अत्यधीक changes ध into धी and breaks the second word. अतियधिक is wrong because अतियधिक keeps an extra इ and does not make the sandhi properly."},{"id":"h-correction-13","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"विशेषण की दृष्टि से शुद्ध वाक्य कौन-सा है?","options":["काला घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है","काली घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है","काला घोड़ा तेज दौड़ती है","काले घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is काला घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है because घोड़ा is masculine singular, so the adjective is काला and the verb is दौड़ता है. काली घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है is wrong because काली घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है uses the feminine adjective काली for a masculine noun. काला घोड़ा तेज दौड़ती है is wrong because काला घोड़ा तेज दौड़ती है uses a feminine verb for घोड़ा. काले घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है is wrong because काले घोड़ा तेज दौड़ता है uses the plural oblique काले with a singular subject."},{"id":"h-correction-14","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"ने वाले भूतकाल का शुद्ध वाक्य चुनो।","options":["वह ने सच कहा","उसने सच कहा","वह सच कहा","उसने सच कही"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is उसने सच कहा because वह plus ने becomes उसने, and masculine सच takes कहा. वह ने सच कहा is wrong because वह ने सच कहा keeps वह and ने separate, which is not the correct form. वह सच कहा is wrong because वह सच कहा drops ने, and a past transitive verb needs it. उसने सच कही is wrong because उसने सच कही uses feminine कही, but सच is masculine."},{"id":"h-correction-15","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"लड़के के भूतकाल का शुद्ध वाक्य कौन-सा है?","options":["लड़का ने गाना गाया","लड़के ने गाना गाई","लड़के ने गाना गाया","लड़के गाना गाया"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is लड़के ने गाना गाया because before ने the subject becomes लड़के, and masculine गाना takes गाया. लड़का ने गाना गाया is wrong because लड़का ने गाना गाया keeps the direct form लड़का before ने. लड़के ने गाना गाई is wrong because लड़के ने गाना गाई uses feminine गाई for the masculine noun गाना. लड़के गाना गाया is wrong because लड़के गाना गाया drops the ने that a past transitive verb needs."},{"id":"h-correction-16","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"आदर और स्त्रीलिंग के साथ शुद्ध वाक्य चुनो।","options":["माता जी आ रहा है","माता जी आ रहे हो","माता जी आ रही हो","माता जी आ रही हैं"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is माता जी आ रही हैं because honorific माता जी takes a plural verb, and the feminine form is रही हैं. माता जी आ रहा है is wrong because माता जी आ रहा है uses masculine singular रहा है, missing both gender and respect. माता जी आ रहे हो is wrong because माता जी आ रहे हो uses हो, which is the तुम ending, and रहे is masculine. माता जी आ रही हो is wrong because माता जी आ रही हो keeps feminine रही but the तुम ending हो, not the honorific हैं."},{"id":"h-correction-17","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"«वर्षा» के साथ शुद्ध वाक्य कौन-सा है?","options":["वर्षा हो रही है","वर्षा हो रहा है","वर्षा हो रही हैं","वर्षा हो रहा हूँ"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is वर्षा हो रही है because वर्षा is feminine singular, so the continuous verb is हो रही है. वर्षा हो रहा है is wrong because वर्षा हो रहा है uses masculine रहा. वर्षा हो रही हैं is wrong because वर्षा हो रही हैं uses plural हैं for one rainfall. वर्षा हो रहा हूँ is wrong because वर्षा हो रहा हूँ uses masculine रहा and the first-person हूँ."},{"id":"h-correction-18","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"दो कर्ताओं वाला शुद्ध वाक्य चुनो।","options":["राम और श्याम बाजार गया","राम और श्याम बाजार गए","राम और श्याम बाजार गई","राम और श्याम बाजार गया है"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is राम और श्याम बाजार गए because two masculine subjects together take the plural गए. राम और श्याम बाजार गया is wrong because राम और श्याम बाजार गया uses the singular गया for two people. राम और श्याम बाजार गई is wrong because राम और श्याम बाजार गई uses the feminine गई. राम और श्याम बाजार गया है is wrong because राम और श्याम बाजार गया है is still singular, गया है, so it does not agree with two subjects."},{"id":"h-correction-19","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"परिमाण की दृष्टि से शुद्ध वाक्य कौन-सा है?","options":["थोड़ी दूध पी लो","थोड़े दूध पी लो","थोड़ा दूध पी लो","थोड़ी दूध पी लो है"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is थोड़ा दूध पी लो because दूध is a masculine mass noun, so the quantity word is थोड़ा. थोड़ी दूध पी लो is wrong because थोड़ी दूध पी लो uses feminine थोड़ी, which would suit चाय, not दूध. थोड़े दूध पी लो is wrong because थोड़े दूध पी लो uses the plural countable form थोड़े. थोड़ी दूध पी लो है is wrong because थोड़ी दूध पी लो है keeps the wrong gender and adds an extra है."},{"id":"h-correction-20","topicId":"h-correction","subject":"hindi","stem":"अनिवार्यता का शुद्ध वाक्य कौन-सा है?","options":["मैंने घर जाना है","मेरे को घर जाना है","मैं घर जाना है","मुझे घर जाना है"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is मुझे घर जाना है because necessity is expressed with मुझे and है, so मुझे घर जाना है is correct. मैंने घर जाना है is wrong because मैंने घर जाना है uses the past transitive marker मैंने, which does not make this obligation. मेरे को घर जाना है is wrong because मेरे को घर जाना है is the nonstandard stack मेरे को. मैं घर जाना है is wrong because मैं घर जाना है leaves the subject and है unmatched; the दative मुझे is required."},{"id":"t-parliament-19","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"Together with the two Houses, Parliament also includes","options":["only the Supreme Court","only the state governors","the President","the board of a steel company"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is the President because Parliament consists of the President, the Lok Sabha, and the Rajya Sabha. only the Supreme Court is wrong because the Supreme Court is part of the judiciary. only the state governors is wrong because governors head the states. They are not the third part of Parliament. the board of a steel company is wrong because a company board is not a house of Parliament.\nयाद रखो: दोनों सदनों के साथ संसद में राष्ट्रपति भी शामिल हैं। सुप्रीम कोर्ट नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: only the Supreme Court सिर्फ सुप्रीम कोर्ट संसद का तीसरा अंग नहीं।"},{"id":"t-parliament-20","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"Citizens take part in law-making when they","options":["are barred from every election","leave every decision to a foreign trading company","are told that criticism is always a crime","elect representatives and campaign for the laws they think the country needs"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is elect representatives and campaign for the laws they think the country needs because elections, public debate, and organised demand are how people push Parliament to act. are barred from every election is wrong because barring elections would end that participation. leave every decision to a foreign trading company is wrong because a foreign company is not the law-maker of the Republic. are told that criticism is always a crime is wrong because criticism of unjust laws is allowed.\nयाद रखो: नागरिक प्रतिनिधि चुनकर और ज़रूरी कानूनों के लिए अभियान चलाकर कानून बनाने में हिस्सा लेते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: leave every decision to a foreign trading company हर फैसला विदेशी कंपनी को सौंपना हिस्सा लेना नहीं।"},{"id":"t-parliament-21","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"A money bill is introduced in the Lok Sabha because","options":["the directly elected house has the main voice on taxes and spending","only the Rajya Sabha may tax the people, with no role for the Lok Sabha","the army introduces every tax","a weekly village market passes the Union budget"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is the directly elected house has the main voice on taxes and spending because money bills start in the house that the people elect directly. only the Rajya Sabha may tax the people, with no role for the Lok Sabha is wrong because the Rajya Sabha does not have the sole power to tax. the army introduces every tax is wrong because the army does not introduce tax bills. a weekly village market passes the Union budget is wrong because the Union budget is not passed by a village market.\nयाद रखो: धन विधेयक लोकसभा में आता है क्योंकि सीधे चुना सदन कर और खर्च पर मुख्य आवाज़ रखता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: only the Rajya Sabha may tax the people, with no role for the Lok Sabha सिर्फ राज्यसभा कर लगाए, यह उल्टा है।"},{"id":"t-parliament-22","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"The Rajya Sabha differs from the Lok Sabha because","options":["every adult votes for it in the same direct way","it represents the states and is not elected directly by all the people","it commands the three armed forces","it cannot discuss a national issue"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is it represents the states and is not elected directly by all the people because state legislatures elect its members, so it speaks for the states rather than by a direct national poll. every adult votes for it in the same direct way is wrong because direct election of all adults describes the Lok Sabha, not the Rajya Sabha. it commands the three armed forces is wrong because it does not command the armed forces. it cannot discuss a national issue is wrong because it does discuss national issues, including most bills.\nयाद रखो: राज्यसभा राज्यों का प्रतिनिधित्व करती है और सब लोगों द्वारा सीधे नहीं चुनी जाती।\nगलत मत याद करना: every adult votes for it in the same direct way हर वयस्क का सीधा वोट लोकसभा वाला तरीका है।"},{"id":"t-parliament-23","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"Before a proposal is passed and becomes law, it is called","options":["an FIR","a population pyramid","a bill","a subsidiary alliance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is a bill because a bill is the draft placed before Parliament. After passage and assent it is an Act. an FIR is wrong because an FIR is the first police report of a cognizable offence. a population pyramid is wrong because a population pyramid is a diagram of age groups. a subsidiary alliance is wrong because a subsidiary alliance was a colonial treaty with an Indian ruler.\nयाद रखो: पास होकर कानून बनने से पहले प्रस्ताव को विधेयक कहते हैं। एफआईआर नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: an FIR एफआईआर पुलिस की पहली सूचना है, विधेयक नहीं।"},{"id":"t-parliament-24","topicId":"t-parliament","subject":"sst","stem":"The final assent that turns a passed bill into an Act is given by","options":["the public prosecutor","a district judge acting without Parliament","the chairperson of a milk cooperative","the President"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is the President because after both Houses have done their part, the President assents and the bill becomes law. the public prosecutor is wrong because a public prosecutor argues criminal cases and does not assent to bills. a district judge acting without Parliament is wrong because a district judge does not replace Parliament and the President. the chairperson of a milk cooperative is wrong because a cooperative chairperson runs a members' enterprise, not the statute book.\nयाद रखो: पास विधेयक को अधिनियम बनाने वाली आखिरी स्वीकृति राष्ट्रपति देते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the public prosecutor लोक अभियोजक राष्ट्रपति की स्वीकृति नहीं देता।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-13","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"Public interest litigation lets a person","options":["approach a High Court or the Supreme Court about a public issue, not only a personal injury","file a case only about his or her own private shop","avoid every court","punish someone without a hearing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is approach a High Court or the Supreme Court about a public issue, not only a personal injury because PIL widened access so that a public wrong could be raised even by someone who was not the direct victim. Sometimes a letter has been treated as a petition. file a case only about his or her own private shop is wrong because a case only about one's own shop is an ordinary personal case, not the special point of PIL. avoid every court is wrong because PIL uses the courts. It does not avoid them. punish someone without a hearing is wrong because no one is punished without a hearing.\nयाद रखो: जनहित याचिका सार्वजनिक मुद्दे पर उच्च न्यायालय या सुप्रीम कोर्ट जाने देती है, सिर्फ निजी चोट पर नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: file a case only about his or her own private shop सिर्फ अपनी दुकान का मुकदमा जनहित नहीं।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-14","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"PIL has been important because","options":["it stops poor people from ever seeing a judge","it helps a public wrong reach the court when the affected people cannot easily file themselves","it removes the need for any law","it is a tax on salt"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is it helps a public wrong reach the court when the affected people cannot easily file themselves because groups and individuals have used PIL to raise issues that affect many people who lack the means to sue. it stops poor people from ever seeing a judge is wrong because PIL was meant to open the courts, not to close them to the poor. it removes the need for any law is wrong because the court still applies the law. it is a tax on salt is wrong because the salt tax belonged to the colonial salt law, not to PIL.\nयाद रखो: जनहित याचिका इसलिए महत्वपूर्ण है कि प्रभावित लोग खुद दाखिल न कर पाएँ तो भी सार्वजनिक गलती अदालत तक पहुँचे।\nगलत मत याद करना: it stops poor people from ever seeing a judge गरीबों को जज से दूर रखना इसका फायदा नहीं।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-15","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"An FIR is","options":["a bill that has received the President's assent","a diagram of age groups","the first information of a cognizable offence recorded by the police","the charter of the East India Company"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is the first information of a cognizable offence recorded by the police because FIR means First Information Report. It is the police record that a cognizable offence, a serious crime they can investigate, has been reported. a bill that has received the President's assent is wrong because a bill that has been assented to is an Act. a diagram of age groups is wrong because a diagram of age groups is a population pyramid. the charter of the East India Company is wrong because the Company's charter dates from 1600.\nयाद रखो: एफआईआर संज्ञेय अपराध की पहली सूचना है जिसे पुलिस दर्ज करती है। कंपनी का चार्टर नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the charter of the East India Company 1600 का चार्टर एफआईआर नहीं।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-16","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"The FIR is given to","options":["the Speaker, as if it were a money bill","the Drafting Committee of 1946","a map-maker","the police"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is the police because the information is lodged at a police station, and that starts the criminal investigation. the Speaker, as if it were a money bill is wrong because the Speaker presides over the Lok Sabha and does not register crimes. the Drafting Committee of 1946 is wrong because the Drafting Committee wrote the Constitution. a map-maker is wrong because a map-maker draws maps and does not record offences.\nयाद रखो: एफआईआर पुलिस को दी जाती है। स्पीकर को धन विधेयक की तरह नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the Speaker, as if it were a money bill स्पीकर के पास एफआईआर धन विधेयक नहीं बनती।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-17","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"In a criminal trial the public prosecutor","options":["represents the state","is the judge of the case","represents only the private business of the accused","is a soldier of the Meerut cantonment"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is represents the state because the public prosecutor conducts the case for the state, and the role begins after the police investigation. is the judge of the case is wrong because the judge is a different person and must stay neutral. represents only the private business of the accused is wrong because the prosecutor does not act as the accused person's private lawyer. is a soldier of the Meerut cantonment is wrong because Meerut's soldiers belong to the story of 1857.\nयाद रखो: फौजदारी मुकदमे में लोक अभियोजक राज्य का प्रतिनिधित्व करता है। जज नहीं बनता।\nगलत मत याद करना: is the judge of the case अभियोजक और जज एक कुर्सी पर नहीं बैठते।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-18","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"During a trial the judge","options":["must support the police even when there is no evidence","does not take sides and decides on the evidence and the law","must acquit the accused even when the crime is proved","leaves the verdict to a roadside crowd"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is does not take sides and decides on the evidence and the law because the judge hears both the prosecution and the defence and stays impartial. must support the police even when there is no evidence is wrong because a verdict needs evidence. The police are not automatically right. must acquit the accused even when the crime is proved is wrong because a proved crime is not brushed aside. The judge applies the law to the proof. leaves the verdict to a roadside crowd is wrong because a crowd does not deliver the court's verdict.\nयाद रखो: मुकदमे में जज पक्ष नहीं लेता। सबूत और कानून देखकर फैसला करता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: must support the police even when there is no evidence बिना सबूत पुलिस का साथ देना न्याय नहीं।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-19","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"A criminal case deals with","options":["only a private argument about the boundary of a field, with no crime","the price list of a shopping complex","a crime against society, such as theft or assault","the method of contour ploughing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is a crime against society, such as theft or assault because the state prosecutes a criminal case because the offence is treated as a wrong to society. only a private argument about the boundary of a field, with no crime is wrong because a boundary quarrel with no crime is a civil dispute. the price list of a shopping complex is wrong because a price list is not a criminal charge. the method of contour ploughing is wrong because contour ploughing is a farming method.\nयाद रखो: फौजदारी मामला समाज के खिलाफ अपराध है, जैसे चोरी या हमला। खेत की निजी सीमा नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: only a private argument about the boundary of a field, with no crime बिना अपराध खेत की सीमा दीवानी जैसी बात है।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-20","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"A civil case deals with","options":["a murder prosecuted by the state as a crime against society","the grease said to be on the cartridges of 1857","the royal charter of 1600","a dispute between persons, such as property or a contract"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is a dispute between persons, such as property or a contract because in a civil case one party sues another, often for compensation or an order about a private right. a murder prosecuted by the state as a crime against society is wrong because murder is prosecuted as a criminal case. the grease said to be on the cartridges of 1857 is wrong because the cartridge dispute is part of the history of 1857. the royal charter of 1600 is wrong because the charter of 1600 is the Company's grant from Queen Elizabeth I.\nयाद रखो: दीवानी मामला व्यक्तियों का विवाद है, जैसे संपत्ति या करार। राज्य की हत्या का मुकदमा नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: a murder prosecuted by the state as a crime against society हत्या का राजकीय मुकदमा फौजदारी है।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-21","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"An accused person is","options":["presumed innocent until the charge is proved","treated as guilty the moment a neighbour complains","denied any defence","the same official as the judge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is presumed innocent until the charge is proved because the prosecution must prove guilt. Until then the accused is presumed innocent. treated as guilty the moment a neighbour complains is wrong because a complaint is not itself a conviction. denied any defence is wrong because the accused has the right to defend the case. the same official as the judge is wrong because the judge is a neutral official, not the accused.\nयाद रखो: आरोपी तब तक निर्दोष माना जाता है जब तक आरोप साबित न हो। पड़ोसी की शिकायत से दोषी नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: treated as guilty the moment a neighbour complains पड़ोसी की शिकायत पर तुरंत दोषी मानना गलत है।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-22","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"The right to defend oneself means that the accused","options":["must stay silent while the police write the verdict","may have a lawyer and may challenge the evidence","is never told what the charge is","is sentenced before any trial begins"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is may have a lawyer and may challenge the evidence because a fair trial includes knowing the charge, testing the evidence, and being represented. must stay silent while the police write the verdict is wrong because the police do not write the verdict. The judge does, after the trial. is never told what the charge is is wrong because the charge has to be known so that a defence is possible. is sentenced before any trial begins is wrong because sentence comes after the trial, not before it.\nयाद रखो: बचाव का अधिकार: आरोपी वकील रख सकता है और सबूत को चुनौती दे सकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: must stay silent while the police write the verdict पुलिस फैसला लिखे और आरोपी चुप रहे, यह बचाव नहीं।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-23","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"Which order of courts runs from the top downward?","options":["Subordinate courts, High Courts, Supreme Court","Rajya Sabha, Lok Sabha, Supreme Court","Supreme Court, High Courts, subordinate courts","A district court, Parliament, a factory"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is Supreme Court, High Courts, subordinate courts because the Supreme Court is highest, then the High Courts, then the subordinate courts such as the district courts. Subordinate courts, High Courts, Supreme Court is wrong because that list is upside down. Rajya Sabha, Lok Sabha, Supreme Court is wrong because the two Houses are Parliament, not rungs of the judiciary. A district court, Parliament, a factory is wrong because Parliament and a factory are not courts in this pyramid.\nयाद रखो: ऊपर से नीचे: सुप्रीम कोर्ट, उच्च न्यायालय, फिर अधीनस्थ अदालतें।\nगलत मत याद करना: Subordinate courts, High Courts, Supreme Court यह क्रम उल्टा है, नीचे से ऊपर चढ़ाई।"},{"id":"t-judiciary-24","topicId":"t-judiciary","subject":"sst","stem":"The public prosecutor is expected to","options":["hide evidence that would help the accused","sit as the judge and also as the defence lawyer","refuse to appear in every criminal case","present the case fairly, because the aim is justice rather than a win at any cost"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is present the case fairly, because the aim is justice rather than a win at any cost because the prosecutor represents society and must act impartially, putting the full and fair case before the court. hide evidence that would help the accused is wrong because hiding helpful evidence would betray that duty. sit as the judge and also as the defence lawyer is wrong because the prosecutor is neither the judge nor the defence lawyer. refuse to appear in every criminal case is wrong because conducting the prosecution is the prosecutor's work.\nयाद रखो: लोक अभियोजक से उम्मीद है कि मामला निष्पक्ष रखे। जीत नहीं, न्याय लक्ष्य है।\nगलत मत याद करना: hide evidence that would help the accused आरोपी की मदद करने वाला सबूत छिपाना निष्पक्ष नहीं।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-13","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"The government must provide public facilities because","options":["a private company may not serve people who cannot pay","private firms always supply the poor free of cost","safe water is needed only by the rich","the Constitution forbids public schools"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is a private company may not serve people who cannot pay because profit-seeking firms can skip poor areas, so the state has to arrange water, health, and schooling. private firms always supply the poor free of cost is wrong because private firms do not always serve the poor for free. safe water is needed only by the rich is wrong because safe water is a need of every person. the Constitution forbids public schools is wrong because the Constitution supports education. It does not forbid public schools.\nयाद रखो: निजी कंपनी गरीब को छोड़ सकती है, इसलिए सरकार पानी, स्वास्थ्य और स्कूल दे।\nगलत मत याद करना: private firms always supply the poor free of cost निजी फर्म गरीब को हमेशा मुफ्त नहीं देतीं।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-14","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Equity means","options":["giving identical things and ignoring very different needs","giving people what they need so that they can be equal","helping only those who are already far ahead","closing schools in the poorest neighbourhoods"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is giving people what they need so that they can be equal because equity looks at unequal starting points and supplies what each person needs in order to stand equally. giving identical things and ignoring very different needs is wrong because identical treatment can leave a disadvantaged person still behind. helping only those who are already far ahead is wrong because helping only the advantaged widens the gap. closing schools in the poorest neighbourhoods is wrong because closing poor schools removes a facility people need.\nयाद रखो: इक्विटी यानी ज़रूरत के हिसाब से देना, ताकि लोग बराबर खड़े हो सकें।\nगलत मत याद करना: giving identical things and ignoring very different needs सबको एक जैसी चीज़, अलग ज़रूरत अनदेखी, इक्विटी नहीं।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-15","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Chennai is used as an example of water because","options":["every lane receives the same plentiful free supply and nobody is short","the city has no use for water","supply is unequal, and people who can pay often buy tankers while poorer areas get less","a water tanker is a type of soil"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is supply is unequal, and people who can pay often buy tankers while poorer areas get less because the chapter shows that scarce municipal water pushes the poor into long waits while others purchase private tankers. every lane receives the same plentiful free supply and nobody is short is wrong because the point of the example is shortage and unequal access, not plenty for all. the city has no use for water is wrong because a city cannot live without water. a water tanker is a type of soil is wrong because a tanker carries water. It is not soil.\nयाद रखो: चेन्नई में पानी असमान है। जो दे सके टैंकर खरीदे, गरीब इलाके कम पाएँ।\nगलत मत याद करना: every lane receives the same plentiful free supply and nobody is short हर गली में भरपूर मुफ्त पानी इस उदाहरण का उल्टा है।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-16","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Safe water is linked to the right to life because","options":["water is a luxury with no link to life","only factories need water","the right to life forbids anyone to drink","a person cannot live with dignity without it"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is a person cannot live with dignity without it because courts have read the right to life to include basic needs such as safe drinking water. water is a luxury with no link to life is wrong because water is a necessity, not a luxury. only factories need water is wrong because households need water, not factories alone. the right to life forbids anyone to drink is wrong because the right to life supports access to water. It does not forbid drinking.\nयाद रखो: बिना सुरक्षित पानी गरिमा से जीना मुश्किल। यह जीवन के अधिकार से जुड़ा है।\nगलत मत याद करना: water is a luxury with no link to life पानी लग्ज़री नहीं, जीवन की ज़रूरत है।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-17","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Sulabh is known for its work on","options":["sanitation, including low-cost toilets, and against manual scavenging","the steel mills of Pittsburgh","the Battle of Buxar","drawing population pyramids"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is sanitation, including low-cost toilets, and against manual scavenging because Sulabh has built toilet facilities and has campaigned to end the degrading work of manual scavenging. the steel mills of Pittsburgh is wrong because Pittsburgh is a steel centre in the United States. the Battle of Buxar is wrong because Buxar was fought in 1764. drawing population pyramids is wrong because population pyramids are diagrams of age groups.\nयाद रखो: सुलभ सफाई और सस्ते शौचालय के लिए जाना जाता है, हाथ से मैला ढोने के खिलाफ।\nगलत मत याद करना: the steel mills of Pittsburgh पिट्सबर्ग की स्टील मिलें सुलभ का काम नहीं।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-18","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Public transport counts as a public facility because","options":["it is built for one wealthy family and locked to everyone else","it lets people travel even when they cannot buy a private vehicle","it removes the need for any road","the right to travel means the state must give each citizen a private car"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is it lets people travel even when they cannot buy a private vehicle because buses and trains are shared services that widen mobility. it is built for one wealthy family and locked to everyone else is wrong because a locked family vehicle is private, not public. it removes the need for any road is wrong because public transport uses roads. It does not abolish them. the right to travel means the state must give each citizen a private car is wrong because the facility is shared transport, not a private car for each person.\nयाद रखो: बस और रेल उसे भी सफ़र कराती हैं जिसके पास अपनी गाड़ी नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: it is built for one wealthy family and locked to everyone else एक अमीर परिवार का ताला सार्वजनिक सफ़र नहीं।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-19","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Government schools and colleges support equality when","options":["they admit only the rich","they are closed in every poor neighbourhood","children who cannot pay high fees can still study","they refuse pupils from marginalised communities"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is children who cannot pay high fees can still study because public education is a facility that should not depend on the ability to pay a high fee. they admit only the rich is wrong because admitting only the rich would deepen inequality. they are closed in every poor neighbourhood is wrong because closing schools in poor areas withdraws the facility. they refuse pupils from marginalised communities is wrong because refusing marginalised pupils is discrimination.\nयाद रखो: जो ऊँची फीस नहीं दे सकता, वह भी सरकारी स्कूल-कॉलेज में पढ़ सके।\nगलत मत याद करना: they admit only the rich सिर्फ अमीरों का दाखिला समानता को तोड़ता है।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-20","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Health care is treated as a public facility because","options":["the law must turn the poor away from every hospital","health has no connection with the right to life","a doctor is a kind of mineral ore","illness does not wait until a person becomes rich"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is illness does not wait until a person becomes rich because public hospitals and health services exist so that treatment is not only for those who can pay. the law must turn the poor away from every hospital is wrong because turning the poor away would deny a basic facility. health has no connection with the right to life is wrong because health is closely tied to a life with dignity. a doctor is a kind of mineral ore is wrong because a doctor is a person, not an ore.\nयाद रखो: बीमारी अमीर बनने का इंतज़ार नहीं करती। इलाज सिर्फ पैसे वालों के लिए नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: the law must turn the poor away from every hospital गरीब को हर अस्पताल से भगाना कानून का हुक्म नहीं।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-21","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Sanitation is a public concern because","options":["unsafe waste spreads disease through a whole neighbourhood","dirt never affects anyone beyond a single person","the city must not think about toilets","Sulabh worked to expand manual scavenging"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct choice is unsafe waste spreads disease through a whole neighbourhood because drains and toilets protect everyone's health, so sanitation cannot be left as a purely private matter. dirt never affects anyone beyond a single person is wrong because disease from waste travels beyond one household. the city must not think about toilets is wrong because toilets are a core public facility. Sulabh worked to expand manual scavenging is wrong because Sulabh has worked against manual scavenging, not to expand it.\nयाद रखो: गंदा कचरा पूरे मोहल्ले में बीमारी फैलाता है। शौचालय निजी शौक नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: dirt never affects anyone beyond a single person गंदगी सिर्फ एक आदमी तक रुके, यह सच नहीं।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-22","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"When public facilities fail, marginalised groups are hurt more because","options":["they can buy private services more easily than the rich","they have less money to buy a private substitute","they do not need water or schools","the market always serves them first"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is they have less money to buy a private substitute because without public provision, those who cannot pay are left without water, health care, or school. they can buy private services more easily than the rich is wrong because the rich, not the marginalised, find private substitutes easier to buy. they do not need water or schools is wrong because water and schools are basic needs. the market always serves them first is wrong because the market often skips people who cannot pay.\nयाद रखो: हाशिये वाले निजी विकल्प कम खरीद पाते हैं। अमीर टैंकर ले लेता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: they can buy private services more easily than the rich गरीब अमीर से आसान निजी सेवा खरीद ले, यह उल्टा है।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-23","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"A private company may skip a poor neighbourhood because","options":["profit never influences a private business","the Constitution forbids government pipes and buses","it may see little profit there","the law says the poor must be served and the rich ignored"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is it may see little profit there because private firms follow paying customers, which is why the government has to provide basic facilities. profit never influences a private business is wrong because profit is exactly why a private firm chooses its customers. the Constitution forbids government pipes and buses is wrong because the Constitution supports public facilities such as water and transport. the law says the poor must be served and the rich ignored is wrong because equity does not mean ignoring the rich. It means the poor are not left out.\nयाद रखो: गरीब मोहल्ले में मुनाफा कम दिखे तो निजी कंपनी उसे छोड़ सकती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: profit never influences a private business मुनाफा निजी धंधे को नहीं छूता, यह मज़ाक है।"},{"id":"t-marginalisation-24","topicId":"t-marginalisation","subject":"sst","stem":"Laws such as the Prevention of Atrocities Act matter because","options":["they protect the person who commits the humiliation","they cancel Article 17","they make manual scavenging compulsory","they give victims a legal way to challenge violence and humiliation"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct choice is they give victims a legal way to challenge violence and humiliation because a clear offence and a punishment let people use the courts against caste violence. they protect the person who commits the humiliation is wrong because the Act is aimed at the offender, not at shielding the offender. they cancel Article 17 is wrong because Article 17, which abolishes untouchability, stands. The Act supports that promise. they make manual scavenging compulsory is wrong because manual scavenging is prohibited, not made compulsory.\nयाद रखो: पीड़ित हिंसा और अपमान के खिलाफ अदालत का रास्ता पाते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: they protect the person who commits the humiliation अपमान करने वाले को बचाना इस कानून का काम नहीं।"},{"id":"m-proportion-16","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"If 2 : 10 = 3 : x, then x is","options":["0.6","11","60","15"],"answer":3,"explanation":"In a proportion, product of extremes = product of means. 2 × x = 10 × 3, so x = 30/2 = 15. 0.6 swaps the positions. 11 treats the proportion like a subtraction pattern. The product of all three known numbers is not x."},{"id":"m-proportion-17","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"A can finish a job in 8 days and B can finish it in 8 days. Working together, they finish it in","options":["4 days","16 days","8 days","64 days"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A's one day of work is 1/8 and B's is 1/8. Together they do 1/4 of the job per day, so the time is 64/16 = 4 days. Adding the days, taking the faster person alone, or multiplying the days all ignore that they share the work."},{"id":"m-proportion-18","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"8 workers finish a wall in 9 days. How many days will 16 workers take, at the same rate?","options":["18 days","4.5 days","9 days","144 days"],"answer":1,"explanation":"This is inverse proportion: more workers, fewer days. 8 × 9 = 16 × days, so days = 4.5. Doubling the workers doubles the days only in direct proportion, which this is not. The worker-days product is not the number of days."},{"id":"m-proportion-19","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"7 notebooks cost ₹70. The cost of 14 notebooks at the same rate is","options":["₹84","₹70","₹140","₹10"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Cost is directly proportional to the number of notebooks. Double the notebooks means double the cost: ₹140. Adding the new count to the old price mixes rupees and notebooks. ₹10 is the price of one notebook, not of 14."},{"id":"m-proportion-20","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"If 2 : 12 = 7 : x, then x is","options":["1.1666666666666667","17","168","42"],"answer":3,"explanation":"In a proportion, product of extremes = product of means. 2 × x = 12 × 7, so x = 84/2 = 42. 1.1666666666666667 swaps the positions. 17 treats the proportion like a subtraction pattern. The product of all three known numbers is not x."},{"id":"m-proportion-21","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"6 workers finish a wall in 6 days. How many days will 12 workers take, at the same rate?","options":["12 days","3 days","6 days","72 days"],"answer":1,"explanation":"This is inverse proportion: more workers, fewer days. 6 × 6 = 12 × days, so days = 3. Doubling the workers doubles the days only in direct proportion, which this is not. The worker-days product is not the number of days."},{"id":"m-proportion-22","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"If 2 : 14 = 6 : x, then x is","options":["0.8571428571428571","18","168","42"],"answer":3,"explanation":"In a proportion, product of extremes = product of means. 2 × x = 14 × 6, so x = 84/2 = 42. 0.8571428571428571 swaps the positions. 18 treats the proportion like a subtraction pattern. The product of all three known numbers is not x."},{"id":"m-proportion-23","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"4 workers finish a wall in 10 days. How many days will 8 workers take, at the same rate?","options":["20 days","5 days","10 days","80 days"],"answer":1,"explanation":"This is inverse proportion: more workers, fewer days. 4 × 10 = 8 × days, so days = 5. Doubling the workers doubles the days only in direct proportion, which this is not. The worker-days product is not the number of days."},{"id":"m-proportion-24","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"If 2 : 16 = 5 : x, then x is","options":["0.625","19","160","40"],"answer":3,"explanation":"In a proportion, product of extremes = product of means. 2 × x = 16 × 5, so x = 80/2 = 40. 0.625 swaps the positions. 19 treats the proportion like a subtraction pattern. The product of all three known numbers is not x."},{"id":"m-proportion-25","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"12 workers finish a wall in 7 days. How many days will 24 workers take, at the same rate?","options":["14 days","3.5 days","7 days","168 days"],"answer":1,"explanation":"This is inverse proportion: more workers, fewer days. 12 × 7 = 24 × days, so days = 3.5. Doubling the workers doubles the days only in direct proportion, which this is not. The worker-days product is not the number of days."},{"id":"m-proportion-26","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"If 2 : 18 = 4 : x, then x is","options":["0.4444444444444444","20","144","36"],"answer":3,"explanation":"In a proportion, product of extremes = product of means. 2 × x = 18 × 4, so x = 72/2 = 36. 0.4444444444444444 swaps the positions. 20 treats the proportion like a subtraction pattern. The product of all three known numbers is not x."},{"id":"m-proportion-27","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"10 workers finish a wall in 11 days. How many days will 20 workers take, at the same rate?","options":["22 days","5.5 days","11 days","220 days"],"answer":1,"explanation":"This is inverse proportion: more workers, fewer days. 10 × 11 = 20 × days, so days = 5.5. Doubling the workers doubles the days only in direct proportion, which this is not. The worker-days product is not the number of days."},{"id":"m-proportion-28","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"If 2 : 20 = 3 : x, then x is","options":["0.3","21","120","30"],"answer":3,"explanation":"In a proportion, product of extremes = product of means. 2 × x = 20 × 3, so x = 60/2 = 30. 0.3 swaps the positions. 21 treats the proportion like a subtraction pattern. The product of all three known numbers is not x."},{"id":"m-proportion-29","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"8 workers finish a wall in 8 days. How many days will 16 workers take, at the same rate?","options":["16 days","4 days","8 days","128 days"],"answer":1,"explanation":"This is inverse proportion: more workers, fewer days. 8 × 8 = 16 × days, so days = 4. Doubling the workers doubles the days only in direct proportion, which this is not. The worker-days product is not the number of days."},{"id":"m-proportion-30","topicId":"m-proportion","subject":"maths","stem":"If 2 : 22 = 7 : x, then x is","options":["0.6363636363636364","27","308","77"],"answer":3,"explanation":"In a proportion, product of extremes = product of means. 2 × x = 22 × 7, so x = 154/2 = 77. 0.6363636363636364 swaps the positions. 27 treats the proportion like a subtraction pattern. The product of all three known numbers is not x."},{"id":"m-mensuration-16","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a rectangle 7 cm by 6 cm is","options":["26 cm²","13 cm²","42 cm²","84 cm²"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth = 7 × 6 = 42 cm². 26 is the perimeter in cm, not the area. 13 adds the sides. 84 doubles the area."},{"id":"m-mensuration-17","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a triangle with base 8 cm and height 8 cm is","options":["64 cm²","16 cm²","128 cm²","32 cm²"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Area of a triangle = (1/2) × base × height = (1/2) × 8 × 8 = 32 cm². 64 forgets the half and is the area of the related rectangle. Adding the sides is not an area. Doubling the product is four times the triangle's area."},{"id":"m-mensuration-18","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The volume of a cuboid 5 cm × 4 cm × 5 cm is","options":["130 cm³","100 cm³","20 cm³","14 cm³"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Volume = length × breadth × height = 5 × 4 × 5 = 100 cm³. 130 is the surface area. 20 is the area of the base only. The sum of the three edges is not a volume."},{"id":"m-mensuration-19","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"5 m² is equal to how many cm²?","options":["500","5000","500000","50000"],"answer":3,"explanation":"1 m = 100 cm, so 1 m² = 100 × 100 = 10,000 cm². 5 m² = 50000 cm². Multiplying by 100 converts metres to centimetres once, which is right for length, not for area. 1,000 is the factor for metres to millimetres in length."},{"id":"m-mensuration-20","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a rectangle 5 cm by 7 cm is","options":["35 cm²","24 cm²","12 cm²","70 cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth = 5 × 7 = 35 cm². 24 is the perimeter in cm, not the area. 12 adds the sides. 70 doubles the area."},{"id":"m-mensuration-21","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a triangle with base 8 cm and height 4 cm is","options":["32 cm²","16 cm²","12 cm²","64 cm²"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Area of a triangle = (1/2) × base × height = (1/2) × 8 × 4 = 16 cm². 32 forgets the half and is the area of the related rectangle. Adding the sides is not an area. Doubling the product is four times the triangle's area."},{"id":"m-mensuration-22","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The volume of a cuboid 6 cm × 6 cm × 5 cm is","options":["192 cm³","36 cm³","17 cm³","180 cm³"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Volume = length × breadth × height = 6 × 6 × 5 = 180 cm³. 192 is the surface area. 36 is the area of the base only. The sum of the three edges is not a volume."},{"id":"m-mensuration-23","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"6 m² is equal to how many cm²?","options":["600","60000","6000","600000"],"answer":1,"explanation":"1 m = 100 cm, so 1 m² = 100 × 100 = 10,000 cm². 6 m² = 60000 cm². Multiplying by 100 converts metres to centimetres once, which is right for length, not for area. 1,000 is the factor for metres to millimetres in length."},{"id":"m-mensuration-24","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a rectangle 11 cm by 3 cm is","options":["28 cm²","14 cm²","33 cm²","66 cm²"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth = 11 × 3 = 33 cm². 28 is the perimeter in cm, not the area. 14 adds the sides. 66 doubles the area."},{"id":"m-mensuration-25","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The volume of a cuboid 7 cm × 4 cm × 5 cm is","options":["166 cm³","140 cm³","28 cm³","16 cm³"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Volume = length × breadth × height = 7 × 4 × 5 = 140 cm³. 166 is the surface area. 28 is the area of the base only. The sum of the three edges is not a volume."},{"id":"m-mensuration-26","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a rectangle 9 cm by 4 cm is","options":["36 cm²","26 cm²","13 cm²","72 cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth = 9 × 4 = 36 cm². 26 is the perimeter in cm, not the area. 13 adds the sides. 72 doubles the area."},{"id":"m-mensuration-27","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The volume of a cuboid 8 cm × 6 cm × 5 cm is","options":["236 cm³","48 cm³","19 cm³","240 cm³"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Volume = length × breadth × height = 8 × 6 × 5 = 240 cm³. 236 is the surface area. 48 is the area of the base only. The sum of the three edges is not a volume."},{"id":"m-mensuration-28","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a rectangle 7 cm by 5 cm is","options":["24 cm²","12 cm²","35 cm²","70 cm²"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth = 7 × 5 = 35 cm². 24 is the perimeter in cm, not the area. 12 adds the sides. 70 doubles the area."},{"id":"m-mensuration-29","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The volume of a cuboid 4 cm × 4 cm × 5 cm is","options":["112 cm³","80 cm³","16 cm³","13 cm³"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Volume = length × breadth × height = 4 × 4 × 5 = 80 cm³. 112 is the surface area. 16 is the area of the base only. The sum of the three edges is not a volume."},{"id":"m-mensuration-30","topicId":"m-mensuration","subject":"maths","stem":"The area of a rectangle 5 cm by 6 cm is","options":["30 cm²","22 cm²","11 cm²","60 cm²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Area of a rectangle = length × breadth = 5 × 6 = 30 cm². 22 is the perimeter in cm, not the area. 11 adds the sides. 60 doubles the area."},{"id":"m-triangles-16","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 45° and 40°. The third angle is","options":["85°","135°","45°","95°"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 45 − 40 = 95°. 85° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 135° forgets to subtract 40°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-17","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 46° and 41°. The third angle is","options":["93°","87°","134°","46°"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 46 − 41 = 93°. 87° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 134° forgets to subtract 41°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-18","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 47° and 42°. The third angle is","options":["89°","91°","133°","47°"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 47 − 42 = 91°. 89° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 133° forgets to subtract 42°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-19","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 48° and 43°. The third angle is","options":["91°","132°","89°","48°"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 48 − 43 = 89°. 91° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 132° forgets to subtract 43°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-20","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 49° and 44°. The third angle is","options":["93°","131°","49°","87°"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 49 − 44 = 87°. 93° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 131° forgets to subtract 44°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-21","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 50° and 25°. The third angle is","options":["105°","75°","130°","50°"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 50 − 25 = 105°. 75° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 130° forgets to subtract 25°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-22","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 51° and 26°. The third angle is","options":["77°","103°","129°","51°"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 51 − 26 = 103°. 77° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 129° forgets to subtract 26°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-23","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 52° and 27°. The third angle is","options":["79°","128°","101°","52°"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 52 − 27 = 101°. 79° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 128° forgets to subtract 27°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-24","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 53° and 28°. The third angle is","options":["81°","127°","53°","99°"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 53 − 28 = 99°. 81° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 127° forgets to subtract 28°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-25","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 54° and 29°. The third angle is","options":["97°","83°","126°","54°"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 54 − 29 = 97°. 83° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 126° forgets to subtract 29°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-26","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 30° and 30°. The third angle is","options":["60°","120°","150°","30°"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 30 − 30 = 120°. 60° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 150° forgets to subtract 30°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-27","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 31° and 31°. The third angle is","options":["62°","149°","118°","31°"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 31 − 31 = 118°. 62° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 149° forgets to subtract 31°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-28","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 32° and 32°. The third angle is","options":["64°","148°","32°","116°"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 32 − 32 = 116°. 64° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 148° forgets to subtract 32°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-29","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 33° and 33°. The third angle is","options":["114°","66°","147°","33°"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 33 − 33 = 114°. 66° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 147° forgets to subtract 33°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-triangles-30","topicId":"m-triangles","subject":"maths","stem":"Two angles of a triangle are 34° and 34°. The third angle is","options":["68°","112°","146°","34°"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Angle sum is 180°. Third angle = 180 − 34 − 34 = 112°. 68° is the sum of the two given angles, not the third. 146° forgets to subtract 34°. The remaining option treats the triangle as if it had a fixed 90° split, which was not given."},{"id":"m-quads-16","topicId":"m-quads","subject":"maths","stem":"The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with 20 sides is","options":["3600°","3420°","360°","3240°"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Interior sum = (n − 2) × 180° = (20 − 2) × 180 = 3240°. 3600 forgets to subtract the two triangles' worth that close the shape. 3420 subtracts only one. 360° is the quadrilateral sum, or the exterior sum, not this polygon's interior sum unless n = 4."},{"id":"m-quads-17","topicId":"m-quads","subject":"maths","stem":"The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with 21 sides is","options":["3420°","3780°","3600°","360°"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Interior sum = (n − 2) × 180° = (21 − 2) × 180 = 3420°. 3780 forgets to subtract the two triangles' worth that close the shape. 3600 subtracts only one. 360° is the quadrilateral sum, or the exterior sum, not this polygon's interior sum unless n = 4."},{"id":"m-quads-18","topicId":"m-quads","subject":"maths","stem":"The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with 22 sides is","options":["3960°","3600°","3780°","360°"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Interior sum = (n − 2) × 180° = (22 − 2) × 180 = 3600°. 3960 forgets to subtract the two triangles' worth that close the shape. 3780 subtracts only one. 360° is the quadrilateral sum, or the exterior sum, not this polygon's interior sum unless n = 4."},{"id":"m-quads-19","topicId":"m-quads","subject":"maths","stem":"The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with 23 sides is","options":["4140°","3960°","3780°","360°"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Interior sum = (n − 2) × 180° = (23 − 2) × 180 = 3780°. 4140 forgets to subtract the two triangles' worth that close the shape. 3960 subtracts only one. 360° is the quadrilateral sum, or the exterior sum, not this polygon's interior sum unless n = 4."},{"id":"m-quads-20","topicId":"m-quads","subject":"maths","stem":"The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with 24 sides is","options":["4320°","4140°","360°","3960°"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Interior sum = (n − 2) × 180° = (24 − 2) × 180 = 3960°. 4320 forgets to subtract the two triangles' worth that close the shape. 4140 subtracts only one. 360° is the quadrilateral sum, or the exterior sum, not this polygon's interior sum unless n = 4."},{"id":"s-acids-23","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Litmus is obtained from which living source?","options":["Coal tar","Lichens","Iron ore","Petroleum"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Lichens\". Litmus dye is extracted from lichens. \"Coal tar\" is wrong because coal tar is a product of coal, not the source of litmus. \"Iron ore\" is wrong because iron ore is a mineral, not the source of this indicator. \"Petroleum\" is wrong because petroleum is a fossil fuel.\nयाद रखो: लिटमस लाइकेन से मिलता है। कोलतार और पेट्रोलियम के कुएँ नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Coal tar काला गाढ़ा तरल है, लिटमस की खदान नहीं।"},{"id":"s-acids-24","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"A solution changes neither red litmus nor blue litmus. What is it?","options":["A strong acid","A strong base","Acid rain","A neutral solution"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A neutral solution\". Neutral substances do not change the colour of litmus. \"A strong acid\" is wrong because a strong acid turns blue litmus red. \"A strong base\" is wrong because a strong base turns red litmus blue. \"Acid rain\" is wrong because acid rain is acidic and would change blue litmus.\nयाद रखो: न लाल लिटमस बदले, न नीला: घोल उदासीन है। अम्ल या क्षार किसी एक को ज़रूर रंग देता।\nगलत मत याद करना: A strong acid नीले लिटमस को लाल किए बिना नहीं छिपता।"},{"id":"s-acids-25","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"What colour does phenolphthalein give with an acid and with a base?","options":["Pink in an acid and colourless in a base","Colourless in an acid and pink in a base","Green in an acid and dark pink in a base","Red in both an acid and a base"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Colourless in an acid and pink in a base\". Phenolphthalein is an indicator that stays colourless in acidic solution and turns pink when the solution is basic. \"Pink in an acid and colourless in a base\" is wrong because that reverses the two colours. \"Green in an acid and dark pink in a base\" is wrong because those colours belong to china rose indicator, not to phenolphthalein. \"Red in both an acid and a base\" is wrong because phenolphthalein does not turn red in an acid.\nयाद रखो: फीनॉल्फथेलिन अम्ल में रंगहीन रहता है और क्षार में गुलाबी शरमाता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Pink in an acid and colourless in a base गुलाबी को अम्ल की तरफ मत ले जाना।"},{"id":"s-acids-26","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"What is the role of the normal amount of hydrochloric acid in the stomach?","options":["It is an antacid","It turns the stomach contents into a base","It is the same substance as baking soda","It helps in the digestion of food"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"It helps in the digestion of food\". The acid in gastric juice helps digestion. \"It is an antacid\" is wrong because an antacid is a base used when there is too much acid. \"It turns the stomach contents into a base\" is wrong because the stomach acid does not convert everything into a base. \"It is the same substance as baking soda\" is wrong because baking soda is a base, and hydrochloric acid is an acid.\nयाद रखो: पेट में सामान्य हाइड्रोक्लोरिक अम्ल भोजन पचाने में मदद करता है। एंटासिड तो अतिरिक्त अम्ल बुझाता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: It is an antacid एंटासिड मिल्क ऑफ मैग्नीशिया जैसा क्षार है, पेट का अपना अम्ल नहीं।"},{"id":"s-acids-27","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"A yellow turmeric stain on cloth turns reddish when washed with soap. Why?","options":["Soap is a strong acid, and turmeric turns red only in acids","The cloth has become a cloud of acid rain","Soap is basic, and turmeric changes colour in a base","Turmeric turns red only in lemon juice, and soap is lemon juice"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Soap is basic, and turmeric changes colour in a base\". The red colour is the turmeric test for a base. \"Soap is a strong acid, and turmeric turns red only in acids\" is wrong because soap is basic, and turmeric turns red in bases. \"The cloth has become a cloud of acid rain\" is wrong because a stain on cloth is not acid rain. \"Turmeric turns red only in lemon juice, and soap is lemon juice\" is wrong because lemon juice is acidic and does not turn turmeric red, and soap is not lemon juice.\nयाद रखो: साबुन क्षारीय है। हल्दी क्षार में लालिमा ले आती है, इसलिए पीला दाग लाल-भूरा दिखता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Soap is a strong acid, and turmeric turns red only in acids साबुन अम्ल नहीं, हल्दी अम्ल में नहीं लाल होती।"},{"id":"s-acids-28","topicId":"s-acids","subject":"science","stem":"Which word equation shows neutralisation?","options":["Acid plus base gives salt plus water","Metal plus oxygen gives only hydrogen","Fuel plus oxygen gives a salt","Acid plus acid gives a base"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Acid plus base gives salt plus water\". That is the neutralisation reaction. \"Metal plus oxygen gives only hydrogen\" is wrong because a metal and oxygen give an oxide, not hydrogen as the only product. \"Fuel plus oxygen gives a salt\" is wrong because burning gives heat and new substances such as carbon dioxide, not the salt of neutralisation. \"Acid plus acid gives a base\" is wrong because two acids do not neutralise each other to form a base.\nयाद रखो: उदासीनीकरण: अम्ल जमा क्षार बराबर नमक जमा पानी। अम्ल जमा अम्ल क्षार नहीं बनता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Acid plus acid gives a base दो अम्ल मिलकर क्षार की मिठाई नहीं बनाते।"},{"id":"s-combustion-16","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"Incomplete burning of carbon in a closed room can produce which poisonous gas?","options":["Oxygen","Nitrogen, which supports burning better than oxygen","Carbon monoxide","Water vapour, as the poisonous product of this incomplete burning"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Carbon monoxide\". Carbon monoxide forms when carbon burns in insufficient air. \"Oxygen\" is wrong because oxygen supports life and burning, and it is not the poison formed here. \"Nitrogen, which supports burning better than oxygen\" is wrong because nitrogen does not support burning better than oxygen. \"Water vapour, as the poisonous product of this incomplete burning\" is wrong because the dangerous gas named for incomplete burning is carbon monoxide.\nयाद रखो: बंद कमरे में कार्बन अधूरा जले तो जहरीली कार्बन मोनोऑक्साइड बन सकती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Oxygen साँस की गैस है, अधूरे जलने का ज़हर नहीं।"},{"id":"s-combustion-17","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"Why is carbon monoxide dangerous to breathe?","options":["It reduces the ability of the blood to carry oxygen","It is the same gas as oxygen and helps breathing","It is used only to fill toy balloons and is harmless","It turns blood into a substance that makes bones stronger"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"It reduces the ability of the blood to carry oxygen\". A closed room with a coal fire can fill with this poisonous gas. \"It is the same gas as oxygen and helps breathing\" is wrong because it is not oxygen, and it harms breathing. \"It is used only to fill toy balloons and is harmless\" is wrong because it is poisonous, not a harmless balloon gas. \"It turns blood into a substance that makes bones stronger\" is wrong because it interferes with oxygen transport and does not strengthen bones.\nयाद रखो: कार्बन मोनोऑक्साइड खून की ऑक्सीजन ढोने की ताकत घटाती है। वह ऑक्सीजन की बहन नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: It is the same gas as oxygen and helps breathing यह गैस साँस नहीं बढ़ाती, छीनती है।"},{"id":"s-combustion-18","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"A gas stove burns LPG with a blue flame. What does the blue flame suggest?","options":["A large amount of unburnt carbon is glowing","The fuel is not burning","Combustion is more complete","The flame is the cool inner zone of a candle"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Combustion is more complete\". A blue flame means the fuel is burning more completely than a sooty yellow flame. \"A large amount of unburnt carbon is glowing\" is wrong because unburnt carbon gives a yellow, sooty flame. \"The fuel is not burning\" is wrong because a flame means the fuel is burning. \"The flame is the cool inner zone of a candle\" is wrong because the inner candle zone is the least hot, and a blue gas flame is a hot complete burn.\nयाद रखो: एलपीजी की नीली लौ बताती है कि जलना ज़्यादा पूरा हो रहा है। पीली लौ में कार्बन अधजला चमकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A large amount of unburnt carbon is glowing अधजला कार्बन पीली चमक देता है, नीली पूरी लौ नहीं।"},{"id":"s-combustion-19","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"Wax burns with a flame, but charcoal glows without a tall flame. Why does the wax give a flame?","options":["Charcoal is a gas and wax is a metal","Wax vapour burns, and substances that form vapour burn with a flame","A flame appears only when oxygen is absent","Wax does not really burn, and the flame is only a mirror image"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Wax vapour burns, and substances that form vapour burn with a flame\". Charcoal does not produce such vapour, so it glows instead. \"Charcoal is a gas and wax is a metal\" is wrong because charcoal is a solid form of carbon, and wax is not a metal. \"A flame appears only when oxygen is absent\" is wrong because combustion needs oxygen. \"Wax does not really burn, and the flame is only a mirror image\" is wrong because the flame comes from burning wax vapour, not from a mirror.\nयाद रखो: जो चीज़ वाष्प बनाती है वह लौ से जलती है। मोम वाष्प बनता है, लकड़ी का कोयला सिर्फ दहकता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Charcoal is a gas and wax is a metal कोयला गैस नहीं, मोम धातु नहीं।"},{"id":"s-combustion-20","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"Which of these is an explosion?","options":["Iron rusting slowly in moist air","Ice melting on a plate","A cup of water warming slowly","A firecracker bursting suddenly with heat, light, sound, and a large volume of gas"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A firecracker bursting suddenly with heat, light, sound, and a large volume of gas\". An explosion is combustion that happens very fast and produces a large amount of gas. \"Iron rusting slowly in moist air\" is wrong because rusting is a slow chemical change, not an explosion. \"Ice melting on a plate\" is wrong because melting is a physical change. \"A cup of water warming slowly\" is wrong because slow warming is not an explosion.\nयाद रखो: पटाखा अचानक गर्मी, प्रकाश, आवाज़ और बहुत गैस के साथ फटता है। यही विस्फोट है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Iron rusting slowly in moist air धीमी जंग है, धमाका नहीं।"},{"id":"s-combustion-21","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"The head of a modern safety match contains antimony trisulphide and potassium chlorate. What is on the rubbing surface?","options":["Only water and sand","Powdered glass and a little red phosphorus","White phosphorus left open on the box, as in the earliest unsafe matches","Sodium metal kept in kerosene on the box"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Powdered glass and a little red phosphorus\". Striking the match heats the red phosphorus and starts the combustion of the head. \"Only water and sand\" is wrong because water and sand are used to control some fires, not as the matchbox side. \"White phosphorus left open on the box, as in the earliest unsafe matches\" is wrong because modern safety matches keep red phosphorus on the rubbing surface, not white phosphorus in the open. \"Sodium metal kept in kerosene on the box\" is wrong because sodium is a reactive metal stored in kerosene, and it is not the matchbox coating.\nयाद रखो: माचिस की रगड़ने वाली सतह पर चूर्ण काँच और थोड़ा लाल फॉस्फोरस होता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: White phosphorus left open on the box पुरानी असुरक्षित माचिस की बात है, आज की सतह की नहीं।"},{"id":"s-combustion-22","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"Heat and temperature are not the same. Which statement is correct?","options":["Heat and temperature are two names for the same reading in degrees","Temperature is measured in kilograms of fuel","Heat always flows from a cold object to a hot object","Heat is energy that flows from a hotter object to a colder one, and temperature measures how hot an object is"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Heat is energy that flows from a hotter object to a colder one, and temperature measures how hot an object is\". A large pot of water at 40 degrees Celsius holds more heat energy than a cup at the same temperature. \"Heat and temperature are two names for the same reading in degrees\" is wrong because temperature is the degree of hotness, and heat is the energy transferred. \"Temperature is measured in kilograms of fuel\" is wrong because temperature is measured on a scale such as degrees Celsius, not in kilograms. \"Heat always flows from a cold object to a hot object\" is wrong because heat flows from the hotter object to the colder one.\nयाद रखो: ऊष्मा गर्म से ठंडे की तरफ बहने वाली ऊर्जा है। ताप बताता है कि चीज़ कितनी गर्म है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Heat always flows from a cold object to a hot object गर्मी ठंडे से गर्म की तरफ नहीं चढ़ती।"},{"id":"s-combustion-23","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"A metal pan has a plastic handle. Why is the handle safer to hold while cooking?","options":["Plastic conducts heat better than metal","A metal handle would stay cold while plastic burnt the hand for the opposite reason","Plastic is a poor conductor of heat, while the metal pan conducts heat well","Plastic and metal conduct heat equally well"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Plastic is a poor conductor of heat, while the metal pan conducts heat well\". The plastic does not pass heat to the hand as quickly as metal would. \"Plastic conducts heat better than metal\" is wrong because metals are the better conductors. \"A metal handle would stay cold while plastic burnt the hand for the opposite reason\" is wrong because metal would conduct heat to the hand, which is why the handle is plastic. \"Plastic and metal conduct heat equally well\" is wrong because they do not, and that difference is why the handle is plastic.\nयाद रखो: प्लास्टिक ऊष्मा का खराब चालक है, धातु की कड़ाही अच्छी चालक। इसलिए प्लास्टिक हत्था सुरक्षित है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Plastic conducts heat better than metal धातु गर्मी ले जाती है, प्लास्टिक रोकता है।"},{"id":"s-combustion-24","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"A clinical thermometer has a short range and a kink. What is that range, and what does the kink do?","options":["About 35 degrees Celsius to 42 degrees Celsius, and the kink holds the mercury level until the reading is taken","About minus 10 degrees Celsius to 110 degrees Celsius, with no kink","0 degrees Celsius to 100 degrees Celsius, used only as a boiling scale","It measures calorific value in kilojoules"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"About 35 degrees Celsius to 42 degrees Celsius, and the kink holds the mercury level until the reading is taken\". This thermometer is meant for body temperature, and a jerk brings the mercury down again. \"About minus 10 degrees Celsius to 110 degrees Celsius, with no kink\" is wrong because that description fits a laboratory thermometer. \"0 degrees Celsius to 100 degrees Celsius, used only as a boiling scale\" is wrong because the clinical range matches body temperature, not the full boiling scale of water. \"It measures calorific value in kilojoules\" is wrong because a clinical thermometer measures temperature, not calorific value.\nयाद रखो: डॉक्टरी थर्मामीटर लगभग 35 से 42 डिग्री तक है। मोड़ पारे को पढ़ने तक रोककर रखता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: About minus 10 degrees Celsius to 110 degrees Celsius, with no kink प्रयोगशाला वाले थर्मामीटर की बड़ी पट्टी है।"},{"id":"s-combustion-25","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"During the day at the seashore, wind often blows from the sea toward the land. Why?","options":["Land and sea heat at exactly the same rate, so no breeze can form","The sea heats faster than the land by day, so the breeze blows from land to sea","Land heats faster than the sea, air rises over the land, and cooler air from the sea moves in","The breeze is caused by the calorific value of sand"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Land heats faster than the sea, air rises over the land, and cooler air from the sea moves in\". This daytime wind is the sea breeze. \"Land and sea heat at exactly the same rate, so no breeze can form\" is wrong because unequal heating is what starts the breeze. \"The sea heats faster than the land by day, so the breeze blows from land to sea\" is wrong because by day the land heats faster, and the breeze blows from sea to land. \"The breeze is caused by the calorific value of sand\" is wrong because calorific value is about fuels, not about this wind.\nयाद रखो: दिन में ज़मीन जल्दी गर्म होती है, हवा ऊपर उठती है, समुद्र की ठंडी हवा ज़मीन की तरफ आती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: The sea heats faster than the land by day समुद्र दिन में ज़मीन से तेज़ गर्म नहीं होता।"},{"id":"s-combustion-26","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"At night the land cools faster than the sea. Which breeze is then expected?","options":["A land breeze, blowing from the land toward the sea","A sea breeze in the same direction as at noon","No movement of air is possible at night","A breeze caused by the combustion of sea water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A land breeze, blowing from the land toward the sea\". Cooler air over the land moves out to sea. \"A sea breeze in the same direction as at noon\" is wrong because the daytime sea breeze and the night land breeze blow in opposite directions. \"No movement of air is possible at night\" is wrong because the unequal cooling still moves the air. \"A breeze caused by the combustion of sea water\" is wrong because sea water is not burning to make this wind.\nयाद रखो: रात में ज़मीन जल्दी ठंडी होती है, हवा ज़मीन से समुद्र की तरफ चलती है। यही थल समीर है।\nगलत मत याद करना: A sea breeze in the same direction as at noon दोपहर वाली समुद्र समीर रात को उल्टी हो जाती है।"},{"id":"s-combustion-27","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"Woollen clothes keep us warm in winter mainly because of what?","options":["Wool is a metal and carries body heat away quickly","Wool produces heat by spontaneous combustion on the skin","Wool lowers the ignition temperature of the skin","Wool traps air, and air is a poor conductor of heat, so body heat escapes slowly"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Wool traps air, and air is a poor conductor of heat, so body heat escapes slowly\". The trapped air insulates the body. \"Wool is a metal and carries body heat away quickly\" is wrong because wool is not a metal, and it slows heat loss. \"Wool produces heat by spontaneous combustion on the skin\" is wrong because wool does not catch fire by itself at body temperature. \"Wool lowers the ignition temperature of the skin\" is wrong because clothing does not work by changing the ignition temperature of skin.\nयाद रखो: ऊन हवा को फँसाती है। हवा ऊष्मा की खराब चालक है, इसलिए शरीर की गर्मी धीरे बाहर जाती है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Wool is a metal and carries body heat away quickly ऊन धातु नहीं, गर्मी चुराती नहीं।"},{"id":"s-combustion-28","topicId":"s-combustion","subject":"science","stem":"A paper cup of water can be heated over a flame for a short time without the paper burning. Why?","options":["Paper has no ignition temperature","The water absorbs heat, so the paper stays below its ignition temperature","The water is the fuel that makes the paper burn","The flame has no hot outer zone when a cup is present"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"The water absorbs heat, so the paper stays below its ignition temperature\". The paper does not reach the temperature at which it would catch fire. \"Paper has no ignition temperature\" is wrong because paper does have an ignition temperature, and the water keeps the cup below it. \"The water is the fuel that makes the paper burn\" is wrong because the water prevents burning in this activity. \"The flame has no hot outer zone when a cup is present\" is wrong because the flame zones are still there, and the water is what protects the paper.\nयाद रखो: कप का पानी गर्मी सोख लेता है, कागज़ ज्वलन ताप से नीचे रहता है, इसलिए जल्दी नहीं जलता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Paper has no ignition temperature कागज़ का ज्वलन ताप होता है, पानी उसे वहाँ तक नहीं पहुँचने देता।"},{"id":"s-coal-16","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Which pair sorts the resources correctly?","options":["Coal is inexhaustible, and sunlight is exhaustible","Both coal and petroleum are inexhaustible","Air is exhaustible, and petroleum is inexhaustible","Sunlight is inexhaustible, and coal is exhaustible"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Sunlight is inexhaustible, and coal is exhaustible\". Sunlight and air are not used up in the way coal is, and coal reserves are limited. \"Coal is inexhaustible, and sunlight is exhaustible\" is wrong because that swaps the two groups. \"Both coal and petroleum are inexhaustible\" is wrong because both are fossil fuels with limited reserves. \"Air is exhaustible, and petroleum is inexhaustible\" is wrong because air is treated as inexhaustible in this chapter, and petroleum is exhaustible.\nयाद रखो: सूरज अक्षय है, कोयला समाप्त होने वाला है। जोड़ी उल्टी मत लिखना।\nगलत मत याद करना: Coal is inexhaustible, and sunlight is exhaustible दोनों लेबल अदला-बदली हैं।"},{"id":"s-coal-17","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Why must coal and petroleum be used carefully?","options":["They form again inside every home within a few days","Their reserves are limited, and they take millions of years to form","They are metals that can be melted and used again with no limit on the resource","They are present in unlimited amount, like sunlight"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Their reserves are limited, and they take millions of years to form\". They cannot be replaced quickly in the laboratory or in nature on a human time scale. \"They form again inside every home within a few days\" is wrong because formation takes millions of years. \"They are metals that can be melted and used again with no limit on the resource\" is wrong because they are fuels, not recyclable metals, and the deposits are limited. \"They are present in unlimited amount, like sunlight\" is wrong because sunlight is the inexhaustible comparison, and these fuels are not unlimited.\nयाद रखो: कोयला और पेट्रोलियम सीमित हैं और बनने में लाखों साल लेते हैं। घर में कुछ दिन में नहीं बनते।\nगलत मत याद करना: They form again inside every home within a few days रसोई में नया कोयला नहीं उगता।"},{"id":"s-coal-18","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Petroleum is sometimes called black gold because of what?","options":["It is a yellow metal like gold","It is dug only from gold mines","It can be beaten into shiny sheets","Its great commercial importance"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Its great commercial importance\". Many useful fuels and products come from it, so it is very valuable. \"It is a yellow metal like gold\" is wrong because petroleum is a dark oily liquid, not a metal. \"It is dug only from gold mines\" is wrong because it comes from oil wells, not from gold mines. \"It can be beaten into shiny sheets\" is wrong because that property is malleability of metals, not of petroleum.\nयाद रखो: पेट्रोलियम काला सोना इसलिए कहलाता है क्योंकि व्यापार में इसकी कीमत बहुत है। वह पीसी हुई सोने की चादर नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: It is a yellow metal like gold तेल पीली धातु नहीं है।"},{"id":"s-coal-19","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Which driving habit matches a PCRA tip for saving petrol or diesel?","options":["Speed up and brake hard again and again","Keep the tyres soft and underinflated","Switch off the engine while waiting at a traffic light","Skip all servicing of the vehicle"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Switch off the engine while waiting at a traffic light\". PCRA advises this so that fuel is not burnt while the vehicle is standing. \"Speed up and brake hard again and again\" is wrong because uneven, aggressive driving wastes fuel. \"Keep the tyres soft and underinflated\" is wrong because PCRA asks for correct tyre pressure, not soft tyres. \"Skip all servicing of the vehicle\" is wrong because regular maintenance is one of the tips.\nयाद रखो: बत्ती पर इंतज़ार में इंजन बंद करो। यही पेट्रोल बचाने वाली PCRA आदत है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Keep the tyres soft and underinflated पिचके टायर ईंधन फूँकते हैं, बचाते नहीं।"},{"id":"s-coal-20","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Which other PCRA habit saves fuel?","options":["Drive at a steady moderate speed and keep the tyre pressure correct","Race the engine while the vehicle is parked","Remain in neutral and rev at every traffic light","Carry unneeded load and ignore maintenance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Drive at a steady moderate speed and keep the tyre pressure correct\". Steady speed and correct pressure reduce wasted fuel. \"Race the engine while the vehicle is parked\" is wrong because revving a parked engine burns fuel for no travel. \"Remain in neutral and rev at every traffic light\" is wrong because the advice is to switch the engine off while waiting. \"Carry unneeded load and ignore maintenance\" is wrong because extra load and poor maintenance increase fuel use.\nयाद रखो: समान मध्यम गति और सही टायर दाब ईंधन बचाते हैं। बेकार बोझ और रेस इंजन उल्टा करते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Race the engine while the vehicle is parked खड़ी गाड़ी में रेस ईंधन जलाती है।"},{"id":"s-coal-21","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"In India, the chapter says natural gas has been found in which of these regions?","options":["Only inside packets of table salt","Only in drums of coal tar","Tripura, Rajasthan, Maharashtra, and the Krishna Godavari delta","In every limestone hill, as pure oxygen"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Tripura, Rajasthan, Maharashtra, and the Krishna Godavari delta\". Those are the places named for natural gas reserves. \"Only inside packets of table salt\" is wrong because salt is not a natural gas field. \"Only in drums of coal tar\" is wrong because coal tar is a coal product, not these gas fields. \"In every limestone hill, as pure oxygen\" is wrong because the reserves are natural gas in the named regions, not oxygen in limestone.\nयाद रखो: भारत में प्राकृतिक गैस त्रिपुरा, राजस्थान, महाराष्ट्र और कृष्णा-गोदावरी डेल्टा में मिली है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Only inside packets of table salt नमक की पुड़िया गैस का कुआँ नहीं।"},{"id":"s-coal-22","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Where and when was the world's first oil well drilled, according to the chapter?","options":["Pennsylvania, USA, in 1859","Makum in Assam in 1859","A coal mine in every country in that same year","Under a forest that was turning into coke"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Pennsylvania, USA, in 1859\". The chapter states that the first oil well was drilled there in 1859. \"Makum in Assam in 1859\" is wrong because oil was struck at Makum later, in 1867, and 1859 is the Pennsylvania well. \"A coal mine in every country in that same year\" is wrong because the chapter names one first well, in Pennsylvania. \"Under a forest that was turning into coke\" is wrong because coke is a coal product, and the first oil well was drilled in Pennsylvania.\nयाद रखो: दुनिया का पहला तेल कुआँ 1859 में अमेरिका के पेनसिल्वेनिया में खुदा। मकुम असम बाद की कहानी है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Makum in Assam in 1859 असम में तेल 1867 में लगा, 1859 अमेरिका का साल है।"},{"id":"s-coal-23","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"In which year was oil struck at Makum in Assam?","options":["1859","1947","2000","1867"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"1867\". That was eight years after the 1859 well in Pennsylvania. \"1859\" is wrong because 1859 is the year of the Pennsylvania well, not Makum. \"1947\" is wrong because 1947 is not the year given for Makum. \"2000\" is wrong because the strike at Makum was in the nineteenth century, in 1867.\nयाद रखो: असम के मकुम में तेल 1867 में लगा। 1859 पेनसिल्वेनिया का साल है, आज़ादी 1947।\nगलत मत याद करना: 1859 दुनिया के पहले कुएँ का साल है, मकुम का नहीं।"},{"id":"s-coal-24","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Lubricating oil from petroleum is used mainly for what?","options":["Surfacing roads","Reducing friction in machines and engines","Filling CNG cylinders","Making naphthalene balls"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Reducing friction in machines and engines\". A thin film of oil lets parts move with less friction. \"Surfacing roads\" is wrong because road surfacing uses bitumen. \"Filling CNG cylinders\" is wrong because CNG cylinders hold compressed natural gas, not lubricating oil. \"Making naphthalene balls\" is wrong because naphthalene balls come from coal tar.\nयाद रखो: स्नेहक तेल मशीन और इंजन में घर्षण घटाता है। सड़क बिटुमन की है, नैफ्थलीन कोलतार की।\nगलत मत याद करना: Surfacing roads सड़क पर बिटुमन बिछता है, स्नेहक तेल नहीं।"},{"id":"s-coal-25","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Which substance is porous, tough, almost pure carbon, and burns with little smoke?","options":["Coal tar","Petroleum gas","Bitumen","Coke"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Coke\". Coke is the nearly pure carbon obtained from coal. \"Coal tar\" is wrong because coal tar is a black liquid, not this porous solid. \"Petroleum gas\" is wrong because petroleum gas is a fuel gas, not a porous solid of carbon. \"Bitumen\" is wrong because bitumen is the dark material used for roads and paints.\nयाद रखो: कोक छिद्रयुक्त, सख्त, लगभग शुद्ध कार्बन है और कम धुएँ से जलता है। कोलतार काला तरल है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Coal tar गाढ़ा बदबूदार तरल है, छिद्रयुक्त ठोस कार्बन नहीं।"},{"id":"s-coal-26","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Which list contains only exhaustible natural resources?","options":["Sunlight, air, coal, and petroleum","Coal, petroleum, natural gas, and forests","Air and sunlight only","Sunlight and air only"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Coal, petroleum, natural gas, and forests\". Each of these can be used up by human activity. \"Sunlight, air, coal, and petroleum\" is wrong because sunlight and air are inexhaustible, so the list is mixed. \"Air and sunlight only\" is wrong because those two are inexhaustible. \"Sunlight and air only\" is wrong because those are inexhaustible resources, not exhaustible ones.\nयाद रखो: समाप्त होने वाले: कोयला, पेट्रोलियम, प्राकृतिक गैस और वन। सूरज और हवा इस सूची में नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Sunlight, air, coal, and petroleum सूरज और हवा खत्म नहीं होते, सूची गंदी हो गई।"},{"id":"s-coal-27","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Coal is used as a fuel in thermal power stations. What is being burnt to help produce electricity?","options":["Coal, a fossil fuel formed from vegetation","Limestone, described as a fossil fuel","Distilled water, described as a fuel","Dry sand"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Coal, a fossil fuel formed from vegetation\". Heat from the coal is used in the power station. \"Limestone, described as a fossil fuel\" is wrong because limestone is not the fossil fuel burnt for this purpose. \"Distilled water, described as a fuel\" is wrong because water is heated by a fuel, and water itself is not the fuel. \"Dry sand\" is wrong because sand does not burn as the station fuel.\nयाद रखो: ताप बिजलीघर में कोयला जलता है, जो वनस्पति से बना जीवाश्म ईंधन है। रेत ईंधन नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Limestone, described as a fossil fuel चूना पत्थर को इस अध्याय का जीवाश्म ईंधन नहीं कहा गया।"},{"id":"s-coal-28","topicId":"s-coal","subject":"science","stem":"Bitumen and kerosene both come from petroleum, but their uses differ. Which pairing is right?","options":["Bitumen fills a domestic LPG cylinder, and kerosene is used only for roads","Both are gases called CNG","Kerosene fuels stoves and jet aircraft, and bitumen is used for roads","Kerosene is the almost pure carbon called coke"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Kerosene fuels stoves and jet aircraft, and bitumen is used for roads\". The refining table gives each fraction its own uses. \"Bitumen fills a domestic LPG cylinder, and kerosene is used only for roads\" is wrong because that swaps a gas fuel with the road material and misuses kerosene. \"Both are gases called CNG\" is wrong because neither fraction is CNG. \"Kerosene is the almost pure carbon called coke\" is wrong because coke comes from coal, and kerosene is a liquid petroleum fraction.\nयाद रखो: मिट्टी का तेल चूल्हे और जेट का ईंधन है। बिटुमन सड़कों पर बिछता है। कोक लगभग शुद्ध कार्बन है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Bitumen fills a domestic LPG cylinder रसोई के सिलेंडर में बिटुमन नहीं भरा जाता।"},{"id":"s-fibres-16","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Melamine is used for kitchenware that holds hot food. Which property makes it suitable?","options":["It resists fire and tolerates heat better than many other plastics","It melts at the temperature of hot tea","It is a good conductor of electricity","It is a thermoplastic that must be reshaped after every meal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"It resists fire and tolerates heat better than many other plastics\". Melamine does not soften the way a thermoplastic would. \"It melts at the temperature of hot tea\" is wrong because it is chosen because it resists heat, not because it melts in tea. \"It is a good conductor of electricity\" is wrong because conduction is not the reason it is used for plates. \"It is a thermoplastic that must be reshaped after every meal\" is wrong because melamine is thermosetting and is not reshaped after each use.\nयाद रखो: मेलामाइन आग सहता है और कई प्लास्टिक से बेहतर गर्मी झेलता है, इसलिए गर्म बर्तन बनते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: It melts at the temperature of hot tea गर्म चाय में पिघलना मेलामाइन का गुण नहीं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-17","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"A plastic bag left on open ground remains for a very long time. What kind of material is it in the environment?","options":["Biodegradable in the same way as vegetable peels","A metal that rusts away in a few days","Non-biodegradable","A gas that mixes with the air at once"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Non-biodegradable\". Plastics are not broken down easily by natural processes. \"Biodegradable in the same way as vegetable peels\" is wrong because peels rot, and plastic does not rot like them. \"A metal that rusts away in a few days\" is wrong because plastic is not iron, and it does not rust away quickly. \"A gas that mixes with the air at once\" is wrong because a bag is a solid and stays in the soil.\nयाद रखो: प्लास्टिक थैली बहुत देर तक पड़ी रहती है, वह अनिम्नीकरणीय है। सब्जी के छिलके सड़ जाते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Biodegradable in the same way as vegetable peels छिलके सड़ते हैं, थैली नहीं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-18","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"The chapter asks citizens to remember which set of actions for plastic waste?","options":["Reduce, Reuse, Recycle, and Recover","Burn, Bury, Break, and Buy more","Reflect, Refract, Disperse, and Invert","Reduce, Rust, Refine, and Radiate"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Reduce, Reuse, Recycle, and Recover\". These four actions are the 4 Rs for dealing with materials such as plastic. \"Burn, Bury, Break, and Buy more\" is wrong because burning plastic can release poisonous gases, and buying more does not reduce waste. \"Reflect, Refract, Disperse, and Invert\" is wrong because those words belong to the study of light. \"Reduce, Rust, Refine, and Radiate\" is wrong because rusting, refining, and radiation are not the 4 Rs.\nयाद रखो: प्लास्टिक के लिए चार काम: घटाओ, फिर इस्तेमाल करो, पुनर्चक्रण करो, और पुनर्प्राप्त करो।\nगलत मत याद करना: Burn, Bury, Break, and Buy more जलाना और और खरीदना किताब का मंत्र नहीं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-19","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Why should plastic waste not be burnt in the open?","options":["Plastic burns into pure oxygen","Plastic is a metal and melts into drinking water","Open burning turns plastic into humus","Burning plastic can release poisonous gases"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Burning plastic can release poisonous gases\". Open burning is harmful to health and to the air. \"Plastic burns into pure oxygen\" is wrong because burning plastic does not make pure oxygen. \"Plastic is a metal and melts into drinking water\" is wrong because plastic is not a metal, and the melt is not drinking water. \"Open burning turns plastic into humus\" is wrong because humus comes from rotting plant and animal matter, not from burning plastic.\nयाद रखो: प्लास्टिक खुले में जलाने पर जहरीली गैसें निकल सकती हैं। ह्यूमस नहीं बनता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Open burning turns plastic into humus जलाने से खाद नहीं, ज़हर बन सकता है।"},{"id":"s-fibres-20","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Which habit follows the idea of using less plastic?","options":["Ask for two plastic bags when one would do","Carry a cloth or jute bag instead of taking a new plastic bag each time","Throw vegetable peels and plastic into the same drain","Burn old bags in the yard"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Carry a cloth or jute bag instead of taking a new plastic bag each time\". A reusable bag reduces the number of plastic bags used. \"Ask for two plastic bags when one would do\" is wrong because that increases plastic use. \"Throw vegetable peels and plastic into the same drain\" is wrong because wastes should be separated, and a drain is not a disposal place. \"Burn old bags in the yard\" is wrong because burning plastic releases poisonous gases.\nयाद रखो: कम प्लास्टिक का तरीका: कपड़े या जूट का थैला ले जाओ, हर बार नया प्लास्टिक मत लो।\nगलत मत याद करना: Ask for two plastic bags when one would do एक की जगह दो थैले खर्च बढ़ाते हैं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-21","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"A plastic comb softens when heated carefully and can be reshaped. It is most likely made of what?","options":["Bakelite","Melamine that has already set","Coke","A thermoplastic such as polythene or PVC"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A thermoplastic such as polythene or PVC\". Thermoplastics soften on heating and can be shaped again. \"Bakelite\" is wrong because bakelite does not soften again after it is set. \"Melamine that has already set\" is wrong because set melamine is thermosetting and does not reshape like this. \"Coke\" is wrong because coke is almost pure carbon from coal, not a comb plastic.\nयाद रखो: जो कंघी सावधानी से गर्म होकर नया आकार ले, वह पॉलिथीन या पीवीसी जैसा तापसुघट्य है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Bakelite तापदृढ़ है, गर्म कंघी की तरह फिर नहीं मुड़ता।"},{"id":"s-fibres-22","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Which of these is biodegradable?","options":["A polythene bag","A vegetable peel","A PVC pipe","A bakelite switch"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A vegetable peel\". Peels are broken down by natural processes. \"A polythene bag\" is wrong because polythene is non-biodegradable. \"A PVC pipe\" is wrong because PVC is a plastic and does not rot like a peel. \"A bakelite switch\" is wrong because bakelite stays in the environment for a long time.\nयाद रखो: सब्जी का छिलका सड़ जाता है, इसलिए जैव निम्नीकरणीय है। पॉलिथीन और पीवीसी नहीं सड़ते।\nगलत मत याद करना: A polythene bag सालों पड़ी रहती है, सड़ने वाली सूची में नहीं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-23","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Rayon mixed with cotton is often used for which household item?","options":["Bedsheets","Electrical switches","Food cans coated with tin","CNG cylinders"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Bedsheets\". The chapter gives bedsheets as a use of rayon mixed with cotton. \"Electrical switches\" is wrong because switches are a use of bakelite. \"Food cans coated with tin\" is wrong because tin coating is electroplating, not a rayon fabric. \"CNG cylinders\" is wrong because CNG cylinders store gas and are not made of rayon cloth.\nयाद रखो: कपास में मिला रेयॉन अक्सर चादरों में इस्तेमाल होता है। स्विच बेकेलाइट के हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Electrical switches बेकेलाइट के होते हैं, रेयॉन-कपास की चादर के नहीं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-24","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Which material is used as a non-stick coating on some cookware?","options":["Rayon made from wood pulp","Acrylic used as a wool substitute","Teflon","Litmus obtained from lichens"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Teflon\". Teflon is a plastic used as a non-stick coating so that food does not stick to the pan. \"Rayon made from wood pulp\" is wrong because rayon is a semi-synthetic fibre, not a non-stick coating. \"Acrylic used as a wool substitute\" is wrong because acrylic is used for sweaters and shawls. \"Litmus obtained from lichens\" is wrong because litmus is an acid-base indicator, not a cookware coating.\nयाद रखो: कुछ बर्तनों की नॉन-स्टिक परत टेफ्लॉन की है। रेयॉन लकड़ी से, ऐक्रिलिक ऊन की नकल।\nगलत मत याद करना: Rayon made from wood pulp रेशम जैसी चादर है, कड़ाही की परत नहीं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-25","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Polyester blended with wool is called what?","options":["Polywool","Bakelite","Rayon pulp","Melamine"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Polywool\". A polyester and wool blend is polywool, and a polyester and cotton blend is polycot. \"Bakelite\" is wrong because bakelite is a thermosetting plastic. \"Rayon pulp\" is wrong because rayon comes from wood pulp and is not the name of the wool blend. \"Melamine\" is wrong because melamine is a heat-resistant plastic for kitchenware.\nयाद रखो: पॉलिएस्टर और ऊन का मिश्रण पॉलीऊल कहलाता है। बेकेलाइट स्विच का प्लास्टिक है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Bakelite कपड़े का मिश्रण नहीं, तापदृढ़ प्लास्टिक है।"},{"id":"s-fibres-26","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Which statement sorts the two types of plastic correctly?","options":["Both types become soft every time they are heated","Thermosetting plastics are used for carry bags because they melt in the sun and can be reshaped in a pan","A thermoplastic can be reshaped on heating, and a thermosetting plastic cannot","Thermoplastics are used for switches because they never soften"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A thermoplastic can be reshaped on heating, and a thermosetting plastic cannot\". Polythene is thermoplastic, while bakelite and melamine are thermosetting. \"Both types become soft every time they are heated\" is wrong because thermosetting plastics do not soften again. \"Thermosetting plastics are used for carry bags because they melt in the sun and can be reshaped in a pan\" is wrong because carry bags are thermoplastics, and thermosetting plastics are not melted and reshaped that way. \"Thermoplastics are used for switches because they never soften\" is wrong because switches use bakelite, which does not soften, and thermoplastics do soften.\nयाद रखो: तापसुघट्य गर्म होकर फिर बन सकता है। तापदृढ़ एक बार ढलने के बाद नहीं मुड़ता।\nगलत मत याद करना: Both types become soft every time they are heated तापदृढ़ दोबारा मुलायम नहीं होता।"},{"id":"s-fibres-27","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Plastic containers are useful for storing many chemicals. Which property explains this?","options":["Plastics react faster than sodium with those chemicals","Many plastics do not react with the chemicals and do not corrode like iron","Plastics are good conductors, so they cool the chemicals","Plastics rot within a day, so the chemical is lost"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Many plastics do not react with the chemicals and do not corrode like iron\". They are light, durable, and often non-reactive. \"Plastics react faster than sodium with those chemicals\" is wrong because sodium is highly reactive, and the containers are chosen because plastics are not. \"Plastics are good conductors, so they cool the chemicals\" is wrong because plastics are poor conductors, and that is not the storage reason given here. \"Plastics rot within a day, so the chemical is lost\" is wrong because plastics last a long time, which is why they are a disposal problem and also why they can store chemicals.\nयाद रखो: कई प्लास्टिक रसायनों से नहीं लड़ते और लोहे की तरह जंग नहीं खाते, इसलिए डिब्बे बनते हैं।\nगलत मत याद करना: Plastics react faster than sodium with those chemicals सोडियम से तेज़ प्रतिक्रिया प्लास्टिक का गुण नहीं।"},{"id":"s-fibres-28","topicId":"s-fibres","subject":"science","stem":"Which thermosetting plastic is used where a dining surface must resist heat?","options":["Polythene","PVC","Acrylic fibre used for a sweater","Melamine"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Melamine\". Melamine resists fire and is used for kitchenware. \"Polythene\" is wrong because polythene is a thermoplastic and can soften when heated. \"PVC\" is wrong because PVC is a thermoplastic. \"Acrylic fibre used for a sweater\" is wrong because acrylic is a wool-like fibre, not the heat-resistant cookware plastic.\nयाद रखो: जहाँ खाने की मेज को गर्मी सहनी हो, वहाँ तापदृढ़ मेलामाइन इस्तेमाल होता है। पॉलिथीन पिघल जाएगी।\nगलत मत याद करना: Polythene तापसुघट्य है, गर्म मेज की सतह नहीं।"},{"id":"s-conservation-16","topicId":"s-conservation","subject":"science","stem":"Which food chain can occur in a forest?","options":["Coal is eaten by petrol, and petrol by kerosene","Grass is eaten by a grasshopper, the grasshopper by a frog, and the frog by a snake","A mirror eats light, and light eats a prism","Bakelite is eaten by melamine"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Grass is eaten by a grasshopper, the grasshopper by a frog, and the frog by a snake\". Each organism is food for the next, which is how a food chain works. \"Coal is eaten by petrol, and petrol by kerosene\" is wrong because those are fuels, not a forest food chain. \"A mirror eats light, and light eats a prism\" is wrong because mirrors and prisms do not form a food chain. \"Bakelite is eaten by melamine\" is wrong because those are plastics, not forest organisms.\nयाद रखो: जंगल की एक शृंखला: घास, टिड्डा, मेंढक, फिर साँप। हर कड़ी अगली का भोजन है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Coal is eaten by petrol, and petrol by kerosene ईंधन एक-दूसरे को नहीं खाते।"},{"id":"s-conservation-17","topicId":"s-conservation","subject":"science","stem":"The variety of plants, animals, and microorganisms found in a region is called what?","options":["Calorific value","Ignition temperature","Ductility","Biodiversity"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Biodiversity\". Biosphere reserves are meant to conserve this variety. \"Calorific value\" is wrong because calorific value is heat from 1 kg of fuel. \"Ignition temperature\" is wrong because ignition temperature is the temperature at which a substance catches fire. \"Ductility\" is wrong because ductility is the ability of a metal to be drawn into wire.\nयाद रखो: किसी इलाके के पौधे, जानवर और सूक्ष्मजीवों की विविधता जैव विविधता है।\nगलत मत याद करना: Calorific value ईंधन की गर्मी है, जीवों की विविधता नहीं।"},{"id":"s-conservation-18","topicId":"s-conservation","subject":"science","stem":"Plants of a region are its flora. What are the animals of that region called?","options":["Fuels","Fauna","Fractions","Filaments"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The correct option is \"Fauna\". Flora and fauna together are the plant and animal life of the area. \"Fuels\" is wrong because fuels are substances that burn. \"Fractions\" is wrong because fractions are the separated parts of petroleum. \"Filaments\" is wrong because a filament is a thin wire or thread, not the animal life of a region.\nयाद रखो: इलाके के पौधे वनस्पति हैं, जानवर प्राणिजात। फौना जानवर, फ्लोरा पौधे।\nगलत मत याद करना: Fuels ईंधन हैं, जंगल के जानवरों का नाम नहीं।"},{"id":"s-conservation-19","topicId":"s-conservation","subject":"science","stem":"Project Tiger was launched for which purpose?","options":["To protect tigers and help their population survive","To increase deforestation","To refine petroleum","To electroplate iron cans with tin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The correct option is \"To protect tigers and help their population survive\". The project aims at the survival of tigers in their forest habitat. \"To increase deforestation\" is wrong because clearing forests would harm tigers. \"To refine petroleum\" is wrong because refining is an oil-industry process. \"To electroplate iron cans with tin\" is wrong because tin plating is a use of electric current, not a wildlife project.\nयाद रखो: प्रोजेक्ट टाइगर बाघों को बचाने और उनकी संख्या टिकाने के लिए शुरू हुआ। जंगल काटने के लिए नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: To increase deforestation बाघ परियोजना जंगल काटने की योजना नहीं।"},{"id":"s-conservation-20","topicId":"s-conservation","subject":"science","stem":"The Class 8 chapter mentions Great Nicobar as which kind of protected area?","options":["An oil refinery","A coal mine","A biosphere reserve","A factory for thermosetting plastic"],"answer":2,"explanation":"The correct option is \"A biosphere reserve\". It names the Great Nicobar Biosphere Reserve among famous protected areas. \"An oil refinery\" is wrong because an oil refinery is not a biosphere reserve. \"A coal mine\" is wrong because a coal mine is not this protected area. \"A factory for thermosetting plastic\" is wrong because plastic manufacture is not the protected area named in the chapter.\nयाद रखो: कक्षा 8 का अध्याय ग्रेट निकोबार को जीवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र कहता है। तेल की रिफाइनरी नहीं।\nगलत मत याद करना: An oil refinery पेट्रोलियम साफ करती है, द्वीप का आरक्षित जंगल नहीं।"}]}] as TestView[];
